,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/abefb1fb785861f05d4d6ee4e9c07b2fb0843ab8","node_id":"C_kwDOR4JmSdoAKGFiZWZiMWZiNzg1ODYxZjA1ZDRkNmVlNGU5YzA3YjJmYjA4NDNhYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/6d64220d11b3c5f4baaf35c11cfb3e0440c1b4cf","sha":"6d64220d11b3c5f4baaf35c11cfb3e0440c1b4cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/6d64220d11b3c5f4baaf35c11cfb3e0440c1b4cf"}],"sha":"abefb1fb785861f05d4d6ee4e9c07b2fb0843ab8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/abefb1fb785861f05d4d6ee4e9c07b2fb0843ab8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/6d64220d11b3c5f4baaf35c11cfb3e0440c1b4cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-23T13:28:06Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-23T13:28:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema): FromStruct tag helper for simple TableDef generation (#108) (#109)\n\n* feat(schema): add FromStruct tag helper for simple TableDef generation (#108)\n\nFromStruct[T](name) derives a *TableDef from a Go struct with `chuck` field\ntags. Intentionally bounded: column name override, nullability, varchar\nsize, primary key, auto-increment, unique, and literal defaults. Returned\nvalue is a normal *TableDef so callers compose Indexes, WithSchema, traits\nand other builders on top. Unsupported field kinds and conflicting tag\ncombinations fail loud via panic at table-declaration time. The explicit\nNewTable / Col DSL stays the primary, recommended schema path.\n\n* fix(schema): FromStruct rejects unknown bare tag tokens (#108)\n\nThe earlier parser silently treated any unknown bare token as a\ncolumn-name override, so typoed flags like `chuck:\"notnul\"`, `\"uniqe\"`,\nor `\"pkk\"` produced a column named after the typo instead of failing\nloud. Similarly `chuck:\"-,notnull\"` would create a column literally\nnamed `-` because the skip shortcut only matched when the tag was\nexactly `-`.\n\nTighten the parser so any non-key=value token outside the known flag\nset (`pk`, `auto`, `unique`, `notnull`, `null`) returns an error.\nRenames must now go through explicit `name=<col>`. The `-` skip is\nhonored only when the entire tag is exactly `-`; mixing it with other\ntokens fails loud. README, godoc, the example, and the in-package\nfixtures switch from bare-name tags to `name=` so the documented\ngrammar matches the implementation. New regression tests cover the\ntypoed flag cases, the malformed skip combinations, and the positive\n`name=` rename path.\n\n* fix(schema): satisfy FromStruct lint check (#108)","tree":{"sha":"327b15f66ba3b47e1ba5bd2a93fb6c57ffef725c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/327b15f66ba3b47e1ba5bd2a93fb6c57ffef725c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/6d64220d11b3c5f4baaf35c11cfb3e0440c1b4cf","verification":{"payload":"tree 327b15f66ba3b47e1ba5bd2a93fb6c57ffef725c\nparent 7d85e28f7367c0209c831e5e25b929b5349699f7\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779542886 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779542886 -0500\n\nfeat(schema): FromStruct tag helper for simple TableDef generation (#108) (#109)\n\n* feat(schema): add FromStruct tag helper for simple TableDef generation (#108)\n\nFromStruct[T](name) derives a *TableDef from a Go struct with `chuck` field\ntags. Intentionally bounded: column name override, nullability, varchar\nsize, primary key, auto-increment, unique, and literal defaults. Returned\nvalue is a normal *TableDef so callers compose Indexes, WithSchema, traits\nand other builders on top. Unsupported field kinds and conflicting tag\ncombinations fail loud via panic at table-declaration time. The explicit\nNewTable / Col DSL stays the primary, recommended schema path.\n\n* fix(schema): FromStruct rejects unknown bare tag tokens (#108)\n\nThe earlier parser silently treated any unknown bare token as a\ncolumn-name override, so typoed flags like `chuck:\"notnul\"`, `\"uniqe\"`,\nor `\"pkk\"` produced a column named after the typo instead of failing\nloud. Similarly `chuck:\"-,notnull\"` would create a column literally\nnamed `-` because the skip shortcut only matched when the tag was\nexactly `-`.\n\nTighten the parser so any non-key=value token outside the known flag\nset (`pk`, `auto`, `unique`, `notnull`, `null`) returns an error.\nRenames must now go through explicit `name=<col>`. The `-` skip is\nhonored only when the entire tag is exactly `-`; mixing it with other\ntokens fails loud. README, godoc, the example, and the in-package\nfixtures switch from bare-name tags to `name=` so the documented\ngrammar matches the implementation. New regression tests cover the\ntypoed flag cases, the malformed skip combinations, and the positive\n`name=` rename path.\n\n* fix(schema): satisfy FromStruct lint check (#108)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqEatmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp6IQAIRom3tfT2cdGkqqX6XrqUKW\nKy2Tov39KDvbXnOIsUKa3RDzKXiTXSkpmW3Pt8UoHNALmTSZtzHr1v/NutQvjE3D\nH6j+w1K6GwIugOs51Pw9Xxuv6gQGvfOjozFRbqXkp6kB1sa51mPdylWU94K6lQsO\nYhiHtjWY1t9DuMA5UR6u9VPtk6bRY1q4yNYPfO5hnUVHHK9GDY/xuk6pqJRfcIPe\nNmQAeK5l/iTk85h3rqKZaZYPn1/4cEFvHipwTt+Z4iNlK+vM/5GwmFX++hz0yzyD\nqlZ3CMUTbcdsnm5GynaF5t5I2hM4k+7jdtNxNNzwQoW260MBk2cjoc8m625wDWtu\n4ottrTEL+J2OW1nyI6uGgIzKM2cDtUwYjz3udQDTZo/kpIyqLWbESpsrSp8etdiU\nvFB0/RXvOy0x/vcsoSZkUAsn57CK771jKZhnFOVBUY+hH65nTWugCaUJaCAdNpo9\ncLI3U2EKZliRst3O9MHANsPTO8Hq0bVGh/Je/wHdRi0nybF15YUJOGJYZrfF9wzb\n5qXdvqjBah1QlYDpTictTub6yiW2NyzWuXC9mecJBOvwCG0XJWedxfOnAo0VqaPy\n8+i5LFM+bl+dJDwllMjelrRDzq3cBHy/F//hZu27gH5FM80BEUsG4egOiv3d8efi\nPQPrGIBUFuVMSjp4mqpL\n=cocd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-23T13:28:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.g