dc9c21c7d98a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-22T01:14:48Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-22T01:14:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema,dbrepo): split audit trail into timestamps, actors, and delete actor (#106) (#107)\n\nReshape the audit-trail API so the four concerns are independent traits\ninstead of one bundled spec, and tables only pay for what they use:\n\n- WithTimestamps()              -> CreatedAt, UpdatedAt\n- WithAuditActors(spec)         -> CreatedBy, UpdatedBy\n- WithSoftDelete()              -> DeletedAt\n- WithDeleteActor(col)          -> DeletedBy\n- WithAuditTrail(spec)          -> convenience bundle of WithTimestamps +\n                                   WithAuditActors (no delete semantics)\n\nSchema-side renames:\n\n- AuditTrailSpec               -> AuditActorsSpec (CreatedBy, UpdatedBy only)\n- AuditColumnDefs              -> AuditActorColumnDefs (+ new DeleteActorColumnDef)\n- DefaultStringAuditTrail()    -> DefaultStringAuditActors() + DefaultStringDeleteActor()\n- WithAuditTrail(spec) is now a bundle that does NOT touch delete semantics\n- New WithAuditActors(spec) and WithDeleteActor(col) primitives\n\ndbrepo-side renames (helpers stay generic over the actor type, nil-safe):\n\n- SetCreateAudit  -> SetCreateActor\n- SetUpdateAudit  -> SetUpdateActor\n- SetDeleteAudit  -> SetDeleteActor\n\nBreak clean per the plan: no deprecated aliases, no compatibility shims.\n\nExamples, table tests, and README updated to reflect the split. The\nconvenience bundle is shown alongside the explicit composition so callers\ncan pick whichever matches their table''s audit shape.\n\nCloses #106","tree":{"sha":"a16e8847c75149b6c0be9c91c4dd27b7c1619031","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/a16e8847c75149b6c0be9c91c4dd27b7c1619031"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/aaf6fe0430cd6ad070aabebe4acdc9c21c7d98a7","verification":{"payload":"tree a16e8847c75149b6c0be9c91c4dd27b7c1619031\nparent dfd1baff38e44cfd288117d9505bc08f1370be30\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779412488 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779412488 -0500\n\nfeat(schema,dbrepo): split audit trail into timestamps, actors, and delete actor (#106) (#107)\n\nReshape the audit-trail API so the four concerns are independent traits\ninstead of one bundled spec, and tables only pay for what they use:\n\n- WithTimestamps()              -> CreatedAt, UpdatedAt\n- WithAuditActors(spec)         -> CreatedBy, UpdatedBy\n- WithSoftDelete()              -> DeletedAt\n- WithDeleteActor(col)          -> DeletedBy\n- WithAuditTrail(spec)          -> convenience bundle of WithTimestamps +\n                                   WithAuditActors (no delete semantics)\n\nSchema-side renames:\n\n- AuditTrailSpec               -> AuditActorsSpec (CreatedBy, UpdatedBy only)\n- AuditColumnDefs              -> AuditActorColumnDefs (+ new DeleteActorColumnDef)\n- DefaultStringAuditTrail()    -> DefaultStringAuditActors() + DefaultStringDeleteActor()\n- WithAuditTrail(spec) is now a bundle that does NOT touch delete semantics\n- New WithAuditActors(spec) and WithDeleteActor(col) primitives\n\ndbrepo-side renames (helpers stay generic over the actor type, nil-safe):\n\n- SetCreateAudit  -> SetCreateActor\n- SetUpdateAudit  -> SetUpdateActor\n- SetDeleteAudit  -> SetDeleteActor\n\nBreak clean per the plan: no deprecated aliases, no compatibility shims.\n\nExamples, table tests, and README updated to reflect the split. The\nconvenience bundle is shown alongside the explicit composition so callers\ncan pick whichever matches their table''s audit shape.\n\nCloses #106","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqD64ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyeUQAD6hg6z/WHYVJC/YKzDvjzF7\n2zkysOeEHogztpG33cMiuakzfnO4Y2ODzZeu7WDeObK8y4R4yFn/yf3EQxollRG7\n0FZ5g3Z