ll}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/dfd1baff38e44cfd288117d9505bc08f1370be30","node_id":"C_kwDOR4JmSdoAKGRmZDFiYWZmMzhlNDRjZmQyODgxMTdkOTUwNWJjMDhmMTM3MGJlMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/c1458b8c46152f37a0711b3f7086e91e115e31a8","sha":"c1458b8c46152f37a0711b3f7086e91e115e31a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/c1458b8c46152f37a0711b3f7086e91e115e31a8"}],"sha":"dfd1baff38e44cfd288117d9505bc08f1370be30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/dfd1baff38e44cfd288117d9505bc08f1370be30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/c1458b8c46152f37a0711b3f7086e91e115e31a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-22T00:02:55Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-22T00:02:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema,dbrepo): typed audit actor columns via AuditTrailSpec (#105)\n\n* feat(schema,dbrepo): typed audit actor columns via AuditTrailSpec (#104)\n\nReplace the no-arg WithAuditTrail() trait with a spec-driven API so audit\nactor identity can be typed however the caller stores it (free-form string,\ninteger FK to a Users table, UUID, etc.) instead of being hardcoded to\nVARCHAR(255) CreatedBy/UpdatedBy/DeletedBy. Each field on AuditTrailSpec is\nthe caller''s own ColumnDef — chuck never imposes a type, nullability, or\nmutability on actor columns.\n\n- schema.AuditTrailSpec carries CreatedBy / UpdatedBy / DeletedBy ColumnDefs\n- schema.DefaultStringAuditTrail() preserves the historical string shape\n  (VARCHAR(255), CreatedBy immutable) as a convenience preset\n- (t *TableDef).WithAuditTrail(spec) is now spec-driven; no-arg form is\n  removed (break clean per issue #104)\n- AuditColumnDefs(spec) and the trait helper layout follow the same shape\n\ndbrepo audit helpers go generic over the actor type so callers do not need\nparallel helper families:\n\n- SetCreateAudit[T any](createdBy, updatedBy *T, actor T)\n- SetUpdateAudit[T any](updatedBy *T, actor T)\n- SetDeleteAudit[T any](deletedAt *time.Time, deletedBy *T, actor T)\n\nNil safety preserved; tests cover string and int64 actor types.\n\nREADME/examples updated to show both the string preset and a typed\n(int64-FK) actor configuration end-to-end.\n\nCloses #104\n\n* docs(readme): clarify WithAuditTrail trait table wording","tree":{"sha":"4419d8c41bb0d3259133c2ba89291735c54f936d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/4419d8c41bb0d3259133c2ba89291735c54f936d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/c1458b8c46152f37a0711b3f7086e91e115e31a8","verification":{"payload":"tree 4419d8c41bb0d3259133c2ba89291735c54f936d\nparent 3c798743712e0d20c21bf96e0afa8115ee956fdb\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779408175 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779408175 -0500\n\nfeat(schema,dbrepo): typed audit actor columns via AuditTrailSpec (#105)\n\n* feat(schema,dbrepo): typed audit actor columns via AuditTrailSpec (#104)\n\nReplace the no-arg WithAuditTrail() trait with a spec-driven API so audit\nactor identity can be typed however the caller stores it (free-form string,\ninteger FK to a Users table, UUID, etc.) instead of being hardcoded to\nVARCHAR(255) CreatedBy/UpdatedBy/DeletedBy. Each field on AuditTrailSpec is\nthe caller''s own ColumnDef — chuck never imposes a type, nullability, or\nmutability on actor columns.\n\n- schema.AuditTrailSpec carries CreatedBy / UpdatedBy / DeletedBy ColumnDefs\n- schema.DefaultStringAuditTrail() preserves the historical string shape\n  (VARCHAR(255), CreatedBy immutable) as a convenience preset\n- (t *TableDef).WithAuditTrail(spec) is now spec-driven; no-arg form is\n  removed (break clean per issue #104)\n- AuditColumnDefs(spec) and the trait helper layout follow the same shape\n\ndbrepo audit helpers go generic over the actor type so callers do not need\nparallel helper families:\n\n- SetCreateAudit[T any](createdBy, updatedBy *T, actor T)\n- SetUpdateAudit[T any](updatedBy *T, actor T)\n- SetDeleteAudit[T any](deletedAt *time.Time, deletedBy *T, actor T)\n\nNil safety preserved; tests cover string and int64 actor types.\n\nREADME/examples updated to show both the string preset and a typed\n(int64-FK) actor configuration end-to-end.\n\nCloses #104\n\n* docs(readme): clarify WithAuditTrail trait table wording","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqD50vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm+IQAJw/dySPe37YRSxYHgwZSsj2\n40KMtkk5hBx9PuwvQcoAruf1/ryU+oKia5dHbbJcUqH4ikFyQ5UHujRdvcIH1XHY\ntQCWCq35vlTdcJgFtTWPdv5G2yVYgdi77Iatxy9k8NzeLuuk8U9g1CqCq0mBaXdD\nJ9HoxH3fYRr1xoqPC31WZXwcFMWO+/iG+RfG7vQly4ziIF0iS8lQUWHNcQ8EaANP\nYnmaX8AetP+8YrwBztiHbwMav+qOoSFeVS1J4lJ9y+Mc8Gwc3T8QAqCFJPON5axO\nzjge6FjMiKJZrN8rY91Ku9156pe7w4P5I+h4h6Lk1tbS5QtVmq7C0EonSqiVdC1q\nWPRIq2MZb+H0XSd8n1RxvWqRPJhONPFav2fhHaAn+LSi4KgxL4DOXrgvASMhg5On\nUmOR6TuLAwce9XZHcdKzCiYlzZ+mMOacheE76I0X6unjdffAa6khlttmjboi7LrE\nxe195pznkZcStQ2F72wrgj+10O95eGvTqSsaHuL/OJ94zsnMVZha/WPi8R/wZG9a\naoT4BwEnEB+dH2DBRXO5+zW2ZH0gCA+GAphjzs5k6cxd2gIWZ5ZL2I9hgaNgLViH\n7igLsftx93Sh37e7IQg6tObqIw2W/DkshV66yjY+1ovnecHZwGsYw9mmuXAy8zxE\nybvnOew0wYxYBwly0r5b\n=0GvD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-22T00:02:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-fl