avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/463c25e822d8b52e201012f4359609b311ca6bac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-21T11:12:56Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-21T11:12:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema): opt-in snapshot operational metadata tables for owned code objects (#100)\n\n* feat(schema): opt-in snapshot operational metadata tables for owned code objects\n\nAdd an opt-in snapshot ledger that records provenance for owned views and\nprocedures: first/last applied timestamps, last changed timestamp, current\ndefinition hash, and optional source repo/rev/tool version. The ledger is\nstrictly apply-side and snapshot only — one current row per owner in\nchuck_database_metadata and one row per owned object in\nchuck_object_metadata; no append-only history table in this first pass.\n\nCallers opt in by setting CodeObjectOptions.Metadata to a populated\nMetadataConfig and running EnsureMetadataTables once before the first\nmetadata-aware apply. Bare apply and the Validate* lane both ignore the\nnew field so existing behaviour is preserved.\n\nThe hash uses the same canonical form as the validate path (leading block\ncomments stripped, whitespace collapsed) so comment-only changes do not\nmove last_changed_at_utc, matching the comment-insensitive drift contract.\n\nEmpty provenance fields are stored as SQL NULL so the ledger can\ndistinguish \"not recorded\" from \"recorded as empty string\".\n\nIncludes SQLite end-to-end coverage of the snapshot timestamp semantics\nplus dialect-agnostic unit tests for hash stability and the per-dialect\nCREATE statements.\n\n* fix(schema): metadata ledger keys object_schema by live-inspection default\n\nrecordCodeObjectMetadata was deriving object_schema via normalizedObject,\nwhich returns \"\" whenever a declaration omits an explicit schema. That is\nwrong for schemaful engines: an unqualified owned object on Postgres\nphysically lives in \"public\", and on MSSQL in \"dbo\", but the ledger row\nrecorded \"\". This both weakened provenance and risked splitting a single\nphysical object across two rows if a caller later switched from a bare\nname to the explicit default schema.\n\nRoute object_schema keying through a new metadataObjectColumns helper that\nreuses the resolveSchemaForInspection contract already used by the\nlive-database introspection paths: empty schema on SQLite (no namespace),\n\"public\" on Postgres for unqualified, \"dbo\" on MSSQL for unqualified, and\ncaller-supplied schema preserved unchanged on all engines.\n\nAdds focused unit coverage for the keying across all three dialects plus\na SQLite end-to-end probe confirming the stored object_schema column.","tree":{"sha":"9d180103654f0077d92426913ab482e4e8ed0669","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/9d180103654f0077d92426913ab482e4e8ed0669"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/463c25e822d8b52e201012f4359609b311ca6bac","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d180103654f0077d92426913ab482e4e8ed0669\nparent 98ad03ed85be2504d3351d93bae2da7c48c12ef4\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779361976 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779361976 -0500\n\nfeat(schema): opt-in snapshot operational metadata tables for owned code objects (#100)\n\n* feat(schema): opt-in snapshot operational metadata tables for owned code objects\n\nAdd an opt-in snapshot ledger that records provenance for owned views and\nprocedures: first/last applied timestamps, last changed timestamp, current\ndefinition hash, and optional source repo/rev/tool version. The ledger is\nstrictly apply-side and snapshot only — one current row per owner in\nchuck_database_metadata and one row per owned object in\nchuck_object_metadata; no append-only history table in this first pass.\n\nCallers opt in by setting CodeObjectOptions.Metadata to a populated\nMetadataConfig and running EnsureMetadataTables once before the first\nmetadata-aware apply. Bare apply and the Validate* lane both ignore the\nnew field so existing behaviour is preserved.\n\nThe hash uses the same canonical form as the validate path (leading block\ncomments stripped, whitespace collapsed) so comment-only changes do not\nmove last_changed_at_utc, matching the comment-insensitive drift contract.\n\nEmpty provenance fields are stored as SQL NULL so the ledger can\ndistinguish \"not recorded\" from \"recorded as empty string\".\n\nIncludes SQLite end-to-end coverage of the snapshot timestamp semantics\nplus dialect-agnostic unit tests for hash stability and the per-dialect\nCREATE statements.\n\n* fix(schema): metadata ledger keys object_schema by live-inspection default\n\nrecordCodeObjectMetadata was deriving object_schema via normalizedObject,\nwhich returns \"\" whenever a declaration omits an explicit schema. That is\nwrong for schemaful engines: an unqualified owned object on Postgres\nphysically lives in \"public\", and on MSSQL in \"dbo\", but the ledger row\nrecorded \"\". This both weakened provenance and risked splitting a single\nphysical object across two rows if a caller later switched from a bare\nname to the explicit default schema.\n\nRoute object_schema keying through a new metadataObjectColumns helper that\nreuses the resolveSchemaForInspection contract already used by the\nlive-database introspection paths: empty schema on SQLite (no namespace),\n\"public\" on Postgres for unqualified, \"dbo\" on MSSQL for unqualified, and\ncaller-supplied schema preserved unchanged on all engines.\n\nAdds focused unit coverage for the keying across all three dialects plus\na SQLite end-to-end probe confirming the stored object_schema column.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDui4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAV74QAJ6wcT8SNmNTgd2iNk7zq+Bq\nW4Zra6r3mbr7XTWo5h+X+64ZkRz8L0gMTcbmmvlLhA9bLJP7QRSL3SNH5RfQAvKe\n+0/Bw4ERzZ2bwoBcA5T4+YRP4NOja+2HaOAFcp+b2/drMZ6qkfX6mnn51TQj3gGg\n/Uuzecaor7PJBuUAnlafilPDw6SfRPLChsgaTMUD2U7fI1NJvwh/Ypsu2UgPqzY8\navyTIGTBjn6VltBJusQUZDF3gj2Yp9uGTcjWrVXVAh337y2NnbQDbBmkHDrOTcqN\nNSm76TvozjG9zCxziIeSB9hH7M8H94bBW3UZlbbH7gM5hHW5bAeQVf2dElH9txl0\nt5YwdUNPRwyXy8E2uscHd5QYBwVCxxh7YiHHj8V+UJxGowHnyLwOfhC4Sh7EhLzl\nYzUpw1etiP2TpM13iqWmtyQ6BifzC0IARnGFCL2MU3aU5+j9VRBAVXaBrWLE6NEJ\nNsMqP8US+RnsPcTayL9KfYbsPwKsB5sMAyHMYW3v1wovyBTSOpSBC5YSD67ppLGJ\nqHGWKeHmC0FOL/DVdPpYGTm++gjFxM9YFahNV6sDOO+jMMZNrVKI34gga8L4t1Jt\nZ3etLElOV7QU4U5jMbInaY1MdQ/i9T4pY4w9C6pcArVgvAFx7nkHsk1JedwaOozr\nhCdVLeuZ/Tk9b5hWtR+P\n=ahsa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-21T11:12:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","g