shipNotice first (#99)\n\n* refactor(schema): owned code-object comments render OwnershipNotice first\n\nReorder the rendered leading-comment stack on owned ViewDef and ProcedureDef\noutput so the chuck-owned OwnershipNotice block renders first (most prominent\nto DB-side readers), DocPreamble second, and the per-object WithDocAnnotation\ncomment last — closest to the SQL body so it reads like a docstring on the\nobject. Strip helper, godocs, unit tests, integration assertions, and the\nREADME \"Opt-in ownership notice\" section move to the same order. Validation\nsemantics are unchanged: comment-only front matter is still ignored, and\napply-owned tolerance still lets validate pass without markers present live.\n\n* docs(schema): drop plan artifact and stale comment wording","tree":{"sha":"71dc513cdf089988e78b620561cc2f8cbee4d98c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/71dc513cdf089988e78b620561cc2f8cbee4d98c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/22e304a933f78313751b055ac42684c76ba4e969","verification":{"payload":"tree 71dc513cdf089988e78b620561cc2f8cbee4d98c\nparent a25b5e8a18c976ebed52e58440ba26f7112563f9\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779286199 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779286199 -0500\n\nrefactor(schema): owned code-object comments render OwnershipNotice first (#99)\n\n* refactor(schema): owned code-object comments render OwnershipNotice first\n\nReorder the rendered leading-comment stack on owned ViewDef and ProcedureDef\noutput so the chuck-owned OwnershipNotice block renders first (most prominent\nto DB-side readers), DocPreamble second, and the per-object WithDocAnnotation\ncomment last — closest to the SQL body so it reads like a docstring on the\nobject. Strip helper, godocs, unit tests, integration assertions, and the\nREADME \"Opt-in ownership notice\" section move to the same order. Validation\nsemantics are unchanged: comment-only front matter is stil