://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/a25b5e8a18c976ebed52e58440ba26f7112563f9","node_id":"C_kwDOR4JmSdoAKGEyNWI1ZThhMThjOTc2ZWJlZDUyZTU4NDQwYmEyNmY3MTEyNTYzZjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/56b8826b966d76a411877e3e0ed49a8d53770d85","sha":"56b8826b966d76a411877e3e0ed49a8d53770d85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/56b8826b966d76a411877e3e0ed49a8d53770d85"}],"sha":"a25b5e8a18c976ebed52e58440ba26f7112563f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/a25b5e8a18c976ebed52e58440ba26f7112563f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/56b8826b966d76a411877e3e0ed49a8d53770d85/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T14:58:06Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T14:58:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema): explicit rename/tombstone support for owned code objects (#94) (#97)\n\n* feat(schema): explicit rename/tombstone support for owned views and procedures (#94)\n\nAdd WithReplaces(names ...chuck.ObjectName) on ViewDef and ProcedureDef so\ncallers can retire renamed or replaced code objects explicitly without\nunsafe schema-wide pruning.\n\nApply semantics:\n- only explicitly listed prior names are dropped, exact (schema + name)\n  match, same object type only (views drop views, procedures drop\n  procedures)\n- ApplyViews / ApplyProcedures dedupe duplicate replacement names across\n  the batch so the same prior name is only dropped once\n- replacement drops use the existing dialect-aware DropSQL renderer\n  (SQLite DROP VIEW IF EXISTS, MSSQL sys.views / sys.procedures guarded\n  drop)\n\nValidate semantics:\n- current object continues to validate as before\n- each listed prior name still present in the live DB surfaces as a\n  ViewDrift / ProcedureDrift entry with ReplacementStale=true\n- new sentinels ErrViewReplacementStillExists and\n  ErrProcedureReplacementStillExists; aggregated drift errors unwrap to\n  these when stale replacements are the only drift cause\n- batch validate dedupes replacement-name checks across defs\n\nNon-goals: no cross-type replacement, no migration planner, no automatic\nname inference, no schema-wide pruning.\n\nTests: SQLite unit tests for apply-side drop, batch dedup, validate\nstale-replacement drift, unwrap branches; SQLite integration test for\nfull rename rollout including out-of-band resurrection and batch-dedup\ndrift. Procedure side covered by unit-level builder + unwrap tests\n(integration is MSSQL-only and follows the same code path).\n\nREADME documents the new lane and the apply / validate semantics.\n\n* docs(readme): caveat stale replacement unwrap on Postgres","tree":{"sha":"552979a1db8a414a09e2788448c18742ed822f18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/552979a1db8a414a09e2788448c18742ed822f18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/56b8826b966d76a411877e3e0ed49a8d53770d85","verification":{"payload":"tree 552979a1db8a414a09e2788448c18742ed822f18\nparent 3d61489a62365275f37e56ad131fbf93a761d367\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779202686 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779202686 -0500\n\nfeat(schema): explicit rename/tombstone support for owned code objects (#94) (#97)\n\n* feat(schema): explicit rename/tombstone support for owned views and procedures (#94)\n\nAdd WithReplaces(names ...chuck.ObjectName) on ViewDef and ProcedureDef so\ncallers can retire renamed or replaced code objects explicitly without\nunsafe schema-wide pruning.\n\nApply semantics:\n- only explicitly listed prior names are dropped, exact (schema + name)\n  match, same object type only (views drop views, procedures drop\n  procedures)\n- ApplyViews / ApplyProcedures dedupe duplicate replacement names across\n  the batch so the same prior name is only dropped once\n- replacement drops use the existing dialect-aware DropSQL renderer\n  (SQLite DROP VIEW IF EXISTS, MSSQL sys.views / sys.procedures guarded\n  drop)\n\nValidate semantics:\n- current object continues to validate as before\n- each listed prior name still present in the live DB surfaces as a\n  ViewDrift / ProcedureDrift entry with ReplacementStale=true\n- new sentinels ErrViewReplacementStillExists and\n  ErrProcedureReplacementStillExists; aggregated drift errors unwrap to\n  these when stale replacements are the only drift cause\n- batch validate dedupes replacement-name checks across defs\n\nNon-goals: no cross-type replacement, no migration planner, no automatic\nname inference, no schema-wide pruning.\n\nTests: SQLite unit tests for apply-side drop, batch dedup, validate\nstale-replacement drift, unwrap branches; SQLite integration test for\nfull rename rollout including out-of-band resurrection and batch-dedup\ndrift. Procedure side covered by unit-level builder + unwrap tests\n(integration is MSSQL-only and follows the same code path).\n\nREADME documents the new lane and the apply / validate semantics.\n\n* docs(readme): caveat stale replacement unwrap on Postgres","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDHp+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlPUQAD7ka+rZErE3RFzg5r1trbt+\nAR8W0Tp7gjtcohZfSyMiCWw+V6qt9IZjpm5R28eAiCMY3fpt/AVcfE1O+FBmNAyH\n7Vr67sngOFReNQosOOXbKT5+ou8RyzOxQi5Z8FJW6HpTrSozbEGLwewNMme+oOLM\nZ5Mv58jGRGnwFSFi1mexpm63qyuQnlPPJTJBZifZw0AhnaI/xfLptGs8tpC3hn6a\nWYNXgpoOuGBgWF96ZCef9p9WRHO7/IccW5L4S7uy35j9PM+G7iVoR0iQWJwwKcpH\nio4Ayr/+wWlQR4Y9mT7NxSmiSV3iEuYp4lwsTNqK0tKYuMUk24fXnGgur5vI7OVV\n4u9bEYPSn7iiKDJF0bmbZN66cKvp+OvcgE0QPqMRQMtvce+eo2tHUFGiBDq1Gd12\nN19zrUNoL3vfCYMiSVavtk6seAXfgQWfuoT1ApyBRnhrcaJQ+1hNJn/imGXOTaPF\noUt/Qfs5nVqJv1LK2KucESlRT0kxJrVCsuTYpAe2Ri/sT0BzMjPLWQuRO2vimYth\nLBzNlqrhJU17aRFZv5369jxt6xggW1SfGgsmnLgJEWhYW1YHao7lO1/ZXZKBxFbe\nZOBqAKw0g0bt/x1YAMmvmrHDQo2wQg/AvdXXUgBm8XQ/VKF8fKFOyKL0eD2YAc3X\nwGntPhvFuwveKlpEv4A5\n=YRoy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T14:58:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-fl