/3d61489a62365275f37e56ad131fbf93a761d367/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T14:58:02Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T14:58:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(audit): plan-015 repo audit artifact (#90)\n\n* chore(audit): plan-015 repo audit artifact\n\nRead-heavy diagnosis pass across root package, schema/, and dbrepo/.\nProduces one prioritized artifact with file refs and severity ratings;\nno code changes. Verified the highest-impact claims by hand (corrected\ntwo agent false positives along the way).\n\nHighlights:\n- F1: SQLite/Postgres QuoteIdentifier does not escape embedded `\"` (filed #87)\n- F2: MSSQL CreateTableIfNotExists / DropTableIfExists embed bracket-\n  quoted name into N''...'' literal without escaping single quotes (#88)\n- F3: canonicalizeViewBody is reused for procedures and should be\n  renamed canonicalizeStatement (#89)\n- F4-F10: smaller refactor / coverage / docs-drift items recorded for\n  follow-up; recommend bundling rather than per-issue spam.\n\n* chore(audit): drop overclaimed F8 docs-drift finding\n\ndbrepo/fragments.go package doc already covers both @Name and\nQ-suffixed lanes and the lib/pq + sqlx.Rebind caveats. F8 claim\n\"still claims dialect-agnostic\" is not supported by file text;\nremove the finding and sync executive summary, remaining-findings\nlist, and Lane C grouping.","tree":{"sha":"f0f793c6173f1d6ee0ed9e2cae7e38f801af7a18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/f0f793c6173f1d6ee0ed9e2cae7e38f801af7a18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/3d61489a62365275f37e56ad131fbf93a761d367","verification":{"payload":"tree f0f793c6173f1d6ee0ed9e2cae7e38f801af7a18\nparent 5513eb1ad5d4fe77d99b8ce386e20a991eaa708c\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779202682 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779202682 -0500\n\nchore(audit): plan-015 repo audit artifact (#90)\n\n* chore(audit): plan-015 repo audit artifact\n\nRead-heavy diagnosis pass across root package, schema/, and dbrepo/.\nProduces one prioritized artifact with file refs and severity ratings;\nno code changes. Verified the highest-impact claims by hand (corrected\ntwo agent false positives along the way).\n\nHighlights:\n- F1: SQLite/Postgres QuoteIdentifier does not escape embedded `\"` (filed #87)\n- F2: MSSQL CreateTableIfNotExists / DropTableIfExists embed bracket-\n  quoted name into N''...'' literal without escaping single quotes (#88)\n- F3: canonicalizeViewBody is reused for procedures and should be\n  renamed canonicalizeStatement (#89)\n- F4-F10: smaller refactor / coverage / docs-drift items recorded for\n  follow-up; recommend bundling rather than per-issue spam.\n\n* chore(audit): drop overclaimed F8 docs-drift finding\n\ndbrepo/fragments.go package doc already covers both @Name and\nQ-suffixed lanes and the lib/pq + sqlx.Rebind caveats. F8 claim\n\"still claims dialect-agnostic\" is not supported by file text;\nremove the finding and sync executive summary, remaining-findings\nlist, and Lane C grouping.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDHp6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ5QQAKYKDtueWR6oSsQ3n8Ay4dL+\nXye017jjfKM7ty40tyfPzOq6PEvBmRJLsCiILOkt8+kSDsY5h6ZFtNJWNmj6wGE+\nbmBeUBOybPRYjXFCmLQ5U3I+U48Cl3AcaUmTRLfH3caJV5qeNEso4OXLNaOSA9Oz\nokSCaIQYc1ueirIHT/rygmyr8zczABpWNrmAKimKsMQ1UrgPrTCOamBmDUzB0Ovu\njF21eeMe6r09PMTELL8XqqFVheK2bLCZzyjhWYX812zFtFojpv4j+wKGU8cKc/Jh\nwmY2ogjVDRmh8Uy/qyjD9JdBOjVNeQR7NIRhYCBMgrDgp80SukrZJN7Z0KkwqH8G\nAEW3a3YSWmZvdaGzd1+JAL19HQaT++dEwxyIT57NGmFBGJxF3xEqJ15x2wvmHhSC\ndD9HcbsDuokpNNYyuQKV4GN7hCvasLE3ZSKYZi8Lm6D5GyPCkyKKBSv3yHfHGqwE\niWCKfl1KRzFYCGb8D1TQ84om6+2aIPiSqt+KBbhj8KpPbSCkgXZfgV1tg+5C3FzZ\nMAmGBvjpRIPKpeRbA3mIhRRxUYkbiaxURbGyKtjb/Kn6cQAd/hrl7CxZtTwqqH96\nuoaKk+hZIVYXDAPSjthbpdVS7ah8l+O6PcelTiTPI2GFqhrnwEkgQ/m8ZrCNIBF4\n0ZhWKZBIBxLtn2wJzJsU\