":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/741b7380fc01beccfc33198d3972f0201eea2892","node_id":"C_kwDOR4JmSdoAKDc0MWI3MzgwZmMwMWJlY2NmYzMzMTk4ZDM5NzJmMDIwMWVlYTI4OTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/b74219d6e63cf442863d310cbe0a124adfe6ee30","sha":"b74219d6e63cf442863d310cbe0a124adfe6ee30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/b74219d6e63cf442863d310cbe0a124adfe6ee30"}],"sha":"741b7380fc01beccfc33198d3972f0201eea2892","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/741b7380fc01beccfc33198d3972f0201eea2892"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/b74219d6e63cf442863d310cbe0a124adfe6ee30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T13:06:51Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T13:06:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema): gate ownership notice to apply-owned code objects (#84) (#86)\n\nReworks the CodeObjectOptions contract so the ownership notice and an\noptional caller-controlled doc preamble are apply-owned decoration rather\nthan declaration-owned content. Validate*WithOptions strips the exact\nconfigured prefix from live text before canonical comparison and\ntolerates its absence, letting validate-only callers pass options\nwithout forcing markers to exist in the live database. Live text that\ncarries a different leading comment still reports drift.\n\nAPI:\n- CodeObjectOptions.OwnershipNotice unchanged (chuck-marker, soft text).\n- CodeObjectOptions.DocPreamble added (caller commentary; not ownership).\n- Render order when both set: DocPreamble first, then OwnershipNotice,\n  then the payload. Each non-empty field becomes a \"/* ... */ \" segment.\n\nHelpers:\n- renderApplyPrefix builds the combined preamble+notice prefix.\n- stripConfiguredApplyPrefix strips the exact configured prefix from\n  live text, in the same render order, tolerating absent fields.\n\nValidateView/ProcedureWithOptions:\n- Compare canonical(declared body) against canonical(stripped live)\n  rather than prefixing the declared side. Postgres view path remains\n  existence-only and unchanged.\n\nTests:\n- Unit coverage for both fields, ordering, strip tolerance, wrong-order\n  prefixes, and different leading comment.\n- SQLite integration test now exercises preamble+notice together,\n  asserts render order in sqlite_master.sql, and verifies apply-owned\n  tolerance (bare apply + validate-with-options = clean) plus drift\n  detection for unconfigured leading comments.\n- MSSQL integration test (gated) exercises the same tolerance contract\n  for procedures.\n\nDocs:\n- README \"Opt-in ownership notice\" subsection rewritten to describe the\n  apply-owned contract, document the render order, and replace the\n  same-options-required wording with the new tolerance table.","tree":{"sha":"4b5cf4197ff38471380c3d758a26c215242c8ba7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/4b5cf4197ff38471380c3d758a26c215242c8ba7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/b74219d6e63cf442863d310cbe0a124adfe6ee30","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b5cf4197ff38471380c3d758a26c215242c8ba7\nparent d68be3c743dfbc71453d64bbc3772f343033e44b\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779196011 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779196011 -0500\n\nfeat(schema): gate ownership notice to apply-owned code objects (#84) (#86)\n\nReworks the CodeObjectOptions contract so the ownership notice and an\noptional caller-controlled doc preamble are apply-owned decoration rather\nthan declaration-owned content. Validate*WithOptions strips the exact\nconfigured prefix from live text before canonical comparison and\ntolerates its absence, letting validate-only callers pass options\nwithout forcing markers to exist in the live database. Live text that\ncarries a different leading comment still reports drift.\n\nAPI:\n- CodeObjectOptions.OwnershipNotice unchanged (chuck-marker, soft text).\n- CodeObjectOptions.DocPreamble added (caller commentary; not ownership).\n- Render order when both set: DocPreamble first, then OwnershipNotice,\n  then the payload. Each non-empty field becomes a \"/* ... */ \" segment.\n\nHelpers:\n- renderApplyPrefix builds the combined preamble+notice prefix.\n- stripConfiguredApplyPrefix strips the exact configured prefix from\n  live text, in the same render order, tolerating absent fields.\n\nValidateView/ProcedureWithOptions:\n- Compare canonical(declared body) against canonical(stripped live)\n  rather than prefixing the declared side. Postgres view path remains\n  existence-only and unchanged.\n\nTests:\n- Unit coverage for both fields, ordering, strip tolerance, wrong-order\n  prefixes, and different leading comment.\n- SQLite integration test now exercises preamble+notice together,\n  asserts render order in sqlite_master.sql, and verifies apply-owned\n  tolerance (bare apply + validate-with-options = clean) plus drift\n  detection for unconfigured leading comments.\n- MSSQL integration test (gated) exercises the same tolerance contract\n  for procedures.\n\nDocs:\n- README \"Opt-in ownership notice\" subsection rewritten to describe the\n  apply-owned contract, document the render order, and replace the\n  same-options-required wording with the new tolerance table.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDGBrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALKMQAGY2U6AKxkyHLmDOZC6DuEOA\n3DxX3LHXt6LHSMgEGNIFu4+maJNra1vfxo9d5+VBJLTvVLXLmUt56XpXViNy1/vF\nBLNJ5857t+K/ce4CNBll34Jv2rGTpJV9PteAaB5dV2vtfaGkVcO/prxZPqZVPzOs\nM8ut94I82BXTDcA98zXC9gV0OSiicVG5AAneXCjmQ7eIQ58dloZPqaOKF2OzcDj+\nKh8y5fsyhAuhrBsEY79P2gj+lx889/irwEAItztQbw5ZckSMDfhyX6NGROpg2fBR\nj7TmVtSHt9Al4g2SquPkdFNLDdSVOO4QxMIY9gFSK78YWYK3SJirNNmw7v3vaNZe\nkCjUSQeRZqk80euiauAqDrubBQN5pQX0yIQJCGviY9C9BY3dcPlcArvFdlqcoPp7\nCM0RJpzBe4MWbIiPH8/lv3eNsgTVqqdDELW95pbVetntWaqWoctfnZZMSqg9a6F4\nRgBSUTcdwlnq8J5hExMSXkuC2G14iJubFIIttmopFdfkdrtnxkLBDhthPPETyFXb\nU7cb1mbSF/Yo/bk0znl7gWkl+KOWbnY78WPj27YUxSzAa4DIVbm8xSvzBtOgXava\nUv05agOyrjioc5SqEyBanjdR5OLg3cgRF/iXAue++KfLcdl+h4Bdt4vveSOqepEt\nJYS57BiIRgwFR6A+VHcW\n=lrOe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T13:06:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/b74219d6e63cf442863d310cbe0a124adfe6ee30","node_id":"C_kwDOR4JmSdoAKGI3NDIxOWQ2ZTYzY2Y0NDI4NjNkMzEwY2JlMGExMjRhZGZlNmVlMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/d68be3c743dfbc71453d64bbc3772f343033e44b","sha":"d68be3c743dfbc71453d64bbc3772f343033e44b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/d68be3c743dfbc71453d64bbc3772f343033e44b"}],"sha":"b74219d6e63cf442863d310cbe0a124adfe6ee30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/b74219d6e63cf442863d310cbe0a124adfe6ee30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/d68be3c743dfbc71453d64bbc3772f343033e44b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T12:21:16Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T12:21:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema): opt-in ownership notice for owned views and procedures (#84) (#85)\n\n* feat(schema): opt-in ownership notice for owned views and procedures (#84)\n\nOwned views and procedures can now carry an embedded ownership notice\nso DB-side readers can tell the object is code-owned without forcing\nevery call site to thread a per-definition banner. The notice is\nopt-in, set once on a `schema.CodeObjectOptions` struct, and consumed\nby the new `*WithOptions` apply/validate helpers. Default behavior is\nunchanged: existing callers using the bare `ApplyView` /\n`ValidateView` / `ApplyProcedure` / `ValidateProcedure` helpers see no\nemitted comment.\n\nNew public API:\n\n  schema.CodeObjectOptions{OwnershipNotice string}\n  schema.DefaultOwnershipNotice  // canonical wording from #84\n\n  // Views (all dialects):\n  schema.ApplyViewWithOptions / schema.ApplyViewsWithOptions\n  schema.ValidateViewWithOptions / schema.ValidateViewsWithOptions\n\n  // Procedures (MSSQL only):\n  schema.ApplyProcedureWithOptions / schema.ApplyProceduresWithOptions\n  schema.ValidateProcedureWithOptions / schema.ValidateProceduresWithOptions\n\nThe bare `Apply* / Validate*` helpers now delegate to their\n`*WithOptions` counterparts with the zero `CodeObjectOptions`, so the\ndefault no-notice path stays a single code path.\n\nCoherence: the option-aware Validate* helpers prepend the same notice\nto the declared body/definition before canonicalization, so apply\nfollowed by validate using the same options never reports false drift.\nMixing bare apply with option-aware validate (or vice versa) honestly\nreports body drift — proven by the SQLite e2e test which exercises\nboth directions.\n\nInjection points:\n\n- ViewDef: notice prepended to body, then rendered through the same\n  per-engine create/replace template (`CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW <qn> AS\n  /* notice */ <body>` etc.). View.go grows an unexported\n  `createOrReplaceWithBody` helper used by both the public method and\n  the option-aware apply path.\n\n- ProcedureDef: notice prepended to the definition payload, sitting\n  between the qualified procedure name and the first token of the\n  caller''s definition (`CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE <qn> /* notice */\n  @AgentID INT AS ...`). T-SQL accepts block comments anywhere\n  whitespace is legal, so the comment is grammar-safe before\n  parameter declarations and before AS. procedure.go grows an\n  unexported `createOrAlterWithDefinition` helper.\n\nEngine notes (documented in `schema.CodeObjectOptions` godoc and\nREADME):\n\n- SQLite: comment survives in `sqlite_master.sql`.\n- MSSQL: comment survives in `sys.sql_modules.definition`.\n- Postgres: `pg_get_viewdef` reconstructs SELECT from the parse tree\n  and discards comments. The notice still lands in the issued\n  CREATE statement but is invisible via pg_get_viewdef. This does\n  NOT produce false drift because Postgres view validation is\n  existence-only (ErrViewBodyComparisonUnsupported, see #84 nuance).\n\nTests:\n\n- `schema/code_object_options_test.go`: unit coverage for\n  `renderOwnershipComment`, `applyOwnershipNoticePrefix`, default-path\n  regression on both view and procedure renderers, notice-bearing\n  render across SQLite / MSSQL / Postgres dialects, and engine-guard\n  preservation on `ApplyProcedureWithOptions` /\n  `ValidateProceduresWithOptions` for non-MSSQL dialects.\n- `schema/integration_test.go`:\n  * `TestViewValidateApplyWithOptions_SQLite_OwnershipNotice` —\n    full SQLite cycle, asserts notice lands in sqlite_master.sql,\n    bare-validate sees option-apply as drift, and the inverse.\n  * `TestProcedureValidateApplyWithOptions_MSSQL` — same cycle\n    for MSSQL procedures, gated by CHUCK_MSSQL_URL.\n\nDocs: README \"Code-Object Validate and Apply\" section gains an\n\"Opt-in ownership notice\" subsection with central-config example,\ncoherence contract, and engine-by-engine visibility table.\n\n* docs(schema): use GitHub URL in DefaultOwnershipNotice (#84)\n\nReplace bare \"chuck\" wording with the explicit\nhttps://github.com/catgoose/chuck URL in DefaultOwnershipNotice so DB\nreaders who do not recognize the project name can find it directly.\n\n- schema/code_object_options.go: update const + godoc rationale\n- schema/code_object_options_test.go: assertion now matches URL form\n- schema/integration_test.go: SQLite + MSSQL e2e assertions updated\n- README.md: prose description quotes the new URL form\n\nNo API or behavior change; the const value is the only user-visible\nshift and remains a soft notice.","tree":{"sha":"03a1ed057a794cb5bf308fb5101794b399ae6ba1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/03a1ed057a794cb5bf308fb5101794b399ae6ba1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/d68be3c743dfbc71453d64bbc3772f343033e44b","verification":{"payload":"tree 03a1ed057a794cb5bf308fb5101794b399ae6ba1\nparent cdd05ce6f74612f0046b77021cc860e921b967eb\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779193276 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779193276 -0500\n\nfeat(schema): opt-in ownership notice for owned views and procedures (#84) (#85)\n\n* feat(schema): opt-in ownership notice for owned views and procedures (#84)\n\nOwned views and procedures can now carry an embedded ownership notice\nso DB-side readers can tell the object is code-owned without forcing\nevery call site to thread a per-definition banner. The notice is\nopt-in, set once on a `schema.CodeObjectOptions` struct, and consumed\nby the new `*WithOptions` apply/validate helpers. Default behavior is\nunchanged: existing callers using the bare `ApplyView` /\n`ValidateView` / `ApplyProcedure` / `ValidateProcedure` helpers see no\nemitted comment.\n\nNew public API:\n\n  schema.CodeObjectOptions{OwnershipNotice string}\n  schema.DefaultOwnershipNotice  // canonical wording from #84\n\n  // Views (all dialects):\n  schema.ApplyViewWithOptions / schema.ApplyViewsWithOptions\n  schema.ValidateViewWithOptions / schema.ValidateViewsWithOptions\n\n  // Procedures (MSSQL only):\n  schema.ApplyProcedureWithOptions / schema.ApplyProceduresWithOptions\n  schema.ValidateProcedureWithOptions / schema.ValidateProceduresWithOptions\n\nThe bare `Apply* / Validate*` helpers now delegate to their\n`*WithOptions` counterparts with the zero `CodeObjectOptions`, so the\ndefault no-notice path stays a single code path.\n\nCoherence: the option-aware Validate* helpers prepend the same notice\nto the declared body/definition before canonicalization, so apply\nfollowed by validate using the same options never reports false drift.\nMixing bare apply with option-aware validate (or vice versa) honestly\nreports body drift — proven by the SQLite e2e test which exercises\nboth directions.\n\nInjection points:\n\n- ViewDef: notice prepended to body, then rendered through the same\n  per-engine create/replace template (`CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW <qn> AS\n  /* notice */ <body>` etc.). View.go grows an unexported\n  `createOrReplaceWithBody` helper used by both the public method and\n  the option-aware apply path.\n\n- ProcedureDef: notice prepended to the definition payload, sitting\n  between the qualified procedure name and the first token of the\n  caller''s definition (`CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE <qn> /* notice */\n  @AgentID INT AS ...`). T-SQL accepts block comments anywhere\n  whitespace is legal, so the comment is grammar-safe before\n  parameter declarations and before AS. procedure.go grows an\n  unexported `createOrAlterWithDefinition` helper.\n\nEngine notes (documented in `schema.CodeObjectOptions` godoc and\nREADME):\n\n- SQLite: comment survives in `sqlite_master.sql`.\n- MSSQL: comment survives in `sys.sql_modules.definition`.\n- Postgres: `pg_get_viewdef` reconstructs SELECT from the parse tree\n  and discards comments. The notice still lands in the issued\n  CREATE statement but is invisible via pg_get_viewdef. This does\n  NOT produce false drift because Postgres view validation is\n  existence-only (ErrViewBodyComparisonUnsupported, see #84 nuance).\n\nTests:\n\n- `schema/code_object_options_test.go`: unit coverage for\n  `renderOwnershipComment`, `applyOwnershipNoticePrefix`, default-path\n  regression on both view and procedure renderers, notice-bearing\n  render across SQLite / MSSQL / Postgres dialects, and engine-guard\n  preservation on `ApplyProcedureWithOptions` /\n  `ValidateProceduresWithOptions` for non-MSSQL dialects.\n- `schema/integration_test.go`:\n  * `TestViewValidateApplyWithOptions_SQLite_OwnershipNotice` —\n    full SQLite cycle, asserts notice lands in sqlite_master.sql,\n    bare-validate sees option-apply as drift, and the inverse.\n  * `TestProcedureValidateApplyWithOptions_MSSQL` — same cycle\n    for MSSQL procedures, gated by CHUCK_MSSQL_URL.\n\nDocs: README \"Code-Object Validate and Apply\" section gains an\n\"Opt-in ownership notice\" subsection with central-config example,\ncoherence contract, and engine-by-engine visibility table.\n\n* docs(schema): use GitHub URL in DefaultOwnershipNotice (#84)\n\nReplace bare \"chuck\" wording with the explicit\nhttps://github.com/catgoose/chuck URL in DefaultOwnershipNotice so DB\nreaders who do not recognize the project name can find it directly.\n\n- schema/code_object_options.go: update const + godoc rationale\n- schema/code_object_options_test.go: assertion now matches URL form\n- schema/integration_test.go: SQLite + MSSQL e2e assertions updated\n- README.md: prose description quotes the new URL form\n\nNo API or behavior change; the const value is the only user-visible\nshift and remains a soft notice.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDFW8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgywQAJPxFTnaa/kdim6doBcCvwl4\nZnhxMDcEfrW6A1jyk1jzllVbZIsJ0rqu1cTIDe5woJ+8M5taUo4CF/SIIaKOpmBi\nJWax+Eiyu5EEQPIhTr8afW4CZTpBLJva1Te2jiH/Qt9gQBAy+NbsQzR2SqSUrAAE\nvM38PXQr38FSXTBhvoRNwFrOJwW1vNVWc0k9VkuOJIfjhpaHGoGHP3Ug5QbNleI/\nC5xHmpTComS3gf4kqmqs9lWLa5XnrZUYinOLllapleHuSQATW5apeN8DUa0ls/a9\nHFN0V3eJvOvOchxi8rznGbDNR0h3FOueiHLXes4Yj3uRaxBFxDYWrJ6fZnKIpM8N\n3o2dmfbb0c5EE6caLr0LdaWAEFT8mH4AFxroCnvh/iMaveijU36G8db2J2HdGaeT\nX4DxXkfPdqVlBmHtSzBpNRHu+MINg6VkyQgLT5zZ/nm7W0V5sb+BHTZY2dotxFP3\nc24TDKUAhUHwWStCUiz/+8hSF2M+V3N0spOxyhDRdQRDa8xVNdPrvLyH02BpNpml\nBfdO4E/lz2OpXlvknrVzeBNV7P1HmuT5Cio+KWm8J2qsGft1mbzJCzJrLhcncnIC\noqN6CzJPK6M3D/9wZG1+6pv24rp8O8NRlpjuE6tsddkGrPAfLfzTHY4D6velEMcQ\nOBaxHYKnJl+1UOMA/2RE\n=GbJB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T12:21:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/d68be3c743dfbc71453d64bbc3772f343033e44b","node_id":"C_kwDOR4JmSdoAKGQ2OGJlM2M3NDNkZmJjNzE0NTNkNjRiYmMzNzcyZjM0MzAzM2U0NGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/cdd05ce6f74612f0046b77021cc860e921b967eb","sha":"cdd05ce6f74612f0046b77021cc860e921b967eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/cdd05ce6f74612f0046b77021cc860e921b967eb"}],"sha":"d68be3c743dfbc71453d64bbc3772f343033e44b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/d68be3c743dfbc71453d64bbc3772f343033e44b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/cdd05ce6f74612f0046b77021cc860e921b967eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T00:30:55Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T00:30:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dbrepo): UpdateBuilder.SetValues positional-bind opt-out (#71) (#83)\n\nUpdateBuilder previously emitted `SET col = @col` placeholders\nunconditionally via SetClause / SetClauseQ, with no caller-visible way\nto swap in positional placeholders. The @Name token survives\n`database/sql` drivers that translate sql.NamedArg natively\n(go-sqlite3, go-mssqldb, pgx) but it does not survive lib/pq or\nsqlx.Rebind — both leave `@col` verbatim and Postgres rejects the\nparse. Issue #71 documents the failure on the lib/pq + sqlx stack.\n\nAdds an additive `SetValues(values ...any)` method on UpdateBuilder\nthat switches the SET clause to `?` placeholders and prepends the\nsupplied values to the returned args slice (followed by the\nWHERE-clause args). The default named path is untouched: existing\ncallers see no behavior change unless they explicitly opt in.\n\nContract:\n  - len(values) must match len(columns) — Build panics on mismatch\n    rather than silently emitting a malformed statement.\n  - Returned args slice is <SET values...> <WHERE args...>; SET first\n    so sqlx.Rebind rewrites left-to-right against deterministic input.\n  - Dialect identifier quoting (WithDialect) still applies to column\n    identifiers; only the placeholder shape changes.\n  - Placeholder is always `?` (independent of dialect) because the path\n    targets sqlx.Rebind-style rewriting; callers using native Postgres\n    positional ($N) on lib/pq route through `sqlx.Rebind(sqlx.DOLLAR, ...)`.\n\nDocs: package-level @Name claim in dbrepo/fragments.go corrected to\nname the drivers it actually works on (go-sqlite3, go-mssqldb, pgx) and\nto point lib/pq / sqlx callers at the positional escape hatches. README\ngets a new \"Positional bind opt-out (SetValues)\" subsection under\nUpdateBuilder and a corrected \"dbrepo intro\" paragraph that no longer\nimplies universal driver-agnostic safety.\n\nTests: nine subtests under TestUpdateBuilder_SetValues covering ?\nemission, SET-before-WHERE arg ordering, per-dialect quoting,\nRETURNING composition, schema-qualified table quoting, the\nzero-cols/zero-values edge, the count-mismatch panic, and a regression\nguard that the default @Name path is unchanged. Adds\nExampleUpdateBuilder_SetValues for godoc.","tree":{"sha":"d6f21f994e8efcbd3b617b6429b08569f8f9ee15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/d6f21f994e8efcbd3b617b6429b08569f8f9ee15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/cdd05ce6f74612f0046b77021cc860e921b967eb","verification":{"payload":"tree d6f21f994e8efcbd3b617b6429b08569f8f9ee15\nparent 82a36c9a4e896fdbd50f144ae96e9df59112b2ae\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779150655 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779150655 -0500\n\nfeat(dbrepo): UpdateBuilder.SetValues positional-bind opt-out (#71) (#83)\n\nUpdateBuilder previously emitted `SET col = @col` placeholders\nunconditionally via SetClause / SetClauseQ, with no caller-visible way\nto swap in positional placeholders. The @Name token survives\n`database/sql` drivers that translate sql.NamedArg natively\n(go-sqlite3, go-mssqldb, pgx) but it does not survive lib/pq or\nsqlx.Rebind — both leave `@col` verbatim and Postgres rejects the\nparse. Issue #71 documents the failure on the lib/pq + sqlx stack.\n\nAdds an additive `SetValues(values ...any)` method on UpdateBuilder\nthat switches the SET clause to `?` placeholders and prepends the\nsupplied values to the returned args slice (followed by the\nWHERE-clause args). The default named path is untouched: existing\ncallers see no behavior change unless they explicitly opt in.\n\nContract:\n  - len(values) must match len(columns) — Build panics on mismatch\n    rather than silently emitting a malformed statement.\n  - Returned args slice is <SET values...> <WHERE args...>; SET first\n    so sqlx.Rebind rewrites left-to-right against deterministic input.\n  - Dialect identifier quoting (WithDialect) still applies to column\n    identifiers; only the placeholder shape changes.\n  - Placeholder is always `?` (independent of dialect) because the path\n    targets sqlx.Rebind-style rewriting; callers using native Postgres\n    positional ($N) on lib/pq route through `sqlx.Rebind(sqlx.DOLLAR, ...)`.\n\nDocs: package-level @Name claim in dbrepo/fragments.go corrected to\nname the drivers it actually works on (go-sqlite3, go-mssqldb, pgx) and\nto point lib/pq / sqlx callers at the positional escape hatches. README\ngets a new \"Positional bind opt-out (SetValues)\" subsection under\nUpdateBuilder and a corrected \"dbrepo intro\" paragraph that no longer\nimplies universal driver-agnostic safety.\n\nTests: nine subtests under TestUpdateBuilder_SetValues covering ?\nemission, SET-before-WHERE arg ordering, per-dialect quoting,\nRETURNING composition, schema-qualified table quoting, the\nzero-cols/zero-values edge, the count-mismatch panic, and a regression\nguard that the default @Name path is unchanged. Adds\nExampleUpdateBuilder_SetValues for godoc.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqC69ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAF5sQAD5zeiqho7p//nZixAe2+R+N\n1EBKN/rNWe8hGLHnjxUI1sAR+OUhA+q/zzFdy6OY0dpfQVO7Kc1I3ttSY1KL4hy4\nlU/fI529f3BIJWa/uA+2h94rDumrKjbaxpHBRFC/RrKP9Mw8nlJmXEdY2OMzKjQb\nrbPhv8WqwCAZP4pg5WRPz+9SBvY+L/OeiOqNBHSFAnzYOhpYYUItwPJDMcGyqHvC\nUE1xHawgvxlrQf+Pmq+GMr6B8bqrsXan9nI+YMIe+AtoqcQ3kssyv1WJs3DItA1u\nvHb7KYMsj17+qVqGwEWREd94cBKLJXc33riKPS09l3nip1RRGp34lC/6JtHoeaJ9\nYVe8Gboqn/jW/L7lnSWmW/cvlqVg9dpPUaAL32s+0F1XQ+IR9mIvh8ORvzS8ZgYQ\nZxtw0caAqksc2U/UBqQX9trJtMsXkcV1dAj0Ibor/VW2mYHeiqQhlTWTqMDrZ1VL\na9f6jIlxzVTVns3QONqUke/BHyH4au+otgFFo3KKmNFiQiVsod01qXUFP+rkmfuW\nETUNclE1dKVa9DPrMLZO/ox58LrK54x0UHdxxLN7PicRxCBdoHgJ7P/WCSO4aSIG\nJNQGvoIJqEgdhO8DVGc/LQag4cP5K9k/3rSGQgi8XWx+vrwny7eMxPkBeHCVHMH8\nSN3lAtGVlB6cN+5KF/f0\n=RNXX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T00:30:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/cdd05ce6f74612f0046b77021cc860e921b967eb","node_id":"C_kwDOR4JmSdoAKGNkZDA1Y2U2Zjc0NjEyZjAwNDZiNzcwMjFjYzg2MGU5MjFiOTY3ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/82a36c9a4e896fdbd50f144ae96e9df59112b2ae","sha":"82a36c9a4e896fdbd50f144ae96e9df59112b2ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/82a36c9a4e896fdbd50f144ae96e9df59112b2ae"}],"sha":"cdd05ce6f74612f0046b77021cc860e921b967eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/cdd05ce6f74612f0046b77021cc860e921b967eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/82a36c9a4e896fdbd50f144ae96e9df59112b2ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T00:13:03Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T00:13:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema): explicit validate/apply for owned views and procedures (#82)\n\n* feat(schema): explicit validate/apply for owned views and procedures\n\nAdds dedicated validate-or-apply helpers for owned views and owned\nprocedures, kept deliberately separate from the table Ensure() / DiffSchema()\ncovenant. Tables remain strict — drift is always an error and nothing is\nauto-migrated. Views and procedures get explicit, caller-chosen behavior\nbecause their bodies are code: callers usually want them to track the\ndeclaration the same way application code tracks source.\n\nNew public API:\n- View lane (all dialects):\n    schema.ApplyView / schema.ApplyViews\n    schema.ValidateView / schema.ValidateViews\n    schema.LiveViewBody  (introspection escape hatch)\n    schema.ViewDrift, schema.ViewDriftError\n    schema.ErrViewMissing, schema.ErrViewBodyDrift\n- Procedure lane (MSSQL only):\n    schema.ApplyProcedure / schema.ApplyProcedures\n    schema.ValidateProcedure / schema.ValidateProcedures\n    schema.LiveProcedureDefinition\n    schema.ProcedureDrift, schema.ProcedureDriftError\n    schema.ErrProcedureMissing, schema.ErrProcedureDefinitionDrift\n\nApply* is one-way: declared definition overwrites the live object.\nIdempotent on Postgres / MSSQL (CREATE OR REPLACE / CREATE OR ALTER) and\neffectively idempotent on SQLite (DROP IF EXISTS + CREATE). Apply* does\nno pre-flight drift check; callers wanting validate-then-apply call\nValidate* first.\n\nValidate* confirms existence and, where the engine stores definitions\nverbatim (SQLite, MSSQL — both code-objects, plus MSSQL procedures from\nsys.sql_modules), also confirms body / definition text matches after\ncanonical normalization (whitespace collapse, trailing-semicolon strip,\nCREATE-preamble strip). On Postgres, pg_get_viewdef canonicalizes view\ndefinitions too aggressively (star expansion, full qualification,\ninserted casts) to support honest text comparison against a hand-written\ndeclared body — ValidateView on Postgres confirms existence only, and\nLiveViewBody is exposed so callers needing stricter assertions can run\ntheir own comparison.\n\nDrift surfaces as *ViewDriftError / *ProcedureDriftError with one entry\nper offending object. The errors unwrap to ErrViewMissing /\nErrViewBodyDrift (and the procedure equivalents) when every drift in\nthe batch has the same cause, so single-cause results can be branched\nwith errors.Is; mixed-cause results intentionally do not wrap either\nsentinel so callers can''t be misled when the real failure mode is\nheterogeneous.\n\nProcedure helpers are MSSQL-only. Non-MSSQL calls return\nErrProcedureDialectUnsupported rather than silently no-op''ing, so\nbootstrap callers running against the wrong engine fail loud instead of\ndropping owned-procedure coverage from the apply set.\n\nREADME adds a \"Code-Object Validate and Apply\" section documenting the\nintended ordering (tables strict, views second, procedures last),\nsketches the expected bootstrap-code shape, and explicitly calls out\nthe Postgres view-body comparison limitation.\n\nTests:\n- Unit coverage for normalization (stripCreateViewPreamble,\n  stripCreateProcedurePreamble, canonicalizeViewBody) and for\n  drift-error sentinel unwrapping (missing-only vs body-only vs mixed).\n- SQLite end-to-end validate/apply for views, including drift drift\n  detection after out-of-band stomp and re-apply restoration.\n- ValidateProcedure / ApplyProcedure unsupported-dialect guard tests for\n  Postgres and SQLite, including the batch (zero-procedure) path.\n- MSSQL integration test gated by CHUCK_MSSQL_URL covering missing →\n  apply → validate clean → out-of-band drift → re-apply → clean.\n\n* fix(schema): Postgres ValidateView fails loud instead of silent success\n\nPostgres `ValidateView` previously returned `nil` after the existence\nprobe, even though `pg_get_viewdef` canonicalization meant body\ncomparison was skipped. Callers asking for \"validate\" could read silent\nsuccess as a clean body match when in reality drift may have been\npresent.\n\nPostgres `ValidateView` now returns a `*ViewDriftError` whose single\nentry has `BodyComparisonSkipped=true` and unwraps to a new exported\nsentinel `ErrViewBodyComparisonUnsupported`. Existence is still\nconfirmed: missing-view paths continue to unwrap to `ErrViewMissing`.\n`ViewDriftError.Unwrap` gains the third single-cause branch so callers\nthat explicitly want existence-only semantics on Postgres can opt in via\n`errors.Is(err, schema.ErrViewBodyComparisonUnsupported)`; callers that\nneed stricter body assertions can still fetch `LiveViewBody` and run\ntheir own comparison.\n\nUnit tests cover the new Unwrap branches (all-skipped, mixed\nskipped+missing). New `TestValidateView_Postgres_FailsLoud` integration\ntest (gated by `CHUCK_POSTGRES_URL`) drives the full path: missing →\nErrViewMissing, applied → ErrViewBodyComparisonUnsupported with\nBodyComparisonSkipped flag set. README comparison table, prose, and\ndrift-error example updated to match.","tree":{"sha":"99475df035c7629ad2bc54588e9eec1c9d7c0f3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/99475df035c7629ad2bc54588e9eec1c9d7c0f3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/82a36c9a4e896fdbd50f144ae96e9df59112b2ae","verification":{"payload":"tree 99475df035c7629ad2bc54588e9eec1c9d7c0f3a\nparent e7826387b562cd67a661669f0cbcff42b33cfba8\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779149583 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779149583 -0500\n\nfeat(schema): explicit validate/apply for owned views and procedures (#82)\n\n* feat(schema): explicit validate/apply for owned views and procedures\n\nAdds dedicated validate-or-apply helpers for owned views and owned\nprocedures, kept deliberately separate from the table Ensure() / DiffSchema()\ncovenant. Tables remain strict — drift is always an error and nothing is\nauto-migrated. Views and procedures get explicit, caller-chosen behavior\nbecause their bodies are code: callers usually want them to track the\ndeclaration the same way application code tracks source.\n\nNew public API:\n- View lane (all dialects):\n    schema.ApplyView / schema.ApplyViews\n    schema.ValidateView / schema.ValidateViews\n    schema.LiveViewBody  (introspection escape hatch)\n    schema.ViewDrift, schema.ViewDriftError\n    schema.ErrViewMissing, schema.ErrViewBodyDrift\n- Procedure lane (MSSQL only):\n    schema.ApplyProcedure / schema.ApplyProcedures\n    schema.ValidateProcedure / schema.ValidateProcedures\n    schema.LiveProcedureDefinition\n    schema.ProcedureDrift, schema.ProcedureDriftError\n    schema.ErrProcedureMissing, schema.ErrProcedureDefinitionDrift\n\nApply* is one-way: declared definition overwrites the live object.\nIdempotent on Postgres / MSSQL (CREATE OR REPLACE / CREATE OR ALTER) and\neffectively idempotent on SQLite (DROP IF EXISTS + CREATE). Apply* does\nno pre-flight drift check; callers wanting validate-then-apply call\nValidate* first.\n\nValidate* confirms existence and, where the engine stores definitions\nverbatim (SQLite, MSSQL — both code-objects, plus MSSQL procedures from\nsys.sql_modules), also confirms body / definition text matches after\ncanonical normalization (whitespace collapse, trailing-semicolon strip,\nCREATE-preamble strip). On Postgres, pg_get_viewdef canonicalizes view\ndefinitions too aggressively (star expansion, full qualification,\ninserted casts) to support honest text comparison against a hand-written\ndeclared body — ValidateView on Postgres confirms existence only, and\nLiveViewBody is exposed so callers needing stricter assertions can run\ntheir own comparison.\n\nDrift surfaces as *ViewDriftError / *ProcedureDriftError with one entry\nper offending object. The errors unwrap to ErrViewMissing /\nErrViewBodyDrift (and the procedure equivalents) when every drift in\nthe batch has the same cause, so single-cause results can be branched\nwith errors.Is; mixed-cause results intentionally do not wrap either\nsentinel so callers can''t be misled when the real failure mode is\nheterogeneous.\n\nProcedure helpers are MSSQL-only. Non-MSSQL calls return\nErrProcedureDialectUnsupported rather than silently no-op''ing, so\nbootstrap callers running against the wrong engine fail loud instead of\ndropping owned-procedure coverage from the apply set.\n\nREADME adds a \"Code-Object Validate and Apply\" section documenting the\nintended ordering (tables strict, views second, procedures last),\nsketches the expected bootstrap-code shape, and explicitly calls out\nthe Postgres view-body comparison limitation.\n\nTests:\n- Unit coverage for normalization (stripCreateViewPreamble,\n  stripCreateProcedurePreamble, canonicalizeViewBody) and for\n  drift-error sentinel unwrapping (missing-only vs body-only vs mixed).\n- SQLite end-to-end validate/apply for views, including drift drift\n  detection after out-of-band stomp and re-apply restoration.\n- ValidateProcedure / ApplyProcedure unsupported-dialect guard tests for\n  Postgres and SQLite, including the batch (zero-procedure) path.\n- MSSQL integration test gated by CHUCK_MSSQL_URL covering missing →\n  apply → validate clean → out-of-band drift → re-apply → clean.\n\n* fix(schema): Postgres ValidateView fails loud instead of silent success\n\nPostgres `ValidateView` previously returned `nil` after the existence\nprobe, even though `pg_get_viewdef` canonicalization meant body\ncomparison was skipped. Callers asking for \"validate\" could read silent\nsuccess as a clean body match when in reality drift may have been\npresent.\n\nPostgres `ValidateView` now returns a `*ViewDriftError` whose single\nentry has `BodyComparisonSkipped=true` and unwraps to a new exported\nsentinel `ErrViewBodyComparisonUnsupported`. Existence is still\nconfirmed: missing-view paths continue to unwrap to `ErrViewMissing`.\n`ViewDriftError.Unwrap` gains the third single-cause branch so callers\nthat explicitly want existence-only semantics on Postgres can opt in via\n`errors.Is(err, schema.ErrViewBodyComparisonUnsupported)`; callers that\nneed stricter body assertions can still fetch `LiveViewBody` and run\ntheir own comparison.\n\nUnit tests cover the new Unwrap branches (all-skipped, mixed\nskipped+missing). New `TestValidateView_Postgres_FailsLoud` integration\ntest (gated by `CHUCK_POSTGRES_URL`) drives the full path: missing →\nErrViewMissing, applied → ErrViewBodyComparisonUnsupported with\nBodyComparisonSkipped flag set. README comparison table, prose, and\ndrift-error example updated to match.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqC6sPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO9UQAIEHlGgz0B5nqknxuebTkag4\nanp/PR0BOI5EWQuo/AM5FodS2sJIWyjUQW2VbyVoDgcYR7kdoZTFWl/UMNa52mX1\niFO3s6HAcIt+DlIeRzmLVP8ag/hwyhstEGiy4HV/VbCsmf2MzQr9aJE49dEuJBUp\nNysJarYDDMfANZo8+oAa81eHPiZXkxEfGnNE3ix6XZozjaM4udBnB48LaN1S5QVH\nlnM7fR5aJqeF7gq8F+7r7wuhwqKvJ6pFJAxV/NyirqtxYkE20tPviqnz/6Eoip7I\nHHo0X3sk1+E/U2fON/lPzadmKy7qRKgAHTivm1hBEyAJNgeK9WRfidR7Lm5p39cR\neiW7tqHMjLKpqyWbb2Azap45VVNK/x6xd1tbykE+VLnnB3Yxwvr7dwB0Ak36kBTy\nm7aeSYAnVm2ZVqSD51qfnUL7MRITUTGy3BZSMpG4QQk+3Rho35iSuE56V6xK1qv4\nYbryTmS6DBsQ+yLCX2cI9k7Vy7wr/UKlHHHBXAMNCWGE7k4ICUwjrBSz3p3cAtxH\nrFSMHdhYpqKfNgELvjoYWF3h7EJofdprZi8asFmsQzVCRDIZa2V7HOx5m3bltGSR\n0abqetPLh/wXEP8LDYk1vnEuPpd1viCL0/IodqfVunj/TTkaOwOcMg1857u9SKnm\nK9B+mA+Wd2xkXYg5NhCk\n=f3Uc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T00:13:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/82a36c9a4e896fdbd50f144ae96e9df59112b2ae","node_id":"C_kwDOR4JmSdoAKDgyYTM2YzlhNGU4OTZmZGJkNTBmMTQ0YWU5NmU5ZGY1OTExMmIyYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/e7826387b562cd67a661669f0cbcff42b33cfba8","sha":"e7826387b562cd67a661669f0cbcff42b33cfba8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/e7826387b562cd67a661669f0cbcff42b33cfba8"}],"sha":"82a36c9a4e896fdbd50f144ae96e9df59112b2ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/82a36c9a4e896fdbd50f144ae96e9df59112b2ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/e7826387b562cd67a661669f0cbcff42b33cfba8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-18T23:48:07Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-18T23:48:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema): first-class ProcedureDef for owned MSSQL stored procedures (#80) (#81)\n\n* feat(schema): first-class ProcedureDef for owned MSSQL stored procedures (#80)\n\nAdds ProcedureDef alongside ViewDef so MSSQL refresh / migration\nentrypoints stop being raw checked-in .sql outside chuck ownership.\n\n- NewProcedure / NewQualifiedProcedure / WithSchema / Schema / Body /\n  Object / QualifiedNameFor mirror the ViewDef shape so callers can mix\n  declaration styles in the same owned-schema bundle.\n- CreateOrAlterSQL emits CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE [schema].[name] AS\n  <body> as a single MSSQL 2016+ batch.\n- DropSQL wraps DROP PROCEDURE in a sys.procedures existence probe,\n  matching the table-drop pattern so callers can run it unconditionally\n  during teardown.\n- Postgres / SQLite are explicitly unsupported in this first pass:\n  lifecycle methods return ErrProcedureDialectUnsupported so bootstrap\n  callers fail loud instead of silently dropping owned procedures from\n  the apply set on the wrong engine.\n- Ordering between procedures and tables/views stays caller-owned. SQL\n  Agent jobs and msdb admin objects are out of scope for this primitive.\n- README documents owned-procedure usage, MSSQL-first scope, and the\n  errors.Is path for the unsupported-dialect branch.\n- Focused unit coverage for identity, qualified-name rendering, both\n  lifecycle SQL methods, and the explicit non-MSSQL error path; live\n  MSSQL integration test gated by CHUCK_MSSQL_URL exercises idempotent\n  create-or-alter and idempotent drop end-to-end.\n\n* fix(schema): allow parameters and pre-AS options in ProcedureDef (#80)\n\nResolves PR #81 review blocker: T-SQL grammar places parameter\ndeclarations and procedure options between the procedure name and the\nAS keyword, but the first cut of ProcedureDef injected `AS` itself and\nappended the caller''s text after it. That shape cannot represent any\nparameterized procedure or a `WITH RECOMPILE` / `WITH ENCRYPTION`\nheader at all, and the README example promised syntax MSSQL would\nreject.\n\nRenames the second constructor payload from `body` to `definition` and\nmoves the `AS` keyword into the caller''s hands. The package now\ncontributes only `CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE <qualified-name>` and the\ncaller supplies everything from optional parameters through `AS`\nthrough the body — matching T-SQL ordering exactly. Zero-parameter\nprocedures keep working: their definition just begins with `AS`.\n\n- procedure.go: `Body()` -> `Definition()`; CREATE OR ALTER renders as\n  `CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE <name> <definition>` (no implicit AS).\n- procedure_test.go: parameterized + `WITH` shape coverage, plus an\n  ordering assertion that params precede AS precedes BEGIN.\n- integration_test.go: TestProcedureLifecycleMSSQL now exercises a\n  procedure with an `@Probe INT = 1` parameter so the pre-AS slot is\n  proven end-to-end when `CHUCK_MSSQL_URL` is set.\n- README: rewrite Owned Procedures example to include parameters and a\n  `WITH RECOMPILE` option, plus a zero-parameter shorthand.\n\n* docs(schema): fix README proc example and drop PR-history comments (#80)\n\n- README owned-procedure example: nullable parameter guard was\n  `([AsOf] IS NULL OR [RecordedAt] <= @AsOf)` which mixes the parameter\n  with a same-named column identifier and would not compile as written.\n  Switch to `(@AsOf IS NULL OR [RecordedAt] <= @AsOf)` so the\n  copy-pasteable shipped example matches T-SQL.\n- Drop \"PR #81\" / \"blocking review finding\" wording from\n  schema/procedure_test.go and schema/integration_test.go comments. The\n  intent (parameters belong between the name and AS) survives without\n  the PR-history reference, which would only rot post-merge.\n\nNo behavior or API change.","tree":{"sha":"0c4a6812897333bb043c1b4f46976a8cec836ee4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/0c4a6812897333bb043c1b4f46976a8cec836ee4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/e7826387b562cd67a661669f0cbcff42b33cfba8","verification":{"payload":"tree 0c4a6812897333bb043c1b4f46976a8cec836ee4\nparent ab41566879e1159aa37a2e46e31ef871e9851ced\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1779148087 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779148087 -0500\n\nfeat(schema): first-class ProcedureDef for owned MSSQL stored procedures (#80) (#81)\n\n* feat(schema): first-class ProcedureDef for owned MSSQL stored procedures (#80)\n\nAdds ProcedureDef alongside ViewDef so MSSQL refresh / migration\nentrypoints stop being raw checked-in .sql outside chuck ownership.\n\n- NewProcedure / NewQualifiedProcedure / WithSchema / Schema / Body /\n  Object / QualifiedNameFor mirror the ViewDef shape so callers can mix\n  declaration styles in the same owned-schema bundle.\n- CreateOrAlterSQL emits CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE [schema].[name] AS\n  <body> as a single MSSQL 2016+ batch.\n- DropSQL wraps DROP PROCEDURE in a sys.procedures existence probe,\n  matching the table-drop pattern so callers can run it unconditionally\n  during teardown.\n- Postgres / SQLite are explicitly unsupported in this first pass:\n  lifecycle methods return ErrProcedureDialectUnsupported so bootstrap\n  callers fail loud instead of silently dropping owned procedures from\n  the apply set on the wrong engine.\n- Ordering between procedures and tables/views stays caller-owned. SQL\n  Agent jobs and msdb admin objects are out of scope for this primitive.\n- README documents owned-procedure usage, MSSQL-first scope, and the\n  errors.Is path for the unsupported-dialect branch.\n- Focused unit coverage for identity, qualified-name rendering, both\n  lifecycle SQL methods, and the explicit non-MSSQL error path; live\n  MSSQL integration test gated by CHUCK_MSSQL_URL exercises idempotent\n  create-or-alter and idempotent drop end-to-end.\n\n* fix(schema): allow parameters and pre-AS options in ProcedureDef (#80)\n\nResolves PR #81 review blocker: T-SQL grammar places parameter\ndeclarations and procedure options between the procedure name and the\nAS keyword, but the first cut of ProcedureDef injected `AS` itself and\nappended the caller''s text after it. That shape cannot represent any\nparameterized procedure or a `WITH RECOMPILE` / `WITH ENCRYPTION`\nheader at all, and the README example promised syntax MSSQL would\nreject.\n\nRenames the second constructor payload from `body` to `definition` and\nmoves the `AS` keyword into the caller''s hands. The package now\ncontributes only `CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE <qualified-name>` and the\ncaller supplies everything from optional parameters through `AS`\nthrough the body — matching T-SQL ordering exactly. Zero-parameter\nprocedures keep working: their definition just begins with `AS`.\n\n- procedure.go: `Body()` -> `Definition()`; CREATE OR ALTER renders as\n  `CREATE OR ALTER PROCEDURE <name> <definition>` (no implicit AS).\n- procedure_test.go: parameterized + `WITH` shape coverage, plus an\n  ordering assertion that params precede AS precedes BEGIN.\n- integration_test.go: TestProcedureLifecycleMSSQL now exercises a\n  procedure with an `@Probe INT = 1` parameter so the pre-AS slot is\n  proven end-to-end when `CHUCK_MSSQL_URL` is set.\n- README: rewrite Owned Procedures example to include parameters and a\n  `WITH RECOMPILE` option, plus a zero-parameter shorthand.\n\n* docs(schema): fix README proc example and drop PR-history comments (#80)\n\n- README owned-procedure example: nullable parameter guard was\n  `([AsOf] IS NULL OR [RecordedAt] <= @AsOf)` which mixes the parameter\n  with a same-named column identifier and would not compile as written.\n  Switch to `(@AsOf IS NULL OR [RecordedAt] <= @AsOf)` so the\n  copy-pasteable shipped example matches T-SQL.\n- Drop \"PR #81\" / \"blocking review finding\" wording from\n  schema/procedure_test.go and schema/integration_test.go comments. The\n  intent (parameters belong between the name and AS) survives without\n  the PR-history reference, which would only rot post-merge.\n\nNo behavior or API change.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqC6U3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3GgQAGUWZdiSS3Ob0wYBeS+/q0Hr\ni2Y0y3Pe5KZfEBkFFVxOzebXVCHqseVcKk3ReUzZXaHRMAtVXUDLDhwEig5nkr4U\n8c1zVPbre+qNXczCvG/FIxFv6f3Y7H4uvAzyLjYmjqskuB9bSdgKBplmOdr4bxrN\nFGL/kAo55PPpVXZH20+bMJqfwvbwiPPZQcqzA86G0mSSag3l0tlsDeDKMpWMFGmU\ntWCvtDKU2hRgNwGTG8mvWkzcej7ArfzTTUprBqa1feUz4km2J7w0EQNLl5nO9mhN\nrzdcXXciHDS4oh1kZwbqwbgwEIMCYKDhYIIQg1dWvg/wjKLOBsDH4E2pixjOTaIj\n0/024h0Csr4Yb8aFGBy3qF76mgzExenCS/WBcuSZyrR0wrwY5VasRqNyPvJtb4Zh\n/GkkrpqrpnruP38wyJuyS/pGsQAaa+xQpI1Zsd10PKb1T13uacQdR0/r+hoWUXGk\nD7xIQTS4EdK3boiDvh+y3zb/6QIemK2OfPdn8mIppXsTXsdiz3saUOvY5L+p5KvK\nYoBw0pHNNCaCA4EIevvBlVREZMYIQYH0BEePUubLe1qi1qV8Ky8AoQanK1uvPSkE\nollpZ2r6Pod3xBnlS6PpvMllW1g8iF2heLBLQs2AGixzeykEtHMdg4CWekvjDlVY\nkCZ02Y7M52+D9galQ0Wq\n=kC1q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-18T23:48:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/e7826387b562cd67a661669f0cbcff42b33cfba8","node_id":"C_kwDOR4JmSdoAKGU3ODI2Mzg3YjU2MmNkNjdhNjYxNjY5ZjBjYmNmZjQyYjMzY2ZiYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/ab41566879e1159aa37a2e46e31ef871e9851ced","sha":"ab41566879e1159aa37a2e46e31ef871e9851ced","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/ab41566879e1159aa37a2e46e31ef871e9851ced"}],"sha":"e7826387b562cd67a661669f0cbcff42b33cfba8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/e7826387b562cd67a661669f0cbcff42b33cfba8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/ab41566879e1159aa37a2e46e31ef871e9851ced/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-15T14:10:37Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-15T14:10:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema): first-class ViewDef for owned-view lifecycle (#76) (#79)\n\nTables, indexes, foreign keys, and seed data are already declarative in\nchuck/schema, but views were a permanent raw-SQL exception: apps had to\nkeep adjacent CREATE VIEW string constants and wire separate drop/create\ninto bootstrap, splitting ownership across files. Adding a new owned\nview silently risked drift against that parallel list.\n\nAdd ViewDef as a first-class owned object that mirrors TableDef''s\nidentity model and emits dialect-aware lifecycle SQL through the shared\nqualified-rendering path:\n\n- ViewDef carries an optional schema namespace and verbatim SELECT body\n- NewView, NewQualifiedView, WithSchema, Schema, Body, Object, and\n  QualifiedNameFor mirror the TableDef ergonomics\n- CreateSQL emits a plain CREATE VIEW for the simple bootstrap case\n- CreateOrReplaceSQL returns dialect-idiomatic idempotent replace:\n  Postgres CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW (single statement), MSSQL\n  CREATE OR ALTER VIEW (single statement, MSSQL 2016+), SQLite\n  DROP VIEW IF EXISTS + CREATE VIEW (run in order)\n- DropSQL emits DROP VIEW IF EXISTS; on MSSQL it wraps the drop in a\n  sys.views existence probe matching the table-drop pattern\n- view bodies are verbatim so callers keep explicit control over inner\n  identifier quoting, consistent with chuck''s \"explicit SQL, composable\n  helpers\" stance\n- ordering between views and the tables they read stays caller-owned;\n  views typically form a short linear chain on top of owned tables, so\n  forcing a generalized scheduler abstraction would add weight without\n  buying clarity. README documents the recommended pattern.\n\nCoverage:\n\n- schema/view_test.go pins identity, qualified-name rendering, and the\n  three lifecycle SQL forms across MSSQL, Postgres, and SQLite, plus\n  MSSQL drops for both qualified and unqualified probes\n- integration_test.go adds TestViewLifecycleSQLite which executes plain\n  create, create-or-replace (DROP+CREATE on SQLite), and idempotent\n  drop end-to-end against in-memory SQLite to catch surface-level\n  rendering breakage that pure string tests would miss\n- README adds an Owned Views section under the schema ownership group","tree":{"sha":"22f78ce23959c7ac939e90fd0c3ffff7bd4e6f1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/22f78ce23959c7ac939e90fd0c3ffff7bd4e6f1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/ab41566879e1159aa37a2e46e31ef871e9851ced","verification":{"payload":"tree 22f78ce23959c7ac939e90fd0c3ffff7bd4e6f1d\nparent 3e671e09c600d9e6214d33940fa9c859dfc58c41\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1778854237 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778854237 -0500\n\nfeat(schema): first-class ViewDef for owned-view lifecycle (#76) (#79)\n\nTables, indexes, foreign keys, and seed data are already declarative in\nchuck/schema, but views were a permanent raw-SQL exception: apps had to\nkeep adjacent CREATE VIEW string constants and wire separate drop/create\ninto bootstrap, splitting ownership across files. Adding a new owned\nview silently risked drift against that parallel list.\n\nAdd ViewDef as a first-class owned object that mirrors TableDef''s\nidentity model and emits dialect-aware lifecycle SQL through the shared\nqualified-rendering path:\n\n- ViewDef carries an optional schema namespace and verbatim SELECT body\n- NewView, NewQualifiedView, WithSchema, Schema, Body, Object, and\n  QualifiedNameFor mirror the TableDef ergonomics\n- CreateSQL emits a plain CREATE VIEW for the simple bootstrap case\n- CreateOrReplaceSQL returns dialect-idiomatic idempotent replace:\n  Postgres CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW (single statement), MSSQL\n  CREATE OR ALTER VIEW (single statement, MSSQL 2016+), SQLite\n  DROP VIEW IF EXISTS + CREATE VIEW (run in order)\n- DropSQL emits DROP VIEW IF EXISTS; on MSSQL it wraps the drop in a\n  sys.views existence probe matching the table-drop pattern\n- view bodies are verbatim so callers keep explicit control over inner\n  identifier quoting, consistent with chuck''s \"explicit SQL, composable\n  helpers\" stance\n- ordering between views and the tables they read stays caller-owned;\n  views typically form a short linear chain on top of owned tables, so\n  forcing a generalized scheduler abstraction would add weight without\n  buying clarity. README documents the recommended pattern.\n\nCoverage:\n\n- schema/view_test.go pins identity, qualified-name rendering, and the\n  three lifecycle SQL forms across MSSQL, Postgres, and SQLite, plus\n  MSSQL drops for both qualified and unqualified probes\n- integration_test.go adds TestViewLifecycleSQLite which executes plain\n  create, create-or-replace (DROP+CREATE on SQLite), and idempotent\n  drop end-to-end against in-memory SQLite to catch surface-level\n  rendering breakage that pure string tests would miss\n- README adds an Owned Views section under the schema ownership group","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqByldCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8xUQAHgz+yaSTtjEOt0eFNXhiXF+\nwlt954O8KijOoT7bL1OD3jJ4eCkS4sZn2ONWCGC+/uc7lGqCuNNnUb2dv9088e6L\nh+6a1niXcLam51jc1FKa2Fb97EnmJ7GcC8jKVkEkvUccTu4I+cCY07D1qPZGd9ew\nQt1pD/Phc2JK4F7KNKGXuPGJsv69sKB4xuQmIzvUTm5kVWD4Cp0pPyBEUh4w3WI3\ny2cBGK7OKWi3vMycDN+kwwmG1W2eJTLiYjTSENUBVdhBmNbBQ+yFEQllMaFiQeWJ\n4iy1kGftwCJx7TAkPtVRtD25l3aeJM2k9jZXdYOtrUF9gEiblutAK6YtrebtVAga\n63wZPQB81hxDJTFhtf6sJHUXTQKxOP0Nyzbq5804GKI4V8+4r5stxKZfwMFJ8Erm\n658F3+4C3m24g2zXujRdDpHErnepKpva0ZLHk/nQ6ERYaQWM74WVMaElzRHNcW32\nXoNVAM+8507k1fJWvOzfphu201c/0ldtdlplUtDvoLkJscKNkpHTQIHq4o087qRl\nvRUq3PXtC28xNCnLe/ur4snxmzipIoZVfA+EtAI5pjLtVXoL618fWBsW+cqRQMcA\nYZadPaj2wzzZ5ZX4SSa2cxwQpUGr/xe8l6Hk3JNcsIGL7gUiA/U7603hBVspdL4w\nF3+lO+mKeuLJecinP1lu\n=3euk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-15T14:10:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/ab41566879e1159aa37a2e46e31ef871e9851ced","node_id":"C_kwDOR4JmSdoAKGFiNDE1NjY4NzllMTE1OWFhMzdhMmU0NmUzMWVmODcxZTk4NTFjZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/3e671e09c600d9e6214d33940fa9c859dfc58c41","sha":"3e671e09c600d9e6214d33940fa9c859dfc58c41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/3e671e09c600d9e6214d33940fa9c859dfc58c41"}],"sha":"ab41566879e1159aa37a2e46e31ef871e9851ced","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/ab41566879e1159aa37a2e46e31ef871e9851ced"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/3e671e09c600d9e6214d33940fa9c859dfc58c41/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-15T14:07:04Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-15T14:07:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema): MSSQL inbound foreign-key teardown helper (#77) (#78)\n\nInline FKs declared via chuck/schema emit auto-generated constraint names\non MSSQL (e.g. FK__Goals__AgentID__1234ABCD). DropOrder solves table\nordering, but DROP TABLE still fails while an inbound FK pins the table.\nApps that use chuck/schema as canonical ownership had to maintain a\nhandwritten FK-drop helper next to the declarative schema — a drift\npoint each new owned table can silently break.\n\nAdd a first-class destructive-bootstrap helper that derives the owned set\nfrom the declared *TableDef inputs and detaches matching FKs by name:\n\n- ForeignKeyRef captures a single inbound FK with both endpoints\n- InboundForeignKeys queries sys.foreign_keys and returns the FKs whose\n  parent or referenced table belongs to the owned set; non-MSSQL engines\n  return (nil, nil) so dialect-agnostic bootstrap can call unconditionally\n- DropForeignKeySQL renders ALTER TABLE ... DROP CONSTRAINT via the shared\n  dialect quoting path\n- DropInboundForeignKeys executes the drops in discovery order and\n  reports what it removed\n- owned-set keys default unqualified declarations to the engine default\n  schema (dbo) so a mix of NewTable and NewQualifiedTable lines up with\n  sys.objects output\n- README documents the recipe alongside DropOrder\n\nCoverage:\n\n- unit tests pin DropForeignKeySQL output for both dbo-default and\n  schema-qualified parents, validate ownedTableKeySet defaulting, and\n  cover both ownedFK match sides plus the fully-external skip case\n- non-MSSQL and empty-set short-circuits are verified without a DB\n- MSSQL integration test (CHUCK_MSSQL_URL) creates a parent/child pair\n  with an inline FK, asserts a naive DROP TABLE on the parent fails\n  while the FK is in place, then exercises DropInboundForeignKeys +\n  DropOrder to prove the destructive rebuild path succeeds end-to-end","tree":{"sha":"67be6e7f547af6fffd4333bae62b8459786b7b91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/67be6e7f547af6fffd4333bae62b8459786b7b91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/3e671e09c600d9e6214d33940fa9c859dfc58c41","verification":{"payload":"tree 67be6e7f547af6fffd4333bae62b8459786b7b91\nparent 20d832ae40a7ffe7caa67584d18874b52affb120\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1778854024 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778854024 -0500\n\nfeat(schema): MSSQL inbound foreign-key teardown helper (#77) (#78)\n\nInline FKs declared via chuck/schema emit auto-generated constraint names\non MSSQL (e.g. FK__Goals__AgentID__1234ABCD). DropOrder solves table\nordering, but DROP TABLE still fails while an inbound FK pins the table.\nApps that use chuck/schema as canonical ownership had to maintain a\nhandwritten FK-drop helper next to the declarative schema — a drift\npoint each new owned table can silently break.\n\nAdd a first-class destructive-bootstrap helper that derives the owned set\nfrom the declared *TableDef inputs and detaches matching FKs by name:\n\n- ForeignKeyRef captures a single inbound FK with both endpoints\n- InboundForeignKeys queries sys.foreign_keys and returns the FKs whose\n  parent or referenced table belongs to the owned set; non-MSSQL engines\n  return (nil, nil) so dialect-agnostic bootstrap can call unconditionally\n- DropForeignKeySQL renders ALTER TABLE ... DROP CONSTRAINT via the shared\n  dialect quoting path\n- DropInboundForeignKeys executes the drops in discovery order and\n  reports what it removed\n- owned-set keys default unqualified declarations to the engine default\n  schema (dbo) so a mix of NewTable and NewQualifiedTable lines up with\n  sys.objects output\n- README documents the recipe alongside DropOrder\n\nCoverage:\n\n- unit tests pin DropForeignKeySQL output for both dbo-default and\n  schema-qualified parents, validate ownedTableKeySet defaulting, and\n  cover both ownedFK match sides plus the fully-external skip case\n- non-MSSQL and empty-set short-circuits are verified without a DB\n- MSSQL integration test (CHUCK_MSSQL_URL) creates a parent/child pair\n  with an inline FK, asserts a naive DROP TABLE on the parent fails\n  while the FK is in place, then exercises DropInboundForeignKeys +\n  DropOrder to prove the destructive rebuild path succeeds end-to-end","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqByiICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnTYQAGhi9FDlY+9osupUTBWoylUY\nQoOjIAeS2V21k9kqEuFQppJi5Xx4fI9TlkwbOdMAD0UTm2XMagbw7/UFVqXFM7YH\n82hVfyr6eGDd4s/vmqvYrsyiU62snCjknJHqJaLgYSGCmH4Rksnv6zKC4CpOFbC8\nulKOgbKW2d0zewSQvo8oz2xsK+h16SFDcDUyV1k7Y7h+Jpnm6+EYOjCXfZc6DYvl\nZEzkPPJjNMdKcgzqJ6KUQK25Gc2gDIq5OUMe/31fBIv/R0VnNMckJcPRUhrtdvbn\nVkefLxbjrqYuMuvMvbWDb03oCLeQ/Jf8BhguDToTi8fCQpdnuCxI5a2pNwcIBkv5\n0BMLknEq6hA8HnvIlPU3Anv+MUQCR82SxxMik7R5nWMUq2u0DXjwGI5CLKF5C0f/\nWl5SLZOSnQihAR5Z8/k3GV76omVSrhwOOFO6oddInHAuiHqlpf6jf6hXHmFPcGnE\nDihDZNGKkeJc+js1hum6juC+SjddGbcAzSez7dO70zgX/R/rSUjIoi2qbDB+ycU2\nVIYlasMZiX9xfJ2FwOPNob42YQH3tyJADDOjqEJ3TmRfiPrhxUXussZLqiUXUxJP\nwZMQuN2386aQ2dP4BOWWCV3HIWfVXsWaPlvqtN2yu+6iJ79Q0U0m/L8HkBEM75UH\n7/1AYWSRbBZ9X6jfRpP1\n=21Re\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-15T14:07:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/3e671e09c600d9e6214d33940fa9c859dfc58c41","node_id":"C_kwDOR4JmSdoAKDNlNjcxZTA5YzYwMGQ5ZTYyMTRkMzM5NDBmYTljODU5ZGZjNThjNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose/chuck/commit/20d832ae40a7ffe7caa67584d18874b52affb120","sha":"20d832ae40a7ffe7caa67584d18874b52affb120","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/20d832ae40a7ffe7caa67584d18874b52affb120"}],"sha":"3e671e09c600d9e6214d33940fa9c859dfc58c41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/3e671e09c600d9e6214d33940fa9c859dfc58c41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21010072?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catgoose","id":21010072,"login":"catgoose","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDEwMDcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catgoose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/commits/20d832ae40a7ffe7caa67584d18874b52affb120/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T18:02:55Z","email":"21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Meow Honk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T18:02:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dbrepo): first-class schema-qualified table references (#73) (#75)\n\n* feat(dbrepo): first-class schema-qualified table references (#73)\n\nAdds qualified-table rendering to the dbrepo query builders. Builders now\naccept schema-qualified strings (\"sg.SalesAgents\") and render each part\nthrough the dialect''s quoting, including alias forms. SQLite drops the\nschema component because it has no schema namespace.\n\n- chuck.QualifyTable and chuck.ParseObjectName shared helpers; schema\n  package routes its private qualifyTable through chuck.QualifyTable\n- SelectBuilder FROM/JOIN/CountQuery render schema.table per-part and\n  support \"sg.SalesAgents\", \"sg.SalesAgents sa\", \"sg.SalesAgents AS sa\"\n- quoteDotQualifiedColumns supports 3-part schema.table.column refs;\n  bare names and expressions still pass through unquoted\n- UpdateBuilder, DeleteBuilder route through the shared quoteTable helper\n- InsertIntoQ, BulkInsertInto, UpsertInto, UpsertIntoQ render qualified\n  targets; Upsert paths inline the dialect template only when qualified\n  to avoid double-quoting via Dialect.Upsert\n- README documents qualified usage and SQLite fallback semantics\n\n* fix(dbrepo): render aliased FROM targets through join-target parser\n\nSelectBuilder.Build and CountQuery routed FROM through quoteTable, which\npasses through any input containing whitespace. As a result aliased FROM\ntargets like \"sg.SalesAgents sa\" or \"Users AS u\" rendered the base table\nunquoted even when a dialect was set.\n\nRoute FROM through quoteJoinTarget instead so the same parser that already\nhandles JOIN aliases is reused. Passthrough for derived tables and raw\nsubqueries is preserved by the existing ambiguous-shape branch.","tree":{"sha":"8b0968e23834403c8cc8917d399a1fd90c9863be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/trees/8b0968e23834403c8cc8917d399a1fd90c9863be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catgoose/chuck/git/commits/20d832ae40a7ffe7caa67584d18874b52affb120","verification":{"payload":"tree 8b0968e23834403c8cc8917d399a1fd90c9863be\nparent 68cb1e7e9c799fb6873896a2004dfa54c474aa9d\nauthor Meow Honk <21010072+catgoose@users.noreply.github.com> 1778522575 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778522575 -0500\n\nfeat(dbrepo): first-class schema-qualified table references (#73) (#75)\n\n* feat(dbrepo): first-class schema-qualified table references (#73)\n\nAdds qualified-table rendering to the dbrepo query builders. Builders now\naccept schema-qualified strings (\"sg.SalesAgents\") and render each part\nthrough the dialect''s quoting, including alias forms. SQLite drops the\nschema component because it has no schema namespace.\n\n- chuck.QualifyTable and chuck.ParseObjectName shared helpers; schema\n  package routes its private qualifyTable through chuck.QualifyTable\n- SelectBuilder FROM/JOIN/CountQuery render schema.table per-part and\n  support \"sg.SalesAgents\", \"sg.SalesAgents sa\", \"sg.SalesAgents AS sa\"\n- quoteDotQualifiedColumns supports 3-part schema.table.column refs;\n  bare names and expressions still pass through unquoted\n- UpdateBuilder, DeleteBuilder route through the shared quoteTable helper\n- InsertIntoQ, BulkInsertInto, UpsertInto, UpsertIntoQ render qualified\n  targets; Upsert paths inline the dialect template only when qualified\n  to avoid double-quoting via Dialect.Upsert\n- README documents qualified usage and SQLite fallback semantics\n\n* fix(dbrepo): render aliased FROM targets through join-target parser\n\nSelectBuilder.Build and CountQuery routed FROM through quoteTable, which\npasses through any input containing whitespace. As a result aliased FROM\ntargets like \"sg.SalesAgents sa\" or \"Users AS u\" rendered the base table\nunquoted even when a dialect was set.\n\nRoute FROM through quoteJoinTarget instead so the same parser that already\nhandles JOIN aliases is reused. Passthrough for derived tables and raw\nsubqueries is preserved by the existing ambiguous-shape branch.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAhnPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAegMQAFDpY/kuq5kBMfacKtmHhX6z\nkVsFsK57wxRTU2VNj8GYpd87d0gAFqh984qWNL2N3P8rmcbhiYxDsjZRLQF0M4cz\n4K/QhMl6TamXlLvs2tLFwM+5MBMQ/dZYbZHV+TPQTycpbV1spbHJ3SJpF8Jd6SkO\nFtLbKl+SuUAndZ5DGPzvQfrd3wZmU8pDIz8rqmejUs76J+GBxh650cES5wQqARus\nw5cVFL/Zyb0Kt+Ay6uSbVQSERPDcfEaa4itgQPiT1YlHBpyUZojHLscvZVE2KOOs\nmj5WGCLEXmSgwiJHpBeLPYZ27CbUZoEm1vRA8Ez3yR7z252Di+48wgAqgIDxzFgU\noNbBjBtlLD3k0ENSMYmiO3fL7pKAh7wVQHEZsKan/Jvh+BQnovbhg9bmt2N048O7\nV