red{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbauer83/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbauer83","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mbauer83/sdlc-multi-agent-system/commits/30feec0a001167d0e80b0f70e999b92efe73963c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-04T12:19:54Z","email":"mbauer.mphil@googlemail.com","name":"Michael Bauer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-04T12:19:54Z","email":"mbauer.mphil@googlemail.com","name":"Michael Bauer"},"message":"Stage 4.9f: enforce ArchiMate-layer-aligned grouping colors\n\nProblem: grouping rectangles used arbitrary colors unrelated to the\nArchiMate layer of their contained elements (#E8F5E9 green for business-\nlayer roles, #F3E5F5 purple for business collaborations, etc.).\n\nFix — layer-specific grouping stereotypes:\n- Added 7 stereotypes to _archimate-stereotypes.puml:\n  <<MotivationGrouping>>, <<StrategyGrouping>>, <<BusinessGrouping>>,\n  <<ApplicationGrouping>>, <<TechnologyGrouping>>, <<PhysicalGrouping>>,\n  <<ImplementationGrouping>>\n- Each uses a lighter tint of the correct layer color (container recedes\n  behind contained elements which carry the full layer color)\n- Generic <<Grouping>> removed — it carried no layer information\n- phase-b: CAPS → <<StrategyGrouping>>; all other groups → <<BusinessGrouping>>\n- phase-c: all 5 groups → <<ApplicationGrouping>>\n- All inline #color overrides removed from grouping rectangles\n\nProhibition codified:\n- diagram-conventions.md §11.3: table of required stereotypes per layer;\n  inline #color overrides on grouping rectangles explicitly forbidden;\n  future ModelVerifier rule E360 flagged\n- entity-conventions.md §3.3: grouping stereotype table added\n- src/common/archimate_types.py: ARCHIMATE_GROUPING_STEREOTYPES registry\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9c6b11fa5d41ce23312f4f7b1ee0b32918fd748","url":"https://api.git