3c067674c27a06a1695787a","sha":"c117b814f5b1ff3ea3c067674c27a06a1695787a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/c117b814f5b1ff3ea3c067674c27a06a1695787a"}],"sha":"4854bec8e46f0e6829d8fab5f437c2e4f6ab8f9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/4854bec8e46f0e6829d8fab5f437c2e4f6ab8f9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/c117b814f5b1ff3ea3c067674c27a06a1695787a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T23:56:51Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T23:56:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add a Close button, fix the CTA hover, drop the dead token maps (#61)\n\nThe trials CTA turned green on hover under any brand. Its hover was\nmapped to --success-700, which is the semantic success colour and which\nno brand overrides, so the base followed the brand and the hover did not.\nIt has its own --brand-green-hover token now, defaulting to the same\ngreen so the default brand is unchanged.\n\n  generic   base hsl(146 70% 45%)  hover hsl(152 91% 29%)   unchanged\n  lymphoma  base hsl(258 81% 70%)  hover hsl(260 90% 64%)   was green\n  partner   base hsl(134 25% 45%)  hover hsl(134 25% 30%)\n\nSettings gets a Close button, bottom right. Every change applies as it is\npicked, so it dismisses rather than confirms — Close, not Save, and no\nCancel beside it.\n\nAnd a correction to the previous commit: moving brand values into\nindex.css removed the runtime duplication but left the light/dark maps\nbehind in branding.ts, where nothing read them. That is exactly the drift\nthe move was supposed to prevent, so they are gone; the file now carries\nonly what the picker needs. The swatches are the last colours named in\nTypeScript, and say so.","tree":{"sha":"6d7e18dc22a37642dd44e89fc3c44c2d1113f1b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/6d7e18dc22a37642dd44e89fc3c44c2d1113f1b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/c117b814f5b1ff3ea3c067674c27a06a1695787a","verification":{"payload":"tree 6d7e18dc22a37642dd44e89fc3c44c2d1113f1b3\nparent deed9f18ac8ab08a512d099ecaaacef863d4cb3e\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1786406211 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786406211 -0700\n\nAdd a Close button, fix the CTA hover, drop the dead token maps (#61)\n\nThe trials CTA turned green on hover under any brand. Its hover was\nmapped to --success-700, which is the semantic success colour and which\nno brand overrides, so the base followed the brand and the hover did not.\nIt has its own --brand-green-hover token now, defaulting to the same\ngreen so the default brand is unchanged.\n\n  generic   base hsl(146 70% 45%)  hover hsl(152 91% 29%)   unchanged\n  lymphoma  base hsl(258 81% 70%)  hover hsl(260 90% 64%)   was green\n  partner   base hsl(134 25% 45%)  hover hsl(134 25% 30%)\n\nSettings gets a Close button, bottom right. Every change applies as it is\npicked, so it dismisses rather than confirms — Close, not Save, and no\nCancel beside it.\n\nAnd a correction to the previous commit: moving brand values into\nindex.css removed the runtime duplication but left the light/dark maps\nbehind in branding.ts, where nothing read them. That is exactly the drift\nthe move was supposed to prevent, so they are gone; the file now carries\nonly what the picker needs. The swatches are the last colours named in\nTypeScript, and say so.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqemVDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARkAQAD5IHRVqzO+yanC11GK0XY+0\n420mFFAF8Np3zrA1iTGqJmxmeRYjc3TfXA/Dd0cf1Z7VjBxA5y1KWBhzyZlhOrBg\nMZ5Dt4blPU0HKHB33megiyh8alyzxorEq/DexU9SiOmwfLVYpi5cCcNTnm5yyhmg\ntPh3BZtLT909Qvsyz0tndmBTQHaeoPu3VFM5ta1NRmZP8MZWX2zL0wVdpDV2Gkwh\nJf2/w9SwxepOdxfrsZQwydpv7K9HdwpfWHWiTk3LfqqfN+E5OXJR/4k4OusOgeHy\ndYioO8MM/n1t8W6MFidbNia+clN0OPoid7Xy3X0Ac7OvQ5mQqOv3dhfYCHK3t/8m\nQx9RtESxnQ4aQRpjpKDodZBgC9Zoo5JU/GrhTGGK9tQovkJApUB53+lobe/a99Nu\nwZsCbun9qNQquWRHNq2qh8mn+x7if+SDZWNnMUC8qZOFDfZa/WL85MYcGJrerbSF\noAzLzeIAWgWaPBZpw8Q/db51SHqFzqN1uLy33EwyjbbndBzBlmWx9WIyZAcB0X2l\nhmpYlcmB7k35uF6xxatoIx3UrAZJc0UGqUaQt3Okw5D4X2nF86xrSQ9i3zQY/O8m\nnpdNSqzEa5LK9XOiCdba706rebIuX5SX4pQ0d+SXULFOekC9a6PTRlLjstPJQuOl\nU+q+447tWxmj+/UsI5MS\n=ceM8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T23:56:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/c117b814f5b1ff3ea3c067674c27a06a1695787a","node_id":"C_kwDOR4MqsdoAKGMxMTdiODE0ZjViMWZmM2VhM2MwNjc2NzRjMjdhMDZhMTY5NTc4N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/deed9f18ac8ab08a512d099ecaaacef863d4cb3e","sha":"deed9f18ac8ab08a512d099ecaaacef863d4cb3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/deed9f18ac8ab08a512d099ecaaacef863d4cb3e"}],"sha":"c117b814f5b1ff3ea3c067674c27a06a1695787a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/c117b814f5b1ff3ea3c067674c27a06a1695787a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/deed9f18ac8ab08a512d099ecaaacef863d4cb3e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T23:34:48Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T23:34:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add a Settings dialog with a brand picker (#60)\n\n* Add a Settings dialog with a brand picker\n\nCloses #59.\n\nThe palette is already entirely HSL triplets in custom properties, and no\ncomponent names a colour, so a brand is just a set of token values and\nswitching one is writing those onto the root element — no rebuild, no\nper-brand bundle, no component changes. Three brands: the current\nHealthKey palette, Lymphoma Research Foundation, and a partner green.\n\nGeneric deliberately declares no tokens. Applying it removes the\noverrides so the stylesheet governs again; listing today''s values there\ninstead would need mirroring on every future edit to index.css and would\ndrift the first time someone forgot.\n\nLRF''s own primary is a lavender at 71% lightness, which cannot carry\nwhite text. `--primary` is their deep purple and the lavender becomes the\nring and link colour, where its contrast holds. Transcribing the palette\nliterally would have looked right in a swatch and failed in use.\n\nFederated remotes follow the switch. hk-labs and promop already did —\nthis file declares their token contracts in terms of host tokens, and\nthey read them with var(--host-token, fallback). soc and exact did not,\nso their contracts are mapped here too. Those two declare their defaults\nON their own root element, and a custom property declared on an element\nbeats one inherited from :root, so the mapping has to match the same\nelement with more specificity — `html .soc-root` (0,1,1) over their\n(0,1,0), which also wins regardless of source order, and order matters\nbecause remote CSS is injected at runtime and always lands last.\n\nVerified in a browser against a faithful mimic of soc''s stylesheet\ninjected after ours: the button renders the host blue rather than soc''s\nown #0c5fc0, follows a brand change to #280D50 and #457350, and returns\nto the host default when the brand is cleared.\n\nOnly tokenised colour is reachable this way — anything a remote\nhard-codes outside a custom property stays as it is, and rewriting their\nrules is not an option since their stylesheets are cross-origin and\ncssRules throws.\n\n* Brand the app chrome and the control shape\n\nThe header, the left menu and the button shape were hard-coded to the\ndefault look, so a brand switch reached the page content and stopped at\nthe frame around it. They are tokens now, with the generic brand\ndeclaring none of them — the defaults in index.css are today''s\nappearance expressed as tokens, so the default is a no-op.\n\nValues sampled from the screenshots rather than eyeballed: header\n#250E4D, left menu #9974F1, buttons #9974F0 on a #F8F5FF page.\n\nTwo judgement calls. `--primary` is now the lavender rather than the\ndeep purple, because that is what the site''s buttons actually use; the\npurple keeps `--text-brand-secondary-700`, since at 70% lightness the\nlavender is fine behind a large white button label and fails behind\nsmall text on white. And the pill lives on its own `--radius-control`\nrather than `--radius`, which also drives cards and panels — a pill card\nis not the same request as a pill button.\n\nButtons now agree across the host and soc, which is what \"different on\nsoc and labs\" was about. exact keeps its own shape by request and takes\nonly the palette, so `--exact-border-radius` is deliberately unmapped.\nhk-labs is the exception: its radius token feeds its cards as well as\nits buttons, so matching the pill there would round everything.\n\nMeasured in a browser, LRF against generic:\n\n  header    rgb(37,14,78)    vs rgb(255,255,255)\n  menu      rgb(153,116,241) vs rgb(255,255,255)\n  button    rgb(154,117,240) 9999px vs rgb(11,79,157) 6px\n  soc       rgb(154,117,240) 9999px vs rgb(11,79,157) 6px\n  exact     rgb(154,117,240) 8px    vs rgb(34,195,104) 8px\n\n* Fix unreadable header controls, and keep the sidebar footer on screen\n\nThree things, found from the branded header screenshot.\n\nThe user name was `text-muted-foreground` — a fixed grey chosen against a\nwhite header, invisible once the header took a dark brand colour. It\nfollows `--header-foreground` now, so it stays legible whatever the\nheader is.\n\nThe Sign out button was white-on-white. That is a real bug in the\n`outline` variant rather than a branding problem: it sets a background\nbut no text colour, so it inherits whatever the context provides — white,\nfrom the header — and painted it on a near-white pill. The variant now\nsets `text-foreground` explicitly, which fixes it everywhere, not just\nhere.\n\nAnd the sidebar footer was unreachable. The desktop aside stretches to\nthe document height, so on any page with content it ran to 2164px\nagainst a 700px viewport and the footer — Settings, Admin Panel — sat\nbelow the fold, reachable only by scrolling to the bottom of the page.\n`sticky top-0 h-svh` pins it: measured 700px tall with Settings at y=656,\non screen at any scroll position. Pre-existing, and it applied to Admin\nPanel just as much; it surfaced now because Settings is the item people\ngo looking for.\n\nVerified against the running app rather than a probe page: signed in\nlocally, both brands, footer measured in and out of the viewport before\nand after.\n\n* Review fixes: brand before first paint, admin chrome, a11y\n\nSix findings from /review on this branch. No critical ones.\n\nAuto-fixed:\n\n- AppLayout.tsx mobile menu button was `text-muted-foreground` — the same\n  fixed grey that made the user name invisible on a dark header, one line\n  away. It is `lg:hidden`, which is why the desktop screenshots missed it.\n- `@theme` declared `--radius-control: var(--radius-control)`, a cycle\n  that only resolved because this `:root` is unlayered and beat the\n  layered emit. Renamed the app token to `--control-radius` so the theme\n  entry reads a different name and the cycle is gone.\n- The brand radios are `sr-only`, so keyboard focus was invisible. The\n  label draws the ring now.\n\nDecided and applied:\n\n- Brand values moved from inline styles in JavaScript to `[data-brand]`\n  blocks in index.css, with index.html stamping the attribute before\n  React mounts. Applying them after mount showed a frame of the default\n  blue on every load. Two things fall out for free: no duplicated token\n  list to drift, and the `.dark` variants are ordinary selectors, so the\n  MutationObserver that re-applied on theme change is gone.\n- AdminLayout''s sidebar was still on the old hard-coded classes, so a\n  brand turned the app sidebar lavender and left the admin one white. It\n  is on the same tokens now, with the same sticky fix.\n\nAccepted, not fixed: white on the LRF lavender is 3.41:1, under AA''s 4.5\nfor 14px labels. It is the colour lymphoma.org uses and matching the\nbrand won; recorded in branding.ts with the measured number and the\nlightness that would pass, so the next reader does not silently undo it.\n\nRe-verified after the refactor, since it changed how tokens are applied:\ngeneric, lymphoma, partner and cleared all resolve correctly for the host\nbutton, soc''s button (against soc''s own stylesheet injected after ours),\nthe header and the sidebar — and lymphoma+dark now works with no\nJavaScript at all. In the running app `data-brand` is present at\nnavigation commit, with no inline styles on the root element.","tree":{"sha":"d20b58a72e2056d4e2d19e9982419ebf7636b6cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/d20b58a72e2056d4e2d19e9982419ebf7636b6cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/deed9f18ac8ab08a512d099ecaaacef863d4cb3e","verification":{"payload":"tree d20b58a72e2056d4e2d19e9982419ebf7636b6cb\nparent b906878046bd6585195b0d61ba157c6cd6a7ffc1\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1786404888 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786404888 -0700\n\nAdd a Settings dialog with a brand picker (#60)\n\n* Add a Settings dialog with a brand picker\n\nCloses #59.\n\nThe palette is already entirely HSL triplets in custom properties, and no\ncomponent names a colour, so a brand is just a set of token values and\nswitching one is writing those onto the root element — no rebuild, no\nper-brand bundle, no component changes. Three brands: the current\nHealthKey palette, Lymphoma Research Foundation, and a partner green.\n\nGeneric deliberately declares no tokens. Applying it removes the\noverrides so the stylesheet governs again; listing today''s values there\ninstead would need mirroring on every future edit to index.css and would\ndrift the first time someone forgot.\n\nLRF''s own primary is a lavender at 71% lightness, which cannot carry\nwhite text. `--primary` is their deep purple and the lavender becomes the\nring and link colour, where its contrast holds. Transcribing the palette\nliterally would have looked right in a swatch and failed in use.\n\nFederated remotes follow the switch. hk-labs and promop already did —\nthis file declares their token contracts in terms of host tokens, and\nthey read them with var(--host-token, fallback). soc and exact did not,\nso their contracts are mapped here too. Those two declare their defaults\nON their own root element, and a custom property declared on an element\nbeats one inherited from :root, so the mapping has to match the same\nelement with more specificity — `html .soc-root` (0,1,1) over their\n(0,1,0), which also wins regardless of source order, and order matters\nbecause remote CSS is injected at runtime and always lands last.\n\nVerified in a browser against a faithful mimic of soc''s stylesheet\ninjected after ours: the button renders the host blue rather than soc''s\nown #0c5fc0, follows a brand change to #280D50 and #457350, and returns\nto the host default when the brand is cleared.\n\nOnly tokenised colour is reachable this way — anything a remote\nhard-codes outside a custom property stays as it is, and rewriting their\nrules is not an option since their stylesheets are cross-origin and\ncssRules throws.\n\n* Brand the app chrome and the control shape\n\nThe header, the left menu and the button shape were hard-coded to the\ndefault look, so a brand switch reached the page content and stopped at\nthe frame around it. They are tokens now, with the generic brand\ndeclaring none of them — the defaults in index.css are today''s\nappearance expressed as tokens, so the default is a no-op.\n\nValues sampled from the screenshots rather than eyeballed: header\n#250E4D, left menu #9974F1, buttons #9974F0 on a #F8F5FF page.\n\nTwo judgement calls. `--primary` is now the lavender rather than the\ndeep purple, because that is what the site''s buttons actually use; the\npurple keeps `--text-brand-secondary-700`, since at 70% lightness the\nlavender is fine behind a large white button label and fails behind\nsmall text on white. And the pill lives on its own `--radius-control`\nrather than `--radius`, which also drives cards and panels — a pill card\nis not the same request as a pill button.\n\nButtons now agree across the host and soc, which is what \"different on\nsoc and labs\" was about. exact keeps its own shape by request and takes\nonly the palette, so `--exact-border-radius` is deliberately unmapped.\nhk-labs is the exception: its radius token feeds its cards as well as\nits buttons, so matching the pill there would round everything.\n\nMeasured in a browser, LRF against generic:\n\n  header    rgb(37,14,78)    vs rgb(255,255,255)\n  menu      rgb(153,116,241) vs rgb(255,255,255)\n  button    rgb(154,117,240) 9999px vs rgb(11,79,157) 6px\n  soc       rgb(154,117,240) 9999px vs rgb(11,79,157) 6px\n  exact     rgb(154,117,240) 8px    vs rgb(34,195,104) 8px\n\n* Fix unreadable header controls, and keep the sidebar footer on screen\n\nThree things, found from the branded header screenshot.\n\nThe user name was `text-muted-foreground` — a fixed grey chosen against a\nwhite header, invisible once the header took a dark brand colour. It\nfollows `--header-foreground` now, so it stays legible whatever the\nheader is.\n\nThe Sign out button was white-on-white. That is a real bug in the\n`outline` variant rather than a branding problem: it sets a background\nbut no text colour, so it inherits whatever the context provides — white,\nfrom the header — and painted it on a near-white pill. The variant now\nsets `text-foreground` explicitly, which fixes it everywhere, not just\nhere.\n\nAnd the sidebar footer was unreachable. The desktop aside stretches to\nthe document height, so on any page with content it ran to 2164px\nagainst a 700px viewport and the footer — Settings, Admin Panel — sat\nbelow the fold, reachable only by scrolling to the bottom of the page.\n`sticky top-0 h-svh` pins it: measured 700px tall with Settings at y=656,\non screen at any scroll position. Pre-existing, and it applied to Admin\nPanel just as much; it surfaced now because Settings is the item people\ngo looking for.\n\nVerified against the running app rather than a probe page: signed in\nlocally, both brands, footer measured in and out of the viewport before\nand after.\n\n* Review fixes: brand before first paint, admin chrome, a11y\n\nSix findings from /review on this branch. No critical ones.\n\nAuto-fixed:\n\n- AppLayout.tsx mobile menu button was `text-muted-foreground` — the same\n  fixed grey that made the user name invisible on a dark header, one line\n  away. It is `lg:hidden`, which is why the desktop screenshots missed it.\n- `@theme` declared `--radius-control: var(--radius-control)`, a cycle\n  that only resolved because this `:root` is unlayered and beat the\n  layered emit. Renamed the app token to `--control-radius` so the theme\n  entry reads a different name and the cycle is gone.\n- The brand radios are `sr-only`, so keyboard focus was invisible. The\n  label draws the ring now.\n\nDecided and applied:\n\n- Brand values moved from inline styles in JavaScript to `[data-brand]`\n  blocks in index.css, with index.html stamping the attribute before\n  React mounts. Applying them after mount showed a frame of the default\n  blue on every load. Two things fall out for free: no duplicated token\n  list to drift, and the `.dark` variants are ordinary selectors, so the\n  MutationObserver that re-applied on theme change is gone.\n- AdminLayout''s sidebar was still on the old hard-coded classes, so a\n  brand turned the app sidebar lavender and left the admin one white. It\n  is on the same tokens now, with the same sticky fix.\n\nAccepted, not fixed: white on the LRF lavender is 3.41:1, under AA''s 4.5\nfor 14px labels. It is the colour lymphoma.org uses and matching the\nbrand won; recorded in branding.ts with the measured number and the\nlightness that would pass, so the next reader does not silently undo it.\n\nRe-verified after the refactor, since it changed how tokens are applied:\ngeneric, lymphoma, partner and cleared all resolve correctly for the host\nbutton, soc''s button (against soc''s own stylesheet injected after ours),\nthe header and the sidebar — and lymphoma+dark now works with no\nJavaScript at all. In the running app `data-brand` is present at\nnavigation commit, with no inline styles on the root element.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqemAYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARcAQACDIRNTT8QXXu8LHCKI30fy1\nJDvCJRWbDR8tayCbAogV0v/zyYKBi/FdjKLA5HH6gGXLAzUQr8GZyPokKRX26BSb\nEXUSUB8NGJpAJG+hRXTb9IaLrfsUIVgRzPraHU7Bn+ExMRp/idOyVHPdvotmBf73\ngaxaEED+plLVCK9ilr2srhVEMw/cdvdgndWrnW5nr4lYr/zl6s09Uym95b5/+DEE\nbfaTkxJ5Ey3R0izSJ14VaWJp9rRaspBJlDnpDzCUdBYPciYesJPTxUisvspcwNOj\n14h86KMKiGDw/plcuEOHSsLneXcGjheyYXEuXhCUVrfwy3DYjoGQ44SyGmVXv+PN\ned9CmG4/AiwbYmR2SV9Ppficj3CPYpw5+3GfAcJrOLK8Z2ygdzHDD087tBsr2YuB\nj/9LF0kC4rA/J7KPmoxOmCbFDdJkOWByyiGOokR9a1dgHZpRtucXEbSuLQ5l4GSK\nhU/rlSvKe/zrDl6XyYVP0vkqpxdt1YlNJ98pwQxAMEcokcLoTCNyr6iI5C5X8Gfy\nBIONtUAJSLG8spSqM5f2NMGp2Ta36pHSgrPX2wrsAwP6Va+/MXoSvWFeR2DREJEB\n4nyxttXDL6ML/0s8MqtKVcAhXIsJ3QFxlWAlRS9E2qTktM2w0nRKQ9JH+Xq2n2XO\n0SGXrVTrF/yIY0qwxD4W\n=2wmA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T23:34:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/deed9f18ac8ab08a512d099ecaaacef863d4cb3e","node_id":"C_kwDOR4MqsdoAKGRlZWQ5ZjE4YWM4YWIwOGE1MTJkMDk5ZWNhYWFjZWY4NjNkNGNiM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/b906878046bd6585195b0d61ba157c6cd6a7ffc1","sha":"b906878046bd6585195b0d61ba157c6cd6a7ffc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/b906878046bd6585195b0d61ba157c6cd6a7ffc1"}],"sha":"deed9f18ac8ab08a512d099ecaaacef863d4cb3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/deed9f18ac8ab08a512d099ecaaacef863d4cb3e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/b906878046bd6585195b0d61ba157c6cd6a7ffc1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T21:02:41Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T21:02:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Declare the EXACT build args so the remote URL reaches the bundle (#57)\n\nRender passes service env vars into a Docker build only for names the\nDockerfile declares as ARG. VITE_EXACT_REMOTE_URL and VITE_EXACT_API_URL\nwere set on the service but never declared, so vite fell back to its\nlocalhost defaults and the deployed bundle shipped\nhttp://localhost:9400 — the Find Trials page renders and then fails to\nload its module, with nothing in the build log to say why.\n\nCaught by grepping the deployed bundle: the soc, labs and promop origins\nwere all present and exact''s was not.","tree":{"sha":"5db6d3ef16756f4e75bd9c3dc524dd766544d9a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/5db6d3ef16756f4e75bd9c3dc524dd766544d9a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/b906878046bd6585195b0d61ba157c6cd6a7ffc1","verification":{"payload":"tree 5db6d3ef16756f4e75bd9c3dc524dd766544d9a3\nparent 0c3e0e33fbf2058d050355e192d2f6a5595f4475\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1786395761 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786395761 -0700\n\nDeclare the EXACT build args so the remote URL reaches the bundle (#57)\n\nRender passes service env vars into a Docker build only for names the\nDockerfile declares as ARG. VITE_EXACT_REMOTE_URL and VITE_EXACT_API_URL\nwere set on the service but never declared, so vite fell back to its\nlocalhost defaults and the deployed bundle shipped\nhttp://localhost:9400 — the Find Trials page renders and then fails to\nload its module, with nothing in the build log to say why.\n\nCaught by grepping the deployed bundle: the soc, labs and promop origins\nwere all present and exact''s was not.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqejxxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoaIQAKQ9nWVXfamfgGRnNWPVCk7Q\nL0sFHgOBldiA+PGvf6AKkhrtHPmZ0CLnYbSmdT3rjNAAlvR4MtOVJZYIgO073sxY\nzj/GOx5HThl8vkK0SLshvhsrvTtRHFZqJCXnO8NtOlyXYAXdu2gMHPP4j9piXiyD\niFL3Xu5gnsxjljwI4K45XYEzxehk4+UinPMissxXPFuxL1xOt1ZemFEVmFokE/XY\nQ/6U8MnkhnEMMDuUmLJGdv08/ItPy8YGLNRRp+qE1W8Aa5ATsF01UdKw7G5d5MQK\nVcik3oGEfybg3YG6Gq+StH9Dqe8fzccGk3/MA7hGGX5npHQAUgep7anTY0z4EzVD\nz8QFwYZI3wycNCbv+vY1X+R+cm6fVFgHXKLTb8cmJ59EY5w48PrBH7ep8Xthc6LK\nyLD2821yDEwHc4IM0NEMvZdtwRMmoXrqF8XqdnQ/zbR2a+npDjWktg6G0bBWTzDO\n0QHh8q1MGVh5hoIKKVaDW78pfv9vstYCCxbQwHk5kCnI+CHl0xN6LtEX/EW6cg/1\nDv11Ma4L96oipk4EwFkMbGwey5zQVl3pRseP1cjkRmL+JqUHjjmpiTZDc/9qLpyx\nwT3TChId2ySjrSHvvEvQ5Be2q8whGTO4mLID9owKGiqYbnsA0BoV3rGC/LhH3UNA\nQhQPYLGaD3UOekCi8Ju6\n=pCJ/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T21:02:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/b906878046bd6585195b0d61ba157c6cd6a7ffc1","node_id":"C_kwDOR4MqsdoAKGI5MDY4NzgwNDZiZDY1ODUxOTViMGQ2MWJhMTU3YzZjZDZhN2ZmYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/0c3e0e33fbf2058d050355e192d2f6a5595f4475","sha":"0c3e0e33fbf2058d050355e192d2f6a5595f4475","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/0c3e0e33fbf2058d050355e192d2f6a5595f4475"}],"sha":"b906878046bd6585195b0d61ba157c6cd6a7ffc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/b906878046bd6585195b0d61ba157c6cd6a7ffc1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/0c3e0e33fbf2058d050355e192d2f6a5595f4475/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T20:55:29Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T20:55:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Federate Find Trials from EXACT into the portal (#56)\n\n* Federate Find Trials from EXACT into the portal\n\nAdds the /trials page consuming exact_remote/TrialMatches, an EXACT API\nclient, and the remote declaration.\n\nPatient context is normalised by EXACT itself, through its\n/normalize-ctomop-row/ endpoint, rather than mapped field by field the way\nthe Find Treatments page does. That endpoint converts receptor statuses to\ncodes and TNM strings to short codes; reimplementing it here would drift\nfrom EXACT the moment it changes. The query is left at the default\nstaleTime so it refetches on window focus — a patient who edits their\ncountry and postcode in the Health Profile and comes back sees matches for\nthe new location without a manual reload, and filtering inside the remote\ndoes not remount it.\n\nA record we cannot read or normalise does not block the page: the remote\nstill renders its filters and an unfiltered list, which beats an error.\n\nThe API client carries EXACT''s origin with no path, because this remote\nissues relative paths and EXACT mounts its router at the service root —\ndeliberately unlike soc''s client, whose remote builds its own /api/v1\nprefix from an apiBasePath prop.\n\nThe menu item is gated on VITE_EXACT_REMOTE_URL, so it stays \"Coming soon\"\nwherever EXACT is not configured.\n\nVerified locally against EXACT in Docker: signed in, the item is a live\nlink, /trials loads the remote from localhost:9400 and renders its filter\nUI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Provision an EXACT staging service on Render\n\nUnlike LABS and SOC this creates no project. An EXACT project already\nexisted, holding another team''s Production environment and the service\nrunning there, so Terraform owns only the resources inside a staging\nenvironment added alongside it, addressed by id. Importing that project\nto manage both environments from here was the alternative and was\nrejected: it would put someone else''s production one `terraform destroy`\naway from deletion to gain nothing staging needs.\n\nOnly the service''s own Django database is provisioned. The trial corpus\nstays in the externally managed Postgres the existing instance reads —\nthe Render database behind that service holds nothing but Django\nscaffolding, so there was no copy to make, and duplicating ~271 MB buys\nisolation at the price of a snapshot nothing refreshes. Patient records\nare not a database connection at all: the portal reads them in the\nbrowser with the patient''s own token and posts the row inline, so\nCTOMOP_BASE only backs a server-side resolver the portal never calls.\nIt is derived from promop_api_url so the two cannot drift.\n\nNo PostGIS step: the GeoDjango backend creates the extension during\nmigrate. An earlier attempt ran psql first and failed — Render does not\nexpand $DATABASE_URL in a pre-deploy command, so psql fell through to a\nlocal socket that does not exist.\n\n* Record where Find Trials stands after provisioning staging\n\n* Stop a bare apply from wiping deployment secrets\n\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GS_CREDENTIALS_JSON and TRIALS_DATABASE_URL live in\nstate and nowhere else in the repo — their variables default to \"\" so\nthat nothing secret is committed. That default is the danger: an apply\nrun without the matching TF_VAR exported reads \"\" as the intended value\nand quietly nulls them. It came close three times, most recently while\nprovisioning exact, where the plan offered to null both labs secrets as\na side effect of an unrelated change.\n\nEach failure is silent in the worst way. Labs keeps answering its health\ncheck while extraction and uploads fail; exact falls back to\nsingle-database mode and serves zero trials, and /healthz does not probe\nthat alias by design, so it stays green throughout.\n\nThe trade is that Terraform can no longer change these once set — rotate\nin the dashboard, or drop the entry for the single apply that rotates.\nA rotation is deliberate and watched; an accidental wipe is neither.\n\nCTOMOP_SERVICE_TOKEN is deliberately excluded: it is empty by design, so\nthere is nothing to protect, and ignoring it would swallow the apply\nthat first sets it.\n\n* Pin exact staging to the federation branch for now\n\nexact''s main is governed by a ruleset requiring an approving review, and\nuntil exact#359 lands main builds an image with no federation remote and\nno /healthz — a deploy from it fails its health check and serves nothing\nthe portal can load. Pinning lets the whole path be exercised end to end\nmeanwhile.\n\nRevert to \"main\" as soon as exact#359 merges: the branch is deleted on\nmerge, and deploy-render.yml only fires for main, so the service would\notherwise sit on a commit nothing updates.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8e8f54c87da2a3d024a0907aef765e8e9f6748fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/8e8f54c87da2a3d024a0907aef765e8e9f6748fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/0c3e0e33fbf2058d050355e192d2f6a5595f4475","verification":{"payload":"tree 8e8f54c87da2a3d024a0907aef765e8e9f6748fa\nparent c07597bdc53832b55abc1f8cf764f52e970f7e87\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1786395329 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786395329 -0700\n\nFederate Find Trials from EXACT into the portal (#56)\n\n* Federate Find Trials from EXACT into the portal\n\nAdds the /trials page consuming exact_remote/TrialMatches, an EXACT API\nclient, and the remote declaration.\n\nPatient context is normalised by EXACT itself, through its\n/normalize-ctomop-row/ endpoint, rather than mapped field by field the way\nthe Find Treatments page does. That endpoint converts receptor statuses to\ncodes and TNM strings to short codes; reimplementing it here would drift\nfrom EXACT the moment it changes. The query is left at the default\nstaleTime so it refetches on window focus — a patient who edits their\ncountry and postcode in the Health Profile and comes back sees matches for\nthe new location without a manual reload, and filtering inside the remote\ndoes not remount it.\n\nA record we cannot read or normalise does not block the page: the remote\nstill renders its filters and an unfiltered list, which beats an error.\n\nThe API client carries EXACT''s origin with no path, because this remote\nissues relative paths and EXACT mounts its router at the service root —\ndeliberately unlike soc''s client, whose remote builds its own /api/v1\nprefix from an apiBasePath prop.\n\nThe menu item is gated on VITE_EXACT_REMOTE_URL, so it stays \"Coming soon\"\nwherever EXACT is not configured.\n\nVerified locally against EXACT in Docker: signed in, the item is a live\nlink, /trials loads the remote from localhost:9400 and renders its filter\nUI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Provision an EXACT staging service on Render\n\nUnlike LABS and SOC this creates no project. An EXACT project already\nexisted, holding another team''s Production environment and the service\nrunning there, so Terraform owns only the resources inside a staging\nenvironment added alongside it, addressed by id. Importing that project\nto manage both environments from here was the alternative and was\nrejected: it would put someone else''s production one `terraform destroy`\naway from deletion to gain nothing staging needs.\n\nOnly the service''s own Django database is provisioned. The trial corpus\nstays in the externally managed Postgres the existing instance reads —\nthe Render database behind that service holds nothing but Django\nscaffolding, so there was no copy to make, and duplicating ~271 MB buys\nisolation at the price of a snapshot nothing refreshes. Patient records\nare not a database connection at all: the portal reads them in the\nbrowser with the patient''s own token and posts the row inline, so\nCTOMOP_BASE only backs a server-side resolver the portal never calls.\nIt is derived from promop_api_url so the two cannot drift.\n\nNo PostGIS step: the GeoDjango backend creates the extension during\nmigrate. An earlier attempt ran psql first and failed — Render does not\nexpand $DATABASE_URL in a pre-deploy command, so psql fell through to a\nlocal socket that does not exist.\n\n* Record where Find Trials stands after provisioning staging\n\n* Stop a bare apply from wiping deployment secrets\n\nANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GS_CREDENTIALS_JSON and TRIALS_DATABASE_URL live in\nstate and nowhere else in the repo — their variables default to \"\" so\nthat nothing secret is committed. That default is the danger: an apply\nrun without the matching TF_VAR exported reads \"\" as the intended value\nand quietly nulls them. It came close three times, most recently while\nprovisioning exact, where the plan offered to null both labs secrets as\na side effect of an unrelated change.\n\nEach failure is silent in the worst way. Labs keeps answering its health\ncheck while extraction and uploads fail; exact falls back to\nsingle-database mode and serves zero trials, and /healthz does not probe\nthat alias by design, so it stays green throughout.\n\nThe trade is that Terraform can no longer change these once set — rotate\nin the dashboard, or drop the entry for the single apply that rotates.\nA rotation is deliberate and watched; an accidental wipe is neither.\n\nCTOMOP_SERVICE_TOKEN is deliberately excluded: it is empty by design, so\nthere is nothing to protect, and ignoring it would swallow the apply\nthat first sets it.\n\n* Pin exact staging to the federation branch for now\n\nexact''s main is governed by a ruleset requiring an approving review, and\nuntil exact#359 lands main builds an image with no federation remote and\nno /healthz — a deploy from it fails its health check and serves nothing\nthe portal can load. Pinning lets the whole path be exercised end to end\nmeanwhile.\n\nRevert to \"main\" as soon as exact#359 merges: the branch is deleted on\nmerge, and deploy-render.yml only fires for main, so the service would\notherwise sit on a commit nothing updates.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqejrBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbe8QAFGzuuBCJEXXoZHVynZz3b3a\nhNCA5OVCOwPGbCEKsbPxSM+CCsHJ2K1oaNG0a0JaI1cXj+DQdjYmU7XPvZCnfiWp\nJt6xgIfldKZt9mRMXvDGkyY3r7IVqmiBWeg086jFqjMVq9XWbAO8fspFc0DDPm5U\nL1eIT8ziY7GD/q6lIBBWLMps8NWocw1a4fBQDKygpsBhI2oUpNxH6Fj8gZzVOJfc\n0ZBpzvUw2S+xMQiwIg51OUkj0HT3q1EHA4XA3njfSxDzK/mUY17yRO4d4J/16A9N\nP+4OJfx1pETGDVYjx3hghdVEKn7TgeTblwmUTN7hhJG4arZ8LzsMLkPXZm5/XcO8\neiD2fY9utuBN6VGTOgVZpI0lwNPVu4n0VF8YHQRNyYCqRdE1ic8dVFG8L6ukWYKu\nPGqWafBXBZytpC5AAlmZx6UaPK8poZMWoLtEIfQjrROLaM2kCvNTYpqSeB9fFH9b\nFc+DsSqbT4wqfPk3+GpKuJbucFqK/VivtWKVneKdQTvr3lmtdYTZnnvnT4nfqzNz\njmxo8rpds/ZqnXQHXUD2+uPTclNQPuHl9UFJQlZa/72I385uaGe3tA5B5EI/69gc\nCr0oGIwHVTciVL8vjKS1XDDjB6frxTpjPCErJWR1vEzbaWL7sKUaJIjp3x3ll3YI\nbMIAe/+nEFU0JGD0xjUb\n=9VZq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/0c3e0e33fbf2058d050355e192d2f6a5595f4475","node_id":"C_kwDOR4MqsdoAKDBjM2UwZTMzZmJmMjA1OGQwNTAzNTVlMTkyZDJmNmE1NTk1ZjQ0NzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/c07597bdc53832b55abc1f8cf764f52e970f7e87","sha":"c07597bdc53832b55abc1f8cf764f52e970f7e87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/c07597bdc53832b55abc1f8cf764f52e970f7e87"}],"sha":"0c3e0e33fbf2058d050355e192d2f6a5595f4475","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/0c3e0e33fbf2058d050355e192d2f6a5595f4475"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/c07597bdc53832b55abc1f8cf764f52e970f7e87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T19:09:48Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T19:09:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Commit the soc staging config that is already applied (#55)\n\nThese three values were applied to Render while bringing soc up and never\ncommitted. Terraform state here is local and gitignored, so this file is\nthe only record — applying from a clean checkout would have reverted them,\nand one of them is load-bearing.\n\nALLOWED_HOSTS: settings/staging.py raises at import when it is unset, so\nthe service crash-loops rather than starting. The infrastructure would have\nlooked healthy and the container would have been dead.\n\nPARTNER_AUTH_PROVIDERS: portal-only. There is no Firebase on Render, and\nlisting a provider with no credentials logs \"no credentials configured\" for\nevery token that is not ours.\n\nsoc_url: enables the portal''s Find Treatments item, which is gated on\nVITE_SOC_REMOTE_URL. Note it bakes in at image build time, so changing it\nneeds a portal rebuild rather than a restart. Clearing it and rebuilding is\nalso how the item gets hidden again if the catalog (soc#267) is not ready\nin time.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8e3c407805ae48c06548dd6ecefd4cf47ac9caf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/8e3c407805ae48c06548dd6ecefd4cf47ac9caf9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/c07597bdc53832b55abc1f8cf764f52e970f7e87","verification":{"payload":"tree 8e3c407805ae48c06548dd6ecefd4cf47ac9caf9\nparent 52146b1076706f75e7695d207e0ad9a980c8daa7\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1786388988 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786388988 -0700\n\nCommit the soc staging config that is already applied (#55)\n\nThese three values were applied to Render while bringing soc up and never\ncommitted. Terraform state here is local and gitignored, so this file is\nthe only record — applying from a clean checkout would have reverted them,\nand one of them is load-bearing.\n\nALLOWED_HOSTS: settings/staging.py raises at import when it is unset, so\nthe service crash-loops rather than starting. The infrastructure would have\nlooked healthy and the container would have been dead.\n\nPARTNER_AUTH_PROVIDERS: portal-only. There is no Firebase on Render, and\nlisting a provider with no credentials logs \"no credentials configured\" for\nevery token that is not ours.\n\nsoc_url: enables the portal''s Find Treatments item, which is gated on\nVITE_SOC_REMOTE_URL. Note it bakes in at image build time, so changing it\nneeds a portal rebuild rather than a restart. Clearing it and rebuilding is\nalso how the item gets hidden again if the catalog (soc#267) is not ready\nin time.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqeiH8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn40QABnX6l/oQOssVzonzJsD7OFR\nJxzRPmFFPDDs2ZV0g/j91LO/De6gmkVJinHfW3/crRF6ShpH/6Xne9Ti3RBamZY6\nfY6Qr0x3d7xwS4i0fPxAh/VL8xeBq1Z02GPrlNH0s/gD6UL1eRhRlomgcnHnPf9l\nMw7Bnb6jxTmDSbRPLxVO8qJG7EE9CNxMB0ctIRXlR4M6sGHHviHorYX1krHMUmOG\n8xy8Wze8LU08fE/E7dkpdLKXUNSwya80QyJ4Aq/invUO1U8rfkSh9XEeFvPn86kb\nOLKo43E8HKpnXNJTd3Dun7V6o1xUkvDyVMiUoSCIDVTNliQAytsAvE3vhCsRkvYv\nN0QDRbT6K4ppEZGudZ3vepKdc/T/21DItb5cuRRt6ZE/GwVqdJrnEWLBkoWJ41PZ\n83HcsxDuKFx0Y8jOhb5YfJoMcxsf/dvrPh+XtJCCKMitRU+ussq6/VbaIsMjXddG\nymx8MiK7nIQBXYW0IknFQhLkBh6dFOBK7ikB5XeRFBxdgEvEYOExkk+IqCbXCFKK\nLSXN9fuFQ7JG/qkWn2CzQoSwgLFiX3y0guHslejvmyuEu4A6fLfg4qsV0Lrt3EXP\nOTz3F6uM0OI10ufVfcjOu+AIvOjqiuO51FdjjFcCspK8RwdPmSP5C3BvVn92MMBr\nNO4Dr0q/MZt+fFaExfSY\n=9OPW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T19:09:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/c07597bdc53832b55abc1f8cf764f52e970f7e87","node_id":"C_kwDOR4MqsdoAKGMwNzU5N2JkYzUzODMyYjU1YWJjMWY4Y2Y3NjRmNTJlOTcwZjdlODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/52146b1076706f75e7695d207e0ad9a980c8daa7","sha":"52146b1076706f75e7695d207e0ad9a980c8daa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/52146b1076706f75e7695d207e0ad9a980c8daa7"}],"sha":"c07597bdc53832b55abc1f8cf764f52e970f7e87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/c07597bdc53832b55abc1f8cf764f52e970f7e87"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/52146b1076706f75e7695d207e0ad9a980c8daa7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:50:29Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:50:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Federate Find Treatments from soc into the portal (#53)\n\n* Federate Find Treatments from soc into the portal\n\nAdds the /treatments page consuming soc_remote/Recommendations, a soc API\nclient, the remote declaration, and Terraform for running soc on Render.\n\nPatient context comes from promop''s /patient-info/me/, projected onto soc''s\npatient_info contract. The projection is deliberately partial: soc tolerates\nsparse input and falls back to UNKNOWN, so a field is forwarded only where\nboth services agree on its shape — passing a value whose meaning differs\nwould mislead the pipeline more than omitting it.\n\nDisease resolves by slug rather than display title, and the two catalogs\ndiverge: promop emits multiple-myeloma where soc keys the same disease as\nmyeloma, and an unmapped slug 404s the recommend lookup. Only known\ndivergences are mapped; anything else passes through. A record whose\ndisease was typed into the form has no slug at all, so the title is\nslugified as a fallback — both paths then land on the same key.\n\nThe menu item is gated on VITE_SOC_REMOTE_URL, so it stays \"Coming soon\"\nwherever soc is not configured, matching how uploads work.\n\nsoc''s remote is served from the site root rather than under /static/,\nbecause it configures whitenoise with WHITENOISE_ROOT.\n\nThe Terraform is written but NOT applied: soc''s main branch has no node\nstage yet, so a service built from it would serve no remote. Sequence is in\nTODO.md — merge soc#263, deploy, then set soc_url and rebuild the portal so\nthe build args bake in.\n\nVerified locally against soc in Docker: signed in, the menu item is a live\nlink, /treatments loads the remote from localhost:9300 and renders, with no\nconsole errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Point the soc client at the origin, not /api\n\nsoc''s remote builds its own path — it posts to `${apiBasePath}/recommend`\nwith apiBasePath defaulting to \"/api/v1\" — so a base URL ending in /api\nproduced /api/api/v1/recommend.\n\nFixed in the hook default, the local env file and the Terraform build arg,\nwith a comment at the hook: this is deliberately unlike useLabsApi, whose\nremotes issue relative paths and whose client therefore does include\n/api/v1. Without the note someone will \"fix\" it back.\n\nVerified against soc in Docker: /treatments renders recommendations and\nsoc''s log shows the request arriving at /api/v1/recommend.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Rewrite the Find Treatments entry around the catalog blocker\n\nThe previous version listed seeding soc''s catalog as step 5, which read as\na finishing touch. It is the gate: soc''s Disease and treatment options come\nonly from a Firestore sync, the Render installation has no Firestore, and a\ndeployment without them authenticates perfectly and recommends nothing.\nThe entry now leads with that, states what was actually observed, and puts\nthe deployment steps behind the decision it depends on.\n\nAlso records two traps found while wiring it up: the promop/soc disease\nslug divergence, and soc''s refusal to guess a therapy-line count, which\nturns a record missing that field into a validation error rather than\nrecommendations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c5c1fa9b07ee8a1ddf2eabee7a006db9eebae7c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/c5c1fa9b07ee8a1ddf2eabee7a006db9eebae7c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/52146b1076706f75e7695d207e0ad9a980c8daa7","verification":{"payload":"tree c5c1fa9b07ee8a1ddf2eabee7a006db9eebae7c3\nparent 6f617d087caca26a2a5fcf8213881b620976cdc3\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1786380629 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786380629 -0700\n\nFederate Find Treatments from soc into the portal (#53)\n\n* Federate Find Treatments from soc into the portal\n\nAdds the /treatments page consuming soc_remote/Recommendations, a soc API\nclient, the remote declaration, and Terraform for running soc on Render.\n\nPatient context comes from promop''s /patient-info/me/, projected onto soc''s\npatient_info contract. The projection is deliberately partial: soc tolerates\nsparse input and falls back to UNKNOWN, so a field is forwarded only where\nboth services agree on its shape — passing a value whose meaning differs\nwould mislead the pipeline more than omitting it.\n\nDisease resolves by slug rather than display title, and the two catalogs\ndiverge: promop emits multiple-myeloma where soc keys the same disease as\nmyeloma, and an unmapped slug 404s the recommend lookup. Only known\ndivergences are mapped; anything else passes through. A record whose\ndisease was typed into the form has no slug at all, so the title is\nslugified as a fallback — both paths then land on the same key.\n\nThe menu item is gated on VITE_SOC_REMOTE_URL, so it stays \"Coming soon\"\nwherever soc is not configured, matching how uploads work.\n\nsoc''s remote is served from the site root rather than under /static/,\nbecause it configures whitenoise with WHITENOISE_ROOT.\n\nThe Terraform is written but NOT applied: soc''s main branch has no node\nstage yet, so a service built from it would serve no remote. Sequence is in\nTODO.md — merge soc#263, deploy, then set soc_url and rebuild the portal so\nthe build args bake in.\n\nVerified locally against soc in Docker: signed in, the menu item is a live\nlink, /treatments loads the remote from localhost:9300 and renders, with no\nconsole errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Point the soc client at the origin, not /api\n\nsoc''s remote builds its own path — it posts to `${apiBasePath}/recommend`\nwith apiBasePath defaulting to \"/api/v1\" — so a base URL ending in /api\nproduced /api/api/v1/recommend.\n\nFixed in the hook default, the local env file and the Terraform build arg,\nwith a comment at the hook: this is deliberately unlike useLabsApi, whose\nremotes issue relative paths and whose client therefore does include\n/api/v1. Without the note someone will \"fix\" it back.\n\nVerified against soc in Docker: /treatments renders recommendations and\nsoc''s log shows the request arriving at /api/v1/recommend.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Rewrite the Find Treatments entry around the catalog blocker\n\nThe previous version listed seeding soc''s catalog as step 5, which read as\na finishing touch. It is the gate: soc''s Disease and treatment options come\nonly from a Firestore sync, the Render installation has no Firestore, and a\ndeployment without them authenticates perfectly and recommends nothing.\nThe entry now leads with that, states what was actually observed, and puts\nthe deployment steps behind the decision it depends on.\n\nAlso records two traps found while wiring it up: the promop/soc disease\nslug divergence, and soc''s refusal to guess a therapy-line count, which\nturns a record missing that field into a validation error rather than\nrecommendations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqegFVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9HQQAJS0ZD7eDxyEx3wKdoaZj8Tk\nh34XTdQMB8PB1IL7mXyIcMNZsilTt+R+3VSVUkc1O9NrGywS+cJnoCgwzrT670Na\nBkpNZTRvVU04O3deuGaKYZW9nk3ZEDqColYwVLEn6cbX6Q605OS/0hPufUJiyiHP\n9eA6jIjZkzxoGJL1R6mTuDhIDt6bpx7wOth/ETicWWSYalMpf9iARbkcVcXgfdER\ngF0/H7JfqzBRTm7n3K6q+v9kE+DWHekvaAIMLN90HlMzRnOXiUO9KIEcnwqVU6MI\nNc9NbWbXrjWaV9NxtI0nJPxvmAQcYij0xDQ0NOMpYF9erl9IR5GLQCLSpGuC5e8L\n8QHFYM4ODwg8iReTBpXGsme1mAQdub6Wxjjlja5JWQTEE6iACSQOwx7WB6C131AB\nhxBSp05eXSYQiO6AkZQw7gBpCFYT1D/wHSFoWKh6MoJD90DfZJU9uxpA194L4neS\n59PGQS9Qr3CtuXxbjxAN3CM1+iybgugxX9ft8NdKF6hLBsSlg7IKFX20bFXC5Usc\n+G/kS1ZzHKxj2y3MkiTfk4Um8usJRrMpou8N9F4i5y5ZHTe+Be0eqw3m45Eb9Z4+\nbdWHwKZiag+7sHxufZkS71xif9DRbX7zF2U3lo7QuWWPUDG3dgrvawF3RqHDYet3\nHNz3wOeYfejn/J29oijB\n=U80X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T16:50:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/52146b1076706f75e7695d207e0ad9a980c8daa7","node_id":"C_kwDOR4MqsdoAKDUyMTQ2YjEwNzY3MDZmNzVlNzY5NWQyMDdlMGFkOWE5ODBjOGRhYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/6f617d087caca26a2a5fcf8213881b620976cdc3","sha":"6f617d087caca26a2a5fcf8213881b620976cdc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/6f617d087caca26a2a5fcf8213881b620976cdc3"}],"sha":"52146b1076706f75e7695d207e0ad9a980c8daa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/52146b1076706f75e7695d207e0ad9a980c8daa7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/6f617d087caca26a2a5fcf8213881b620976cdc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T19:53:09Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T19:53:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Trial the medium LOINC confidence floor on labs (#52)\n\nLAB_LOINC_MIN_CONFIDENCE decides which self-reported extractor claims are\nexamined at all; every code still has to survive the name, specimen,\nunit-family and value-type gates regardless.\n\nMeasured across five sample reports before choosing: rows carrying a real\nLOINC code went from 6 to 31, and the codes the model got wrong were caught\nby the name check rather than by the floor — it returned 2714-4 for DHEA-S,\nwhich is oxyhemoglobin in arterial blood, and the claim was rejected\nbecause its own stated name did not describe that code.\n\nA variable rather than a hand-edit on the service, so the setting is\nvisible in review and one line to revert.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2062fae894f664e6ced7a4ed7b39397b375ed4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/b2062fae894f664e6ced7a4ed7b39397b375ed4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/6f617d087caca26a2a5fcf8213881b620976cdc3","verification":{"payload":"tree b2062fae894f664e6ced7a4ed7b39397b375ed4b\nparent 23c888c53e91fd42032bb9825bc922fd1213a438\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1786132389 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786132389 -0700\n\nTrial the medium LOINC confidence floor on labs (#52)\n\nLAB_LOINC_MIN_CONFIDENCE decides which self-reported extractor claims are\nexamined at all; every code still has to survive the name, specimen,\nunit-family and value-type gates regardless.\n\nMeasured across five sample reports before choosing: rows carrying a real\nLOINC code went from 6 to 31, and the codes the model got wrong were caught\nby the name check rather than by the floor — it returned 2714-4 for DHEA-S,\nwhich is oxyhemoglobin in arterial blood, and the claim was rejected\nbecause its own stated name did not describe that code.\n\nA variable rather than a hand-edit on the service, so the setting is\nvisible in review and one line to revert.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdjelCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhLUQAJOu704VnUkbIXVP2HMKrofw\ndyAJgUSMQCEvdW95TrsaeecWNr2dA36nMyTJmpEM0b8q2Ja8MFnZ41A7Kd2vQEBW\n8cxgw3eV