pi.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/23c888c53e91fd42032bb9825bc922fd1213a438"}],"sha":"6f617d087caca26a2a5fcf8213881b620976cdc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/6f617d087caca26a2a5fcf8213881b620976cdc3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/23c888c53e91fd42032bb9825bc922fd1213a438/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:47:39Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:47:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Point the labs services at promop so saved results reach the record (#51)\n\nSaving lab values on Render appeared to work and then went nowhere: the\nlabs database recorded them as committed while phr''s Lab Results page,\nwhich reads from promop, stayed empty. CTOMOP_SYNC_URL was left unset when\nlabs first deployed — deliberately, to keep that deploy from writing to a\nshared record before object storage existed — and never revisited once\nuploads went live. The logs said so plainly: \"ctomop sync skipped:\nCTOMOP_SYNC_URL not configured\".\n\nDerived from promop_api_url, the same promop the SPA renders Lab Results\nfrom, so the write target and the read target cannot drift apart. No\nservice token: sync forwards the patient''s own bearer token, which promop\naccepts for their own record.\n\nVerified against production: committing a result returned sync_error false\nand it is now queryable at promop''s lab-results summary for that patient.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"624c5703f044f5b8d729e31a9a574c738d0c74c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/624c5703f044f5b8d729e31a9a574c738d0c74c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/23c888c53e91fd42032bb9825bc922fd1213a438","verification":{"payload":"tree 624c5703f044f5b8d729e31a9a574c738d0c74c1\nparent da071a46193b1d60ff903ddbd1543524c1bfc394\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1786074459 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786074459 -0700\n\nPoint the labs services at promop so saved results reach the record (#51)\n\nSaving lab values on Render appeared to work and then went nowhere: the\nlabs database recorded them as committed while phr''s Lab Results page,\nwhich reads from promop, stayed empty. CTOMOP_SYNC_URL was left unset when\nlabs first deployed — deliberately, to keep that deploy from writing to a\nshared record before object storage existed — and never revisited once\nuploads went live. The logs said so plainly: \"ctomop sync skipped:\nCTOMOP_SYNC_URL not configured\".\n\nDerived from promop_api_url, the same promop the SPA renders Lab Results\nfrom, so the write target and the read target cannot drift apart. No\nservice token: sync forwards the patient''s own bearer token, which promop\naccepts for their own record.\n\nVerified against production: committing a result returned sync_error false\nand it is now queryable at promop''s lab-results summary for that patient.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdVVbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIzYQAKmKLkyAdzjpg92dCQWxIB/g\nJv0HSwWsJlACOxnaWCqZZBuRjEd7/HhRmHlruH0m3mPCVxc2RINVCAWfSwn+EvKi\nnD+Gj6gqJfp8Ow1sOoVU0CVb7fh1cntSs709Sn/UxpC48PbcOIUIYB9+9YR8uduI\nnvtyXsrFgDqsOhGIY8I1VUBy16aUUfeKKE9AT9HEsmTNyHK8ujCq/uJQhNyvytKy\nV5wPJrIk4KrSXLztw8la4W1NOjSxuq4WkRdOt94ND6V2tVVhqV+K4i2xj//4YaBN\n1Gk8+6lsj1vmBWebkyApAmI3k8uiHq99PADmRR1iO19kqmoAEuQ4xOSAN7O7TkZk\nH8+yuTHY5bCL5+qu/u68dYtCG/nKbnctJmr9nZ7Re4kereDQVIPXMEsXVeU6oPei\nQaEiFJmLLCGIBy6XOUWiHdg9LLl76adz7xg7w3/zecw+zQk0Y25GJaOhH+XyjYaA\nvSWc9MrSPqtfnx6O0kwuMBiN3sloUwydQndxrsdbbtYskjVN1cj3Gk4oJaFHdEVB\nZlTaEocG30jOL/5XwEdunsJ36E7dqsnv/jY0k+6J06YscW509xbci5WlSASzTSw6\njIQWb0BHPqJmKp3fyUvDBaJPe7BZJR2JxGxIYvfyDt/y5vtIypONTBPN5giOwyxV\nyMDOZUXuk309lY5btV9D\n=zJwG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-07T03:47:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/23c888c53e91fd42032bb9825bc922fd1213a438","node_id":"C_kwDOR4MqsdoAKDIzYzg4OGM1M2U5MWZkNDIwMzJiYjk4MjViYzkyMmZkMTIxM2E0Mzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/da071a46193b1d60ff903ddbd1543524c1bfc394","sha":"da071a46193b1d60ff903ddbd1543524c1bfc394","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/da071a46193b1d60ff903ddbd1543524c1bfc394"}],"sha":"23c888c53e91fd42032bb9825bc922fd1213a438","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/23c888c53e91fd42032bb9825bc922fd1213a438"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/da071a46193b1d60ff903ddbd1543524c1bfc394/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:35:53Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:35:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stop the staging deploy failing when Render already has one queued (#50)\n\nThe trigger step piped the POST response straight into a JSON parser. Render\nanswers 201 with the new deploy, but 202 with an empty body when the service\nalready has a deploy queued, so the parser died on an empty string and failed\nthe run — while the deploy Render had accepted went ahead anyway. Any second\ntrigger arriving close behind the first hits this, which is what happened when\na manual redeploy overlapped the push-triggered one.\n\nThe step now reads the status code, treats any 2xx as accepted, and adopts the\nin-flight deploy when the body is empty rather than inventing a failure. A\nnon-2xx still fails, and now prints what Render actually said instead of a\nPython traceback.\n\nThe wait step had the same shape: one blank response from a transient API\nhiccup killed the run. A poll that comes back empty now costs a retry.\n\nVerified against all three response shapes (201 with body, 202 empty, 409\nrefused), and both steps pass bash -n with the embedded Python dedenting to\ncolumn 0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2486fb948e3ccd721aa12c45000f94e8b5ee0b84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/2486fb948e3ccd721aa12c45000f94e8b5ee0b84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/da071a46193b1d60ff903ddbd1543524c1bfc394","verification":{"payload":"tree 2486fb948e3ccd721aa12c45000f94e8b5ee0b84\nparent d83c77efba91a12d5938943946a82addf7fd0d63\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1786073753 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786073753 -0700\n\nStop the staging deploy failing when Render already has one queued (#50)\n\nThe trigger step piped the POST response straight into a JSON parser. Render\nanswers 201 with the new deploy, but 202 with an empty body when the service\nalready has a deploy queued, so the parser died on an empty string and failed\nthe run — while the deploy Render had accepted went ahead anyway. Any second\ntrigger arriving close behind the first hits this, which is what happened when\na manual redeploy overlapped the push-triggered one.\n\nThe step now reads the status code, treats any 2xx as accepted, and adopts the\nin-flight deploy when the body is empty rather than inventing a failure. A\nnon-2xx still fails, and now prints what Render actually said instead of a\nPython traceback.\n\nThe wait step had the same shape: one blank response from a transient API\nhiccup killed the run. A poll that comes back empty now costs a retry.\n\nVerified against all three response shapes (201 with body, 202 empty, 409\nrefused), and both steps pass bash -n with the embedded Python dedenting to\ncolumn 0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdVKZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtFgQAGMGt7rmSRMgF7GksiCqUCGV\n8/bvWzYcliNCJy+M3sOIeoed2hF/RE7gwvuMiFBTXDlWQ2osODpZd/bBvk6kUmaR\n0DtHzJ4EjUJOl+iGYf6h7cetpWSj9BDoPnuzX0/BdddibEi6DO26xZwv7s78lkTp\nq3Fi0NY1nLe30xnoqEUBJKrfLzpRChw3yO53bG4+vzM9lb0tCDQgQTOXul/1pcpA\nzjPis+9NePSqZHPL9L2Z3N+3vHUjaB3RENEwPmr1sn4uZAFnCxChZOsWk82WXtdw\njbLqcThgb3s0YEVmsvRYhiYH2hIhyg3fNYvutP2/lRiCGbp5htX4PVa8GE2DJjmV\n2vWSR1FaVY2e2I/pmimA0fwG8A/xzXMBczjZwoALpt3uzYgW8SzORtAnhaAXHL2s\nfd6oanP4avm8exXPzoO9c+0053q/orCKm+TULwUiTM6uFxtiRZjC2WR3wdRGuy4L\nX8tIM2p1e1XMAjBsau2YLDPA5eoVCr5LzfDQGdH3pq9WY1nYF3jXgJ712T6XqXBU\nAmMaFvDdX3wkVFefc4KC/G6bn5RQa08oaYM5AQ73qRXAZgNfbKbFd1x8+JtBWR1B\n1s6MqvadJ8JmbJdls+GVyx0rc4Ixmy6xT1b2Cg3fLPBi9/iRx98Q6O39OP5OThT3\niEHUmRIIeLsf81E+bIPd\n=2f88\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-07T03:36:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/da071a46193b1d60ff903ddbd1543524c1bfc394","node_id":"C_kwDOR4MqsdoAKGRhMDcxYTQ2MTkzYjFkNjBmZjkwM2RkYmQxNTQzNTI0YzFiZmMzOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/d83c77efba91a12d5938943946a82addf7fd0d63","sha":"d83c77efba91a12d5938943946a82addf7fd0d63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/d83c77efba91a12d5938943946a82addf7fd0d63"}],"sha":"da071a46193b1d60ff903ddbd1543524c1bfc394","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/da071a46193b1d60ff903ddbd1543524c1bfc394"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/d83c77efba91a12d5938943946a82addf7fd0d63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:28:31Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:28:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Federate the labs remote into phr and store uploads in GCS (#49)\n\nPoints phr''s SPA at the labs service on Render and turns uploads on.\n\nVITE_LABS_REMOTE_URL and VITE_LABS_API_URL are Docker build args, so they\nbake into the bundle and a change needs a rebuild rather than a restart.\nThey are pinned to a variable instead of referencing render_web_service.labs\ndirectly: labs reads phr''s URL for PHR_BASE_URL and CORS, so referencing it\nback is a dependency cycle. This is the safer side to pin — a stale labs URL\nbreaks the uploads page, while a stale phr URL inside labs would fail every\ntoken verification and take that service down entirely.\n\nUploads go to object storage rather than a Render disk. Disks attach to a\nsingle service, so a PDF the web service wrote would be invisible to the\nworker that rasterises it. Both services address the same bucket, reusing\nthe GCP deployment''s for now — object names are UUIDs and each deployment\nonly references its own rows, so they do not collide. The credential behind\nit belongs to a service account holding object access to that one bucket\nand nothing else; Render cannot use workload identity, so it needs a\ndownloadable key, and the blast radius of one is what decides which account\nto hand out.\n\nThe sidebar item is gated on VITE_LABS_REMOTE_URL, so it enables itself\nwherever the remote is configured and stays \"Coming soon\" where it is not.\n\nVerified against production: registered an account on phr, exchanged the\ntoken at labs (identity auto-provisioned, issuer healthkey-phr), uploaded a\nPDF, and the worker read it back out of the bucket and extracted 3 results.\nThe object is in GCS at the exact byte size uploaded, and /labs/uploads\nrenders the remote with the completed report.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"72751cee13f16bd6ae9ccf6cc59429283908d55b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/72751cee13f16bd6ae9ccf6cc59429283908d55b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/d83c77efba91a12d5938943946a82addf7fd0d63","verification":{"payload":"tree 72751cee13f16bd6ae9ccf6cc59429283908d55b\nparent e82c385d9bcc72d6a01b845f83e0f730ab91ff4f\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1786073311 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786073311 -0700\n\nFederate the labs remote into phr and store uploads in GCS (#49)\n\nPoints phr''s SPA at the labs service on Render and turns uploads on.\n\nVITE_LABS_REMOTE_URL and VITE_LABS_API_URL are Docker build args, so they\nbake into the bundle and a change needs a rebuild rather than a restart.\nThey are pinned to a variable instead of referencing render_web_service.labs\ndirectly: labs reads phr''s URL for PHR_BASE_URL and CORS, so referencing it\nback is a dependency cycle. This is the safer side to pin — a stale labs URL\nbreaks the uploads page, while a stale phr URL inside labs would fail every\ntoken verification and take that service down entirely.\n\nUploads go to object storage rather than a Render disk. Disks attach to a\nsingle service, so a PDF the web service wrote would be invisible to the\nworker that rasterises it. Both services address the same bucket, reusing\nthe GCP deployment''s for now — object names are UUIDs and each deployment\nonly references its own rows, so they do not collide. The credential behind\nit belongs to a service account holding object access to that one bucket\nand nothing else; Render cannot use workload identity, so it needs a\ndownloadable key, and the blast radius of one is what decides which account\nto hand out.\n\nThe sidebar item is gated on VITE_LABS_REMOTE_URL, so it enables itself\nwherever the remote is configured and stays \"Coming soon\" where it is not.\n\nVerified against production: registered an account on phr, exchanged the\ntoken at labs (identity auto-provisioned, issuer healthkey-phr), uploaded a\nPDF, and the worker read it back out of the bucket and extracted 3 results.\nThe object is in GCS at the exact byte size uploaded, and /labs/uploads\nrenders the remote with the completed report.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdVDfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAf00QAIGpPQuWlSuzGQo9DLaUUeRM\nIIbcsLJ6LjeRbMoCO3FgOgHo8WODqJA8fok5opll53Pxu6vDfNhjReC4JYgnAUdj\n5fkqedy62PtE1I6vKetg+r9PIx1L1tzml9ajK4vwEmXtaV/mtzS3D4BJtAch/F/d\nO+Rlc3siRNnfxe+LkZX6lxc/w1SOXqOo7cgo3J2QT2Nn/n13nXMyS0e4IMZZ9z31\nDdqydqQXcMMM2R0yZnUf4YZagUeNbX+MAeMoRVXTqY6ul0LwmxI67JWR9aBYrsly\nfT5vQkxMc16buw9aQey/O+BmeNuOhokGpmx3X7U3Bt2daa5D+4c7PoR8ewjzBsoK\niEou2Vw9k4/R+kbg3KQkw6zxL8wBjsLXnrg2qiHK9bA5/FmbdGHNLDuMZoHF/gFq\n+12Up+Fppzrjo7hZ24NelMz1nc61QEKOZ+N4e7wvCEEczkuvDuckNdSoi6wORyFG\nDTxcJ/n/7yHd229St9CoU96Ho3Fyjbhflndf9Gs3Bkrib+/6Vjk5YLsJrZ/6fHGp\nwO5wzmzr5wt2+usw6sLVI0aamqbQhb3RG5vDWPKy26Ny8s5Grfgwoj9u1VlfHCaE\n9QGZC0fvYSwuhIhy14rUCZ1Y5gR+AwGmVuuUyjiWkaK3d3DWnU8x2XNfK/+pk5Lo\n4gp/NQh7lAWmRaeJHufh\n=1lNU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-07T03:28:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/d83c77efba91a12d5938943946a82addf7fd0d63","node_id":"C_kwDOR4MqsdoAKGQ4M2M3N2VmYmE5MWExMmQ1OTM4OTQzOTQ2YTgyYWRkZjdmZDBkNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/e82c385d9bcc72d6a01b845f83e0f730ab91ff4f","sha":"e82c385d9bcc72d6a01b845f83e0f730ab91ff4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/e82c385d9bcc72d6a01b845f83e0f730ab91ff4f"}],"sha":"d83c77efba91a12d5938943946a82addf7fd0d63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/d83c77efba91a12d5938943946a82addf7fd0d63"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/e82c385d9bcc72d6a01b845f83e0f730ab91ff4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:00:57Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"Vladimir Tarasov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T03:00:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add the LABS Render project: labs web service, worker, database, broker (#48)\n\nLab report uploads and extraction, deployed as two services off the one\nimage already in the hk-labs repo. The web service answers the API and\nserves the federation remote at /static/remoteEntry.js; the worker runs\nextraction, which takes 30-120s against a vision model and cannot live\ninside a request.\n\nIts own Render project rather than phr''s environment: labs owns its\ndatabase and broker, and reaches phr only over the public API to verify\ntokens against JWKS, so there is nothing to share.\n\nUploads ship disabled. Render disks attach to a single service and cannot\nbe shared, so a PDF the web service writes locally is invisible to the\nworker that has to rasterise it — every upload would be accepted and then\nfail in extraction. LAB_UPLOAD_ENABLED flips to true once the object\nstorage bucket exists.\n\nThe broker uses noeviction: a queued extraction job is work we cannot\nreconstruct, so an enqueue should fail loudly rather than have Render\nsilently drop jobs to reclaim memory.\n\nApplied: 6 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed — phr''s resources untouched.\nBoth services are live, /api/v1/health/ returns database ok (so the\npre-deploy migration ran), the remote serves with\nAccess-Control-Allow-Origin, and the worker is consuming from the broker.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be85fb830ed658448d8bf54341b537d1414f83cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/be85fb830ed658448d8bf54341b537d1414f83cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/e82c385d9bcc72d6a01b845f83e0f730ab91ff4f","verification":{"payload":"tree be85fb830ed658448d8bf54341b537d1414f83cb\nparent 193a7d65176193ae7bda464ee6d915a03e6bbd7a\nauthor Vladimir Tarasov <vtrv101@gmail.com> 1786071657 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786071657 -0700\n\nAdd the LABS Render project: labs web service, worker, database, broker (#48)\n\nLab report uploads and extraction, deployed as two services off the one\nimage already in the hk-labs repo. The web service answers the API and\nserves the federation remote at /static/remoteEntry.js; the worker runs\nextraction, which takes 30-120s against a vision model and cannot live\ninside a request.\n\nIts own Render project rather than phr''s environment: labs owns its\ndatabase and broker, and reaches phr only over the public API to verify\ntokens against JWKS, so there is nothing to share.\n\nUploads ship disabled. Render disks attach to a single service and cannot\nbe shared, so a PDF the web service writes locally is invisible to the\nworker that has to rasterise it — every upload would be accepted and then\nfail in extraction. LAB_UPLOAD_ENABLED flips to true once the object\nstorage bucket exists.\n\nThe broker uses noeviction: a queued extraction job is work we cannot\nreconstruct, so an enqueue should fail loudly rather than have Render\nsilently drop jobs to reclaim memory.\n\nApplied: 6 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed — phr''s resources untouched.\nBoth services are live, /api/v1/health/ returns database ok (so the\npre-deploy migration ran), the remote serves with\nAccess-Control-Allow-Origin, and the worker is consuming from the broker.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdUppCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVOMQAENKhg90gJgJUwH1mbMQgMbD\n8eB8dot7nOjRu8sq2KPxyft95GE+X+RCWeHCFBa7mWEaDY/Zxu4XffRhdOz640FX\n3emdvZAfKXR0tlR9l8buRA6XssoALvDLtwbodU01nZs16/9uAft0Ktl3Ib/68nNK\nAe0nEg10aHdEwz+fn3k8EWQxDDdDmCtMQ4DsED4JtKSL+9PvnPcSl5ZPbezILvQ+\n9xde/DJl8aCNFAql8XhttRT5m25FYzbmpOizmMACHVhrerDRFFlHvYVFeM0yjKsq\nLuQXHWYwGOlS/aDb/5LQ2e9DERDve5RKUY6DjTnTl2dUadILWuz+P9Kf88E65uos\nCsTd//P2GRlVBMJu61AIlAJE/t