42656adda2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/3d9c460f7daba34959a5773a9e55b642656adda2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/371304fab944b6f7a546ec3e77829c342414b68a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-15T18:38:02Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-15T18:38:02Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"message":"labs: editor, trend chart polish, detail UX, sparkline rebuild\n\nBackend:\n- PATCH /api/v1/labs/results/{id}/ via LabResultUpdateSerializer.\n  test_type_id is immutable on update; value/unit/date/range are\n  re-normalised through the same helpers as create. Provenance\n  fields (source, match_method, confidence) are preserved.\n- Extracted _validate_value_fields + _apply_normalised_fields shared\n  between create and update so the two paths can''t drift.\n- 7 new API tests covering PATCH value, PATCH unit triggers\n  re-normalization, PATCH date only, PATCH report range, PATCH other\n  user''s result -> 404, PATCH incompatible unit -> 400, PATCH with\n  test_type_id silently ignored. 73 backend tests passing.\n\nLabTrendChart:\n- LineChart -> AreaChart with vertical gradient fill clipped by the\n  curve (not a rectangular ReferenceArea).\n- Reference range rendered as two horizontal dashed ReferenceLines in\n  muted-foreground (not green, which was blending into the blue fill);\n  numeric bounds moved to a legend caption above the chart with a\n  matching dashed swatch.\n- Data points: r=5 filled circles with background ring, activeDot r=7.\n- Tooltip: dashed cursor guide, full \"March 15, 2026\" date via\n  labelFormatter reading the raw ISO date from the payload, value+unit.\n- Plot area left-aligned via margin.left = -24 so the curve starts\n  flush with the card edge.\n\nLabValueCard:\n- Sparkline rebuilt: stretches to fill card width via\n  preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"; data points are HTML divs absolutely\n  positioned over the polyline SVG so CSS border-radius circles stay\n  perfectly round under non-uniform scaling (SVG <circle> would deform\n  into an ellipse). Pointer-gated hover tooltip.\n- Sparkline bumped to h-12 (48px) so the trend shape is more\n  pronounced.\n- Value + Normal range stacked on the left, sparkline spans both lines\n  vertically on the right, items-center aligned.\n- \"No range\" italic placeholder when the test has no reference range,\n  so all cards end up the same height regardless of the test.\n- StatusChip returns null for status=unknown to avoid duplicating the\n  \"No range\" label that the range line now owns.\n- New TrendBadge replaces the bare muted arrow: coloured pill with\n  signed delta and direction arrow. Colour tone is distance-to-range\n  (closer -> improving/green, farther -> worsening/amber, equal ->\n  stable/gray) -- not naive up/down, because \"up is good\" isn''t\n  universal across lab tests.\n- Header truncation fix for long test names.\n\nLabTrendDetail:\n- Edit button on every history row; opens the dialog in edit mode\n  pre-filled with that row.\n- Chart section hidden entirely for qualitative tests (HIV, HBsAg,\n  HCV Ab) since trends don''t apply to reactive/non-reactive values.\n\nLabManualEntryDialog:\n- Edit mode via new editingResult prop. Pre-fills from source_text /\n  source_unit (the verbatim original input) so editing a row entered\n  as \"125 g/L\" shows \"125 g/L\" again, not the normalised \"12.5 g/dL\".\n- useUpdateLabResult() hook invalidates the shared labs.results query\n  key so every surface that shows the value re-renders after save.\n- Merged hydration and preselect effects into a single atomic reset()\n  call to eliminate a two-render race that occasionally dropped the\n  pre-selection.\n- Test selector locked when opened from a detail page (disabled on\n  isEditing || Boolean(defaultTestAbbrev)) so clicking Add on\n  /dashboard/records/labs/hgb can''t accidentally file a row under a\n  different test.\n- Qualitative Select made controlled (value={watch(...)}); editing an\n  HBsAg/HIV/HCV row now shows the stored result pre-selected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e821baacfd09175f86bbb9603bd9bb7b109e486","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/0e821baacfd09175f86bbb9603bd9bb7b109e486"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/371304fab944b6f7a546ec3e77829c342414b68a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/371304fab944b6f7a546ec3e77829c342414b68a","node_id":"C_kwDOR4MqsdoAKDM3MTMwNGZhYjk0NGI2ZjdhNTQ2ZWMzZTc3ODI5YzM0MjQxNGI2OGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/c11bc57f11f74ff5a0ee8e142d8cbc78c03268e4","sha":"c11bc57f11f74ff5a0ee8e142d8cbc78c03268e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/c11bc57f11f74ff5a0ee8e142d8cbc78c03268e4"}],"sha":"371304fab944b6f7a546ec3e77829c342414b68a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/371304fab944b6f7a546ec3e77829c342414b68a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/c11bc57f11f74ff5a0ee8e142d8cbc78c03268e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-15T16:39:46Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-15T16:39:46Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"message":"labs: add trend detail route, lazy-load recharts, untrack tsbuildinfo\n\nNew /dashboard/records/labs/:abbreviation route renders a dedicated\nLabTrendDetail page with the full LabTrendChart, a chronological history\nlist with per-row delete, and a pre-filled \"Add measurement\" button.\nLabValueCard is now a Link wrapping the whole card, so tapping any value\non the Records tab navigates to its trend.\n\nThe detail route is code-split via React.lazy because it pulls in\nrecharts. Main bundle drops from 805 KB to 66 KB (gz 18 KB). Recharts\nloads on demand only when the patient opens a trend.\n\nAlso: frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo is now gitignored (TypeScript\nincremental build cache, regenerated on every `tsc -b`) and untracked\nvia `git rm --cached`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"10fef2c4739cc87afc0ea4a397b6fd39f11d8374","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/trees/10fef2c4739cc87afc0ea4a397b6fd39f11d8374"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/git/commits/c11bc57f11f74ff5a0ee8e142d8cbc78c03268e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/c11bc57f11f74ff5a0ee8e142d8cbc78c03268e4","node_id":"C_kwDOR4MqsdoAKGMxMWJjNTdmMTFmNzRmZjVhMGVlOGUxNDJkOGNiYzc4YzAzMjY4ZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/phr/commit/06ae5c721af5b0b306c06fd2e773b994307c43fa","sha":"06ae5c721af5b0b306c06fd2e773b994307c43fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/06ae5c721af5b0b306c06fd2e773b994307c43fa"}],"sha":"c11bc57f11f74ff5a0ee8e142d8cbc78c03268e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/c11bc57f11f74ff5a0ee8e142d8cbc78c03268e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25243?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vtrv101","id":25243,"login":"vtrv101","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vtrv101","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/phr/commits/06ae5c721af5b0b306c06fd2e773b994307c43fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-15T16:32:29Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-15T16:32:29Z","email":"vtrv101@gmail.com","name":"vtrv101"},"message":"Phase 2a labs: catalog, manual entry, alt units, per-unit ranges\n\nImplements the Phase 2a slice of docs/patient-app-lab-upload-design.md:\ncanonical test catalog, manual entry with unit normalisation, and the\nfrontend LabValueCard + LabTrendChart wired to real data. Extends it with\nregional alternative units (UK/EU/US), per-unit placeholders, and\npre-computed per-unit reference ranges served from the catalog so the UI\nstays free of unit-conversion math.\n\nBackend (new `apps.labs`):\n- LabCategory / LabTestType / LabResult models with MatchMethod +\n  ReferenceSource + ValueType enums. Cascade delete wired through User FK.\n- Canonical catalog fixture: 37 tests across 7 categories (CBC, renal,\n  liver, multiple myeloma, breast, cardiac & metabolic, infection screen),\n  each with LOINC code, aliases, default + alternative units, sample\n  values per unit, reference range, molecular weight where applicable.\n- unit_converter.py (pint-based): NFKD + explicit µ→u folding, custom\n  mIU/uIU unit definitions, molar↔mass bridge via molecular_weight, full\n  alias map for lab-report unit strings.\n- Serializers: catalog with computed reference_ranges_by_unit field,\n  manual entry serializer that validates unit convertibility and\n  normalises to default_unit on save (report range wins over catalog\n  default per eng review §CQ2).\n- Views: CatalogView + LabResultViewSet (list / create / retrieve /\n  destroy) with select_related for performance and own-results-only\n  isolation.\n- signals.py: post_delete stub logging audit pseudonymisation intent;\n  real audit app lands in a later phase.\n- Tests: 66 passing covering converter edge cases, regional alt units,\n  API happy + failure paths, cascade delete, fixture invariants\n  (sample_values + reference_ranges_by_unit cover every numeric alt).\n\nFrontend (new `components/labs/`, `features/labs/`, `types/labs.ts`):\n- types/labs.ts: full TypeScript mirror of the backend types.\n- features/labs/api.ts: useCatalog (24h cache), useLabResults,\n  useCreateLabResult, useDeleteLabResult React Query hooks.\n- components/ui/dialog.tsx: shadcn Dialog primitive.\n- LabValueCard: latest value with trend arrow, inline sparkline of last\n  6 points, status chip, DataSourceBadge.\n- LabTrendChart: Recharts line chart with shaded reference band,\n  status-coloured dots, single-point fallback, empty-state copy.\n- LabManualEntryDialog: grouped-by-category test selector, unit Select\n  populated from [default_unit, ...alternative_units] when alternatives\n  exist (read-only label otherwise), placeholder driven by\n  sample_values[unit] from the catalog, \"Normal range: X-Y unit\"\n  caption driven by reference_ranges_by_unit[unit] and tracking the\n  selected unit in real time.\n- Records tab: new Labs section with \"Add lab result\" CTA, grid of\n  LabValueCard per unique test the patient has entered, empty-state.\n\nMisc:\n- vite.config.ts: dns.setDefaultResultOrder(\"ipv4first\") so proxy\n  target \"localhost\" resolves IPv4 (Django dev server binds IPv4 only).\n- frontend index.html: inline dark-mode bootstrap runs before React to\n  avoid flash of light theme; respects prefers-color-scheme and an\n  optional hk_theme localStorage override.\n- lib/utils.ts: extendTailwindMerge registers the custom font-size and\n  healthkey-* color groups so Button text-white isn''t silently stripped\n  when colliding with text-body-lg in the size=\"lg\" variant.\n- Family history matrix: CSS-grid layout that fits iPhone SE (375px)\n  without horizontal scroll; \"Maternal grandparent\" abbreviated to\n  \"Maternal GP\" with full text in aria-label + title.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{