026-09-04T19:22:48Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"message":"feat: allow more than one approver, and re-notify a pending request\n\nOWNER_PHONE now takes a comma-separated list, so a second person can approve\nwithout a code change. Every number is normalised before comparison — 03xx,\n+92 3xx and 923xx are the same person, and only the last form ever appears in\na WhatsApp id, so a config written in the local form would otherwise never\nmatch. The linked account is always kept in the list: a typo in OWNER_PHONE\nmust not be able to mute the system entirely.\n\nApproval requests fan out to every listed number, and one unreachable approver\nno longer stops the others being told.\n\n/api/internal/hitl/notify re-sends a still-pending request. Adding an approver\ndoes not reach back into messages already sent, and the request is still\nvalid, so it needs a way to be shown to the new number without opening a\nsecond request for the same item — hence createHitlRequest now accepts an\nexisting ref and rewrites that row in place.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NpL7ozKxd1uMzVxtsJrDKA","tree":{"sha":"81de152681e094cfd361f3f2d7a5018bd4a87f10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/trees/81de152681e094cfd361f3f2d7a5018bd4a87f10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/commits/7aa24bd8c8e5e4fdc5440d2959b3bfa079f2f968","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/7aa24bd8c8e5e4fdc5440d2959b3bfa079f2f968","node_id":"C_kwDOR4Pv49oAKDdhYTI0YmQ4YzhlNWU0ZmRjNTQ0MGQyOTU5YjNiZmEwNzlmMmY5Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/00cea26a27593747dc782676f4bbd0adae680887","sha":"00cea26a27593747dc782676f4bbd0adae680887","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/00cea26a27593747dc782676f4bbd0adae680887"}],"sha":"7aa24bd8c8e5e4fdc5440d2959b3bfa079f2f968","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/7aa24bd8c8e5e4fdc5440d2959b3bfa079f2f968"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/00cea26a27593747dc782676f4bbd0adae680887/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:09:45Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T19:09:45Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"message":"fix: read owner commands from the self-chat, where they actually arrive\n\nThe linked WhatsApp account is the owner''s own number, so every approval we\nsend lands in their \"Message yourself\" chat — and a reply typed there is an\nOUTGOING message. whatsapp-web.js fires ''message'' only for messages received\nfrom someone else, so \"1 APPROVE\" never reached handleOwnerCommand and the\nrequest sat pending with no error anywhere to explain it.\n\n''message_create'' fires for those, gated on fromMe plus an isOwner check on the\nchat so the bot does not act on the owner''s messages in unrelated chats, and\non a short-lived record of what we ourselves sent so a reply template can\nnever start an echo loop.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NpL7ozKxd1uMzVxtsJrDKA","tree":{"sha":"5d316d64f133ec6680f2690f6fcbf796c7dfcfc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/trees/5d316d64f133ec6680f2690f6fcbf796c7dfcfc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/commits/00cea26a27593747dc782676f4bbd0adae680887","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/00cea26a27593747dc782676f4bbd0adae680887","node_id":"C_kwDOR4Pv49oAKDAwY2VhMjZhMjc1OTM3NDdkYzc4MjY3NmY0YmJkMGFkYWU2ODA4ODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/4215fa11c03f57ffb2f237846f3446e4d4a3d7d8","sha":"4215fa11c03f57ffb2f237846f3446e4d4a3d7d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/4215fa11c03f57ffb2f237846f3446e4d4a3d7d8"}],"sha":"00cea26a27593747dc782676f4bbd0adae680887","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/00cea26a27593747dc782676f4bbd0adae680887"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/4215fa11c03f57ffb2f237846f3446e4d4a3d7d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T18:59:11Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T18:59:11Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"message":"feat: approve a generated post from WhatsApp before it publishes\n\nScheduled posts publish unattended, which is what they are for. This adds the\nother path: /posts/generate-for-approval parks the system''s own drafts in\npending_approval and raises a HITL request, so nothing reaches a platform\nuntil a decision comes back.\n\nApproving a post is not a vault file move, so decide() branches on kind:\npost approvals publish each drafted row through publishPost() and record the\nreturned URL, rejections mark the rows so no later sweep picks them back up,\nand an edit is clamped per platform before it goes out — the owner''s text\nwould otherwise fail at the platform on hashtag count.\n\nforceImages on generateDailyPosts bypasses the image rotation without\nadvancing it, so an explicitly requested with-image batch does not knock the\nalternating pattern out of step.\n\nAlso accept `from` as well as `sender` on /internal/process-email: the Gmail\nwatcher posts one and replays post the other, and a blank sender silently\ndisables every domain-based triage rule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NpL7ozKxd1uMzVxtsJrDKA","tree":{"sha":"b06ff752df3947516650fc049b54843c52622958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/trees/b06ff752df3947516650fc049b54843c52622958"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/commits/4215fa11c03f57ffb2f237846f3446e4d4a3d7d8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/4215fa11c03f57ffb2f237846f3446e4d4a3d7d8","node_id":"C_kwDOR4Pv49oAKDQyMTVmYTExYzAzZjU3ZmZiMmYyMzc4NDZmMzQ0NmU0ZDRhM2Q3ZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/59f7c8adeb06620811b71f31bd3d606bfd6606ed","sha":"59f7c8adeb06620811b71f31bd3d606bfd6606ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/59f7c8adeb06620811b71f31bd3d606bfd6606ed"}],"sha":"4215fa11c03f57ffb2f237846f3446e4d4a3d7d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/4215fa11c03f57ffb2f237846f3446e4d4a3d7d8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/59f7c8adeb06620811b71f31bd3d606bfd6606ed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T18:06:25Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T18:06:25Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"message":"feat: triage inbound mail, approve from WhatsApp, fix posting rules\n\nThe pipeline drafted a job-application reply to an Instagram digest and to\nan empty WhatsApp message, while a real inbound lead (\"We ARe looking for\nFDE engineer\") produced a task file and then nothing. Both came from the\nsame place: the only sender filter was `noreply@` plus a few promo words,\nand the only WhatsApp escalation was gated on priority === ''high''.\n\nemailTriage.js gives every email exactly one verdict before anything is\nwritten — junk (DB row only), info (no reply, no ping), actionable (draft +\nowner approval). Deterministic rules decide first and the model is asked\nonly about what they leave open; a triage failure escalates rather than\ndrops, because a false ping costs one message and a false drop costs a lead.\n\nhitl.js puts the approval on WhatsApp: every actionable email goes to the\nowner with the draft and a short ref, and `<n> APPROVE|REJECT|EDIT <text>`\ncomes back. Approve/reject are vault file moves so the orchestrator stays\nthe only sender. taskCapture.js funnels todos from email, WhatsApp and the\nchatbot into one table, and completing a recurring todo rolls it forward\ninstead of closing it.\n\nAlso fixed, all downstream of the same neglect:\n- /api/internal/process-email had two bare returns, so the watcher waited\n  out its 60s timeout and re-submitted the same junk forever.\n- Scheduled posts were \"published\" by an authenticated HTTP call to a\n  vault-file route using a DB integer id — it could never have worked.\n  dueScheduler now calls publishPost() in-process.\n- Hashtags are clamped to the strictest target platform instead of failing\n  the publish with \"8/5 maximum\".\n- Images follow a fixed 2-on/1-off/1-on/2-off rotation so the feed does not\n  read as machine-generated; Gemini is the primary generator when a key is\n  present, with the existing chain as fallback.\n- The email detail view showed the raw nested markdown; it now leads with\n  what was asked, what was sent, and whether it actually went out.\n- The chatbot answered \"last post\" from drafts, and forced five hashtags\n  into every LinkedIn draft.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NpL7ozKxd1uMzVxtsJrDKA","tree":{"sha":"f7615aa019ed42f8ebf73b7da8b3679e93e8d90f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/trees/f7615aa019ed42f8ebf73b7da8b3679e93e8d90f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/commits/59f7c8adeb06620811b71f31bd3d606bfd6606ed","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/59f7c8adeb06620811b71f31bd3d606bfd6606ed","node_id":"C_kwDOR4Pv49oAKDU5ZjdjOGFkZWIwNjYyMDgxMWI3MWYzMWJkM2Q2MDZiZmQ2NjA2ZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/92d81d504d25dc75d130df5c8db53cd033f5f630","sha":"92d81d504d25dc75d130df5c8db53cd033f5f630","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/92d81d504d25dc75d130df5c8db53cd033f5f630"}],"sha":"59f7c8adeb06620811b71f31bd3d606bfd6606ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/59f7c8adeb06620811b71f31bd3d606bfd6606ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/92d81d504d25dc75d130df5c8db53cd033f5f630/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:59:20Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:59:20Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"message":"build: make vercel CLI deploys reproducible from the repo root\n\nThe project''s Root Directory is \"vault-control\", so running `vercel` from\ninside vault-control made Vercel apply that prefix twice and look for the\nbuild output in a stale nested stub directory — every CLI deploy died with\n\"No Output Directory named dist found\" even though vite built fine.\n\nDeploying from the repo root fixes the path, but then the CLI walks the whole\nmonorepo: it tripped over live WhatsApp session files changing mid-scan\n(ENOENT) and would have uploaded dozens of .env backups. .vercelignore\nwhitelists only what `vite build` needs.\n\nvercel.json also pinned installCommand, since a cache-restored build skipped\nthe install and `vite build` exited 127 with \"vite: command not found\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DcvhgfGegfetf7he5W7ZLL","tree":{"sha":"cdbe2674efb2104695b7e32c39acca1e5b2b8248","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/trees/cdbe2674efb2104695b7e32c39acca1e5b2b8248"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/commits/92d81d504d25dc75d130df5c8db53cd033f5f630","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/92d81d504d25dc75d130df5c8db53cd033f5f630","node_id":"C_kwDOR4Pv49oAKDkyZDgxZDUwNGQyNWRjNzVkMTMwZGY1YzhkYjUzY2QwMzNmNWY2MzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/8945bae283377373f4e47125adf36e70fbb22bd4","sha":"8945bae283377373f4e47125adf36e70fbb22bd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/8945bae283377373f4e47125adf36e70fbb22bd4"}],"sha":"92d81d504d25dc75d130df5c8db53cd033f5f630","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/92d81d504d25dc75d130df5c8db53cd033f5f630"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/8945bae283377373f4e47125adf36e70fbb22bd4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:47:28Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:47:28Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"message":"fix: make ENABLE_WHATSAPP env-driven instead of hardcoded true\n\nBoth the local box and the Oracle deployment ran vault-control with a\nhardcoded ENABLE_WHATSAPP=true, so two headless Chrome instances attached\nto the same LocalAuth session name. WhatsApp Web allows one active session,\nso they invalidated each other and both fell into a ''detached Frame'' watchdog\nreconnect loop. Reading the flag from the environment lets exactly one host\nown the session; the default stays ''true'' for a single-host setup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DcvhgfGegfetf7he5W7ZLL","tree":{"sha":"b1d3fac6dabe31e64466fea9330e4aad559f2fd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/trees/b1d3fac6dabe31e64466fea9330e4aad559f2fd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/commits/8945bae283377373f4e47125adf36e70fbb22bd4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/8945bae283377373f4e47125adf36e70fbb22bd4","node_id":"C_kwDOR4Pv49oAKDg5NDViYWUyODMzNzczNzNmNGU0NzEyNWFkZjM2ZTcwZmJiMjJiZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commit/1395bcbb82a8c3e0e55a78e87e4cbeeaa57b8b03","sha":"1395bcbb82a8c3e0e55a78e87e4cbeeaa57b8b03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/1395bcbb82a8c3e0e55a78e87e4cbeeaa57b8b03"}],"sha":"8945bae283377373f4e47125adf36e70fbb22bd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/8945bae283377373f4e47125adf36e70fbb22bd4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161300531?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Awais68","id":161300531,"login":"Awais68","node_id":"U_kgDOCZ1AMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Awais68","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/commits/1395bcbb82a8c3e0e55a78e87e4cbeeaa57b8b03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:41:16Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:41:16Z","email":"hamzajii768@gmail.com","name":"Awais68"},"message":"fix: cap hashtags to strictest platform, widen auth timeout\n\nOne unified caption is published verbatim to every selected platform, but\nthe core prompt asked for 5-7 hashtags while LinkedIn and Facebook both cap\nat 5. A 6-tag caption passed generation and then failed publish validation\nwith \"Too many hashtags (6/5 maximum)\".\n\npostGenerator.js:\n- effectiveHashtagWindow() derives the budget from the STRICTEST platform in\n  the set, not each platform''s own window.\n- clampHashtags() trims the excess deterministically after every regeneration\n  path, so an over-eager model can never block a publish.\n- The prompt now asks for the exact count instead of a range that overshoots.\n\nAuthContext.jsx:\n- Auth calls get a 60s timeout. The server alone allows 30s just to open a\n  Neon connection on a cold start, with bcrypt and the query on top, so at\n  the global 30s default the browser always gave up first and a cold-start\n  login could never succeed.\n- Transport-level failures now surface an actionable message instead of the\n  raw \"timeout of 30000ms exceeded\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DcvhgfGegfetf7he5W7ZLL","tree":{"sha":"a95e4c0b09305d04cc6d3f61026d8655d99f578a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/trees/a95e4c0b09305d04cc6d3f61026d8655d99f578a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Awais68/Digital_Employee/git/commits/1395bcbb82a8c3e0e55a78e87e4cbeeaa57b8b03","veri