.github.com/users/chrisfusion/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisfusion","id":271927933,"login":"chrisfusion","node_id":"U_kgDOEDVKfQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisfusion/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisfusion/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisfusion/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisfusion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisfusion/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisfusion","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisfusion/fusion-spectra/commits/5a11353c474dd46405bd8b2dc64344442387b2fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:22:43Z","email":"christianpeh966@gmail.com","name":"chrisfusion"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:22:43Z","email":"christianpeh966@gmail.com","name":"chrisfusion"},"message":"0.10.35: fix codeSource artifact naming and build-poll race in wizard provisioning\n\nDiscovered end-to-end testing the new Git -> Batch Job wizard against a real\nbuild/run: ensureJobTemplate sent the raw forge build name as codeSource''s\nartifactName instead of fusion-index''s actual \"app.\"-prefixed artifact name,\nand waitForBuild''s reliance on the GitWatcher CR''s transient\nstatus.lastBuildName field could miss a build that finished before the\nwizard''s first poll. Both affected the (already-shipped) Python wizard too,\njust never exercised this far end-to-end before. Verified fixed: a batch job\nnow provisions and its first run actually executes and completes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013GmurGiQgvD1BjSJeWdYWp","tree":{"sha":"468c90ed3ae8b953d6bc39fbf8c3b6d9d96c1bfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chrisfusion/fusion-spectra/git/trees/468c90ed3ae8b953d6bc39fbf8c3b6d9d96c1bfe"}