ctions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/0d53738c90518afd3ea651a995e69e46206bb99a","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKDBkNTM3MzhjOTA1MThhZmQzZWE2NTFhOTk1ZTY5ZTQ2MjA2YmI5OWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/c7c7b44f5cd1f78841d54e085e716a2993ffd05a","sha":"c7c7b44f5cd1f78841d54e085e716a2993ffd05a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c7c7b44f5cd1f78841d54e085e716a2993ffd05a"}],"sha":"0d53738c90518afd3ea651a995e69e46206bb99a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/0d53738c90518afd3ea651a995e69e46206bb99a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c7c7b44f5cd1f78841d54e085e716a2993ffd05a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T17:05:49Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T17:05:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(frontend-core, vue-core): remote-manifest × locally-registered-component pairing (#89)\n\n* feat(frontend-core, vue-core): remote-manifest × locally-registered-component pairing\n\nFormalizes \"backend data selects a locally-installed view\": a remote manifest\ncarries a string discriminator id, the component ships as code and registers\nthrough the normal module → slot path, and the host pairs the two by id at\nrender time.\n\nThe helpers are read-side projections of an already-resolved slot — pure\nfunctions, peers of mergeRemoteManifests/buildSlotsManifest, not a registration\npath — so they add no module type and no new ingress, and a Vue computed (or a\nReact useMemo) re-runs them on reactive change with no library-specific glue.\n\n- @modular-frontend/core: resolveComponentRegistry (get/getEntry/has/ids/\n  entries; throws on duplicate id, onDuplicate last-wins/first-wins to override)\n  and pairById (paired/missing/unref partition). Opaque component type C.\n- @modular-frontend/core: componentPairingPlugin — thin resolve-time\n  reference-integrity validator (peer of validateNoDuplicateIds); static refs\n  only, pairById.missing covers async remote manifests.\n- @modular-vue/core: re-exports the remote-manifest surface and the pairing\n  helpers so Vue consumers stop reaching into the neutral engine.\n  (@modular-react/core surfaces them automatically via export *.)\n- docs: new \"Pairing wire-safe manifests with code-shipped components\" section;\n  the two anti-pattern mentions are redrawn to distinguish conjuring a component\n  from a wire string (forbidden) from selecting among slot-registered code by a\n  data id (supported). Cross-linked from the Nuxt consumer-seam guide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014K55zUxHwzEJEeeCzr99pT\n\n* refactor(frontend-core, vue-core): address review findings on pairing helpers\n\n- resolveComponentRegistry: build ids/entries once at construction — stable\n  referential identity across reads (safe for memoized render paths) and no\n  exposure of the internal order array. Pinned by a new test.\n- pairById: single getEntry lookup per item instead of has + get with a\n  non-null assertion.\n- componentPairingPlugin: re-attribute a duplicate-component-id failure to the\n  plugin and its slot, so a resolve()-time error names the plugin the consumer\n  installed rather than a helper they never called.\n- vue-core: widen the @modular-frontend/core peer to ^0.1.0 || ^0.2.0 — the\n  minor release this PR triggers bumps the engine to 0.2.0, which the old\n  ^0.1.0 range would exclude (the version-bump automation never rewrites peer\n  ranges).\n- core: add a public-surface test for the re-exported remote-manifest and\n  pairing helpers (mirrors vue-core''s). Also puts @modular-react/core in the\n  publish set so its workspace dependency is rewritten against the new engine\n  version.\n- docs: make the componentPairingPlugin staticRefs example runnable instead of\n  a placeholder comment.\n- tests: merge the double toThrow into one assertion; assert plugin\n  attribution on the duplicate-id error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016qJVcnwSu7nPHN1siR1K7M\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f7e3aa43f163a8ddd2757eec40ecc5917b99519","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/4f7e3aa43f163a8ddd2757eec40ecc5917b99519"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/c7c7b44f5cd1f78841d54e085e716a2993ffd05a","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f7e3aa43f163a8ddd2757eec40ecc5917b99519\nparent 6185939532bc6b1f5b56d705a6770021b0ba1488\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784394349 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784394349 +0200\n\nfeat(frontend-core, vue-core): remote-manifest × locally-registered-component pairing (#89)\n\n* feat(frontend-core, vue-core): remote-manifest × locally-registered-component pairing\n\nFormalizes \"backend data selects a locally-installed view\": a remote manifest\ncarries a string discriminator id, the component ships as code and registers\nthrough the normal module → slot path, and the host pairs the two by id at\nrender time.\n\nThe helpers are read-side projections of an already-resolved slot — pure\nfunctions, peers of mergeRemoteManifests/buildSlotsManifest, not a registration\npath — so they add no module type and no new ingress, and a Vue computed (or a\nReact useMemo) re-runs them on reactive change with no library-specific glue.\n\n- @modular-frontend/core: resolveComponentRegistry (get/getEntry/has/ids/\n  entries; throws on duplicate id, onDuplicate last-wins/first-wins to override)\n  and pairById (paired/missing/unref partition). Opaque component type C.\n- @modular-frontend/core: componentPairingPlugin — thin resolve-time\n  reference-integrity validator (peer of validateNoDuplicateIds); static refs\n  only, pairById.missing covers async remote manifests.\n- @modular-vue/core: re-exports the remote-manifest surface and the pairing\n  helpers so Vue consumers stop reaching into the neutral engine.\n  (@modular-react/core surfaces them automatically via export *.)\n- docs: new \"Pairing wire-safe manifests with code-shipped components\" section;\n  the two anti-pattern mentions are redrawn to distinguish conjuring a component\n  from a wire string (forbidden) from selecting among slot-registered code by a\n  data id (supported). Cross-linked from the Nuxt consumer-seam guide.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014K55zUxHwzEJEeeCzr99pT\n\n* refactor(frontend-core, vue-core): address review findings on pairing helpers\n\n- resolveComponentRegistry: build ids/entries once at construction — stable\n  referential identity across reads (safe for memoized render paths) and no\n  exposure of the internal order array. Pinned by a new test.\n- pairById: single getEntry lookup per item instead of has + get with a\n  non-null assertion.\n- componentPairingPlugin: re-attribute a duplicate-component-id failure to the\n  plugin and its slot, so a resolve()-time error names the plugin the consumer\n  installed rather than a helper they never called.\n- vue-core: widen the @modular-frontend/core peer to ^0.1.0 || ^0.2.0 — the\n  minor release this PR triggers bumps the engine to 0.2.0, which the old\n  ^0.1.0 range would exclude (the version-bump automation never rewrites peer\n  ranges).\n- core: add a public-surface test for the re-exported remote-manifest and\n  pairing helpers (mirrors vue-core''s). Also puts @modular-react/core in the\n  publish set so its workspace dependency is rewritten against the new engine\n  version.\n- docs: make the componentPairingPlugin staticRefs example runnable instead of\n  a placeholder comment.\n- tests: merge the double toThrow into one assertion; assert plugin\n  attribution on the duplicate-id error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016qJVcnwSu7nPHN1siR1K7M\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqW7JtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAWQQABHxeC1MZOjHX1LRR7f/PNZy\nHhmmY5xYpUzq3ysPfVsgvo1U6qg30rFKbBZkHFMG/oNPvKQYKt0toiNWR/i9W3v0\nm489SF2fxPNZ/YodpHGNjVGWWwNeL3RKVVV/UKpANk2l6ztTTc+WsOw+or0+agu0\nae8nRehgDmaBylZoHIbununxNE+NF7fYoM4Klr6bmMwBqUEjng5b8oOJ3IwuNXOq\nV62jPyYpATwjQwuQuTqo/m3mIVbOmX+HT8kIi0fu/2nApfkRFtKuHP9+iXDruKfG\nRDyU5HpjwfUOegvrO/Xl0v4mbBJkdDp3mdbU/lhzDTc/55VgOJjCqEileG2rNbd/\n//uWe7TP/7Pwa8FrzHIgzOA7ydYuTjE321mWNGQ0WDwMzrxbnU2R0nsKNWb9s2Qa\nLT5caqe2orzUeHzHCcwYPiDj/r1v/ahQOppbqorXK4lYSPDwn1G68a3I7gOVbyv3\nu2oIKEvf/vqtSjlisdOY3D4uAq9OzmiXN6bmRZcHM6qSl27JAwyqMRJljSxsrrSt\nSuFjz9n1uZtgjzj4RuZfKUPv0kM7+SUrBcY4ugDvPFpxhEqYFX8H+Wvtz2deIMur\nGU9vhfIjZpG7+kiedzc+memub4MGGiNZEPCxqzLa5SAE9iuxNjMPyMFZIYLZFusx\nG/qhRHMgiZ/wjSMP1rOu\n=mDW6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-18T17:05:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/c7c7b44f5cd1f78841d54e08