:"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/ccebed4e9d91e688b2e768f1013f9729fd8a170e","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGNjZWJlZDRlOWQ5MWU2ODhiMmU3NjhmMTAxM2Y5NzI5ZmQ4YTE3MGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/4458c7bbf67090c37813da41c5e48867a8370b1c","sha":"4458c7bbf67090c37813da41c5e48867a8370b1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/4458c7bbf67090c37813da41c5e48867a8370b1c"}],"sha":"ccebed4e9d91e688b2e768f1013f9729fd8a170e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/ccebed4e9d91e688b2e768f1013f9729fd8a170e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/4458c7bbf67090c37813da41c5e48867a8370b1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T18:34:15Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T18:34:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @modular-vue/cli scaffolder (PR-50) (#82)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/cli scaffolder (PR-50)\n\nAdds `@modular-vue/cli` (binary `modular-vue`), the Vue 3 + vue-router\nscaffolder, as a preset over the shared `cli-core` engine — the Vue\ncounterpart of the React CLIs.\n\nThe preset supplies Vue SFC template bodies (shell layout components,\nmodule pages, a route-zone detail panel, Home), a core-`createStore`\n`storeFile`, `@modular-vue/journeys` journey definition + persistence\nbodies, the `createSharedComposables` app-shared contract with the\n`RouteMeta` augmentation, and the `vue` / `vue-router` / `vue-tsc`\npackage.json + tsconfig bodies. `init`, `create module`, `create store`,\n`create journey`, and `create catalog` all work; the generated shell\nowns the router via `createModularApp` with module routes grafted under\na named `root` layout route.\n\ncli-core is now framework-pluggable at the package.json/entry-file layer:\nthe preset gained a `scaffold` block carrying the entry/view extensions\n(`main.ts` + `.vue` vs `main.tsx` + `.tsx`) and optional overrides for\nthe neutral package.json / tsconfig / root vitest.config bodies.\n`init.ts`, `create-module.ts`, and `transform.ts` read the entry\nfilename and journeys binding name from the preset instead of\nhardcoding `main.tsx` / `@modular-react/journeys`. React presets set\nonly `entryMain` / `viewExt`, so cli-core still emits its React-family\ndefaults byte-identically — guarded by the existing react-router (16)\nand tanstack (11) snapshot tests, which stay green.\n\nVerified end-to-end in the workspace: a generated project typechecks\nclean across all five packages (`vue-tsc --noEmit`) and its module tests\npass through `renderModule`. The CLI''s own suite is 13 tests including a\nfull-tree snapshot.\n\nTwo framework-forced choices: module route paths are absolute\n(vue-router rejects relative top-level paths, and `renderModule` mounts\n`createRoutes()` output in isolation), and `AppZones` values are typed\n`UiComponent` (vue''s broader `Component` fails `useZones`''s `ZoneMapOf`\nconstraint). The shell-patterns doc is corrected accordingly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0185QobcTYoTHWKLhwA3T1fV\n\n* refactor(cli): decouple Vue shell journeys version, add catalog tests, sync docs\n\n- cli-core: add optional PresetPackages.journeysVersion so the shell''s direct\n  journeys dep can track the preset''s own family version instead of falling\n  back to the React RUNTIME_VERSIONS.journeys constant. React presets omit it\n  and stay byte-identical (snapshot tests unchanged).\n- vue-cli: pin the shell''s @modular-vue/journeys dep to the Vue family range\n  (MODULAR_VUE_VERSION) via the new preset field, keeping it in sync with the\n  generated journey packages from one source.\n- vue-cli: add standalone `create catalog` tests (wire into existing workspace\n  + reject when already configured).\n- README: mark @modular-vue/* at full parity (both follow-ups PR-43/PR-44 have\n  landed per the tracker).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018YU4kALmunKmR8YxLaqAz8\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: kibertoad <igor@checkbox.com>","tree":{"sha":"e5a3ab43d35143eee513b083713c7097efa0ef65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/e5a3ab43d35143eee513b083713c7097efa0ef65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/4458c7bbf67090c37813da41c5e48867a8370b1c","verification":{"payload":"tree e5a3ab43d35143eee513b083713c7097efa0ef65\nparent 1e05a99c961353dc0789d7acbc9bb2d54eff420f\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784313255 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784313255 +0200\n\nfeat(vue): add @modular-vue/cli scaffolder (PR-50) (#82)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/cli scaffolder (PR-50)\n\nAdds `@modular-vue/cli` (binary `modular-vue`), the Vue 3 + vue-router\nscaffolder, as a preset over the shared `cli-core` engine — the Vue\ncounterpart of the React CLIs.\n\nThe preset supplies Vue SFC template bodies (shell layout components,\nmodule pages, a route-zone detail panel, Home), a core-`createStore`\n`storeFile`, `@modular-vue/journeys` journey definition + persistence\nbodies, the `createSharedComposables` app-shared contract with the\n`RouteMeta` augmentation, and the `vue` / `vue-router` / `vue-tsc`\npackage.json + tsconfig bodies. `init`, `create module`, `create store`,\n`create journey`, and `create catalog` all work; the generated shell\nowns the router via `createModularApp` with module routes grafted under\na named `root` layout route.\n\ncli-core is now framework-pluggable at the package.json/entry-file layer:\nthe preset gained a `scaffold` block carrying the entry/view extensions\n(`main.ts` + `.vue` vs `main.tsx` + `.tsx`) and optional overrides for\nthe neutral package.json / tsconfig / root vitest.config bodies.\n`init.ts`, `create-module.ts`, and `transform.ts` read the entry\nfilename and journeys binding name from the preset instead of\nhardcoding `main.tsx` / `@modular-react/journeys`. React presets set\nonly `entryMain` / `viewExt`, so cli-core still emits its React-family\ndefaults byte-identically — guarded by the existing react-router (16)\nand tanstack (11) snapshot tests, which stay green.\n\nVerified end-to-end in the workspace: a generated project typechecks\nclean across all five packages (`vue-tsc --noEmit`) and its module tests\npass through `renderModule`. The CLI''s own suite is 13 tests including a\nfull-tree snapshot.\n\nTwo framework-forced choices: module route paths are absolute\n(vue-router rejects relative top-level paths, and `renderModule` mounts\n`createRoutes()` output in isolation), and `AppZones` values are typed\n`UiComponent` (vue''s broader `Component` fails `useZones`''s `ZoneMapOf`\nconstraint). The shell-patterns doc is corrected accordingly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0185QobcTYoTHWKLhwA3T1fV\n\n* refactor(cli): decouple Vue shell journeys version, add catalog tests, sync docs\n\n- cli-core: add optional PresetPackages.journeysVersion so the shell''s direct\n  journeys dep can track the preset''s own family version instead of falling\n  back to the React RUNTIME_VERSIONS.journeys constant. React presets omit it\n  and stay byte-identical (snapshot tests unchanged).\n- vue-cli: pin the shell''s @modular-vue/journeys dep to the Vue family range\n  (MODULAR_VUE_VERSION) via the new preset field, keeping it in sync with the\n  generated journey packages from one source.\n- vue-cli: add standalone `create catalog` tests (wire into existing workspace\n  + reject when already configured).\n- README: mark @modular-vue/* at full parity (both follow-ups PR-43/PR-44 have\n  landed per the tracker).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018YU4kALmunKmR8YxLaqAz8\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: kibertoad <igor@checkbox.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnWoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIRcQAIe5mr1qMuN/pdeL05CmsG1i\n1gtFhdIaUpq3r2K4hAgGFtA4quOBtqEP4fj/NfPm9T8UlRrEDpqc5G0w5k+QoeKS\nKmoc/6O8sSs6v+caGVXgnWjWJDQuW2Xe47jDCuJf6zZzga+tl246NZeVdaVNfTn0\njdaJik6jKeG6tPur/r5j7onBXtlTxjKEiYGtnI4xsMDoEQrv+tmKw8k1YJg3bqg0\nXFBxizJJ5EUk2sH+TaQgYGnvx9rmIUIPxIc2ZhSNJxfsvRUL5wEFJz9sjf+3UAGd\nc8kH5RWAmjVGBsyZrgHBJixSER1XNp8T1bpxEcz124IuaZTmw5q+/Rvw2fnOrYE9\n+beHKaYMrdw+3Ciww0ZnpyACpWk5nTNOrtgp/j64VcG9ArP1oOdIJfn7VNufIgoQ\n2i5cBKvZSAUULGly8BmhVtGl8KTpSvKKjsEhQt0IkkvKlZ0YbdEDDxA/zdoEsBV3\nx5v7UEi0r1DG6ML/T/9FQJtV+UMCRRbVhGmEGbxuf6UuxUZi8pHYsiPPAkf8DDeK\nmPr+Zz8aw2lSFnkFPcx8F2Pfo4i+NHnXv5YhwRCmn312kj1TZ6GPSHU/DG3A1fE+\nXJJh0AC4FTJvwg4dR2pTLW+/XGTnvvmk5NSPs9XrWx9FK9jRPJHP3TxsQc1VZj0n\nfqeb+c61XQSiKKWj0GCZ\n=SbqK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T18:34:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/4458c7bbf67090c37813da41c5e48867a8370b1c","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKDQ0NThjN2JiZjY3MDkwYzM3ODEzZGE0MWM1ZTQ4ODY3YTgzNzBiMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/1e05a99c961353dc0789d7acbc9bb2d54eff420f","sha":"1e05a99c961353dc0789d7acbc9bb2d54eff420f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/1e05a99c961353dc0789d7acbc9bb2d54eff420f"}],"sha":"4458c7bbf67090c37813da41c5e48867a8370b1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/4458c7bbf67090c37813da41c5e48867a8370b1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/1e05a99c961353dc0789d7acbc9bb2d54eff420f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T17:54:30Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T17:54:30Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore: bump versions [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"5e0ffb8fac859ff0910f4e77985a9188c7609058","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/5e0ffb8fac859ff0910f4e77985a9188c7609058"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/1e05a99c961353dc0789d7acbc9bb2d54eff420f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/1e05a99c961353dc0789d7acbc9bb2d54eff420f","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKDFlMDVhOTljOTYxMzUzZGMwNzg5ZDdhY2JjOWJiMmQ1NGVmZjQyMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/5f25aea61434a70aee88dc5c5436a45dd580f87a","sha":"5f25aea61434a70aee88dc5c5436a45dd580f87a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/5f25aea61434a70aee88dc5c5436a45dd580f87a"}],"sha":"1e05a99c961353dc0789d7acbc9bb2d54eff420f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/1e05a99c961353dc0789d7acbc9bb2d54eff420f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/5f25aea61434a70aee88dc5c5436a45dd580f87a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T17:53:09Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T17:53:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(journeys): add JourneyHost + useJourneySync on React and Vue (#74)\n\n* feat(journeys): add JourneyHost + useJourneySync on React and Vue\n\nImplements items 1 and 2 of docs/consumer-feedback-production-app.md — the\ntwo largest pieces of glue a production consumer wrote *around* the library:\na ~300-line bidirectional URL reconciler, and a host wrapper duplicated per\njourney. Both ship on React and Vue together so the Vue family doesn''t\ninherit a gap the PR-42 parity audit would have to file.\n\nThe reconciler is a state machine over { status, step, history, future } and\na path string, with no UI framework in it, so it lives in journeys-engine\nbehind a narrow JourneySyncPort seam (read/push/replace/optional go/subscribe)\nthat an app fills in for its router in ~6 lines. React and Vue share one\nimplementation and one 33-case test suite; each binding is a ~110-line\nlifetime wrapper, and nothing router-specific ships in either.\n\nIt is event-sourced rather than a diff. Comparing URL to runtime on every\nrender cannot work: \"the journey advanced\" and \"the user pressed Back\" both\npresent as the URL naming an earlier step than the runtime, and telling them\napart after the fact needs bookkeeping that races the render loop. Reacting\nto the runtime''s notification and the port''s notification as separate signals\nmeans the direction is known before anything is decided. Both directions are\nidempotent, so the sync''s own push re-enters, resolves to \"already there\",\nand stops — no echo-suppression latch.\n\nA URL cannot navigate a journey to an arbitrary step, and the API doesn''t\npretend otherwise. A step is derived from state and JourneyStep carries no\nidentity, so a location can only select frames the journey has already been\nto (rewindTo) or just rewound from (goForward); anything else reports through\nonUnresolved and navigates nothing.\n\nJourneyHost starts on mount and ends *and forgets* on unmount (the outlet\nalone only ends). It starts from an effect, not during render: runtime.start()\nmutates the runtime and may write to persistence, which a render React\ndiscards or replays would duplicate — the hand-rolled\nuseState(() => runtime.start(...)) leaks an instance per mount under\nStrictMode, and the new StrictMode test fails with two instances if the\nhost''s latch is removed.\n\nstepIndex ships; stepCount deliberately does not. A journey''s next step is\ncomputed by a transition handler from live state, so the total isn''t knowable\nfrom a running instance, and a hand-passed total is the duplicated flow\nencoding this API exists to remove. It lands with feedback item 4''s\nresolveStepSequence.\n\nTests: journeys-engine 378 (+33), @modular-react/journeys 93 (+21),\n@modular-vue/journeys 101 (+17).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(journeys): address review findings on JourneyHost + useJourneySync\n\nTwo real bugs and two doc corrections from the review of #74.\n\n**Vue: `:loading-fallback` from a template rendered nothing.** The host reads\n`loadingFallback` off attrs rather than declaring it as a prop, and Vue\ncamelizes kebab keys only for declared props — so a template''s\n`:loading-fallback` arrived as `attrs[\"loading-fallback\"]` and the\npre-instance frame silently rendered null, then started working once the\noutlet mounted (the outlet *declares* the prop, so Vue normalizes it there).\nRead both spellings. Every existing host test used `h(JourneyHost, {...})`\nwith camelCase keys, which is why nothing caught the casing a template\nactually emits; the new test uses the template spelling.\n\n**React: swapping the `runtime` prop wedged the host on loadingFallback.**\nThe effect declared a `runtime` dep, but the start is latched on a ref that\nis only cleared inside the deferred teardown — and that teardown early-returns\nwhen the new effect body has already set `mountedRef`. So a swap started\nnothing on the new runtime, ended nothing on the old, and left\n`useInstanceSnapshot` resolving an id the new runtime had never heard of.\nPin the runtime on first render instead, matching the Vue binding, which\nalready resolved once at setup and never had the bug. The trigger is rare\n(the runtime is normally created once at bootstrap), but the dep advertised\nsupport that was not there, and the failure was silent.\n\n`useJourneyHost` now returns the pinned `runtime` so `<JourneyHost>` can hand\nthe outlet the runtime the instance actually lives on rather than a later\nprop value.\n\nDocs: `useJourneySync`''s \"the port need not be memoized\" holds for read/push/\nreplace/go but not for `subscribe`, which is called once when the sync is\ncreated — noted on both bindings. `onBlocked` fires on \"the journey did not\nend up where the location asked\", which is usually but not always a refusal:\n`rewindTo` re-runs the destination''s `buildInput`, so a `stepToPath` folding\n`step.input` in — what the docs suggest for revisited entries — can rename the\nlanded step after a rewind that succeeded.\n\nBoth fixes are covered by tests verified to fail without them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(journeys): address CodeRabbit review on JourneyHost + useJourneySync\n\nEngine:\n- createJourneySync stop() now returns early when already stopped, so the\n  documented idempotency contract holds even for non-idempotent unsubscribes.\n- Strengthen the \"writes nothing after stop()\" and \"stop() is idempotent\"\n  tests to exercise a real reverse notification and a throw-on-second-call\n  unsubscribe stub.\n\nReact + Vue useJourneySync:\n- Pin stepToPath for the sync''s lifetime instead of reading it live; the engine\n  needs a stable step->path mapping to resolve already-stamped history frames.\n  onUnresolved/onBlocked stay live. Docstrings updated on both bindings.\n\nReact + Vue JourneyHost:\n- Track host ownership of each started instance so a stale host''s deferred\n  end+forget cannot destroy an instance a same-tick replacement host resumed\n  (persistence returns the same id for the same input). Add a handoff\n  regression test on each binding.\n- React: rerender the \"keeps the same instance\" test with a different handle to\n  actually exercise the pinned lifecycle inputs.\n- Vue: make the unmount test''s reverse-detachment assertion trigger a real\n  notification.\n\nDocs:\n- Use the generated triple-hyphen heading anchors in the journeys/vue-journeys\n  READMEs and the consumer-feedback doc.\n- Type step.input before reading itemId in the stepToPath example.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013uTxLUeYecdquRE26eaDL5\n\n* fix(journeys): track all concurrent host owners of a shared instance\n\nThe JourneyHost ownership guard used a single \"latest owner\" token per\ninstance id, so two hosts mounted on the same persisted instance (concurrently,\nor across a route swap) would clobber each other''s token — and the newer host\nunmounting first would end+forget the instance the older one is still showing.\n\nStore a Set of owner tokens per id instead: each mount adds its token, each\nunmount removes only its own, and the deferred end+forget runs only when the\nset is empty. Applied to both React and Vue, with a regression test on each\nthat mounts two hosts on one persisted instance and unmounts the newer first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013uTxLUeYecdquRE26eaDL5\n\n* fix(journeys): address review on JourneySync + JourneyHost teardown\n\nResolves the open review comments on PR #74.\n\nEngine (journey-sync):\n- Guard the async self-rewind `port.go(-n)` with a navigation-generation\n  counter, so a late router echo that lands after a newer runtime advance\n  is recognised as stale and re-asserts the URL instead of rewinding the\n  runtime back over the newer step.\n- On a refused rewind, walk the browser forward by the rejected distance\n  (`port.go(+n)`) when the port supports it, preserving the exact stack\n  and any skipped-over entries, instead of a truncating `push`; `push`\n  stays the fallback for a port without `go`.\n- Document that a sync tracks only the instance it is given and does not\n  follow child journeys (a child in flight reads as a blocked parent frame).\n\nLifecycle teardown (comment: onAbandon can return `{ next }`):\n- Add `end(id, reason, { force })`: `onAbandon`''s terminal result is\n  honoured, but a non-terminal `{ next }`/`{ invoke }` is coerced to an\n  abort so a teardown caller cannot leak a live, unrenderable instance.\n- React + Vue host and outlet unmount teardown now force, so an\n  `onAbandon` returning `{ next }` ends the instance instead of advancing\n  it, and `onAbandon` runs once per unmount rather than twice.\n\nReact binding:\n- Move the latest-value port/options refs out of render into a commit-phase\n  effect, so a discarded render cannot publish an uncommitted port or\n  callback to the live subscription.\n\nDocs (README, CHANGELOG, consumer-feedback):\n- React Router port example reads `window.location` rather than a lagging\n  `useLocation()` ref during `popstate`.\n- Align the \"stepToPath is captured once\" wording with the implementation.\n- Qualify the StrictMode `useState(() => start())` leak claim: deterministic\n  persistence converges both initializer calls; only non-idempotent\n  persistence leaks.\n\nAlso merges latest main (PR-40) and resolves the tracker conflict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GGBfHoHhnY8Yy71TbuwHos\n\n* docs(journeys): clarify end() force, remount key, and no-go fallbacks\n\nAddresses follow-up review on the JourneyHost/useJourneySync docs:\n- `end()` reference no longer reads as if every call force-terminates;\n  a plain `end()` applies a non-terminal `onAbandon` result and leaves\n  the instance active, only `{ force: true }` guarantees teardown.\n- Remount guidance uses a key encoding the full host identity\n  (journey + input/runtime), not just `journeyId`, which would not\n  remount when only the input or runtime changes.\n- Disambiguate the no-`go` fallbacks by navigation type: an in-app\n  rewind falls back to `replace`, a refused Back falls back to `push`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GGBfHoHhnY8Yy71TbuwHos\n\n* fix(journeys): preserve stack on superseded go; layout-phase ref writes\n\nAddress two review follow-ups on PR #74.\n\njourney-sync: when a stale self-rewind `go(-n)` echo is caught as\nsuperseded by a newer runtime advance, re-assert the URL by walking the\nbrowser cursor *forward* the rejected distance (when the port has `go`)\ninstead of calling `writeUrl`, which saw equal depth and `replace`d the\nframe the cursor landed on — silently dropping the entry Back returns to\n(`[a, b]` -> `[b, b]`). Stamp a fresh epoch so a newer advance can\nsupersede the correction in turn. Regression test now delivers the\ncorrective forward `go` and asserts `entries`, not only `read()`.\n\nuse-journey-sync: move the latest-value ref writes from a passive effect\nto a layout effect. A passive effect runs after paint, leaving a window\nin which a layout effect elsewhere in the same commit could drive the\nlive subscription while the refs still held the previous render''s\ncallbacks, firing a stale `onUnresolved`/`onBlocked`. The layout-phase\nwrite closes that window while keeping the discarded-render guarantee.\nAdded a same-commit layout-effect regression test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018JBjUdpCXuV7A5bcnFb7LY\n\n* fix(journeys): close two async-navigation races from PR-74 review\n\nAddresses the two open review threads on #74.\n\njourney-sync (thread #19): a runtime advance that landed *while the\ncorrective `go` was still in flight* re-truncated the stack. The epoch\nguard kept the runtime on the newer step, but the runtime subscriber ran\n`writeUrl` from a cursor a stale `go` had parked on an earlier frame, so\nthe push dropped the entry in between (`[a, b, c]` collapsed to `[a, c]`).\n\nNow the sync defers every runtime-driven write while a `go` is pending —\nthe cursor is unsettled, so a push/replace can only land wrong — and, when\nthe `go` settles as superseded, repairs the URL from the settled cursor:\nit walks forward when the current step''s entry still exists, or re-pushes\nthe tail (tracked via `browserTop`) when the runtime advanced to a step\nwhose entry was never written. The refused-Back forward walk now stamps a\nfresh epoch too, so an advance racing it is caught the same way. Adds a\nFIFO-deferred-port regression test for the advance-during-corrective-go\ninterleaving.\n\nuse-journey-sync (thread #20): publishing the latest port/callbacks in a\n`useLayoutEffect` closed the stale-callback window only for the hook''s own\ncomponent. React runs a child''s layout effects before its parent''s, so a\ndescendant navigating from its layout effect still saw the previous\nrender''s callbacks. Move the ref writes to `useInsertionEffect`, whose\ncallbacks flush tree-wide before any layout effect, so committed values\nare in place before anything downstream can navigate. Adds a\ndescendant-layout-effect regression test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011MZobwDmxuCYsZCMcgm5iG\n\n* fix(journeys): settle the pending-go guard only on its own echo\n\nAddresses the open review comment on PR-74: `readUrl` cleared\n`pendingGoEpoch` on the *next* notification, before confirming it was the\nin-flight `go`''s echo. A manual `sync()` or an unrelated port notification\nfiring while the self-rewind `go` was still in flight would retire the\nguard, leaving the real, later echo unguarded — processed as an ordinary\nlocation change it would rewind newer runtime state, the exact race the\nguard exists to stop.\n\nTrack the destination the `go` was aimed at (`pendingGoPath`) and consume\nthe guard only when the settled cursor reads that path. Any other\nnotification during the in-flight window is deferred, mirroring the runtime\nsubscriber. `writeUrl` also now defers while a `go` is pending, so a manual\n`sync()` cannot corrupt the stack by writing from a cursor that is\nmid-navigation.\n\nRegression test covers an unrelated notification arriving between a\nsuperseding runtime advance and the stale echo; it fails against the old\nguard (the runtime rewinds to `a` instead of staying on `b`).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6iHCFkm4QaVQ7jCBmUCQZ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"83b41b70c1484041663d48057064ac2d80feca05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/83b41b70c1484041663d48057064ac2d80feca05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/5f25aea61434a70aee88dc5c5436a45dd580f87a","verification":{"payload":"tree 83b41b70c1484041663d48057064ac2d80feca05\nparent c0b3e824f81d62211ddd12d5c4d240cd6c0942c0\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784310789 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784310789 +0200\n\nfeat(journeys): add JourneyHost + useJourneySync on React and Vue (#74)\n\n* feat(journeys): add JourneyHost + useJourneySync on React and Vue\n\nImplements items 1 and 2 of docs/consumer-feedback-production-app.md — the\ntwo largest pieces of glue a production consumer wrote *around* the library:\na ~300-line bidirectional URL reconciler, and a host wrapper duplicated per\njourney. Both ship on React and Vue together so the Vue family doesn''t\ninherit a gap the PR-42 parity audit would have to file.\n\nThe reconciler is a state machine over { status, step, history, future } and\na path string, with no UI framework in it, so it lives in journeys-engine\nbehind a narrow JourneySyncPort seam (read/push/replace/optional go/subscribe)\nthat an app fills in for its router in ~6 lines. React and Vue share one\nimplementation and one 33-case test suite; each binding is a ~110-line\nlifetime wrapper, and nothing router-specific ships in either.\n\nIt is event-sourced rather than a diff. Comparing URL to runtime on every\nrender cannot work: \"the journey advanced\" and \"the user pressed Back\" both\npresent as the URL naming an earlier step than the runtime, and telling them\napart after the fact needs bookkeeping that races the render loop. Reacting\nto the runtime''s notification and the port''s notification as separate signals\nmeans the direction is known before anything is decided. Both directions are\nidempotent, so the sync''s own push re-enters, resolves to \"already there\",\nand stops — no echo-suppression latch.\n\nA URL cannot navigate a journey to an arbitrary step, and the API doesn''t\npretend otherwise. A step is derived from state and JourneyStep carries no\nidentity, so a location can only select frames the journey has already been\nto (rewindTo) or just rewound from (goForward); anything else reports through\nonUnresolved and navigates nothing.\n\nJourneyHost starts on mount and ends *and forgets* on unmount (the outlet\nalone only ends). It starts from an effect, not during render: runtime.start()\nmutates the runtime and may write to persistence, which a render React\ndiscards or replays would duplicate — the hand-rolled\nuseState(() => runtime.start(...)) leaks an instance per mount under\nStrictMode, and the new StrictMode test fails with two instances if the\nhost''s latch is removed.\n\nstepIndex ships; stepCount deliberately does not. A journey''s next step is\ncomputed by a transition handler from live state, so the total isn''t knowable\nfrom a running instance, and a hand-passed total is the duplicated flow\nencoding this API exists to remove. It lands with feedback item 4''s\nresolveStepSequence.\n\nTests: journeys-engine 378 (+33), @modular-react/journeys 93 (+21),\n@modular-vue/journeys 101 (+17).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(journeys): address review findings on JourneyHost + useJourneySync\n\nTwo real bugs and two doc corrections from the review of #74.\n\n**Vue: `:loading-fallback` from a template rendered nothing.** The host reads\n`loadingFallback` off attrs rather than declaring it as a prop, and Vue\ncamelizes kebab keys only for declared props — so a template''s\n`:loading-fallback` arrived as `attrs[\"loading-fallback\"]` and the\npre-instance frame silently rendered null, then started working once the\noutlet mounted (the outlet *declares* the prop, so Vue normalizes it there).\nRead both spellings. Every existing host test used `h(JourneyHost, {...})`\nwith camelCase keys, which is why nothing caught the casing a template\nactually emits; the new test uses the template spelling.\n\n**React: swapping the `runtime` prop wedged the host on loadingFallback.**\nThe effect declared a `runtime` dep, but the start is latched on a ref that\nis only cleared inside the deferred teardown — and that teardown early-returns\nwhen the new effect body has already set `mountedRef`. So a swap started\nnothing on the new runtime, ended nothing on the old, and left\n`useInstanceSnapshot` resolving an id the new runtime had never heard of.\nPin the runtime on first render instead, matching the Vue binding, which\nalready resolved once at setup and never had the bug. The trigger is rare\n(the runtime is normally created once at bootstrap), but the dep advertised\nsupport that was not there, and the failure was silent.\n\n`useJourneyHost` now returns the pinned `runtime` so `<JourneyHost>` can hand\nthe outlet the runtime the instance actually lives on rather than a later\nprop value.\n\nDocs: `useJourneySync`''s \"the port need not be memoized\" holds for read/push/\nreplace/go but not for `subscribe`, which is called once when the sync is\ncreated — noted on both bindings. `onBlocked` fires on \"the journey did not\nend up where the location asked\", which is usually but not always a refusal:\n`rewindTo` re-runs the destination''s `buildInput`, so a `stepToPath` folding\n`step.input` in — what the docs suggest for revisited entries — can rename the\nlanded step after a rewind that succeeded.\n\nBoth fixes are covered by tests verified to fail without them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(journeys): address CodeRabbit review on JourneyHost + useJourneySync\n\nEngine:\n- createJourneySync stop() now returns early when already stopped, so the\n  documented idempotency contract holds even for non-idempotent unsubscribes.\n- Strengthen the \"writes nothing after stop()\" and \"stop() is idempotent\"\n  tests to exercise a real reverse notification and a throw-on-second-call\n  unsubscribe stub.\n\nReact + Vue useJourneySync:\n- Pin stepToPath for the sync''s lifetime instead of reading it live; the engine\n  needs a stable step->path mapping to resolve already-stamped history frames.\n  onUnresolved/onBlocked stay live. Docstrings updated on both bindings.\n\nReact + Vue JourneyHost:\n- Track host ownership of each started instance so a stale host''s deferred\n  end+forget cannot destroy an instance a same-tick replacement host resumed\n  (persistence returns the same id for the same input). Add a handoff\n  regression test on each binding.\n- React: rerender the \"keeps the same instance\" test with a different handle to\n  actually exercise the pinned lifecycle inputs.\n- Vue: make the unmount test''s reverse-detachment assertion trigger a real\n  notification.\n\nDocs:\n- Use the generated triple-hyphen heading anchors in the journeys/vue-journeys\n  READMEs and the consumer-feedback doc.\n- Type step.input before reading itemId in the stepToPath example.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013uTxLUeYecdquRE26eaDL5\n\n* fix(journeys): track all concurrent host owners of a shared instance\n\nThe JourneyHost ownership guard used a single \"latest owner\" token per\ninstance id, so two hosts mounted on the same persisted instance (concurrently,\nor across a route swap) would clobber each other''s token — and the newer host\nunmounting first would end+forget the instance the older one is still showing.\n\nStore a Set of owner tokens per id instead: each mount adds its token, each\nunmount removes only its own, and the deferred end+forget runs only when the\nset is empty. Applied to both React and Vue, with a regression test on each\nthat mounts two hosts on one persisted instance and unmounts the newer first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013uTxLUeYecdquRE26eaDL5\n\n* fix(journeys): address review on JourneySync + JourneyHost teardown\n\nResolves the open review comments on PR #74.\n\nEngine (journey-sync):\n- Guard the async self-rewind `port.go(-n)` with a navigation-generation\n  counter, so a late router echo that lands after a newer runtime advance\n  is recognised as stale and re-asserts the URL instead of rewinding the\n  runtime back over the newer step.\n- On a refused rewind, walk the browser forward by the rejected distance\n  (`port.go(+n)`) when the port supports it, preserving the exact stack\n  and any skipped-over entries, instead of a truncating `push`; `push`\n  stays the fallback for a port without `go`.\n- Document that a sync tracks only the instance it is given and does not\n  follow child journeys (a child in flight reads as a blocked parent frame).\n\nLifecycle teardown (comment: onAbandon can return `{ next }`):\n- Add `end(id, reason, { force })`: `onAbandon`''s terminal result is\n  honoured, but a non-terminal `{ next }`/`{ invoke }` is coerced to an\n  abort so a teardown caller cannot leak a live, unrenderable instance.\n- React + Vue host and outlet unmount teardown now force, so an\n  `onAbandon` returning `{ next }` ends the instance instead of advancing\n  it, and `onAbandon` runs once per unmount rather than twice.\n\nReact binding:\n- Move the latest-value port/options refs out of render into a commit-phase\n  effect, so a discarded render cannot publish an uncommitted port or\n  callback to the live subscription.\n\nDocs (README, CHANGELOG, consumer-feedback):\n- React Router port example reads `window.location` rather than a lagging\n  `useLocation()` ref during `popstate`.\n- Align the \"stepToPath is captured once\" wording with the implementation.\n- Qualify the StrictMode `useState(() => start())` leak claim: deterministic\n  persistence converges both initializer calls; only non-idempotent\n  persistence leaks.\n\nAlso merges latest main (PR-40) and resolves the tracker conflict.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GGBfHoHhnY8Yy71TbuwHos\n\n* docs(journeys): clarify end() force, remount key, and no-go fallbacks\n\nAddresses follow-up review on the JourneyHost/useJourneySync docs:\n- `end()` reference no longer reads as if every call force-terminates;\n  a plain `end()` applies a non-terminal `onAbandon` result and leaves\n  the instance active, only `{ force: true }` guarantees teardown.\n- Remount guidance uses a key encoding the full host identity\n  (journey + input/runtime), not just `journeyId`, which would not\n  remount when only the input or runtime changes.\n- Disambiguate the no-`go` fallbacks by navigation type: an in-app\n  rewind falls back to `replace`, a refused Back falls back to `push`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GGBfHoHhnY8Yy71TbuwHos\n\n* fix(journeys): preserve stack on superseded go; layout-phase ref writes\n\nAddress two review follow-ups on PR #74.\n\njourney-sync: when a stale self-rewind `go(-n)` echo is caught as\nsuperseded by a newer runtime advance, re-assert the URL by walking the\nbrowser cursor *forward* the rejected distance (when the port has `go`)\ninstead of calling `writeUrl`, which saw equal depth and `replace`d the\nframe the cursor landed on — silently dropping the entry Back returns to\n(`[a, b]` -> `[b, b]`). Stamp a fresh epoch so a newer advance can\nsupersede the correction in turn. Regression test now delivers the\ncorrective forward `go` and asserts `entries`, not only `read()`.\n\nuse-journey-sync: move the latest-value ref writes from a passive effect\nto a layout effect. A passive effect runs after paint, leaving a window\nin which a layout effect elsewhere in the same commit could drive the\nlive subscription while the refs still held the previous render''s\ncallbacks, firing a stale `onUnresolved`/`onBlocked`. The layout-phase\nwrite closes that window while keeping the discarded-render guarantee.\nAdded a same-commit layout-effect regression test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018JBjUdpCXuV7A5bcnFb7LY\n\n* fix(journeys): close two async-navigation races from PR-74 review\n\nAddresses the two open review threads on #74.\n\njourney-sync (thread #19): a runtime advance that landed *while the\ncorrective `go` was still in flight* re-truncated the stack. The epoch\nguard kept the runtime on the newer step, but the runtime subscriber ran\n`writeUrl` from a cursor a stale `go` had parked on an earlier frame, so\nthe push dropped the entry in between (`[a, b, c]` collapsed to `[a, c]`).\n\nNow the sync defers every runtime-driven write while a `go` is pending —\nthe cursor is unsettled, so a push/replace can only land wrong — and, when\nthe `go` settles as superseded, repairs the URL from the settled cursor:\nit walks forward when the current step''s entry still exists, or re-pushes\nthe tail (tracked via `browserTop`) when the runtime advanced to a step\nwhose entry was never written. The refused-Back forward walk now stamps a\nfresh epoch too, so an advance racing it is caught the same way. Adds a\nFIFO-deferred-port regression test for the advance-during-corrective-go\ninterleaving.\n\nuse-journey-sync (thread #20): publishing the latest port/callbacks in a\n`useLayoutEffect` closed the stale-callback window only for the hook''s own\ncomponent. React runs a child''s layout effects before its parent''s, so a\ndescendant navigating from its layout effect still saw the previous\nrender''s callbacks. Move the ref writes to `useInsertionEffect`, whose\ncallbacks flush tree-wide before any layout effect, so committed values\nare in place before anything downstream can navigate. Adds a\ndescendant-layout-effect regression test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011MZobwDmxuCYsZCMcgm5iG\n\n* fix(journeys): settle the pending-go guard only on its own echo\n\nAddresses the open review comment on PR-74: `readUrl` cleared\n`pendingGoEpoch` on the *next* notification, before confirming it was the\nin-flight `go`''s echo. A manual `sync()` or an unrelated port notification\nfiring while the self-rewind `go` was still in flight would retire the\nguard, leaving the real, later echo unguarded — processed as an ordinary\nlocation change it would rewind newer runtime state, the exact race the\nguard exists to stop.\n\nTrack the destination the `go` was aimed at (`pendingGoPath`) and consume\nthe guard only when the settled cursor reads that path. Any other\nnotification during the in-flight window is deferred, mirroring the runtime\nsubscriber. `writeUrl` also now defers while a `go` is pending, so a manual\n`sync()` cannot corrupt the stack by writing from a cursor that is\nmid-navigation.\n\nRegression test covers an unrelated notification arriving between a\nsuperseding runtime advance and the stale echo; it fails against the old\nguard (the runtime rewinds to `a` instead of staying on `b`).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6iHCFkm4QaVQ7jCBmUCQZ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWmwFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPrcQACngA6gPkqkl0+5iPdnm6Ha/\nw9sI/qmyFoUcIIdeLiFU4MGyaI388APB9Kzk6PTjgdqHOkxEtzRVHqxxP4H8rj+q\nsWbE0TXIZPuRO6FkSqAOxLzyDmJVk+JFRTanL+ke6dTdF0NzY8NIUk3ZIv20XsYK\ngDcuRfUzmtl6Hpy6em7eBBpNDrmVfHHWNZ05AK1TrzodSugYEjVwLRSqNUZIN4VS\n1TR+5wcoa0DBww6pdHCN6OPc6l84L0BzZdeA4CRLcLKB/b3YnV4Uay+If4P6VCYW\nzoRLMyah3lvJuC2BcKHqmnP6ZmoKNAEPLxaOE8JCDGG+k5Jj+aMNWwal3FP6AVUG\nsMSzAYwSmdIv08w3+cqvqLLvzytvRVQTQh6YP8bEuKmO0RvWBhCRyqkmZ28f/xuk\nQNAMg8tS/ogmC9BXIyi2TuuOrITtldznpqF3mzbO3v6cQ2Vry+kze13gtFiDETDK\nevOCCK8yjs1FP3IvZf17n9si+WyX2JK9bcJ061XEEcsmSxcck9awonPs+/0zvqt3\nNRmrbHqgu/n6hf/CR5YMs9xyDDCTRsTE1uvd3+0RPy8SEMtslKQCiu4hhUvfgIH+\nZUMEfaw26L991nKYgPRJWgDFOYUHmEsYmDpnIEmeYk+2itgD50BbZhHoqbCMtakO\nouzCK1o5mvQXvPHPD3CW\n=fcBb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T17:53:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/5f25aea61434a70aee88dc5c5436a45dd580f87a","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKDVmMjVhZWE2MTQzNGE3MGFlZTg4ZGM1YzU0MzZhNDVkZDU4MGY4N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/c0b3e824f81d62211ddd12d5c4d240cd6c0942c0","sha":"c0b3e824f81d62211ddd12d5c4d240cd6c0942c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c0b3e824f81d62211ddd12d5c4d240cd6c0942c0"}],"sha":"5f25aea61434a70aee88dc5c5436a45dd580f87a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/5f25aea61434a70aee88dc5c5436a45dd580f87a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c0b3e824f81d62211ddd12d5c4d240cd6c0942c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T17:13:02Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T17:13:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cli): make cli-core framework-pluggable — move framework bodies to presets (PR-04) (#81)\n\n* feat(cli): make cli-core framework-pluggable — move framework bodies to presets (PR-04)\n\nClose the remaining PR-04 gap in the Vue initiative: the framework-specific\nsource bodies still living in `cli-core/src/templates/*` now emit through the\npreset interface, so `cli-core` holds no JSX-emitting strings and a non-React\nfamily (PR-50''s `@modular-vue/cli`) can supply its own bodies.\n\n- Add preset template methods: shellViteConfig, shellIndexHtml, shellAuthStore,\n  shellConfigStore, shellHome, storeFile, journeyDefinition, journeyPersistence.\n- Drop the shellViteDedupe field (each preset''s shellViteConfig inlines its own\n  dedupe list — the only per-CLI difference in that body).\n- Add a packages.journeys coordinate so cli-core''s neutral journeyPackageJson\n  reads the journeys binding name from the preset.\n- Rehome the React bodies into react-router-cli and tanstack-router-cli\n  (templates/shell.ts + new templates/store.ts, templates/journey.ts); wire\n  create-store / create-journey through preset.templates.*.\n- Add a full generated-tree snapshot test to each CLI''s cli.test.ts.\n\nBoth React CLIs produce byte-identical scaffolds before/after (verified by\ndiffing generated trees and by the new snapshots). Full workspace typecheck\n(145 tasks) passes. Updates docs/vue-support-tracker.md (PR-04 → done).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YQDZwaYDCoTrBRoNRyCF8r\n\n* docs(cli-core): sync preset example with framework-pluggable interface\n\nThe README''s `CliPreset` example still documented the removed\n`shellViteDedupe` field and omitted the new preset template methods\n(`shellViteConfig`, `shellIndexHtml`, `shellAuthStore`,\n`shellConfigStore`, `shellHome`, `storeFile`, `journeyDefinition`,\n`journeyPersistence`) and the new `packages.journeys` coordinate — so\nfollowing it produced a `CliPreset` that fails to typecheck. Update the\nexample and the template-inventory bullet to match the shipped interface.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fi8FUFFVoeYETduddquwyU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"312b089f12c762efd51b59e9f4d764c7db2af615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/312b089f12c762efd51b59e9f4d764c7db2af615"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/c0b3e824f81d62211ddd12d5c4d240cd6c0942c0","verification":{"payload":"tree 312b089f12c762efd51b59e9f4d764c7db2af615\nparent c12e1b82468664705030e874aebfaf80e73df092\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784308382 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784308382 +0200\n\nfeat(cli): make cli-core framework-pluggable — move framework bodies to presets (PR-04) (#81)\n\n* feat(cli): make cli-core framework-pluggable — move framework bodies to presets (PR-04)\n\nClose the remaining PR-04 gap in the Vue initiative: the framework-specific\nsource bodies still living in `cli-core/src/templates/*` now emit through the\npreset interface, so `cli-core` holds no JSX-emitting strings and a non-React\nfamily (PR-50''s `@modular-vue/cli`) can supply its own bodies.\n\n- Add preset template methods: shellViteConfig, shellIndexHtml, shellAuthStore,\n  shellConfigStore, shellHome, storeFile, journeyDefinition, journeyPersistence.\n- Drop the shellViteDedupe field (each preset''s shellViteConfig inlines its own\n  dedupe list — the only per-CLI difference in that body).\n- Add a packages.journeys coordinate so cli-core''s neutral journeyPackageJson\n  reads the journeys binding name from the preset.\n- Rehome the React bodies into react-router-cli and tanstack-router-cli\n  (templates/shell.ts + new templates/store.ts, templates/journey.ts); wire\n  create-store / create-journey through preset.templates.*.\n- Add a full generated-tree snapshot test to each CLI''s cli.test.ts.\n\nBoth React CLIs produce byte-identical scaffolds before/after (verified by\ndiffing generated trees and by the new snapshots). Full workspace typecheck\n(145 tasks) passes. Updates docs/vue-support-tracker.md (PR-04 → done).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YQDZwaYDCoTrBRoNRyCF8r\n\n* docs(cli-core): sync preset example with framework-pluggable interface\n\nThe README''s `CliPreset` example still documented the removed\n`shellViteDedupe` field and omitted the new preset template methods\n(`shellViteConfig`, `shellIndexHtml`, `shellAuthStore`,\n`shellConfigStore`, `shellHome`, `storeFile`, `journeyDefinition`,\n`journeyPersistence`) and the new `packages.journeys` coordinate — so\nfollowing it produced a `CliPreset` that fails to typecheck. Update the\nexample and the template-inventory bullet to match the shipped interface.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fi8FUFFVoeYETduddquwyU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWmKeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEzUQAEuB4xeoRnITOUcjh