8664705030e874aebfaf80e73df092","sha":"c12e1b82468664705030e874aebfaf80e73df092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c12e1b82468664705030e874aebfaf80e73df092"}],"sha":"c0b3e824f81d62211ddd12d5c4d240cd6c0942c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c0b3e824f81d62211ddd12d5c4d240cd6c0942c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c12e1b82468664705030e874aebfaf80e73df092/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T16:24:28Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T16:24:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): catalog Vue support — harvest @modular-vue descriptors (PR-51) (#80)\n\n* feat(vue): catalog Vue support — harvest @modular-vue descriptors (PR-51)\n\nEnable the @modular-react/catalog harvester to load @modular-vue/*\ndescriptors and wire a Vue example into the demo catalog.\n\nThe harvester''s descriptor detection (detect.ts), resolver (resolve.ts),\nand transition-destination analyzer (ast-destinations.ts) are already\nframework-neutral — they key on descriptor/AST shape, not package names —\nso Vue modules and journeys were detected and cross-referenced without\nchange. The real gap was the SSR loader: Vue descriptors eagerly import\n`.vue` single-file components, and the loader ran with `plugins: []`, so\nVite had no transform for `.vue` and every Vue descriptor failed to load.\n\n- Add `plugins?: PluginOption[]` to CatalogConfig, threaded through\n  harvest -> createCatalogSsrServer -> buildSsrServerConfig (mirroring the\n  existing `resolve` passthrough). A Vue config passes `plugins: [vue()]`;\n  the plugin is inert for React/TSX files, so a mixed React + Vue scan\n  lists it unconditionally.\n- Add a `.vue`-importing module fixture plus harvest tests (loads with the\n  vue plugin, errors non-fatally without) and an ssr-server test asserting\n  plugin forwarding. Add @vitejs/plugin-vue + vue as catalog devDeps.\n- Demo catalog now spans two frameworks: examples/catalog scans the\n  @modular-vue integration-manager example (contentful/github/strapi)\n  alongside the tanstack roots — 9 modules + 3 journeys. Update the\n  Playwright e2e spec to match (12/12 passing).\n\nReact source: this mirrors no single file — the catalog is framework-neutral\nby construction; only the SSR-loader plugin seam is new.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G1VcikbjKnyNUTKQrUQbbp\n\n* refactor(catalog): make plugins config readonly + assert defensive copy\n\nAddress review findings on PR-51:\n- `CatalogConfig.plugins` is now `readonly PluginOption[]`, matching the\n  readonly convention used by every other field on the interface (and the\n  existing `resolve.dedupe: readonly string[]`). Signatures of\n  `buildSsrServerConfig` / `createCatalogSsrServer` widened to accept a\n  readonly array; the internal `[...plugins]` spread already produces the\n  mutable list Vite expects.\n- Lock in the defensive-copy behavior with a `not.toBe` assertion so the\n  forwarded plugin list can''t silently become an alias of the caller''s array.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TkbxMdkRRXfHKDnvD1UNWw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"723b4be78cc709a1ad084335d208ab8ceed1e445","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/723b4be78cc709a1ad084335d208ab8ceed1e445"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/c12e1b82468664705030e874aebfaf80e73df092","verification":{"payload":"tree 723b4be78cc709a1ad084335d208ab8ceed1e445\nparent 5cf209f4f66a1f936c18e071db22dfe42d4627c0\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784305468 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784305468 +0200\n\nfeat(vue): catalog Vue support — harvest @modular-vue descriptors (PR-51) (#80)\n\n* feat(vue): catalog Vue support — harvest @modular-vue descriptors (PR-51)\n\nEnable the @modular-react/catalog harvester to load @modular-vue/*\ndescriptors and wire a Vue example into the demo catalog.\n\nThe harvester''s descriptor detection (detect.ts), resolver (resolve.ts),\nand transition-destination analyzer (ast-destinations.ts) are already\nframework-neutral — they key on descriptor/AST shape, not package names —\nso Vue modules and journeys were detected and cross-referenced without\nchange. The real gap was the SSR loader: Vue descriptors eagerly import\n`.vue` single-file components, and the loader ran with `plugins: []`, so\nVite had no transform for `.vue` and every Vue descriptor failed to load.\n\n- Add `plugins?: PluginOption[]` to CatalogConfig, threaded through\n  harvest -> createCatalogSsrServer -> buildSsrServerConfig (mirroring the\n  existing `resolve` passthrough). A Vue config passes `plugins: [vue()]`;\n  the plugin is inert for React/TSX files, so a mixed React + Vue scan\n  lists it unconditionally.\n- Add a `.vue`-importing module fixture plus harvest tests (loads with the\n  vue plugin, errors non-fatally without) and an ssr-server test asserting\n  plugin forwarding. Add @vitejs/plugin-vue + vue as catalog devDeps.\n- Demo catalog now spans two frameworks: examples/catalog scans the\n  @modular-vue integration-manager example (contentful/github/strapi)\n  alongside the tanstack roots — 9 modules + 3 journeys. Update the\n  Playwright e2e spec to match (12/12 passing).\n\nReact source: this mirrors no single file — the catalog is framework-neutral\nby construction; only the SSR-loader plugin seam is new.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G1VcikbjKnyNUTKQrUQbbp\n\n* refactor(catalog): make plugins config readonly + assert defensive copy\n\nAddress review findings on PR-51:\n- `CatalogConfig.plugins` is now `readonly PluginOption[]`, matching the\n  readonly convention used by every other field on the interface (and the\n  existing `resolve.dedupe: readonly string[]`). Signatures of\n  `buildSsrServerConfig` / `createCatalogSsrServer` widened to accept a\n  readonly array; the internal `[...plugins]` spread already produces the\n  mutable list Vite expects.\n- Lock in the defensive-copy behavior with a `not.toBe` assertion so the\n  forwarded plugin list can''t silently become an alias of the caller''s array.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TkbxMdkRRXfHKDnvD1UNWw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWlc8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhTsQAK2mXsoMmYJwJonBL8RnWcsj\nWqcF0cyhbdVv5zF2W+C/Bcx3/uEcvRkktKl3MHjilb53I+bk9nE5CcxCegBSCw96\nq00aNwrJR+R09IL3V0YdOFtrVkI8xd3rnXbXaPadCJbH+xY40e48c6/cFkc/sAJn\nLgDMnt+/lUofPtXjNL9qpKRACXuWAt4JvLPS/Cwg2MciQxR6s3G0NPjYBCyXJZe6\n3Hv8cw2xZXfbVm3OtCbM4D3N5oNg