com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/46eb54d1de6c3e60a230853039fed67f6e39b814/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T14:59:57Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T14:59:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): close parity follow-ups — journey mount adapter + simulateJourney re-export (PR-35, PR-43) (#79)\n\n* feat(vue): close parity follow-ups — journey mount adapter + simulateJourney re-export (PR-35, PR-43)\n\nCloses the two parity-audit follow-up gaps, bringing the @modular-vue/*\nfamily to full parity with the React-router family.\n\nPR-35: @modular-vue/journeys createJourneyMountAdapter (journey-in-zone)\n- Add mount-adapter.ts, the Vue analog of @modular-react/journeys''\n  mount-adapter.ts, exported from the package index. Lets a composition\n  zone mount a journey via the generic RuntimeMountAdapter seam\n  (registerMountAdapter(\"journey\", createJourneyMountAdapter(runtime))) —\n  the one advanced cross-feature integration previously not wireable on Vue.\n- Deviation from React: the Vue adapter binds the captured runtime into a\n  thin Outlet wrapper rather than returning the bare JourneyOutlet and\n  relying on an ambient <JourneyProvider>, because the Vue CompositionOutlet\n  renders adapter.Outlet with only { instanceId, loadingFallback }. This\n  makes the adapter self-contained regardless of provider presence.\n- Tests (mount-adapter.test.ts, 4) exercise the adapter as the composition\n  outlet uses it: start() forwarding + live id, Outlet render/drive to\n  terminal with no provider, end() forwarding with the adapter-end reason.\n\nPR-43: @modular-vue/testing simulateJourney re-export\n- Add a @modular-vue/journeys/testing subpath (package exports + vite\n  multi-entry build) re-exporting createTestHarness/simulateJourney from\n  the framework-neutral engine, mirroring @modular-react/journeys/testing.\n- Re-export simulateJourney/JourneySimulator from @modular-vue/testing,\n  mirroring @react-router-modules/testing, so Vue test code has the same\n  single import surface.\n- Test (simulate-journey.test.ts, 2) drives a journey headlessly through\n  the re-exported surface to its terminal.\n\nUpdates docs/vue-support-tracker.md: status board (PR-35/PR-43 done),\nparity table, gaps section, and test inventory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LcACRoxki1ZCW7xC9vfEtk\n\n* fix(vue-testing): externalize @modular-vue/journeys/testing in vite build\n\nThe PR-43 re-export in `vue-testing/src/index.ts` imports `simulateJourney`\nfrom the `@modular-vue/journeys/testing` subpath, but the vite lib build only\nexternalized the bare `@modular-vue/journeys` id. Rollup string externals match\nexactly (a bare package id does not cover its subpaths), so the subpath — and\ntransitively the `@modular-frontend/journeys-engine/testing` chain — was being\ninlined into the published `@modular-vue/testing` dist instead of left as an\nexternal import.\n\nMirror the React counterpart (`react-router-testing/vite.config.ts`), which\nexternalizes both `@modular-react/journeys` and `@modular-react/journeys/testing`.\nThe dist now emits `import { simulateJourney } from \"@modular-vue/journeys/testing\"`\nwith no engine internals inlined.\n\nNot caught by the test suite because vitest resolves source, bypassing the lib\nbuild entirely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MDtUHgYGCsjCayrhBiQx7q\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9db79f86d1502b12d438cfecbbcb7e41af63f655","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/9db79f86d1502b12d438cfecbbcb7e41af63f655"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/46eb54d1de6c3e60a230853039fed67f6e39b814","verification":{"payload":"tree 9db79f86d1502b12d438cfecbbcb7e41af63f655\nparent faad4394682d31d7b14710e0e92ac5a03f37ec5a\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784300397 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784300397 +0200\n\nfeat(vue): close parity follow-ups — journey mount adapter + simulateJourney re-export (PR-35, PR-43) (#79)\n\n* feat(vue): close parity follow-ups — journey mount adapter + simulateJourney re-export (PR-35, PR-43)\n\nCloses the two parity-audit follow-up gaps, bringing the @modular-vue/*\nfamily to full parity with the React-router family.\n\nPR-35: @modular-vue/journeys createJourneyMountAdapter (journey-in-zone)\n- Add mount-adapter.ts, the Vue analog of @modular-react/journeys''\n  mount-adapter.ts, exported from the package index. Lets a composition\n  zone mount a journey via the generic RuntimeMountAdapter seam\n  (registerMountAdapter(\"journey\", createJourneyMountAdapter(runtime))) —\n  the one advanced cross-feature integration previously not wireable on Vue.\n- Deviation from React: the Vue adapter binds the captured runtime into a\n  thin Outlet wrapper rather than returning the bare JourneyOutlet and\n  relying on an ambient <JourneyProvider>, because the Vue CompositionOutlet\n  renders adapter.Outlet with only { instanceId, loadingFallback }. This\n  makes the adapter self-contained regardless of provider presence.\n- Tests (mount-adapter.test.ts, 4) exercise the adapter as the composition\n  outlet uses it: start() forwarding + live id, Outlet render/drive to\n  terminal with no provider, end() forwarding with the adapter-end reason.\n\nPR-43: @modular-vue/testing simulateJourney re-export\n- Add a @modular-vue/journeys/testing subpath (package exports + vite\n  multi-entry build) re-exporting createTestHarness/simulateJourney from\n  the framework-neutral engine, mirroring @modular-react/journeys/testing.\n- Re-export simulateJourney/JourneySimulator from @modular-vue/testing,\n  mirroring @react-router-modules/testing, so Vue test code has the same\n  single import surface.\n- Test (simulate-journey.test.ts, 2) drives a journey headlessly through\n  the re-exported surface to its terminal.\n\nUpdates docs/vue-support-tracker.md: status board (PR-35/PR-43 done),\nparity table, gaps section, and test inventory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LcACRoxki1ZCW7xC9vfEtk\n\n* fix(vue-testing): externalize @modular-vue/journeys/testing in vite build\n\nThe PR-43 re-export in `vue-testing/src/index.ts` imports `simulateJourney`\nfrom the `@modular-vue/journeys/testing` subpath, but the vite lib build only\nexternalized the bare `@modular-vue/journeys` id. Rollup string externals match\nexactly (a bare package id does not cover its subpaths), so the subpath — and\ntransitively the `@modular-frontend/journeys-engine/testing` chain — was being\ninlined into the published `@modular-vue/testing` dist instead of left as an\nexternal import.\n\nMirror the React counterpart (`react-router-testing/vite.config.ts`), which\nexternalizes both `@modular-react/journeys` and `@modular-react/journeys/testing`.\nThe dist now emits `import { simulateJourney } from \"@modular-vue/journeys/testing\"`\nwith no engine internals inlined.\n\nNot caught by the test suite because vitest resolves source, bypassing the lib\nbuild entirely.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MDtUHgYGCsjCayrhBiQx7q\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWkNtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUNkQAE/a9lbuTH8Hxa4EZEjlnVxT\nWhaMn8EzPd7KbKNkrUaUIsJ517nAjUmjmPg7XT0RgzKXBY86qUtURaRMnO3UHSoF\nCNG0LCOzEy8dsJ1UbLsBwb95fIcmHks50E8nNhr2WHCdDLd7xFYJqxDKw319awcg\nu3CdKvvz4JtaoKSiqtMujguyTaQ3tOJekleqxJTCPSiH1UrBtYcEA+Ese8TlOd/4\nffSRNs+imfAXrrqI1MLcEay4XruArTHcTDiQRKU1o8uc0+eH8yO1QOOuOiNFLnTc\ntQd/gy8aCXKfxIpwCRy6pEC24KvGYjs9S6kOXkMgv4XhDGbDmz49W34AMNRvs/QH\nUiSNndRa75WoRcBZ7QTsp+ioEZVpY7lvyDbqpdtLTI58eFkEQTa/wEa0oa3ytBZ3\n5DJqujOokitn5m7exTr/kGJZ10TQ0zRQwuFn82eb8LSXIiILdaSb6T1z11XdDWql\nq9QxtbjXDzZO+EeE2DFJNXxhXiLAWpS+8En72ukWprZdmwz0NkEd51g6wGr6aE+V\nYc23ZbUgmzmNRu4El/u1NS5XTrjm89IuPYSxqVuHW6O3XbFzvPcivECmSe+GyU9Z\nVTqTQlpmAFvHpyy/RxfwyUJf7G8TfnfL32GEXt8JTVmb27dly3KHIzWFqVdUlLL3\n9o8zqu9jvckATHDuKd1I\n=yrk+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T14:59:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/46eb54d1de6c3e60a230853039fed67f6e39b814","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKDQ2ZWI1NGQxZGU2YzNlNjBhMjMwODUzMDM5ZmVkNjdmNmUzOWI4MTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/faad4394682d31d7b14710e0e92ac5a03f37ec5a","sha":"faad4394682d31d7b14710e0e92ac5a03f37ec5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/faad4394682d31d7b14710e0e92ac5a03f37ec5a"}],"sha":"46eb54d1de6c3e60a230853039fed67f6e39b814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/46eb54d1de6c3e60a230853039fed67f6e39b814"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/faad4394682d31d7b14710e0e92ac5a03f37ec5a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T14:04:54Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T14:04:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(vue): Vue Router docs + parity audit, promote @modular-vue/* to 1.0 (PR-41, PR-42) (#77)\n\n* docs(vue): getting-started + shell-patterns + parity audit, promote @modular-vue/* to 1.0 (PR-41, PR-42)\n\nCompletes Phase 4 of the Vue support initiative.\n\nPR-41 (docs):\n- Add docs/getting-started-vue-router.md — a manual-setup walkthrough (the\n  @modular-vue/cli scaffolder is PR-50, still todo): contract -> module -> shell\n  -> second module -> zones via meta -> store -> beforeEach auth.\n- Add docs/shell-patterns-vue-router.md — router-owning vs framework mode, module\n  route shape, zones/route-data via meta, the RouteMeta augmentation, useRouteData,\n  and the authGuard -> router.beforeEach boundary.\n- Add a \"Reading navigation in a Vue shell\" section + Vue links to docs/navigation.md.\n- Add \"Using this with Vue\" sections to the journeys and compositions READMEs.\n- README: soften the tagline per D1 (React Router / TanStack / Vue Router + a\n  \"name is historical\" note), add a Vue quickstart entry, guide rows, a compact\n  Vue defineModule + shell snippet, the examples/vue/* entries, and package tables\n  for the Vue Router integration and the framework-neutral @modular-frontend/* engine.\nAll doc code is grounded in the shipped examples/vue/* apps and the real exports.\n\nPR-42 (parity audit):\n- Append a parity audit to docs/vue-support-tracker.md comparing every @modular-vue/*\n  package against its React-router counterpart (export surface + test inventory:\n  380 Vue binding tests vs 335 React). Functional parity holds; two gaps filed as\n  follow-ups (PR-35: no Vue createJourneyMountAdapter; PR-43: simulateJourney not\n  re-exported by a Vue package).\n- Promote all six @modular-vue/* packages 0.1.0 -> 1.0.0 and bump inter-package\n  peer ranges to ^1.0.0.\n- Add a \"state your Vue impact\" working-agreement + a repo PR template enforcing it.\n\nFull lint gate (typecheck + oxfmt + oxlint) and all @modular-vue/* test suites pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WJKNSeReyNfJNs8WcRSrPB\n\n* docs(vue): address review findings on PR-41/PR-42 docs\n\n- getting-started: drop the claim that Pinia interop is already documented\n  in Shell Patterns (it isn''t yet — D3 follow-up); state the Store<T>\n  contract inline instead of pointing at a nonexistent interop note\n- README: correct the @modular-frontend/* version blurb (core/testing/\n  compositions-engine are 0.1.x, only journeys-engine carries its 1.x\n  source version) and link the engine peer-range policy\n- tracker: document the engine peer-range policy under Versioning and\n  release; record outcomes for decisions D1, D3 (partial), and D5\n- PR template: use an absolute URL for the tracker link — relative links\n  don''t resolve in rendered PR descriptions\n- navigation.md: add the missing useI18n import so the Vue sidebar\n  snippet compiles; qualify the README parity claim with its two tracked\n  follow-ups and name createSharedComposables in the package table\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GpH8sitUkcG4ZV7XMCNLEh\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3c259628d664a0a5d3e353039e02ec8a9b819609","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/3c259628d664a0a5d3e353039e02ec8a9b819609"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/faad4394682d31d7b14710e0e92ac5a03f37ec5a","verification":{"payload":"tree 3c259628d664a0a5d3e353039e02ec8a9b819609\nparent f5adbc5aac5f3b9c0a290e05e744c5ea412902c7\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784297094 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784297094 +0200\n\ndocs(vue): Vue Router docs + parity audit, promote @modular-vue/* to 1.0 (PR-41, PR-42) (#77)\n\n* docs(vue): getting-started + shell-patterns + parity audit, promote @modular-vue/* to 1.0 (PR-41, PR-42)\n\nCompletes Phase 4 of the Vue support initiative.\n\nPR-41 (docs):\n- Add docs/getting-started-vue-router.md — a manual-setup walkthrough (the\n  @modular-vue/cli scaffolder is PR-50, still todo): contract -> module -> shell\n  -> second module -> zones via meta -> store -> beforeEach auth.\n- Add docs/shell-patterns-vue-router.md — router-owning vs framework mode, module\n  route shape, zones/route-data via meta, the RouteMeta augmentation, useRouteData,\n  and the authGuard -> router.beforeEach boundary.\n- Add a \"Reading navigation in a Vue shell\" section + Vue links to docs/navigation.md.\n- Add \"Using this with Vue\" sections to the journeys and compositions READMEs.\n- README: soften the tagline per D1 (React Router / TanStack / Vue Router + a\n  \"name is historical\" note), add a Vue quickstart entry, guide rows, a compact\n  Vue defineModule + shell snippet, the examples/vue/* entries, and package tables\n  for the Vue Router integration and the framework-neutral @modular-frontend/* engine.\nAll doc code is grounded in the shipped examples/vue/* apps and the real exports.\n\nPR-42 (parity audit):\n- Append a parity audit to docs/vue-support-tracker.md comparing every @modular-vue/*\n  package against its React-router counterpart (export surface + test inventory:\n  380 Vue binding tests vs 335 React). Functional parity holds; two gaps filed as\n  follow-ups (PR-35: no Vue createJourneyMountAdapter; PR-43: simulateJourney not\n  re-exported by a Vue package).\n- Promote all six @modular-vue/* packages 0.1.0 -> 1.0.0 and bump inter-package\n  peer ranges to ^1.0.0.\n- Add a \"state your Vue impact\" working-agreement + a repo PR template enforcing it.\n\nFull lint gate (typecheck + oxfmt + oxlint) and all @modular-vue/* test suites pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WJKNSeReyNfJNs8WcRSrPB\n\n* docs(vue): address review findings on PR-41/PR-42 docs\n\n- getting-started: drop the claim that Pinia interop is already documented\n  in Shell Patterns (it isn''t yet — D3 follow-up); state the Store<T>\n  contract inline instead of pointing at a nonexistent interop note\n- README: correct the @modular-frontend/* version blurb (core/testing/\n  compositions-engine are 0.1.x, only journeys-engine carries its 1.x\n  source version) and link the engine peer-range policy\n- tracker: document the engine peer-range policy under Versioning and\n  release; record outcomes for decisions D1, D3 (partial), and D5\n- PR template: use an absolute URL for the tracker link — relative links\n  don''t resolve in rendered PR descriptions\n- navigation.md: add the missing useI18n import so the Vue sidebar\n  snippet compiles; qualify the README parity claim with its two tracked\n  follow-ups and name createSharedComposables in the package table\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GpH8sitUkcG4ZV7XMCNLEh\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWjaGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA67IQAA9cmMc+mBrbWSd4NnKzKZTw\nEK4QwvTyyMRWWsq2SjgZereNXiujfOPknbDS3wHOKXDC+n+jtXYUH8CN36pkbZty\nZJVXxuva0cqziT59+NZQd8jgc6Uuib6UNMER/TNkZK4vSzESoCpw3dU94AXXgogt\ne8rQTB3gy4yCkfwzFx7dL5Rnr44mjbehhyCieR1aK33gUtvkCTF3UIzaXGSGlKcb\njFcuRZuWkT2icVjcukXB63qgPDVe6EIRPXE1pezxJo+UQqJJMBPaFM9zXi0NPvQW\nHc0SxoXK1EVUXXlJK9Qnk/dUGSCYq1Xq4ObptzqFgiScSmZWxs5kjwkCE1N1+cF5\nbBmaRCNPSwDkK1dHaud7ZZyJdO29CTSb9lKtO04z2Jws/PRwe/PAC7Bt1S6VS3Dk\n8oviN3hLN2VWPiaTP6dPGXsXtip0bLm0V0erKe++02hOgJHQtFK/ey+22pUTlGUO\nW6XJpYMp5rAAbN/sNkWjk+7+3xZoyTWMrCDcVXhBFuuT08Ra7wK/acgKpRp3V/Kg\n+SK8fZwd4R5YR4cAVaeLrau0uD4nWRi4pFtm8AAv3GR7EV2RDo0Z1L2YTplCNser\n/BDLiYBfsfQWUJ0WGfe9IZnJHihyyp+M1pZgf9Rn8H1UOWXtTQAnLOGUR+/lINVe\n/VtfRLJKeDwibGmM0o4d\n=pMz+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T14:04:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/faad4394682d31d7b14710e0e92ac5a03f37ec5a","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGZhYWQ0Mzk0NjgyZDMxZDdiMTQ3MTBlMGU5MmFjNWEwM2YzN2VjNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/f5adbc5aac5f3b9c0a290e05e744c5ea412902c7","sha":"f5adbc5aac5f3b9c0a290e05e744c5ea412902c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/f5adbc5aac5f3b9c0a290e05e744c5ea412902c7"}],"sha":"faad4394682d31d7b14710e0e92ac5a03f37ec5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/faad4394682d31d7b14710e0e92ac5a03f37ec5a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/f5adbc5aac5f3b9c0a290e05e744c5ea412902c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T06:25:32Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T06:25:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add examples/vue-router example apps (PR-40) (#76)\n\n* feat(vue): add examples/vue-router example apps (PR-40)\n\nPhase 4 of the Vue support initiative: three self-contained example\nworkspaces under examples/vue-router/, mirroring the react-router /\ntanstack-router families and authored with SFCs (decision D4).\n\n- integration-manager: sibling modules sharing a screen. Route modules\n  render a shared IntegrationManager.vue; the shell grafts module routes\n  onto its own router via createModularApp({ router, parentRouteName })\n  and reads the active integration through useRouteData off vue-router\n  `meta` (typed via a RouteMeta augmentation in app-shared).\n- customer-onboarding-journey: the profile -> plan -> billing journey via\n  @modular-vue/journeys. Journey steps are module-entry SFCs, one lazy\n  step, workspace-tab persistence via a reactive store +\n  createWebStoragePersistence, and tab rehydration with UnknownJourneyError\n  discrimination. Wired through resolveManifest() so the plugin''s\n  <JourneyProvider> is threaded into Providers.\n- editor-composition: the editor screen via @modular-vue/compositions.\n  CompositionOutlet''s render-prop becomes a scoped slot; the cross-team\n  WritableStore projection is read via a small useReactiveStore bridge,\n  the inspector uses in-team useCompositionState.\n\nEnabling changes (framework-forced, outside the example dirs):\n\n- Neutral entry validator accepts object components. @modular-frontend/core\n  validateModuleEntryExit required `component` to be a function\n  (React-centric); Vue SFCs compile to objects, so SFC journey/composition\n  entry modules failed resolveManifest() validation. Relaxed to accept a\n  function or a non-null object (also covers React memo/forwardRef) and\n  made the message framework-neutral.\n- SFC tooling: @vitejs/plugin-vue + vue-tsc as example devDeps; packages\n  with/importing .vue typecheck via vue-tsc.\n- CI: registered the three e2e shells in the examples-e2e matrix and\n  extended the changed-files trigger to the vue/engine/frontend-core paths.\n\nEach example ships a headless Playwright smoke suite; docs/vue-support-tracker.md\nand examples/README.md updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012URkDFnEFfNf5EJdkhGE9q\n\n* refactor(vue): rename vue-router examples/packages to vue; address review\n\nNaming: drop the redundant \"-router\" qualifier from the Vue family (Vue\nhas a single router). Package names were already @modular-vue/*, so only\ndirectory paths change:\n- packages/vue-router-core   -> packages/vue-core\n- packages/vue-router-runtime -> packages/vue-runtime\n- examples/vue-router        -> examples/vue\nUpdated the CI matrix example/runtime/core paths, the path->name map,\nrepository.directory fields, and doc/README references.\n\nReview findings:\n- Prefer direct imports over binding re-exports: onboarding app-shared now\n  imports createSharedComposables straight from its source @modular-vue/vue\n  instead of the @modular-vue/core re-export.\n- Simplify billing lazy entry — drop the redundant\n  `.then((m) => ({ default: m.default }))` re-wrap (the SFC already\n  default-exports).\n- Harden the neutral entry validator to reject arrays as component values;\n  add positive (object component) and negative (array) test coverage.\n\nDependencies:\n- Bump vue to ^3.5.40 across the workspace (also resolves prior drift\n  between ^3.5.0 and ^3.5.13).\n- Regenerate pnpm-lock.yaml.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RAKtBrD6TXjoajCPhWLZB4\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a8baa4a4190b0b479f9bd774ec512c0f056b701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/2a8baa4a4190b0b479f9bd774ec512c0f056b701"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/f5adbc5aac5f3b9c0a290e05e744c5ea412902c7","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a8baa4a4190b0b479f9bd774ec512c0f056b701\nparent c85da63b2712163d412caddbc31204c25d6bb7d0\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784269532 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784269532 +0200\n\nfeat(vue): add examples/vue-router example apps (PR-40) (#76)\n\n* feat(vue): add examples/vue-router example apps (PR-40)\n\nPhase 4 of the Vue support initiative: three self-contained example\nworkspaces under examples/vue-router/, mirroring the react-router /\ntanstack-router families and authored with SFCs (decision D4).\n\n- integration-manager: sibling modules sharing a screen. Route modules\n  render a shared IntegrationManager.vue; the shell grafts module routes\n  onto its own router via createModularApp({ router, parentRouteName })\n  and reads the active integration through useRouteData off vue-router\n  `meta` (typed via a RouteMeta augmentation in app-shared).\n- customer-onboarding-journey: the profile -> plan -> billing journey via\n  @modular-vue/journeys. Journey steps are module-entry SFCs, one lazy\n  step, workspace-tab persistence via a reactive store +\n  createWebStoragePersistence, and tab rehydration with UnknownJourneyError\n  discrimination. Wired through resolveManifest() so the plugin''s\n  <JourneyProvider> is threaded into Providers.\n- editor-composition: the editor screen via @modular-vue/compositions.\n  CompositionOutlet''s render-prop becomes a scoped slot; the cross-team\n  WritableStore projection is read via a small useReactiveStore bridge,\n  the inspector uses in-team useCompositionState.\n\nEnabling changes (framework-forced, outside the example dirs):\n\n- Neutral entry validator accepts object components. @modular-frontend/core\n  validateModuleEntryExit required `component` to be a function\n  (React-centric); Vue SFCs compile to objects, so SFC journey/composition\n  entry modules failed resolveManifest() validation. Relaxed to accept a\n  function or a non-null object (also covers React memo/forwardRef) and\n  made the message framework-neutral.\n- SFC tooling: @vitejs/plugin-vue + vue-tsc as example devDeps; packages\n  with/importing .vue typecheck via vue-tsc.\n- CI: registered the three e2e shells in the examples-e2e matrix and\n  extended the changed-files trigger to the vue/engine/frontend-core paths.\n\nEach example ships a headless Playwright smoke suite; docs/vue-support-tracker.md\nand examples/README.md updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012URkDFnEFfNf5EJdkhGE9q\n\n* refactor(vue): rename vue-router examples/packages to vue; address review\n\nNaming: drop the redundant \"-router\" qualifier from the Vue family (Vue\nhas a single router). Package names were already @modular-vue/*, so only\ndirectory paths change:\n- packages/vue-router-core   -> packages/vue-core\n- packages/vue-router-runtime -> packages/vue-runtime\n- examples/vue-router        -> examples/vue\nUpdated the CI matrix example/runtime/core paths, the path->name map,\nrepository.directory fields, and doc/README references.\n\nReview findings:\n- Prefer direct imports over binding re-exports: onboarding app-shared now\n  imports createSharedComposables straight from its source @modular-vue/vue\n  instead of the @modular-vue/core re-export.\n- Simplify billing lazy entry — drop the redundant\n  `.then((m) => ({ default: m.default }))` re-wrap (the SFC already\n  default-exports).\n- Harden the neutral entry validator to reject arrays as component values;\n  add positive (object component) and negative (array) test coverage.\n\nDependencies:\n- Bump vue to ^3.5.40 across the workspace (also resolves prior drift\n  between ^3.5.0 and ^3.5.13).\n- Regenerate pnpm-lock.yaml.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RAKtBrD6TXjoajCPhWLZB4\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWcrcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1mcQAHuVfktxfx/qsLTwLiHOR4/3\nxGAi63nZjxGE2S7Wn5yVSyizr06G+pFst0/EmexlhqNozoVOe8Bs6iR/RnGH+tO7\nJOJppJjcQZeOL0vEJaV0PvJO20f3cDNaZAGmqtp87EL4g8+Y3EBCtATaW1SDt9bD\n7yngjMfgnxFSSo2dTBUskpzxVaN3CRDTysyu/EP9Mmw15zBPpGmA3Oc5hdM3rQnn\nfx2uPMBDp1qUCrq65m60n+A//Xgjf3bt3f4+c1sx7OurB0y8O9ZuaguPqjvSE0LF\n9cg9pxPdk8BKq78S+Hcdr/oUtHWRyOu2N8yvV36ftNzk8saVQKd9uqsH8SD+8zQb\ns6IJhyyCuT50b8M1QfZpxZsjlVg540rZtKY49fI/b05+G22z03bJ3z1FZzP35oMu\nqR6NCy7z0cj6uA62wuK6piuahPblQOaFo6jqzHkeYY/WT00ANQVpulTroc0vZvsO\n/t42j9i2jmJhvvtxiorvDInkgdaQhXGBvDyYljzRIC5SqSWKAlyzARFGLOELfvQQ\nK//gxKKi0UMdRfgZHrPGFsMEjTHzeCmxDJOrJPzu8JTfvhzGc6LX47/nxi4G1XBL\nXOIUU0cRmHV3V6mrGlWNwtvu560hJw8H/3Q6crYcuenz2UgoJrrvMmowCe4Gkbkb\nhoij3/zSOZm1mUfIO6Xc\n=L7ju\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T06:25:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/f5adbc5aac5f3b9c0a290e05e744c5ea412902c7","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGY1YWRiYzVhYWM1ZjNiOWMwYTI5MGUwNWU3NDRjNWVhNDEyOTAyYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/c85da63b2712163d412caddbc31204c25d6bb7d0","sha":"c85da63b2712163d412caddbc31204c25d6bb7d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c85da63b2712163d412caddbc31204c25d6bb7d0"}],"sha":"f5adbc5aac5f3b9c0a290e05e744c5ea412902c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/f5adbc5aac5f3b9c0a290e05e744c5ea412902c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c85da63b2712163d412caddbc31204c25d6bb7d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T00:09:19Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T00:09:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @modular-vue/compositions CompositionOutlet (PR-34) (#75)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/compositions CompositionOutlet (PR-34)\n\nVue analog of the React compositions/src/outlet.tsx (~1,070 LOC). Ships\nCompositionOutlet, its not-found/error prop types, and the __resetNoopExitWarned\ntest latch, completing @modular-vue/compositions'' parity with the React package.\n\n- CompositionOutlet resolves the runtime from prop or <CompositionsProvider>\n  context (toRaw''d for getInternals), subscribes to the instance snapshot via a\n  shallowRef + runtime.subscribe bridge, attaches/detaches across mount/unmount,\n  and renders zones through a scoped default slot (the render-prop analog).\n- Cycle guards (same-instance + definition-depth cap) over a provide/inject\n  compositionAncestryKey; hashInput/computeSelectionKey/NOOP_EXIT copied over.\n- ZoneRenderer subscribes to the composition store, derives the resolution via a\n  computed, provides a per-mount CompositionContextValue by identity, and handles\n  empty / module-entry (mountKinds guard + Suspense) / journey (mount adapter +\n  per-(handle, hash(input)) instance cache with an end-queue drained in\n  onUpdated/onUnmounted) resolutions.\n- ZoneErrorBoundary via onErrorCaptured; keyed by selectionKey:retryKey so a\n  selector change or retry remounts a fresh boundary; renderNullOnError drives\n  the ignore policy.\n\n29 new tests across outlet, behaviors, advanced-behaviors, mount-kinds, and\nruntime rendering suites (@vue/test-utils), ported case-for-case from the React\noutlet suites; React-only StrictMode and framework-neutral engine cases omitted.\nPackage total 61. Updates the Vue support tracker (PR-34 done; Phase 3 complete).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012zxx3k4gq4YYqAp6UkeXEM\n\n* fix(ci): test Vue/engine packages + harden composition outlet\n\nCI: the changed-package detection map in ci.yml was missing every\n`@modular-vue/*` package (plus the shared `@modular-frontend/*` engines,\ncli-core, and angular), so changes under `packages/vue-compositions`\nmatched no package and the build+test matrix was skipped entirely. Add\nthe missing packages so the outlet is actually built and tested in CI.\n\noutlet: contain a throw from a journey `adapter.start` (foreign runtime\ncode invoked during render) in the zone''s error fallback instead of\nletting it escape the per-zone ZoneErrorBoundary and tear down the whole\noutlet. Report through the same channel as a selector error. Adds a\nregression test and documents the setup-time record/store capture invariant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014utK9H32G3GBuWfNwmk4gZ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"438790a06929d47fcb9d10a2cefee06d57be80dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/438790a06929d47fcb9d10a2cefee06d57be80dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/c85da63b2712163d412caddbc31204c25d6bb7d0","verification":{"payload":"tree 438790a06929d47fcb9d10a2cefee06d57be80dc\nparent 993f8829485c92df104772fe71e26d838a815461\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784246959 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784246959 +0200\n\nfeat(vue): add @modular-vue/compositions CompositionOutlet (PR-34) (#75)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/compositions CompositionOutlet (PR-34)\n\nVue analog of the React compositions/src/outlet.tsx (~1,070 LOC). Ships\nCompositionOutlet, its not-found/error prop types, and the __resetNoopExitWarned\ntest latch, completing @modular-vue/compositions'' parity with the React package.\n\n- CompositionOutlet resolves the runtime from prop or <CompositionsProvider>\n  context (toRaw''d for getInternals), subscribes to the instance snapshot via a\n  shallowRef + runtime.subscribe bridge, attaches/detaches across mount/unmount,\n  and renders zones through a scoped default slot (the render-prop analog).\n- Cycle guards (same-instance + definition-depth cap) over a provide/inject\n  compositionAncestryKey; hashInput/computeSelectionKey/NOOP_EXIT copied over.\n- ZoneRenderer subscribes to the composition store, derives the resolution via a\n  computed, provides a per-mount CompositionContextValue by identity, and handles\n  empty / module-entry (mountKinds guard + Suspense) / journey (mount adapter +\n  per-(handle, hash(input)) instance cache with an end-queue drained in\n  onUpdated/onUnmounted) resolutions.\n- ZoneErrorBoundary via onErrorCaptured; keyed by selectionKey:retryKey so a\n  selector change or retry remounts a fresh boundary; renderNullOnError drives\n  the ignore policy.\n\n29 new tests across outlet, behaviors, advanced-behaviors, mount-kinds, and\nruntime rendering suites (@vue/test-utils), ported case-for-case from the React\noutlet suites; React-only StrictMode and framework-neutral engine cases omitted.\nPackage total 61. Updates the Vue support tracker (PR-34 done; Phase 3 complete).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012zxx3k4gq4YYqAp6UkeXEM\n\n* fix(ci): test Vue/engine packages + harden composition outlet\n\nCI: the changed-package detection map in ci.yml was missing every\n`@modular-vue/*` package (plus the shared `@modular-frontend/*` engines,\ncli-core, and angular), so changes under `packages/vue-compositions`\nmatched no package and the build+test matrix was skipped entirely. Add\nthe missing packages so the outlet is actually built and tested in CI.\n\noutlet: contain a throw from a journey `adapter.start` (foreign runtime\ncode invoked during render) in the zone''s error fallback instead of\nletting it escape the per-zone ZoneErrorBoundary and tear down the whole\noutlet. Report through the same channel as a selector error. Adds a\nregression test and documents the setup-time record/store capture invariant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014utK9H32G3GBuWfNwmk4gZ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWXKwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAv24QAAGA0hrBJqgGWp+l2FaCnwGD\nJl8Aj6uplfQgzjlcm5EmFuSeuEoD1q5/HcJauqCHybTK0C8AKMEgcAS8YRQm4bPG\ntaZTWRkY+pnirL847/i12fLp0C2xEBgYwZWxxMgqFkCTdYzgAhnlksWgGbRKXj2m\nN1o5gJLTvVKe84CcuZujg/mT0KGRVDl8NFFLXDC5L7ttnb28IHrKSvMHXPcNSvlr\nimwrB3epedIvSPAIIO8f6RZ2UiOCS/RPseX/0EjQ6mCz70eYGljihmPklwPX5kgr\nx87gsl/e2B4ibNYGp3McfYOlkZyHjgpfwrW4Cs84gsseE/E7kvPgci2dDhL5L4y3\nkYUfJUH1cCh18AYC6kABVIdZyJEmEFP8eG1VXyYdGSGCJy1OdtsTtSlvGJhFni3f\nW5uid4brIj+/Qa03eaTv3fPo109+/qsBcvd3WIxf7wOYUwgeksZ7FJNiphxjIuuu\ng9FctzYwg8xaP6LEB1yulkOFHSpMOQTNF3xHKJQm8q2XtVUveGKn7pxfcsI5pKCO\nIdhSbhrF1R7Y7P5UIGr6ODJ4SYb15QegvbvbFzpYIiUW7JUfXSqQyCXOqR2ecMfA\nt+LMNhW29VGCx834EPTArrmSnS/tG8VSiGTl4orbHv4us/mhAGZlfdpoxSniuvzV\nytL7tO2RP6pLti/Djd2y\n=QuBe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-17T00:09:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/c85da63b2712163d412caddbc31204c25d6bb7d0","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGM4NWRhNjNiMjcxMjE2M2Q0MTJjYWRkYmMzMTIwNGMyNWQ2YmI3ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/993f8829485c92df104772fe71e26d838a815461","sha":"993f8829485c92df104772fe71e26d838a815461","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/993f8829485c92df104772fe71e26d838a815461"}],"sha":"c85da63b2712163d412caddbc31204c25d6bb7d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c85da63b2712163d412caddbc31204c25d6bb7d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/993f8829485c92df104772fe71e26d838a815461/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T20:42:27Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T20:42:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @modular-vue/compositions provider, composables, plugin (PR-33) (#72)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/compositions provider, composables, plugin (PR-33)\n\nNew packages/vue-compositions (@modular-vue/compositions, 0.1.0): the Vue 3\ncompositions binding, part 1 of Phase 3''s compositions work. Ports the React\nprovider.tsx, hooks.ts, and plugin.tsx over @modular-frontend/compositions-engine;\nthe composition outlet stays with PR-34.\n\n- provider.ts: CompositionsProvider / useCompositionsContext / compositionsKey.\n  Provides { runtime } by identity at setup (un-proxied, so identity checks\n  against manifest.extensions.compositions hold), which also gives the React\n  binding''s memo-on-runtime fanout guarantee for free. Unlike JourneyProvider it\n  does not compose over ModuleExitProvider.\n- hooks.ts: panel-side composables reading a per-mount compositionInstanceKey the\n  outlet (PR-34) installs — useCompositionState (reactive ShallowRef),\n  useCompositionDispatch, useCompositionEmit, useCompositionZone, the pre-typed\n  createCompositionContext bundle, and CompositionContextValue.\n- use-composition.ts: host-side useComposition + useCompositionOptions, with the\n  Symbol.for options brand ported verbatim. Mints once in setup and registers a\n  no-op subscription torn down on scope dispose, so a held id disposes via the\n  runtime''s refcount gate without an outlet.\n- plugin.ts: compositionsPlugin() with extend/validate/onResolve and a providers()\n  contributing a Vue CompositionsProvider; resolved-twice + register-after-resolve\n  guards match the React source.\n\nFramework-forced deviations: useCompositionState returns a ShallowRef (reactive-\nsource convention, PR-10/PR-23) instead of the selected value, and drops React''s\ngetSnapshot-cache since Vue''s setup runs once and the store push is event-driven.\n\nTests: 30 across provider/hooks/use-composition/plugin suites + a hooks.test-d.ts,\nporting the use-composition.test.tsx and selector-dispatch.test.tsx intent (outlet-\ndependent and engine-only cases deferred/already covered). Full workspace typecheck\n(124 tasks) and vite build (JS + dts) pass. Tracker updated: PR-33 marked done.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QCgNTenPyTRTU6S8DgovNB\n\n* test(vue-compositions): cover useComposition options-brand disambiguation\n\nAdds two useComposition cases that exercise the Symbol.for options brand,\nwhich no prior test touched:\n- an input shaped like `{ runtime }` (unbranded) is treated as input, not\n  options — minting still uses the context runtime, and a decoy runtime on\n  the input is never consulted\n- a branded `useCompositionOptions({ runtime })` is detected as options\n  while the preceding argument is still forwarded to `runtime.start` as input\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01S5ZzHx6WVWzuoBk8n1UEJv\n\n* fix(vue-compositions): require branded options in useComposition; tracker fixes\n\n- useComposition overloads now accept only BrandedCompositionOptions (the\n  useCompositionOptions() output) instead of a bare UseCompositionOptions.\n  A plain positional `{ runtime }` was type-valid but, being unbranded, was\n  silently consumed as `input` while the supplied runtime was ignored — the\n  type now enforces the same brand the runtime check requires. Exported the\n  BrandedCompositionOptions type.\n- docs/vue-support-tracker.md: correct the PR-33 test tally (32 across the\n  suites: plugin is 8, use-composition is 7) and link the PR (#72) in the\n  status board row per the \"done (link the PR)\" convention.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01S5ZzHx6WVWzuoBk8n1UEJv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0824badac81b95219ca4f9f9ef75b79a3efb89b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/0824badac81b95219ca4f9f9ef75b79a3efb89b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/993f8829485c92df104772fe71e26d838a815461","verification":{"payload":"tree 0824badac81b95219ca4f9f9ef75b79a3efb89b1\nparent f1c3f33d1c606321110e31a05c36e271a4cfae9a\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784234547 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784234547 +0200\n\nfeat(vue): add @modular-vue/compositions provider, composables, plugin (PR-33) (#72)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/compositions provider, composables, plugin (PR-33)\n\nNew packages/vue-compositions (@modular-vue/compositions, 0.1.0): the Vue 3\ncompositions binding, part 1 of Phase 3''s compositions work. Ports the React\nprovider.tsx, hooks.ts, and plugin.tsx over @modular-frontend/compositions-engine;\nthe composition outlet stays with PR-34.\n\n- provider.ts: CompositionsProvider / useCompositionsContext / compositionsKey.\n  Provides { runtime } by identity at setup (un-proxied, so identity checks\n  against manifest.extensions.compositions hold), which also gives the React\n  binding''s memo-on-runtime fanout guarantee for free. Unlike JourneyProvider it\n  does not compose over ModuleExitProvider.\n- hooks.ts: panel-side composables reading a per-mount compositionInstanceKey the\n  outlet (PR-34) installs — useCompositionState (reactive ShallowRef),\n  useCompositionDispatch, useCompositionEmit, useCompositionZone, the pre-typed\n  createCompositionContext bundle, and CompositionContextValue.\n- use-composition.ts: host-side useComposition + useCompositionOptions, with the\n  Symbol.for options brand ported verbatim. Mints once in setup and registers a\n  no-op subscription torn down on scope dispose, so a held id disposes via the\n  runtime''s refcount gate without an outlet.\n- plugin.ts: compositionsPlugin() with extend/validate/onResolve and a providers()\n  contributing a Vue CompositionsProvider; resolved-twice + register-after-resolve\n  guards match the React source.\n\nFramework-forced deviations: useCompositionState returns a ShallowRef (reactive-\nsource convention, PR-10/PR-23) instead of the selected value, and drops React''s\ngetSnapshot-cache since Vue''s setup runs once and the store push is event-driven.\n\nTests: 30 across provider/hooks/use-composition/plugin suites + a hooks.test-d.ts,\nporting the use-composition.test.tsx and selector-dispatch.test.tsx intent (outlet-\ndependent and engine-only cases deferred/already covered). Full workspace typecheck\n(124 tasks) and vite build (JS + dts) pass. Tracker updated: PR-33 marked done.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QCgNTenPyTRTU6S8DgovNB\n\n* test(vue-compositions): cover useComposition options-brand disambiguation\n\nAdds two useComposition cases that exercise the Symbol.for options brand,\nwhich no prior test touched:\n- an input shaped like `{ runtime }` (unbranded) is treated as input, not\n  options — minting still uses the context runtime, and a decoy runtime on\n  the input is never consulted\n- a branded `useCompositionOptions({ runtime })` is detected as options\n  while the preceding argument is still forwarded to `runtime.start` as input\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01S5ZzHx6WVWzuoBk8n1UEJv\n\n* fix(vue-compositions): require branded options in useComposition; tracker fixes\n\n- useComposition overloads now accept only BrandedCompositionOptions (the\n  useCompositionOptions() output) instead of a bare UseCompositionOptions.\n  A plain positional `{ runtime }` was type-valid but, being unbranded, was\n  silently consumed as `input` while the supplied runtime was ignored — the\n  type now enforces the same brand the runtime check requires. Exported the\n  BrandedCompositionOptions type.\n- docs/vue-support-tracker.md: correct the PR-33 test tally (32 across the\n  suites: plugin is 8, use-composition is 7) and link the PR (#72) in the\n  status board row per the \"done (link the PR)\" convention.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01S5ZzHx6WVWzuoBk8n1UEJv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWUIzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0EwQAF550key9eB/JzCsh4yT89Am\nIbz6xmPzCVRywU27y2DTjlfJf6/dsnmHIr3LEklAzhfpjv8IFYmZ7LUWFrRSmoqj\n4dqNrhP2FUZcCecYS3R6R9g+M1R3d+Hv+D7VYH16gdle4BZyuf9cIcjcAiRtIthh\nmLZvvHaaaWDyR7/gOD43eh3TRIqFvrBYoNAFtR0WfClS9eSIcvRAcukJc8mS1KSY\nBq3byI47O0ldVrgvIiCbHnfXJPJ2644FFATZbDFw2cvJO8UGkByhtC1HKVUu8vae\nYnfeJLRVT1LIyEDmYYFCy6h4QAjZbXia24cPmI0lOlDhhThoVmZANWvH3f2Td0sO\nWAseklNeNDNA00Ir+DfZ+3Wk1pyAceUxrJKX2spquDRgkhUjgTR+R+qfXM2xKbCU\ndVwqc0IrtnshUy2QGC19nIX3lB+7tjJi/r7dcjU/ZKCxVNudM+J6mRc36FPHkxRP\nXPMezVYWKFsVPK5HJa9BJyA43h2xzQuSWCTP71qVCwnOTc3w7jrQHzSmNoH5AftZ\nVDoVpKP9et92wruTlKMbC7w7jVtmlMjOaboBWppTLHJKWKaqfX4xCd7OGRHSqg5x\nrU6D0I+pA62CLgNcLnphyR6mGZ7MWTxUoDC3PDqhak0t/cU5eWCaboaHVTCRaTGj\nF5Y9XowolhID3zFxpybt\n=vl5g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-16T20:42:27Z"}},"