7934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/f1c3f33d1c606321110e31a05c36e271a4cfae9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T18:53:28Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T18:53:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: top 10 improvement proposals from a production consumer (#73)\n\nDistills friction points observed in a real-world production app built\non the library family: journey/router URL sync, JourneyHost lifecycle,\ndefineModule literal inference, derived step progress, buildInput input\nwidening, journey state helpers, outlet error/loading defaults, testing\nergonomics, nav ordering stability, and registry-derived module maps.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b0b8854f798ef7892606f940048663d068b3efc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/b0b8854f798ef7892606f940048663d068b3efc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/f1c3f33d1c606321110e31a05c36e271a4cfae9a","verification":{"payload":"tree b0b8854f798ef7892606f940048663d068b3efc6\nparent 80697e2572878b6236bfa35c2465974a875dc715\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784228008 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784228008 +0300\n\ndocs: top 10 improvement proposals from a production consumer (#73)\n\nDistills friction points observed in a real-world production app built\non the library family: journey/router URL sync, JourneyHost lifecycle,\ndefineModule literal inference, derived step progress, buildInput input\nwidening, journey state helpers, outlet error/loading defaults, testing\nergonomics, nav ordering stability, and registry-derived module maps.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWSioCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbgwQAEopRJQgnOQ8ZVAAOIpCR6vL\n8FKFyoQkHN7hsWC3Mx5nOTmhECDpyWd8EI3IhNEHt6s93trIedbVkk4gYuQfIyRs\nJZCzGFx0wcIEP5zw6oQLAW8TXKkRLo+V2ANnu1pbHM2FtqAw8PoCzuhrVhVPTAsA\nisNaZJ/tAmuVxjWu2f2arUK708c//AVVa7ymLk7WfN0/cMUAz12DidicYTh/GE+l\nH+1Q1EzB772gyn4W2iLdzm3E05VYBSIx77YcPX0fYP56TvaxGJnKKlyVHGbeoSsw\ngUJkF0rGqjuzgyHW/oNn9sFukh7XGa4d+UEOQIwMHIgVRB8fYv8lrnnd/CxLC/Lf\nVxRjCD97pj9oyAFHTjRb+IGHzXTH21eGC/27pR0nIpkXWiWnCPoHXLwCRaJ5dTrh\nFRBfkHPFlvJGGVUlho6E0+2z49xP8r5qqg1xzZng2+XOUFmlyRbXvrkTF2CxRyBu\n0pDQOla/M64T3ueWW2FzE6uTXEtwD+CQi49kv1P0ifDVw70lzPqvGVo5XknvakhJ\nNZDU8KhlyWGZtatGnhwuFSBXJ+dGTJK6944FJZwjsPRipvJjpD+2fo5Qr1ebkhsL\nn14Be9p5msD40C+Rvr4uXM7rVdoqW89PTdQkfzxNejR7ITAX686TIV1C1ieTaHAj\nn6c84aWFjEamkQ3zuyYb\n=yRuQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-16T18:53:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/f1c3f33d1c606321110e31a05c36e271a4cfae9a","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGYxYzNmMzNkMWM2MDYzMjExMTBlMzFhMDVjMzZlMjcxYTRjZmFlOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/80697e2572878b6236bfa35c2465974a875dc715","sha":"80697e2572878b6236bfa35c2465974a875dc715","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/80697e2572878b6236bfa35c2465974a875dc715"}],"sha":"f1c3f33d1c606321110e31a05c36e271a4cfae9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/f1c3f33d1c606321110e31a05c36e271a4cfae9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/80697e2572878b6236bfa35c2465974a875dc715/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T17:01:15Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T17:01:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): wire journeys into @modular-vue/runtime + renderJourney (PR-32) (#71)\n\nWire the real @modular-vue/journeys plugin end-to-end into the vue-router\nruntime and add the renderJourney testing helper — closing the PR-21/PR-22\ndeferrals that named PR-32 as the home of concrete journeys-in-runtime.\n\n- runtime: buildAssembly collects plugin-contributed provider components\n  (plugin.providers({ runtime })); resolveManifest() threads them after the\n  user-supplied providers into the framework-mode Providers component (the Vue\n  analog of the React runtime''s combinedProviders). A <JourneyOutlet> inside\n  <router-view> now reads the journey runtime from context automatically.\n- runtime: add registry-journeys.test.ts (real journeysPlugin, ported from the\n  React source) and journeys-integration.test.ts (a branching multi-module\n  journey mounted through a route, driven to terminal via both resolveManifest()\n  and the shell-wrapped resolve() path). registry-plugins.test.ts keeps the\n  framework-neutral plugin-machinery edge cases.\n- testing: add renderJourney (ported from react-router-testing) + its test.\n\nThe router-owning resolve() path does not auto-thread wrapping-component plugin\nproviders (it returns an installable Vue plugin with no library-owned root to\nwrap); shells wrap <router-view> in <JourneyProvider> or use resolveManifest().\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016wh6fB8wMiYhxVx8xuzwRR\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e73c562525fd6c295a19b0be7b8ba2e2f71fed4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/e73c562525fd6c295a19b0be7b8ba2e2f71fed4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/80697e2572878b6236bfa35c2465974a875dc715","verification":{"payload":"tree e73c562525fd6c295a19b0be7b8ba2e2f71fed4d\nparent 0df90aeffd6be1eaf78b12c9972c41817ad5e28e\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784221275 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784221275 +0200\n\nfeat(vue): wire journeys into @modular-vue/runtime + renderJourney (PR-32) (#71)\n\nWire the real @modular-vue/journeys plugin end-to-end into the vue-router\nruntime and add the renderJourney testing helper — closing the PR-21/PR-22\ndeferrals that named PR-32 as the home of concrete journeys-in-runtime.\n\n- runtime: buildAssembly collects plugin-contributed provider components\n  (plugin.providers({ runtime })); resolveManifest() threads them after the\n  user-supplied providers into the framework-mode Providers component (the Vue\n  analog of the React runtime''s combinedProviders). A <JourneyOutlet> inside\n  <router-view> now reads the journey runtime from context automatically.\n- runtime: add registry-journeys.test.ts (real journeysPlugin, ported from the\n  React source) and journeys-integration.test.ts (a branching multi-module\n  journey mounted through a route, driven to terminal via both resolveManifest()\n  and the shell-wrapped resolve() path). registry-plugins.test.ts keeps the\n  framework-neutral plugin-machinery edge cases.\n- testing: add renderJourney (ported from react-router-testing) + its test.\n\nThe router-owning resolve() path does not auto-thread wrapping-component plugin\nproviders (it returns an installable Vue plugin with no library-owned root to\nwrap); shells wrap <router-view> in <JourneyProvider> or use resolveManifest().\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016wh6fB8wMiYhxVx8xuzwRR\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWQ5bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApfAQAC3MjNcPJKwW4OFgdWph+472\n6A54oil4CPP4JPaxB82nPuiTs3lJzYcNbGYeFevrxTM2XUV+0uhWhL8ARwkFY/VM\n0wcM2aPNftugVHGP8XfhnkknjcHjVBkf4p52v5JQbCfuc7FBxe0bV0ZuPX1XGp6R\nDTtOBDT3sm/srFLDsZBje0PXY6A0WipvS2BLmoN+OSwtiourtJYQN10rNvCiHIAA