e2572878b6236bfa35c2465974a875dc715","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/80697e2572878b6236bfa35c2465974a875dc715"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/0df90aeffd6be1eaf78b12c9972c41817ad5e28e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T15:27:22Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T15:27:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @modular-vue/journeys outlet, module-tab, use-wait-for-exit (PR-31) (#70)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/journeys outlet, module-tab, use-wait-for-exit (PR-31)\n\nVue analogs of journeys/src/outlet.tsx, module-tab.tsx, and\nuse-wait-for-exit.ts, completing the journeys UI layer.\n\n- outlet.ts: JourneyOutlet renders the current step, walks the active\n  call chain to the leaf, binds exit/goBack/goForward, fires onFinished\n  once on the root''s terminal, abandons on unmount with the listener-count\n  handoff guard, and does precise/aggressive speculative preload. Ships\n  useJourneyCallStack. The React class StepErrorBoundary becomes an\n  onErrorCaptured-based defineComponent keyed by stepToken:retryKey so a\n  retry remounts a fresh boundary.\n- module-tab.ts: ModuleTab + ModuleTabExitEvent. inheritAttrs:false +\n  reading input from attrs distinguishes \"no input prop\" from an explicit\n  input={undefined} (Vue collapses both for a declared prop).\n- use-wait-for-exit.ts: first-wins channel race over subscribe/poll/\n  timeout. exit and channels accept MaybeRefOrGetter; a watchEffect keeps\n  callbacks live and a watch on a folded scalar key re-arms only on\n  poll.intervalMs / timeout.ms / named-exit changes.\n\nVue-specific fix: toRaw the module/modules/runtime props before touching\nresolveEntryComponent''s per-entry WeakMap and getInternals, since Vue\ndeeply proxies prop objects and would otherwise break chunk sharing and\nruntime-internals lookup.\n\n67 new tests port the React suites case-for-case (StrictMode-only cases\nexcepted); package total 84. Updates the tracker (PR-31 done).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01URM86DAkDCKeZ3byaKLPk1\n\n* fix(vue-journeys): read instanceId at unmount time in JourneyOutlet\n\nThe abandon-on-unmount handler captured `props.instanceId` once at setup\nand used that constant, while every other consumer (root snapshot, leaf\nwalk, the `instance` computed) reads `props.instanceId` reactively. If a\nhost re-bound `instanceId` on a live outlet, unmount would `end()` the\noriginal instance and leak the current one.\n\nRead `props.instanceId` inside `onUnmounted` so the handler targets the\ninstance currently being rendered, matching the React effect whose\ncleanup closure holds the latest id after re-subscription.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YcQZFEswiSrvsU6vW9GHKE\n\n* fix(vue-journeys): address review comments on PR-31 outlet/module-tab\n\n- module-tab: use Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty for entry lookup so\n  inherited names (e.g. \"constructor\") are treated as unknown entries\n  instead of flowing into resolveEntryComponent.\n- outlet: dedupe onFinished per root instance id rather than a\n  component-wide boolean, so a rebound instanceId can fire onFinished.\n- outlet: attach .catch to the speculative preload promise so a rejected\n  lazy import never becomes an unhandled rejection (try/catch only guards\n  synchronous throws).\n- use-wait-for-exit test: assert the winning push unsubscribes\n  immediately, matching the first-wins-teardown-is-immediate contract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016RVRy9TBoQXAA5qqtVRYUZ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9cabd7020eb10d6b3f40a16a9a7b1337d394669","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/a9cabd7020eb10d6b3f40a16a9a7b1337d394669"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/0df90aeffd6be1eaf78b12c9972c41817ad5e28e","verification":{"payload":"tree a9cabd7020eb10d6b3f40a16a9a7b1337d394669\nparent 5fea76adb84d0719a86c3a624d71cee759439589\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784215642 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784215642 +0200\n\nfeat(vue): add @modular-vue/journeys outlet, module-tab, use-wait-for-exit (PR-31) (#70)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/journeys outlet, module-tab, use-wait-for-exit (PR-31)\n\nVue analogs of journeys/src/outlet.tsx, module-tab.tsx, and\nuse-wait-for-exit.ts, completing the journeys UI layer.\n\n- outlet.ts: JourneyOutlet renders the current step, walks the active\n  call chain to the leaf, binds exit/goBack/goForward, fires onFinished\n  once on the root''s terminal, abandons on unmount with the listener-count\n  handoff guard, and does precise/aggressive speculative preload. Ships\n  useJourneyCallStack. The React class StepErrorBoundary becomes an\n  onErrorCaptured-based defineComponent keyed by stepToken:retryKey so a\n  retry remounts a fresh boundary.\n- module-tab.ts: ModuleTab + ModuleTabExitEvent. inheritAttrs:false +\n  reading input from attrs distinguishes \"no input prop\" from an explicit\n  input={undefined} (Vue collapses both for a declared prop).\n- use-wait-for-exit.ts: first-wins channel race over subscribe/poll/\n  timeout. exit and channels accept MaybeRefOrGetter; a watchEffect keeps\n  callbacks live and a watch on a folded scalar key re-arms only on\n  poll.intervalMs / timeout.ms / named-exit changes.\n\nVue-specific fix: toRaw the module/modules/runtime props before touching\nresolveEntryComponent''s per-entry WeakMap and getInternals, since Vue\ndeeply proxies prop objects and would otherwise break chunk sharing and\nruntime-internals lookup.\n\n67 new tests port the React suites case-for-case (StrictMode-only cases\nexcepted); package total 84. Updates the tracker (PR-31 done).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01URM86DAkDCKeZ3byaKLPk1\n\n* fix(vue-journeys): read instanceId at unmount time in JourneyOutlet\n\nThe abandon-on-unmount handler captured `props.instanceId` once at setup\nand used that constant, while every other consumer (root snapshot, leaf\nwalk, the `instance` computed) reads `props.instanceId` reactively. If a\nhost re-bound `instanceId` on a live outlet, unmount would `end()` the\noriginal instance and leak the current one.\n\nRead `props.instanceId` inside `onUnmounted` so the handler targets the\ninstance currently being rendered, matching the React effect whose\ncleanup closure holds the latest id after re-subscription.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YcQZFEswiSrvsU6vW9GHKE\n\n* fix(vue-journeys): address review comments on PR-31 outlet/module-tab\n\n- module-tab: use Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty for entry lookup so\n  inherited names (e.g. \"constructor\") are treated as unknown entries\n  instead of flowing into resolveEntryComponent.\n- outlet: dedupe onFinished per root instance id rather than a\n  component-wide boolean, so a rebound instanceId can fire onFinished.\n- outlet: attach .catch to the speculative preload promise so a rejected\n  lazy import never becomes an unhandled rejection (try/catch only guards\n  synchronous throws).\n- use-wait-for-exit test: assert the winning push unsubscribes\n  immediately, matching the first-wins-teardown-is-immediate contract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016RVRy9TBoQXAA5qqtVRYUZ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWPhaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIakQADGoNNhYtuqS4IO9GqIoBg47\nFAg6xaRPzkZcg8l9QY/OB2PHTD16lnR89kvc+wqAKTPzRdHqjiu6jen2O3wOtm+9\nz1vhRaJnJpeaABbiLQsypo6Bww/ed9rfKUESP1zQDXcLSr1ip3RcFcOUSb3zI7MW\n1AE7I57HhLh95Q/sfoBdGbJ+6vp9NPLbPNvJY4xZHc5FnTXULftlCZ0ETE2q/SG/\nTxfqCYKysH65En7fFkzrRkhfg8agxT3yaLhfaJYqGenJCmNyXC1++P6Rovju+4mh\nRYQib+J8yUxnZ1gtp+/ZT5BL097/cbw51hHKSN2gyOb7Dt4iuS+mz6URT6XZM2/k\nin6J4lZxJoPbVnDfWWWcbxQYiQ1li6Wt4xnp+O0dG7dXBlPuqWwT82uoNT2r/kOP\ngWlxYnAlU6r0mR/jsbXRy6wR0y6uht9QEqBKGWpNT/miiB2b+jLYNrkJK0pBWAwt\nI3J3AUdcY4PZ3k/qj7piIRnaqpP4y62IFjChzmRWqZbQnIxyXZzTQajFPOc5S/Ou\nPNt39oz2jxpCu8Xb/OI3KYzyAMN7yeQAwKMvjsr2+3GZCpwuzZUvMqiYESmsXlur\nFTvcfDkYJcVToW1Xb6Xah8TlSmDManqWFiSotFZukufVy2e17Vi/rZWx4XPI8t/F\n6/sW6cFXtsJOK6xboiPk\n=39Mr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-16T15:27:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/0df90aeffd6be1eaf78b12c9972c41817ad5e28e","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKDBkZjkwYWVmZmQ2YmUxZWFmNzhiMTJjOTk3MmM0MTgxN2FkNWUyOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/5fea76adb84d0719a86c3a624d71cee759439589","sha":"5fea76adb84d0719a86c3a624d71cee759439589","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/5fea76adb84d0719a86c3a624d71cee759439589"}],"sha":"0df90aeffd6be1eaf78b12c9972c41817ad5e28e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/0df90aeffd6be1eaf78b12c9972c41817ad5e28e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/5fea76adb84d0719a86c3a624d71cee759439589/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T13:45:28Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T13:45:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @modular-vue/journeys provider, composables, plugin (PR-30) (#69)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/journeys provider, composables, plugin (PR-30)\n\nStart Phase 3 of the Vue port with the journeys binding layer: a new\n`@modular-vue/journeys` (0.1.0) package over `@modular-frontend/journeys-engine`,\nmirroring `@modular-react/journeys`.\n\n- provider.ts: `JourneyProvider` (defineComponent + render fn) provides the\n  journey runtime and composes over `<ModuleExitProvider>`; `useJourneyContext`.\n- instance-hooks.ts: `useInstanceSnapshot` (watchEffect bridge, the Vue analog\n  of `useSyncExternalStore`), `useCallChain` (hand-managed activeChild\n  subscriptions), `useLeafId`.\n- use-journey-state.ts: `useJourneyState` / `useJourneyInstance` and the\n  leaf-walking `useActiveLeafJourneyState` / `useActiveLeafJourneyInstance`,\n  returning Vue refs (PR-23 reactive-source convention).\n- plugin.ts: `journeysPlugin()` — the concrete plugin PR-21/PR-22 deferred here;\n  identical to the React plugin except `providers()` returns a Vue provider.\n\nComposables accept `MaybeRefOrGetter` ids so a reactive/leaf id stays reactive.\n17 tests (provider, use-journey-state, plugin) pass; workspace typecheck (122\ntasks) and vite build (JS + dts) pass with externals unbundled. Tracker updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MgWjMcA5t8zKEHpjrZhdYT\n\n* refactor(vue-journeys): address review findings on provider + tests\n\n- provider: expose `onModuleExit` on the injected context value through a\n  getter so a swapped handler is visible to consumers that introspect\n  `useJourneyContext().onModuleExit` (parity with the React provider, which\n  rebuilds its value object each render). `runtime` stays a raw, un-proxied\n  reference so identity checks against `manifest.journeys` still hold.\n- tests: add direct coverage for `useJourneyInstance` (full snapshot +\n  no-provider null) instead of relying solely on transitive coverage.\n- tests: add `use-journey-state.test-d.ts` so the type-level coverage the\n  vitest config already enables (`*.test-d.ts`) actually exists, asserting the\n  composable return types and `MaybeRefOrGetter` id acceptance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P1a2CFQmnRZp25ZXAKAMEQ\n\n* fix(vue-journeys): address review comments on plugin type + tracker link\n\n- plugin: reuse the upstream `ModuleExitHandler` for the `onModuleExit`\n  option instead of a duplicated inline event shape, so the full\n  `ModuleExitEvent` (incl. `routeId`) stays in sync with @modular-vue/vue.\n- docs: link PR-30''s `done` status to #69, matching the tracker''s\n  \"link the PR\" convention.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P1a2CFQmnRZp25ZXAKAMEQ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"371025050422a7613e32ef56b34231f1a408cc1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/371025050422a7613e32ef56b34231f1a408cc1b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/5fea76adb84d0719a86c3a624d71cee759439589","verification":{"payload":"tree 371025050422a7613e32ef56b34231f1a408cc1b\nparent b122f14c5fa3e1874cadbea7a4afb8cc72c383f9\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784209528 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784209528 +0200\n\nfeat(vue): add @modular-vue/journeys provider, composables, plugin (PR-30) (#69)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/journeys provider, composables, plugin (PR-30)\n\nStart Phase 3 of the Vue port with the journeys binding layer: a new\n`@modular-vue/journeys` (0.1.0) package over `@modular-frontend/journeys-engine`,\nmirroring `@modular-react/journeys`.\n\n- provider.ts: `JourneyProvider` (defineComponent + render fn) provides the\n  journey runtime and composes over `<ModuleExitProvider>`; `useJourneyContext`.\n- instance-hooks.ts: `useInstanceSnapshot` (watchEffect bridge, the Vue analog\n  of `useSyncExternalStore`), `useCallChain` (hand-managed activeChild\n  subscriptions), `useLeafId`.\n- use-journey-state.ts: `useJourneyState` / `useJourneyInstance` and the\n  leaf-walking `useActiveLeafJourneyState` / `useActiveLeafJourneyInstance`,\n  returning Vue refs (PR-23 reactive-source convention).\n- plugin.ts: `journeysPlugin()` — the concrete plugin PR-21/PR-22 deferred here;\n  identical to the React plugin except `providers()` returns a Vue provider.\n\nComposables accept `MaybeRefOrGetter` ids so a reactive/leaf id stays reactive.\n17 tests (provider, use-journey-state, plugin) pass; workspace typecheck (122\ntasks) and vite build (JS + dts) pass with externals unbundled. Tracker updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MgWjMcA5t8zKEHpjrZhdYT\n\n* refactor(vue-journeys): address review findings on provider + tests\n\n- provider: expose `onModuleExit` on the injected context value through a\n  getter so a swapped handler is visible to consumers that introspect\n  `useJourneyContext().onModuleExit` (parity with the React provider, which\n  rebuilds its value object each render). `runtime` stays a raw, un-proxied\n  reference so identity checks against `manifest.journeys` still hold.\n- tests: add direct coverage for `useJourneyInstance` (full snapshot +\n  no-provider null) instead of relying solely on transitive coverage.\n- tests: add `use-journey-state.test-d.ts` so the type-level coverage the\n  vitest config already enables (`*.test-d.ts`) actually exists, asserting the\n  composable return types and `MaybeRefOrGetter` id acceptance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P1a2CFQmnRZp25ZXAKAMEQ\n\n* fix(vue-journeys): address review comments on plugin type + tracker link\n\n- plugin: reuse the upstream `ModuleExitHandler` for the `onModuleExit`\n  option instead of a duplicated inline event shape, so the full\n  `ModuleExitEvent` (incl. `routeId`) stays in sync with @modular-vue/vue.\n- docs: link PR-30''s `done` status to #69, matching the tracker''s\n  \"link the PR\" convention.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P1a2CFQmnRZp25ZXAKAMEQ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWOB4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABqQQACsAm3ZyxYAcjLHfEbp/vIqZ\n8Gud1tidIHYyf+m2SjlYLcGtgTrmj1rTEm52zy/rbJJlAO7lJSJQ8LIq3R1S2yiz\niwpf5dEhGRX6DSApkHIMXEJ6u63NityvIRZJYna8UOAEFOnnq2h3J4lN/a0FPQd3\nYbCnrR5pSR/GkrCkq5WSfbJXX5pe6i8CLtFej6/7OrRp+VRxkrKfM8FczX7TcIVI\nDyJVB6EH+yPS5vcZpprG3BbSVEHO8tpqtHXquXXpI09ITF3gc43JdJeKQn+rfBy3\n9UITiomDRKg1GgYdz7O2VxDmeKrlJWIz4A8Qp4h1h1WIHEriP7OtjBzsp22O2nKD\n7UvHBJ5jCMmfexzV9BmKUOEpBvC44fs6M4OPSNSxlHbgBbUfPLs37zACLS0/susB\njILFM+6/vQ51I/v52UCW1XPlUxnqQaXYAWasgeIv9dtVzz3rYln+qxtAtekxD+xr\nj8f8VnjZnr5Krq1OKJUo9Mch8NmVnXSmeXIfjIkesmA0oFtbVq2ktxz/4V+yjdkn\nZUb3oDy0bHu+eHFJw8cYMB/uRMBoPr4ptQ32ElGTwVOk80eDmb4lzSI9WlV28E+b\nSvaNhzOB5ztDyU5oocH9Hc0a0BFU6FWIa10m9doO57doW2WrPjllZREFKuanOB20\nQ3QP4ii7B/BAs8N9GxFi\n=F+Cc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-16T13:45:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/5fea76adb84d0719a86c3a624d71cee759439589","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKDVmZWE3NmFkYjg0ZDA3MTlhODZjM2E2MjRkNzFjZWU3NTk0Mzk1ODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/b122f14c5fa3e1874cadbea7a4afb8cc72c383f9","sha":"b122f14c5fa3e1874cadbea7a4afb8cc72c383f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/b122f14c5fa3e1874cadbea7a4afb8cc72c383f9"}],"sha":"5fea76adb84d0719a86c3a624d71cee759439589","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/5fea76adb84d0719a86c3a624d71cee759439589"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/b122f14c5fa3e1874cadbea7a4afb8cc72c383f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T10:43:01Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T10:43:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @modular-vue/testing renderModule (PR-24) (#68)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/testing renderModule (PR-24)\n\nPort react-router-testing/src/render-module.tsx to @modular-vue/testing.\nrenderModule renders a module in isolation across entry-point, route-based\n(createRoutes), and legacy component-only shapes, providing the shared\ndependencies, slots, and module-list injection contexts the runtime installs\nat the app root.\n\nFramework-forced deviations from the React source:\n- returns a @vue/test-utils VueWrapper (the repo-wide Vue test primitive)\n  instead of a @testing-library/react RenderResult; the three JSX context\n  providers become one defineComponent wrapper calling the provide* helpers.\n- the createRoutes path boots a memory-history router, installs it as a\n  plugin, renders <RouterView>, and awaits router.isReady() + flushPromises()\n  before returning, since vue-router resolves navigation asynchronously.\n\nDynamic slots are evaluated eagerly and provided as a static object, reusing\ncore''s buildDepsSnapshot. 7 new tests cover all three modes, the route option,\ndynamic-slot evaluation, dep/module/slot injection, and both error paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0126RQ6QY14J7JFcDh2VyNjE\n\n* test(vue): cover reactive-service injection and default no-op exit in renderModule\n\nAdds two @modular-vue/testing renderModule tests closing coverage gaps from\nreview of PR-24:\n\n- entry mode: omitting the `exit` option falls back to a no-op, so emitting an\n  exit from the rendered entry does not throw.\n- createRoutes mode: a reactive service passed in `deps` is auto-detected into\n  the reactiveServices bucket and injected (read via useReactiveService). The\n  `deps` type models the resolved snapshot shape (Store<T> | T), so the service\n  instance is passed through a localized, documented cast — matching real-app\n  wiring.\n\nPackage total 18 tests (was 16). Typecheck, tests, and oxlint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QoimcQQ6BmtpcYgzGPTbBU\n\n* fix(vue): accept ReactiveService in renderModule deps type; address review\n\nAddresses PR-24 review comments:\n\n- render-module.ts: widen the public `deps` type to accept\n  `ReactiveService<T>` alongside `Store<T>` and the plain value, matching the\n  runtime''s auto-detection (separateDeps). Consumers no longer need a cast to\n  pass a reactive service.\n- render-module.test.ts: drop the now-unneeded cast in the reactive-service\n  test; replace the no-op `resolves.not.toThrow()` matcher on the click promise\n  with a direct await (trigger rejects if the handler throws).\n- vue-support-tracker.md: update the acceptance record to 9 renderModule tests\n  / 18 package total and note reactive-service and default no-op exit coverage.\n\nTypecheck, 18 tests, build (JS + dts), and oxlint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QoimcQQ6BmtpcYgzGPTbBU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a17f242225be382e8ab738799f7986449af3301c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/a17f242225be382e8ab738799f7986449af3301c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/b122f14c5fa3e1874cadbea7a4afb8cc72c383f9","verification":{"payload":"tree a17f242225be382e8ab738799f7986449af3301c\nparent a473db4297490ecde9fee02f6dd78c764d2a844d\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784198581 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784198581 +0200\n\nfeat(vue): add @modular-vue/testing renderModule (PR-24) (#68)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/testing renderModule (PR-24)\n\nPort react-router-testing/src/render-module.tsx to @modular-vue/testing.\nrenderModule renders a module in isolation across entry-point, route-based\n(createRoutes), and legacy component-only shapes, providing the shared\ndependencies, slots, and module-list injection contexts the runtime installs\nat the app root.\n\nFramework-forced deviations from the React source:\n- returns a @vue/test-utils VueWrapper (the repo-wide Vue test primitive)\n  instead of a @testing-library/react RenderResult; the three JSX context\n  providers become one defineComponent wrapper calling the provide* helpers.\n- the createRoutes path boots a memory-history router, installs it as a\n  plugin, renders <RouterView>, and awaits router.isReady() + flushPromises()\n  before returning, since vue-router resolves navigation asynchronously.\n\nDynamic slots are evaluated eagerly and provided as a static object, reusing\ncore''s buildDepsSnapshot. 7 new tests cover all three modes, the route option,\ndynamic-slot evaluation, dep/module/slot injection, and both error paths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0126RQ6QY14J7JFcDh2VyNjE\n\n* test(vue): cover reactive-service injection and default no-op exit in renderModule\n\nAdds two @modular-vue/testing renderModule tests closing coverage gaps from\nreview of PR-24:\n\n- entry mode: omitting the `exit` option falls back to a no-op, so emitting an\n  exit from the rendered entry does not throw.\n- createRoutes mode: a reactive service passed in `deps` is auto-detected into\n  the reactiveServices bucket and injected (read via useReactiveService). The\n  `deps` type models the resolved snapshot shape (Store<T> | T), so the service\n  instance is passed through a localized, documented cast — matching real-app\n  wiring.\n\nPackage total 18 tests (was 16). Typecheck, tests, and oxlint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QoimcQQ6BmtpcYgzGPTbBU\n\n* fix(vue): accept ReactiveService in renderModule deps type; address review\n\nAddresses PR-24 review comments:\n\n- render-module.ts: widen the public `deps` type to accept\n  `ReactiveService<T>` alongside `Store<T>` and the plain value, matching the\n  runtime''s auto-detection (separateDeps). Consumers no longer need a cast to\n  pass a reactive service.\n- render-module.test.ts: drop the now-unneeded cast in the reactive-service\n  test; replace the no-op `resolves.not.toThrow()` matcher on the click promise\n  with a direct await (trigger rejects if the handler throws).\n- vue-support-tracker.md: update the acceptance record to 9 renderModule tests\n  / 18 package total and note reactive-service and default no-op exit coverage.\n\nTypecheck, 18 tests, build (JS + dts), and oxlint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QoimcQQ6BmtpcYgzGPTbBU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWLW1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3iYQAArBxVUYUDzHksDQlR/OAFGo\n2g28obQqMWm5aKhXxGrM8YhfqAgbTEob3qg1d6RuGMrr/nNFT4ILvwHiPjlGCb5h\n6S/IjWcMe2RXxNk/WCBoWOqNIZorMnMjGlYV1VX8LRZNl/NRYoDp2ipQnu+zowRW\nfWlcuquO9X7qkSrSZsc0E