ecde9fee02f6dd78c764d2a844d"}],"sha":"b122f14c5fa3e1874cadbea7a4afb8cc72c383f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/b122f14c5fa3e1874cadbea7a4afb8cc72c383f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/a473db4297490ecde9fee02f6dd78c764d2a844d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T08:57:14Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T08:57:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @modular-vue/runtime zones and route data (PR-23) (#67)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/runtime zones and route data (PR-23)\n\nAdd the zones/route-data composables to @modular-vue/runtime, mirroring\nthe React runtime''s zones.ts, active-zones.ts, and route-data.ts:\n\n- useZones<TZones>() — merged zone components read off route.matched\n  meta, deepest-wins.\n- useRouteData<TRouteData>() — the relaxed-typing counterpart (same\n  merge, no component constraint on values).\n- useActiveZones<TZones>(activeModuleId?) — unifies route zones with the\n  active tab-based module''s zones descriptor field; module zones win.\n\nAll three read useRoute().matched and funnel through core''s\nmergeRouteStaticData with the dev-only override warner. Composables\nreturn a ComputedRef (recomputing on navigation), matching the reactive\nRef convention of @modular-vue/vue''s useSlots; useActiveZones accepts a\nMaybeRefOrGetter so a reactive active-tab selection stays reactive.\n\nExtend the framework-neutral warner in @modular-frontend/core:\nRouteDataRuntimeLabel += \"@modular-vue/runtime\", RouteDataFieldLabel +=\n\"meta\", and readMatchId falls back to a matched record''s name/path since\nvue-router exposes neither id nor routeId.\n\n49 new tests (zones, active-zones, route-data, slots) port the React\nsuites case-for-case; package total 107. Core, both React runtimes, and\nthe Vue runtime all pass; typecheck, build, and lint are green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015zfvwMLDSCygodBqUJbNq1\n\n* docs: don''t rerun tests or check formatting after oxfmt\n\nAdd CLAUDE.md guidance that formatting never changes runtime behavior\n(so tests need not rerun) and that oxfmt --write is authoritative (so a\nseparate --check pass is unnecessary and misleading from a subpath).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015zfvwMLDSCygodBqUJbNq1\n\n* test(vue): cover route-driven recompute; drop `as any` in slot tests\n\nAddress two review findings on PR-23:\n\n- Add a navigation recompute test to zones.test.ts and route-data.test.ts.\n  Each mutates a reactive `route.matched` and asserts the same ComputedRef\n  reflects the new deepest match — locking in the reactive-source behavior\n  that is the headline deviation from the React ports (which none of the\n  existing single-read tests exercised).\n- Replace the `as any` casts in slots.test.ts with typed narrowing: `fn1`/\n  `fn2` are annotated `(): Partial<TestSlots>` so no cast is needed, and the\n  null-returning factory uses `null as unknown as ReturnType<DynamicSlotFactory>`.\n\nPackage tests: 109 passed, no type errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EGtACmRRdJASHLpCds3EDu\n\n* test: cover readMatchId name/path fallbacks; split null/undefined slot case\n\nAddress the two open CodeRabbit review threads on PR-23:\n\n- route-data-warn.test.ts: add coverage for the new `readMatchId` fallbacks —\n  a string `name`, a `path`, and a symbol-valued `name` that must fall through\n  to `path` rather than be stringified into the route ID. Existing id/routeId/\n  empty cases are preserved.\n- slots.test.ts: split \"skips factory that returns null/undefined\" into\n  separate null and undefined cases so the undefined branch is actually\n  exercised.\n- vue-support-tracker.md: reconcile the PR-23 test counts with reality\n  (vue-router-runtime 110, and the route-data-warn suite now covers the\n  name/path/symbol fallbacks).\n\nfrontend-core: 277 passed. @modular-vue/runtime: 110 passed. No type errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EGtACmRRdJASHLpCds3EDu\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"96eea738facccc6c916398cc2da67e4928ab816d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/96eea738facccc6c916398cc2da67e4928ab816d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/a473db4297490ecde9fee02f6dd78c764d2a844d","verification":{"payload":"tree 96eea738facccc6c916398cc2da67e4928ab816d\nparent a94d4eb68967639dd74302407bfe57e94f560f9a\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1784192234 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784192234 +0200\n\nfeat(vue): add @modular-vue/runtime zones and route data (PR-23) (#67)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/runtime zones and route data (PR-23)\n\nAdd the zones/route-data composables to @modular-vue/runtime, mirroring\nthe React runtime''s zones.ts, active-zones.ts, and route-data.ts:\n\n- useZones<TZones>() — merged zone components read off route.matched\n  meta, deepest-wins.\n- useRouteData<TRouteData>() — the relaxed-typing counterpart (same\n  merge, no component constraint on values).\n- useActiveZones<TZones>(activeModuleId?) — unifies route zones with the\n  active tab-based module''s zones descriptor field; module zones win.\n\nAll three read useRoute().matched and funnel through core''s\nmergeRouteStaticData with the dev-only override warner. Composables\nreturn a ComputedRef (recomputing on navigation), matching the reactive\nRef convention of @modular-vue/vue''s useSlots; useActiveZones accepts a\nMaybeRefOrGetter so a reactive active-tab selection stays reactive.\n\nExtend the framework-neutral warner in @modular-frontend/core:\nRouteDataRuntimeLabel += \"@modular-vue/runtime\", RouteDataFieldLabel +=\n\"meta\", and readMatchId falls back to a matched record''s name/path since\nvue-router exposes neither id nor routeId.\n\n49 new tests (zones, active-zones, route-data, slots) port the React\nsuites case-for-case; package total 107. Core, both React runtimes, and\nthe Vue runtime all pass; typecheck, build, and lint are green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015zfvwMLDSCygodBqUJbNq1\n\n* docs: don''t rerun tests or check formatting after oxfmt\n\nAdd CLAUDE.md guidance that formatting never changes runtime behavior\n(so tests need not rerun) and that oxfmt --write is authoritative (so a\nseparate --check pass is unnecessary and misleading from a subpath).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015zfvwMLDSCygodBqUJbNq1\n\n* test(vue): cover route-driven recompute; drop `as any` in slot tests\n\nAddress two review findings on PR-23:\n\n- Add a navigation recompute test to zones.test.ts and route-data.test.ts.\n  Each mutates a reactive `route.matched` and asserts the same ComputedRef\n  reflects the new deepest match — locking in the reactive-source behavior\n  that is the headline deviation from the React ports (which none of the\n  existing single-read tests exercised).\n- Replace the `as any` casts in slots.test.ts with typed narrowing: `fn1`/\n  `fn2` are annotated `(): Partial<TestSlots>` so no cast is needed, and the\n  null-returning factory uses `null as unknown as ReturnType<DynamicSlotFactory>`.\n\nPackage tests: 109 passed, no type errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EGtACmRRdJASHLpCds3EDu\n\n* test: cover readMatchId name/path fallbacks; split null/undefined slot case\n\nAddress the two open CodeRabbit review threads on PR-23:\n\n- route-data-warn.test.ts: add coverage for the new `readMatchId` fallbacks —\n  a string `name`, a `path`, and a symbol-valued `name` that must fall through\n  to `path` rather than be stringified into the route ID. Existing id/routeId/\n  empty cases are preserved.\n- slots.test.ts: split \"skips factory that returns null/undefined\" into\n  separate null and undefined cases so the undefined branch is actually\n  exercised.\n- vue-support-tracker.md: reconcile the PR-23 test counts with reality\n  (vue-router-runtime 110, and the route-data-warn suite now covers the\n  name/path/symbol fallbacks).\n\nfrontend-core: 277 passed. @modular-vue/runtime: 110 passed. No type errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EGtACmRRdJASHLpCds3EDu\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWJzrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVRMQACIGsfV1KJ5ZTIoV4i9SX0mQ\nlaLaQNLVWVodkMfOfNvsP5uiFfJAjFb8hiDxIuta7zULGd