d74302407bfe57e94f560f9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/a94d4eb68967639dd74302407bfe57e94f560f9a"}],"sha":"a473db4297490ecde9fee02f6dd78c764d2a844d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/a473db4297490ecde9fee02f6dd78c764d2a844d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/a94d4eb68967639dd74302407bfe57e94f560f9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T15:46:16Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T15:46:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(angular): add @modular-angular/angular store bridge and DI (PR-A10) (#64)\n\n* feat(angular): add @modular-angular/angular store bridge and DI (PR-A10)\n\nFirst package of the Angular support initiative: plain-TS Angular bindings\nfor @modular-frontend/core, the analog of @modular-react/react (PR) and\n@modular-vue/vue (PR-10). No @Component code (AD3) — rolldown pipeline.\n\n- store-signal.ts: storeSignal / reactiveServiceSignal bridge a neutral\n  Store/ReactiveService into a read-only Signal (signal seeded from the\n  snapshot, pushed from subscribe, torn down via DestroyRef.onDestroy).\n  Selectors layer a computed() whose Object.is equality gives selector\n  equality. Runs in an injection context or takes an { injector } hatch;\n  assertInInjectionContext gives the NG0203-style early error.\n- context.ts: createSharedInjectors → injectStore/injectService/\n  injectReactiveService/injectOptional (analog of createSharedHooks /\n  createSharedComposables).\n- scoped-store.ts, modules/navigation/slots contexts: typed InjectionTokens\n  + provide* factories + inject* accessors. provideDynamicSlots replaces the\n  Vue DynamicSlotsProvider component as a plain provider factory.\n- injection-context.ts: framework-forced runInContext / splitSelectorOptions\n  helper (no React/Vue analog).\n\n43 tests port the PR-10 Vue inventory case-for-case on a zoneless TestBed;\npackage test / typecheck / vite build (JS + dts) pass. Tracker updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(angular): address PR-A10 review findings\n\nCorrectness:\n- storeSignal/reactiveServiceSignal: wrap `subscribe` in an arrow so a\n  method-based Store/ReactiveService keeps its `this` binding (getState was\n  already wrapped; subscribe was passed bare). Matches the Vue binding.\n- requireDep/suggestInjector/injectOptional: use `Object.hasOwn` instead of\n  `key in map`, so a key colliding with an Object.prototype member\n  (`constructor`, `toString`, …) is not mistaken for a registered dependency.\n- injectScoped: run the injection-context guard before `getOrCreate`, so a\n  call that fails the NG0203 check no longer creates and leaks a scope.\n\nCleanup:\n- Add shared `injectRequired(token, message)` helper; collapse the four\n  copy-pasted \"inject token or throw within a modular app\" blocks\n  (shared deps, modules, navigation, slots) onto it.\n- Export `subscribeSignal` and reuse it in `provideDynamicSlots` instead of\n  re-implementing the signal-seed + subscribe + DestroyRef teardown block.\n\nDocs:\n- README: note the `{ injector }` escape hatch is for one-shot reads, not\n  repeated calls (each opens a subscription released only on injector destroy).\n\nAdds regression tests for the this-binding and prototype-member cases\n(46 tests). typecheck, test, and vite build pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c1827e32dc58459f902e6b54ecb034cb28b07404","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/c1827e32dc58459f902e6b54ecb034cb28b07404"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/a94d4eb68967639dd74302407bfe57e94f560f9a","verification":{"payload":"tree c1827e32dc58459f902e6b54ecb034cb28b07404\nparent de7bb6a34309ad79b9abc54b5d943e2192178d3f\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1783352776 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783352776 +0300\n\nfeat(angular): add @modular-angular/angular store bridge and DI (PR-A10) (#64)\n\n* feat(angular): add @modular-angular/angular store bridge and DI (PR-A10)\n\nFirst package of the Angular support initiative: plain-TS Angular bindings\nfor @modular-frontend/core, the analog of @modular-react/react (PR) and\n@modular-vue/vue (PR-10). No @Component code (AD3) — rolldown pipeline.\n\n- store-signal.ts: storeSignal / reactiveServiceSignal bridge a neutral\n  Store/ReactiveService into a read-only Signal (signal seeded from the\n  snapshot, pushed from subscribe, torn down via DestroyRef.onDestroy).\n  Selectors layer a computed() whose Object.is equality gives selector\n  equality. Runs in an injection context or takes an { injector } hatch;\n  assertInInjectionContext gives the NG0203-style early error.\n- context.ts: createSharedInjectors → injectStore/injectService/\n  injectReactiveService/injectOptional (analog of createSharedHooks /\n  createSharedComposables).\n- scoped-store.ts, modules/navigation/slots contexts: typed InjectionTokens\n  + provide* factories + inject* accessors. provideDynamicSlots replaces the\n  Vue DynamicSlotsProvider component as a plain provider factory.\n- injection-context.ts: framework-forced runInContext / splitSelectorOptions\n  helper (no React/Vue analog).\n\n43 tests port the PR-10 Vue inventory case-for-case on a zoneless TestBed;\npackage test / typecheck / vite build (JS + dts) pass. Tracker updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(angular): address PR-A10 review findings\n\nCorrectness:\n- storeSignal/reactiveServiceSignal: wrap `subscribe` in an arrow so a\n  method-based Store/ReactiveService keeps its `this` binding (getState was\n  already wrapped; subscribe was passed bare). Matches the Vue binding.\n- requireDep/suggestInjector/injectOptional: use `Object.hasOwn` instead of\n  `key in map`, so a key colliding with an Object.prototype member\n  (`constructor`, `toString`, …) is not mistaken for a registered dependency.\n- injectScoped: run the injection-context guard before `getOrCreate`, so a\n  call that fails the NG0203 check no longer creates and leaks a scope.\n\nCleanup:\n- Add shared `injectRequired(token, message)` helper; collapse the four\n  copy-pasted \"inject token or throw within a modular app\" blocks\n  (shared deps, modules, navigation, slots) onto it.\n- Export `subscribeSignal` and reuse it in `provideDynamicSlots` instead of\n  re-implementing the signal-seed + subscribe + DestroyRef teardown block.\n\nDocs:\n- README: note the `{ injector }` escape hatch is for one-shot reads, not\n  repeated calls (each opens a subscription released only on injector destroy).\n\nAdds regression tests for the this-binding and prototype-member cases\n(46 tests). typecheck, test, and vite build pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS83ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhPoQADmJuxOAfULDfrG4GKnluq8K\nQ7cR1lgb1oymea/Lo5Y4rpyyzSRgr9ziG75xQseFlewk2d0GFbYJAL7llQ1OBKB7\nvdhCj7UiDXRBUS7Kb3OEZVcki/icDIgkZwguJ7lAc05xAJnlVellLYI72ORZLSWl\nh5SLMaQGuulISZp7xmjTdZhCEn3DONR5EfYwGMRugUEt2rffyw/ugj7iU/GIM9bK\nc+nF3P+jKqVszl9sK5rwU2rrq0n7JxvL+fIhQYaX2ECqB03uWHgkWKP3N8dZybWs\n5dgVSay7VNGYTlbZhLlKV7sJd0ZpzjUUKn2QTS4PKIwOGr76gl3kqFjPh4mAs9hd\nWAz0MRCtF1Q+FPVaINV8AZ3uB99G9wbeSe1Q/xHS6W4hiHEYhi/YvTkac9nPM/qk\nyhnorYAQRHQXnjLJMr/oua9bp7SLYPeW2ehQ0admTaJaaFM3ATWDn4poZK1a3v6J\nZsezxoNaBwJs+peCCPece0fmSFJw36QNYzxchNZXZDD3hODQ/tOwp8tNwAX5C5FS\nrM/cWjpq+v52S5nyeQ8RZlWUH1XxMXL9kTOxbZkqXDeNUVZvpJWGXlgvGMOq7cAg\nG/bx32knGBBqRfEvYXjCW1to+piAZI5HV2XHLKE4hJ8j4+dPp382YQLKFuSTIv+n\ndDJ5f8Ge9zBbCgGrXu2q\n=gluw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T15:46:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/a94d4eb68967639dd74302407bfe57e94f560f9a","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGE5NGQ0ZWI2ODk2NzYzOWRkNzQzMDI0MDdiZmU1N2U5NGY1NjBmOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/de7bb6a34309ad79b9abc54b5d943e2192178d3f","sha":"de7bb6a34309ad79b9abc54b5d943e2192178d3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/de7bb6a34309ad79b9abc54b5d943e2192178d3f"}],"sha":"a94d4eb68967639dd74302407bfe57e94f560f9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/a94d4eb68967639dd74302407bfe57e94f560f9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/de7bb6a34309ad79b9abc54b5d943e2192178d3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T15:24:25Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T15:24:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @modular-vue/runtime route building and app shell (PR-22) (#65)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/runtime route building and app shell (PR-22)\n\nSecond half of the vue-router runtime: the router-owning resolve() entry, the\nroute-builder that grafts module routes via router.addRoute(), the provider\nlayer, and the auth guard.\n\n- route-builder.ts: graftModuleRoutes adds each eager module''s createRoutes()\n  output onto a live router (top-level or under a named parentRouteName\n  boundary); headless modules are skipped, a falsy createRoutes() throws with\n  the module id. createLazyModuleRoute registers a basePath catch-all whose\n  beforeEnter loads the descriptor, grafts its subtree, removes the placeholder,\n  and redirects so vue-router re-resolves into the real routes. An in-flight\n  promise guards against double-loading under concurrent navigation.\n- providers.ts: createModularProvidersPlugin (app-level app.provide for the\n  router-owning path, where the app root is the user''s own <router-view> host)\n  and createModularProvidersComponent (a Providers component for framework\n  mode), over one ModularProvidersConfig. Dynamic slots route through the shared\n  DynamicSlotsProvider in the component form and a shallowRef + slotsSignal\n  subscription in the plugin form.\n- app.ts: createModularApp(registry, options), a thin convenience over\n  registry.resolve so app.use(createModularApp(registry, { router })) is one\n  line.\n- registry.ts: resolve() (single-use) grafts routes, installs authGuard via\n  router.beforeEach, and returns an ApplicationManifest that is itself a Vue\n  plugin carrying router + resolved data. resolveManifest() now also returns a\n  Providers component and eager module routes. resolve()/resolveManifest() are\n  mutually exclusive (mode machinery ported from the React registry).\n\nvue-router registers routes at runtime, so there is no route tree to compose:\nbuildRouteTree becomes graftModuleRoutes over an already-created router, the\nauth boundary is a real addRoute parent (not a pathless-layout trick), and the\nguard is a plain router.beforeEach reading to.meta. The Vue manifest is an\ninstallable plugin rather than a React-style App component. Framework-mode lazy\nmodules stay unwired (grafting needs a router reference) and keep a reworded\ndev warning; resolve() wires them end-to-end.\n\nReact sources: react-router-runtime/route-builder.tsx, providers.tsx, app.tsx,\nand the resolve()/resolveManifest() machinery in registry.ts.\n\n28 new tests (route-builder.test.ts, app.test.ts, resolve-manifest.test.ts);\npackage total 58. Workspace typecheck (120 tasks) and vite build (JS + dts)\npass. Updates the Vue support tracker status board and PR-22 writeup.\n\n* fix(vue): address PR-22 review findings in @modular-vue/runtime\n\nroute-builder:\n- Lazy load failures no longer brick the subtree. The beforeEnter guard\n  resets its in-flight promise on failure so a transient chunk 404 / offline\n  blip retries on the next navigation instead of caching the rejection.\n- A lazy descriptor that grafts no routes now throws with the module id\n  instead of removing the placeholder and stranding the user on a dead route.\n- normalizeBasePath collapses the root (\"/\" or \"\") to \"\" so a root-mounted\n  lazy module gets a valid \"/:pathMatch(.*)*\" catch-all, not \"//:pathMatch(.*)*\".\n- Extract collectEagerRoutes, shared by graftModuleRoutes and the registry''s\n  buildModuleRoutesOnly, so the skip/flatten/validate contract lives once.\n\nregistry:\n- resolve() builds the assembly before committing to resolve-mode, so a\n  recoverable validation / dependency / onRegister failure stays retryable\n  instead of permanently locking the registry (matching resolveManifest).\n\nproviders:\n- The plugin''s slotsSignal subscription is disposed on app.onUnmount, so\n  installing a manifest on more than one app no longer leaks a listener.\n- provideModularContexts centralizes the four-context provide block shared by\n  the plugin and component forms.\n\nAdds tests for lazy retry-after-failure, no-routes throw, root basePath, and\nresolve() retryability. Package total 62 tests, typecheck clean.\n\n* style(docs): apply oxfmt to vue-support-tracker.md\n\nFixes the failing Lint CI check (oxfmt emphasis normalization).","tree":{"sha":"8031021b147493e799e08bae6197b3d3da943849","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/8031021b147493e799e08bae6197b3d3da943849"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/de7bb6a34309ad79b9abc54b5d943e2192178d3f","verification":{"payload":"tree 8031021b147493e799e08bae6197b3d3da943849\nparent e394b2511f3f8851a53e85ea7987d68aab8f0193\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1783351465 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783351465 +0300\n\nfeat(vue): add @modular-vue/runtime route building and app shell (PR-22) (#65)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/runtime route building and app shell (PR-22)\n\nSecond half of the vue-router runtime: the router-owning resolve() entry, the\nroute-builder that grafts module routes via router.addRoute(), the provider\nlayer, and the auth guard.\n\n- route-builder.ts: graftModuleRoutes adds each eager module''s createRoutes()\n  output onto a live router (top-level or under a named parentRouteName\n  boundary); headless modules are skipped, a falsy createRoutes() throws with\n  the module id. createLazyModuleRoute registers a basePath catch-all whose\n  beforeEnter loads the descriptor, grafts its subtree, removes the placeholder,\n  and redirects so vue-router re-resolves into the real routes. An in-flight\n  promise guards against double-loading under concurrent navigation.\n- providers.ts: createModularProvidersPlugin (app-level app.provide for the\n  router-owning path, where the app root is the user''s own <router-view> host)\n  and createModularProvidersComponent (a Providers component for framework\n  mode), over one ModularProvidersConfig. Dynamic slots route through the shared\n  DynamicSlotsProvider in the component form and a shallowRef + slotsSignal\n  subscription in the plugin form.\n- app.ts: createModularApp(registry, options), a thin convenience over\n  registry.resolve so app.use(createModularApp(registry, { router })) is one\n  line.\n- registry.ts: resolve() (single-use) grafts routes, installs authGuard via\n  router.beforeEach, and returns an ApplicationManifest that is itself a Vue\n  plugin carrying router + resolved data. resolveManifest() now also returns a\n  Providers component and eager module routes. resolve()/resolveManifest() are\n  mutually exclusive (mode machinery ported from the React registry).\n\nvue-router registers routes at runtime, so there is no route tree to compose:\nbuildRouteTree becomes graftModuleRoutes over an already-created router, the\nauth boundary is a real addRoute parent (not a pathless-layout trick), and the\nguard is a plain router.beforeEach reading to.meta. The Vue manifest is an\ninstallable plugin rather than a React-style App component. Framework-mode lazy\nmodules stay unwired (grafting needs a router reference) and keep a reworded\ndev warning; resolve() wires them end-to-end.\n\nReact sources: react-router-runtime/route-builder.tsx, providers.tsx, app.tsx,\nand the resolve()/resolveManifest() machinery in registry.ts.\n\n28 new tests (route-builder.test.ts, app.test.ts, resolve-manifest.test.ts);\npackage total 58. Workspace typecheck (120 tasks) and vite build (JS + dts)\npass. Updates the Vue support tracker status board and PR-22 writeup.\n\n* fix(vue): address PR-22 review findings in @modular-vue/runtime\n\nroute-builder:\n- Lazy load failures no longer brick the subtree. The beforeEnter guard\n  resets its in-flight promise on failure so a transient chunk 404 / offline\n  blip retries on the next navigation instead of caching the rejection.\n- A lazy descriptor that grafts no routes now throws with the module id\n  instead of removing the placeholder and stranding the user on a dead route.\n- normalizeBasePath collapses the root (\"/\" or \"\") to \"\" so a root-mounted\n  lazy module gets a valid \"/:pathMatch(.*)*\" catch-all, not \"//:pathMatch(.*)*\".\n- Extract collectEagerRoutes, shared by graftModuleRoutes and the registry''s\n  buildModuleRoutesOnly, so the skip/flatten/validate contract lives once.\n\nregistry:\n- resolve() builds the assembly before committing to resolve-mode, so a\n  recoverable validation / dependency / onRegister failure stays retryable\n  instead of permanently locking the registry (matching resolveManifest).\n\nproviders:\n- The plugin''s slotsSignal subscription is disposed on app.onUnmount, so\n  installing a manifest on more than one app no longer leaks a listener.\n- provideModularContexts centralizes the four-context provide block shared by\n  the plugin and component forms.\n\nAdds tests for lazy retry-after-failure, no-routes throw, root basePath, and\nresolve() retryability. Package total 62 tests, typecheck clean.\n\n* style(docs): apply oxfmt to vue-support-tracker.md\n\nFixes the failing Lint CI check (oxfmt emphasis normalization).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS8ipCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0YgQAHKp1FYKKLlv56yQBaNxqyDU\nJAtyX3N5SUGLE6HrFYPJHnAL9aKvvAbEhqZTKHgK4b6At2YC0ouJQwSQ+iy717EQ\nfNc8+JKMnIX4v/AUYPSaHyqjzSQIDFmQc4bpJI2cvkOhYPPYMwYHbG21Snbru1yC\nBhAhkNYiebwI0BswGDx9noyx5Bx+9Ie4WgsPqM1bJM9J2CHDg4SeOg5FEvBnUBgv\nW8cPtWRBjgtEWgW75+DSsl1MwL2tFI+65mD423pEpdyz8Gr6MVxfs3feTDodr5b+\nsQo5NSjnDnTj0dTUPz5CcTioL+XLSSrCwDEHhD2gSPnjRy2zP44t96T33zgo9I+0\nE1tcG2NknD4MnpY1mQAgzmb/r3ibS5DmJo7+oRQarOWFTIcSSCLMXRHzR+GyOXA2\nfJRl6MM1G0p427dlJKt55xcs3S44XnCMQJeZBWRySQOG8R+Uaa57prwSjlSQ38lw\nEvQH636h+CcMJ3jgcYRfRsNMPGykCvpGvpWNS6JPgnrKzqDPDo3ghrGeiGoE68Df\nJBEmCLiKo/QmxoSJt+cO3vYN9a6TY/cGqGMgiUqv91GZVZIX4GF3AqvMPtZv0Ipw\njLBmezh4+y/l7RIwsOXABxNaHxCKn9RjXsfP0WEi2+8iHYyHm/p5t55HrBpSaR7L\nhiPtTzeqMPTdiXlFSRdv\n=syOO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T15:24:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/de7bb6a34309ad79b9abc54b5d943e2192178d3f","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGRlN2JiNmEzNDMwOWFkNzliOWFiYzU0YjVkOTQzZTIxOTIxNzhkM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/e394b2511f3f8851a53e85ea7987d68aab8f0193","sha":"e394b2511f3f8851a53e85ea7987d68aab8f0193","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/e394b2511f3f8851a53e85ea7987d68aab8f0193"}],"sha":"de7bb6a34309ad79b9abc54b5d943e2192178d3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/de7bb6a34309ad79b9abc54b5d943e2192178d3f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/e394b2511f3f8851a53e85ea7987d68aab8f0193/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T14:31:59Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T14:31:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @modular-vue/runtime registry (PR-21) (#63)\n\n* feat(vue): add @vue-router-modules/runtime registry (PR-21)\n\nPort registry.ts from @react-router-modules/runtime as the first half of the\nvue-router runtime: createRegistry with register/registerLazy/use plugin\nmachinery and an idempotent resolveManifest that assembles navigation, slots,\nmodule descriptors, and plugin extensions. Validation and the deps snapshot\nreuse the neutral @modular-frontend/core helpers directly.\n\nThe router-owning resolve() entry, the Providers context component, and the\nrouter.addRoute() route-builder are deferred to PR-22, matching the boundary\nthe @modular-vue/vue context.ts note already anticipates. The real Vue journeys\nplugin lands in PR-30/PR-32, so plugin machinery is covered here with a\nsynthetic journeys-shaped plugin (registry-plugins.test.ts).\n\nReact source: packages/react-router-runtime/src/registry.ts\n\n30 tests (registry.test.ts, registry-plugins.test.ts, registry.test-d.ts);\nworkspace typecheck (120 tasks) and vite build (JS + dts) pass. Updates the\nVue support tracker status board and PR-21 writeup.\n\n* fix(vue): address PR-21 registry review findings\n\n- use() collision guard: check Object.hasOwn(registry, key) instead of\n  `key in registry`, so a plugin contributing a method named after an\n  Object.prototype key (toString, hasOwnProperty, valueOf, ...) is no\n  longer falsely rejected. Adds a covering test.\n- registerLazy: warn (dev only) when lazy modules are registered, since\n  route grafting is deferred to PR-22 and they otherwise contribute\n  nothing to the resolved manifest with no diagnostic. Adds a covering\n  test asserting the modules are absent but the warning fires.\n- CommonAssembly doc comment now lists every field carried inert for\n  PR-22 (stores/services/reactiveServices as well as slotsSignal/\n  dynamicSlotFactories/slotFilter), so they no longer read as accidental\n  dead code.\n\n* refactor(vue): consolidate router packages under @modular-vue scope\n\nRename @vue-router-modules/{core,runtime} to @modular-vue/{core,runtime}.\nVue has a single router (vue-router), so a router-named scope carries no\ndisambiguating information the way @react-router-modules vs\n@tanstack-react-modules does on the React side. Folding into @modular-vue\ndrops a namespace and sits these packages beside @modular-vue/vue and\n@modular-vue/testing.\n\nNames stay unprefixed (core/runtime, not router-core/router-runtime): the\nrouter-neutral core already lives at @modular-frontend/core, so there is no\n@modular-vue/core framework-alias to collide with.\n\nUpdates package names and deps, source imports and error prefixes, both\npackage READMEs, packages/vue/README.md, the tracker (D1 decision + package\nmap) and port-analysis, and regenerates the lockfile. Both packages are\nunpublished, so there are no consumers to migrate.","tree":{"sha":"ae8e91cccab40164761c75f93376c0d4363b6ff7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/ae8e91cccab40164761c75f93376c0d4363b6ff7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/e394b2511f3f8851a53e85ea7987d68aab8f0193","verification":{"payload":"tree ae8e91cccab40164761c75f93376c0d4363b6ff7\nparent c876cc3cffd4a4bcce1e3f21f4f78464de2af774\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1783348319 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783348319 +0300\n\nfeat(vue): add @modular-vue/runtime registry (PR-21) (#63)\n\n* feat(vue): add @vue-router-modules/runtime registry (PR-21)\n\nPort registry.ts from @react-router-modules/runtime as the first half of the\nvue-router runtime: createRegistry with register/registerLazy/use plugin\nmachinery and an idempotent resolveManifest that assembles navigation, slots,\nmodule descriptors, and plugin extensions. Validation and the deps snapshot\nreuse the neutral @modular-frontend/core helpers directly.\n\nThe router-owning resolve() entry, the Providers context component, and the\nrouter.addRoute() route-builder are deferred to PR-22, matching the boundary\nthe @modular-vue/vue context.ts note already anticipates. The real Vue journeys\nplugin lands in PR-30/PR-32, so plugin machinery is covered here with a\nsynthetic journeys-shaped plugin (registry-plugins.test.ts).\n\nReact source: packages/react-router-runtime/src/registry.ts\n\n30 tests (registry.test.ts, registry-plugins.test.ts, registry.test-d.ts);\nworkspace typecheck (120 tasks) and vite build (JS + dts) pass. Updates the\nVue support tracker status board and PR-21 writeup.\n\n* fix(vue): address PR-21 registry review findings\n\n- use() collision guard: check Object.hasOwn(registry, key) instead of\n  `key in registry`, so a plugin contributing a method named after an\n  Object.prototype key (toString, hasOwnProperty, valueOf, ...) is no\n  longer falsely rejected. Adds a covering test.\n- registerLazy: warn (dev only) when lazy modules are registered, since\n  route grafting is deferred to PR-22 and they otherwise contribute\n  nothing to the resolved manifest with no diagnostic. Adds a covering\n  test asserting the modules are absent but the warning fires.\n- CommonAssembly doc comment now lists every field carried inert for\n  PR-22 (stores/services/reactiveServices as well as slotsSignal/\n  dynamicSlotFactories/slotFilter), so they no longer read as accidental\n  dead code.\n\n* refactor(vue): consolidate router packages under @modular-vue scope\n\nRename @vue-router-modules/{core,runtime} to @modular-vue/{core,runtime}.\nVue has a single router (vue-router), so a router-named scope carries no\ndisambiguating information the way @react-router-modules vs\n@tanstack-react-modules does on the React side. Folding into @modular-vue\ndrops a namespace and sits these packages beside @modular-vue/vue and\n@modular-vue/testing.\n\nNames stay unprefixed (core/runtime, not router-core/router-runtime): the\nrouter-neutral core already lives at @modular-frontend/core, so there is no\n@modular-vue/core framework-alias to collide with.\n\nUpdates package names and deps, source imports and error prefixes, both\npackage READMEs, packages/vue/README.md, the tracker (D1 decision + package\nmap) and port-analysis, and regenerates the lockfile. Both packages are\nunpublished, so there are no consumers to migrate.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS7xfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiBsQAIF6nVz7jFqH5DqOa55o/O3W\ntLctoyG198JiOAwcp4fQZ+N/2I7eayz2oWHz/duxMDPkwJLbO79NntEBlEbSbghy\nuWd8G9vBAGObFBEprxwN1tN43jpe4BUdPT/QdxoOfIxNNkkpNWciKjVFaUmrlRKi\n+XOSET9a1djNfOud/5n9wOlyR72tgoxWhicqaK+2L9/ow2JHLe/n9JarJoZMjQuF\nt9RQgOIU+jhVzh/X3hMwVyWL7YzzzIpkwg30l3aKFMIbzV1XE8jYZb9taxCArG+0\n+d6+qggaVkTb/mFZsynhA59PfQlOD9tS7YnA8wB/ehfw9C9G4teMcPgR6hH2Uqnq\nwcGsKlZwMOfLiTn3DZBsIVEEREMTsg4ZM/pLeMVwnC9E8UbPJdBLChuBMeIql59K\nxDaYYgmbZJuqXxGNgACZhyuw2dDpmeORNCq92AaKz9/IOJVsXosnznR2+v/Gsx6E\nSzlGpG7biEy8OTlSJCRAbBC/dvlLBqFG7bKsT026Py78PpZD4oh4YM6OQhwIySSG\nkZjokP2v/dn9y6eIka9qO176hpHLYSbCe20lScsaWlturnWqSC3iSVzPI8f9IiI8\n45gg2CwlSM3StqJcbj12XUYW6Ka+nfsO6KTCtjwbzXY88GzxtPmjYhKZEU2zMBC0\n6erHhajo2ykO/4+HZ2Vs\n=N6va\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T14:31:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/e394b2511f3f8851a53e85ea7987d68aab8f0193","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGUzOTRiMjUxMWYzZjg4NTFhNTNlODVlYTc5ODdkNjhhYWI4ZjAxOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/c876cc3cffd4a4bcce1e3f21f4f78464de2af774","sha":"c876cc3cffd4a4bcce1e3f21f4f78464de2af774","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c876cc3cffd4a4bcce1e3f21f4f78464de2af774"}],"sha":"e394b2511f3f8851a53e85ea7987d68aab8f0193","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/e394b2511f3f8851a53e85ea7987d68aab8f0193"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c876cc3cffd4a4bcce1e3f21f4f78464de2af774/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T13:23:44Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T13:23:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @vue-router-modules/core (PR-20) (#61)\n\n* feat(vue): add @vue-router-modules/core (PR-20)\n\nKick off Phase 2 of the Vue initiative with the vue-router family core,\nmirroring @react-router-modules/core.\n\n- types.ts: vue-router ModuleDescriptor whose createRoutes() returns\n  RouteRecordRaw | RouteRecordRaw[], plus LazyModuleDescriptor\n  (addRoute-friendly, React Router-shaped) and AnyModuleDescriptor.\n- define-module.ts / define-slots.ts: identity helpers over the\n  vue-router descriptor.\n- route-meta.ts: ModuleRouteMeta helper and the app-level RouteMeta\n  augmentation pattern the runtime (PR-23) reads for zones and static data.\n- index.ts: re-exports the shared composables and scoped store from\n  @modular-vue/vue and the detection helpers from @modular-frontend/core,\n  rather than reimplementing them (no zustand split on the Vue side).\n\n15 tests (define-slots port, re-export barrel smoke, descriptor-inference\ntype tests). Workspace typecheck and vite build pass. Updates the tracker.\n\n* test(vue-router-core): drop unnecessary happy-dom test environment\n\nNone of this package''s tests touch the DOM: the .test-d.ts files are\ntype-only, index.test.ts asserts barrel resolution, and createScopedStore\nis pure state. The happy-dom environment was undeclared in package.json and\nresolved only via pnpm hoisting of a sibling copy. Run under the default\nnode environment instead, matching react-router-core (which has no vitest\nconfig and no happy-dom dependency). All 15 tests still pass.","tree":{"sha":"0a976541e1bf991b56f5a2f10682caed63b8ca0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/0a976541e1bf991b56f5a2f10682caed63b8ca0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/c876cc3cffd4a4bcce1e3f21f4f78464de2af774","verification":{"payload":"tree 0a976541e1bf991b56f5a2f10682caed63b8ca0e\nparent 82f21e685da06f3d84ee2b65946b499c0d2978e1\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1783344224 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783344224 +0300\n\nfeat(vue): add @vue-router-modules/core (PR-20) (#61)\n\n* feat(vue): add @vue-router-modules/core (PR-20)\n\nKick off Phase 2 of the Vue initiative with the vue-router family core,\nmirroring @react-router-modules/core.\n\n- types.ts: vue-router ModuleDescriptor whose createRoutes() returns\n  RouteRecordRaw | RouteRecordRaw[], plus LazyModuleDescriptor\n  (addRoute-friendly, React Router-shaped) and AnyModuleDescriptor.\n- define-module.ts / define-slots.ts: identity helpers over the\n  vue-router descriptor.\n- route-meta.ts: ModuleRouteMeta helper and the app-level RouteMeta\n  augmentation pattern the runtime (PR-23) reads for zones and static data.\n- index.ts: re-exports the shared composables and scoped store from\n  @modular-vue/vue and the detection helpers from @modular-frontend/core,\n  rather than reimplementing them (no zustand split on the Vue side).\n\n15 tests (define-slots port, re-export barrel smoke, descriptor-inference\ntype tests). Workspace typecheck and vite build pass. Updates the tracker.\n\n* test(vue-router-core): drop unnecessary happy-dom test environment\n\nNone of this package''s tests touch the DOM: the .test-d.ts files are\ntype-only, index.test.ts asserts barrel resolution, and createScopedStore\nis pure state. The happy-dom environment was undeclared in package.json and\nresolved only via pnpm hoisting of a sibling copy. Run under the default\nnode environment instead, matching react-router-core (which has no vitest\nconfig and no happy-dom dependency). All 15 tests still pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS6xgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqsgQADu5epFfKkNiQUA1CVwxMZTP\ncG+ZLo12Sq80ZLfKkO9PIKc9wLPH1amCuM5+9nPXU6bIqqsFqmmj/mljrYGTVhLe\nHfIdBmhXowmftv3bSsfdUB3FOncfSDZvTHFVjnoTSH7oFizPCALAyMRLpjm3iqj/\nZmUWQVXEZgxR+2BjzlArXbocYPyIZ3KNREigY7VJkvSV4Em4ggqcr8gTQ29Ria0t\nMrW0kGnqoLeDKQIwrKBBO6ICgO8WjCPHal/bfl7nTP4ksfqtv1kBpoExG4IbijgI\ni5POeDGdSK/ctQvfnFQ9Cthy0l0tGrPxfYR10mV/D+KyWHn/AtX/uvNqJTJ/p2Bz\nskSLKzR3bFXUdrBNqPCZZ/63+deLkzKIgy3j7P3od3s0mYXEOavavqjKnHY2RCCQ\naKo3ozAtunyX4Co8hqCoidcRY0doIgaA5GiG1DdV9ri2hVMNU3Ra0kOXE9H6+XgB\n7fttmGwU3XFY/HWJGRoaaZKDMkYsfCNuqT8399pBTne6o790iDhpdBKcEtUgEZQB\nttXCwTmboZmBb6S6GVYOOQSQdA/1z0//18rnxQ4PcomV/PLLDAkTfc/7O9bByY8y\n9wooAhtKhYVwGl7JORNEJcqkdfi4u9n1hVtGagtjJok5Uhwud3JeISob31QEwoCd\ni2v3Pgj2qpy/Zg49JCc/\n=a2Wl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T13:23:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/c876cc3cffd4a4bcce1e3f21f4f78464de2af774","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGM4NzZjYzNjZmZkNGE0YmNjZTFlM2YyMWY0Zjc4NDY0ZGUyYWY3NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/82f21e685da06f3d84ee2b65946b499c0d2978e1","sha":"82f21e685da06f3d84ee2b65946b499c0d2978e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/82f21e685da06f3d84ee2b65946b499c0d2978e1"}],"sha":"c876cc3cffd4a4bcce1e3f21f4f78464de2af774","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c876cc3cffd4a4bcce1e3f21f4f78464de2af774"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/82f21e685da06f3d84ee2b65946b499c0d2978e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T13:20:07Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T13:20:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(angular): document UiComponent narrowing contract (PR-A01) (#62)\n\nFirst PR of the Angular support initiative''s Phase A0 (seam\ndocumentation). No behavior change.\n\nExtends the `UiComponent` doc comment in `frontend-core/src/ui-types.ts`\nto spell out the call-arm/construct-arm asymmetry: the call arm keeps\nfunction components props-checked against `ModuleEntryProps`, while the\nconstruct arm admits zero-argument-constructor classes with the props\ntype unconsulted (verified against the repo''s strict tsconfig). Documents\nwhy class-component frameworks bind by narrowing `UiComponent` to their\nown component type (`Type<unknown>` for Angular) plus an out-of-band\ninput-shape contract enforced by an authoring helper (AD5), rather than\nleaning on the alias''s structural check.\n\nAdds `frontend-core/src/ui-types.test-d.ts` pinning the seam so a future\ntightening cannot silently break class-component bindings:\n- a zero-arg class is admitted for any `P`;\n- a DI-dependency-constructor class is admitted;\n- a class requiring an incompatible constructor param is rejected (the\n  construct arm is not an unconditional pass-through);\n- the call arm still props-checks function components.\n\nUpdates docs/angular-support-tracker.md: PR-A01 -> in review, AD5 status\nnotes the contract is now documented, and records the delivery. Existing\nentry-exit.test-d.ts assertions unchanged; frontend-core test suite green\n(274 tests).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a3206d2578ee9fd146fdeb3072fcd2ccc0738a4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/a3206d2578ee9fd146fdeb3072fcd2ccc0738a4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/82f21e685da06f3d84ee2b65946b499c0d2978e1","verification":{"payload":"tree a3206d2578ee9fd146fdeb3072fcd2ccc0738a4c\nparent a11954bd2802fb1216ed42769b5d17889d40ea34\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1783344007 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783344007 +0300\n\ndocs(angular): document UiComponent narrowing contract (PR-A01) (#62)\n\nFirst PR of the Angular support initiative''s Phase A0 (seam\ndocumentation). No behavior change.\n\nExtends the `UiComponent` doc comment in `frontend-core/src/ui-types.ts`\nto spell out the call-arm/construct-arm asymmetry: the call arm keeps\nfunction components props-checked against `ModuleEntryProps`, while the\nconstruct arm admits zero-argument-constructor classes with the props\ntype unconsulted (verified against the repo''s strict tsconfig). Documents\nwhy class-component frameworks bind by narrowing `UiComponent` to their\nown component type (`Type<unknown>` for Angular) plus an out-of-band\ninput-shape contract enforced by an authoring helper (AD5), rather than\nleaning on the alias''s structural check.\n\nAdds `frontend-core/src/ui-types.test-d.ts` pinning the seam so a future\ntightening cannot silently break class-component bindings:\n- a zero-arg class is admitted for any `P`;\n- a DI-dependency-constructor class is admitted;\n- a class requiring an incompatible constructor param is rejected (the\n  construct arm is not an unconditional pass-through);\n- the call arm still props-checks function components.\n\nUpdates docs/angular-support-tracker.md: PR-A01 -> in review, AD5 status\nnotes the contract is now documented, and records the delivery. Existing\nentry-exit.test-d.ts assertions unchanged; frontend-core test suite green\n(274 tests).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS6uHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdKsQAEKXGHV+IAiFqrIxY2gBYFVd\nR5Dcqg0jeuKYXsOrIU7MvcEB82f05HVOagzI0AC0107NSaqiisDT1QMaFmmacAm1\nSjyRNjnBELDZ8E7xQJ9ijCy0OlsgtCs7GN3bken