mit/db21126e77231a7787248a2ca747907f0ae2e1d3","sha":"db21126e77231a7787248a2ca747907f0ae2e1d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/db21126e77231a7787248a2ca747907f0ae2e1d3"}],"sha":"807b4891537b5881c5e225f25b8ff5b784cfa237","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/807b4891537b5881c5e225f25b8ff5b784cfa237"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/db21126e77231a7787248a2ca747907f0ae2e1d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T11:48:57Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T11:48:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @modular-vue/vue rendering pieces (PR-11) (#59)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/vue rendering pieces (PR-11)\n\nPort the React binding''s rendering-layer files to Vue, each the analog of\nthe same-named file in @modular-react/react:\n\n- resolve-entry.ts: resolveEntryComponent / preloadEntry over\n  defineAsyncComponent (analog of React.lazy). Memoized by entry identity;\n  lazy entries share one cachedImport closure so preload() warms the same\n  import the async wrapper awaits, the importer fires once, `.default` is\n  normalized, and a sync-throwing importer is trapped as a cached rejection.\n- error-boundary.ts: ModuleErrorBoundary via onErrorCaptured (analog of the\n  React class boundary), returning false to contain the error and swapping\n  the subtree for a notice / custom fallback.\n- module-exit.ts: ModuleExitProvider, useModuleExit, useModuleExitDispatcher,\n  moduleExitKey + event/handler types. Dispatcher provided by identity.\n- module-route.ts: ModuleRoute component + ModuleRouteExitEvent alias, with\n  single-entry auto-resolve, unknown / multi / no-entry-points notices, and\n  legacy component fallback.\n\n36 new tests port the React suites case-for-case (React-only StrictMode and\nSuspense-flash cases excepted); package suite is now 69 tests. Workspace\ntypecheck and vite build (JS + dts) pass. Updates the Vue support tracker.\n\n* fix(vue): make rendering pieces reactive to in-place prop changes\n\nAddress reactivity divergences from the React analogs where values that\nReact rebinds every render were snapshotted once in Vue `setup()`:\n\n- module-route: resolve the entry inside a `computed` so a `<router-view>`-\n  hosted `<ModuleRoute>` reused across navigation (props patched in place,\n  no `:key`) re-resolves `module`/`entry` instead of freezing the first\n  route. Bind the exit to getters over the live props so it dispatches with\n  the current `routeId`/`onExit`/resolved entry.\n- module-exit: provide the dispatcher as a getter over the live `onExit`\n  prop so a swapped provider handler reaches descendants; `useModuleExit`\n  now accepts `MaybeRefOrGetter` inputs and reads them via `toValue` at\n  dispatch time (plain values still work unchanged).\n- resolve-entry: clear the inflight slot on an async import rejection so a\n  transient chunk-fetch failure can retry (and no longer defeats\n  `defineAsyncComponent`''s remount retry); a synchronous throw stays cached\n  as before.\n\nAdds regression tests for each: in-place entry re-resolution, swapped\nonExit/localOnExit tracking, provider handler swap, and async import retry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CvssSEBSw6fkyCjvX8iA2B\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"296db74103a36814e700509247a1d33949c816ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/296db74103a36814e700509247a1d33949c816ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/db21126e77231a7787248a2ca747907f0ae2e1d3","verification":{"payload":"tree 296db74103a36814e700509247a1d33949c816ef\nparent 4d1fc3c1bafbd5027f368278f16f5915c496ca6b\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1783338537 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783338537 +0300\n\nfeat(vue): add @modular-vue/vue rendering pieces (PR-11) (#59)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/vue rendering pieces (PR-11)\n\nPort the React binding''s rendering-layer files to Vue, each the analog of\nthe same-named file in @modular-react/react:\n\n- resolve-entry.ts: resolveEntryComponent / preloadEntry over\n  defineAsyncComponent (analog of React.lazy). Memoized by entry identity;\n  lazy entries share one cachedImport closure so preload() warms the same\n  import the async wrapper awaits, the importer fires once, `.default` is\n  normalized, and a sync-throwing importer is trapped as a cached rejection.\n- error-boundary.ts: ModuleErrorBoundary via onErrorCaptured (analog of the\n  React class boundary), returning false to contain the error and swapping\n  the subtree for a notice / custom fallback.\n- module-exit.ts: ModuleExitProvider, useModuleExit, useModuleExitDispatcher,\n  moduleExitKey + event/handler types. Dispatcher provided by identity.\n- module-route.ts: ModuleRoute component + ModuleRouteExitEvent alias, with\n  single-entry auto-resolve, unknown / multi / no-entry-points notices, and\n  legacy component fallback.\n\n36 new tests port the React suites case-for-case (React-only StrictMode and\nSuspense-flash cases excepted); package suite is now 69 tests. Workspace\ntypecheck and vite build (JS + dts) pass. Updates the Vue support tracker.\n\n* fix(vue): make rendering pieces reactive to in-place prop changes\n\nAddress reactivity divergences from the React analogs where values that\nReact rebinds every render were snapshotted once in Vue `setup()`:\n\n- module-route: resolve the entry inside a `computed` so a `<router-view>`-\n  hosted `<ModuleRoute>` reused across navigation (props patched in place,\n  no `:key`) re-resolves `module`/`entry` instead of freezing the first\n  route. Bind the exit to getters over the live props so it dispatches with\n  the current `routeId`/`onExit`/resolved entry.\n- module-exit: provide the dispatcher as a getter over the live `onExit`\n  prop so a swapped provider handler reaches descendants; `useModuleExit`\n  now accepts `MaybeRefOrGetter` inputs and reads them via `toValue` at\n  dispatch time (plain values still work unchanged).\n- resolve-entry: clear the inflight slot on an async import rejection so a\n  transient chunk-fetch failure can retry (and no longer defeats\n  `defineAsyncComponent`''s remount retry); a synchronous throw stays cached\n  as before.\n\nAdds regression tests for each: in-place entry re-resolution, swapped\nonExit/localOnExit tracking, provider handler swap, and async import retry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CvssSEBSw6fkyCjvX8iA2B\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS5YpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8A4QAG7t8uR8QZxqADR+LKwV5v+Y\nsv2Lddh7reoNqHWs5J5IRRFfg7AbaVvzBcuzh0I1qPGH4n/EDIymmOOqzdAkLObi\ncZUvYDT6kbyDZBFtuRqu7+s44U71MlmhgmJLKz9ectaaPkXImRNfHkOz+BEopi4e\n1PoI2Njk//5pM5Hc6Vd4eh9YPt+eu32wSIjCYebyLT9STxDmXPmIpNo7wlDEjzZZ\nWED5WFCbFb+LpTQGjZcA3ha6AMDWnbo87Xn8V2/VsOmCfqPxVE8HAnclncuqMgFX\nP9CJ0s33jlzSv3Ur9ne9Hva10HUBw8j+lcR7/b3+nfbV0kNmh1RpR+9t4SIV+5wx\nHaIxRLHs6rrLriV/cyiIVQya5FfEqpCURG89CrmV/j15briQ9oVCvxUgfAdv8KOL\n90r+idpy6RIMXY6NFQAH3Lf7jBlIlCxoG/rt7ARCrQ2e/qDxGnmbr4wHEOxYKAws\nC6f12i388KuiZIe5JANJlPCPaPZYpS2z77aih57axVLCkCrukZIG2KH7hAbWYdmf\n1YV6CvIdNaBXDz5QDVfc5DXrS77Gbza/R9JFBowOySbfIo8zHQHHnUbz+4S6+++F\nSyulnzQ0w/7qQtaU6J8PmDeEqa3D0Xd+6cJm1/2NNhms+2lHfH9qALFYmW1BbE7u\nGyLfrqJohYDaOiy+tJaR\n=k6Yz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T11:48:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/db21126e77231a7787248a2ca747907f0ae2e1d3","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGRiMjExMjZlNzcyMzFhNzc4NzI0OGEyY2E3NDc5MDdmMGFlMmUxZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/4d1fc3c1bafbd5027f368278f16f5915c496ca6b","sha":"4d1fc3c1bafbd5027f368278f16f5915c496ca6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/4d1fc3c1bafbd5027f368278f16f5915c496ca6b"}],"sha":"db21126e77231a7787248a2ca747907f0ae2e1d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/db21126e77231a7787248a2ca747907f0ae2e1d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/4d1fc3c1bafbd5027f368278f16f5915c496ca6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T11:02:20Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T11:02:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(build): switch dts generation to rolldown-plugin-dts (#58)\n\n* chore(build): switch dts generation to rolldown-plugin-dts\n\nReplace vite-plugin-dts with rolldown-plugin-dts across all 15 library\npackages. rolldown-plugin-dts is the rolldown-native declaration bundler\n(used by tsdown) and drops the @microsoft/api-extractor dependency chain.\nIt bundles types with the project''s own TypeScript 6.0.3 instead of\napi-extractor''s bundled 5.9.3, so the version-mismatch warning is gone.\n\nConfig changes per package:\n- import { dts } from \"rolldown-plugin-dts\" (default export -> named)\n- gate the plugin to the build command so it does not run under vitest\n  (vite-plugin-dts guarded this internally; this plugin does not, and its\n  buildStart hook throws in serve/test mode)\n- use object-form lib.entry so the emitted chunk keeps its .d.ts extension\n  (a string entry + fileName clobbers it to .ts)\n- add the oxc.exclude guard recommended for Vite so generated declaration\n  files are not re-transformed\n\nThe published type surface is unchanged. The only diff versus the previous\noutput is that api-extractor''s collision rename TransitionEvent_2 is gone;\nthe author''s intended export name TransitionEvent is kept. Declaration\noutput now code-splits shared types into a chunk, mirroring the existing\nJS code-splitting.\n\nAlso bump vite to ^8.1.3 and vitest to ^4.1.10 workspace-wide. pnpm added\na minimumReleaseAgeExclude entry for vitest@4.1.10 since it is newer than\nthe workspace release-age gate.\n\n* chore(build): pin rolldown-plugin-dts backend to a single rolldown\n\npnpm peer resolution was resolving rolldown-plugin-dts against two\ndifferent rolldown backends: most packages got rolldown@1.1.4 (from\nvite 8.1.x), but frontend-core and journeys-engine got the pre-release\nrolldown@1.0.0-rc.18 that is still in the tree via the examples'' vite\n8.0.x. That meant dts for those two packages was generated through a\ndifferent, pre-release backend than the rest of the workspace.\n\nAdd a scoped `rolldown-plugin-dts>rolldown: 1.1.4` override so every\npackage generates declarations through the same rolldown, without\ntouching the examples'' own vite. Full build (34/34) and typecheck\n(113/113) pass.\n\n* chore(examples): bump example shells to vite 8.1.3\n\nMove all 13 example shells to vite ^8.1.3 (nine were on ^8.0.3, four on\n^6.0.0), and bump the four vite-6 shells'' @vitejs/plugin-react to ^6.0.1\nto match the rest. This removes vite 8.0.11 and vite 6 from the tree,\nwhich also removes the pre-release rolldown@1.0.0-rc.18 that the earlier\ndts-backend split resolved through.\n\nThe rolldown-plugin-dts>rolldown override now has nothing older to\nresolve against, so it stays purely as a guard against a future example\nreintroducing an older vite. Comment reworded to reflect that.\n\nAll four vite 6->8 shells build under vite 8.1.3. Full build (34/34) and\ntypecheck (113/113) pass.","tree":{"sha":"17491e1775d6c86ecb06f4bf14ddb4232ac8d973","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/17491e1775d6c86ecb06f4bf14ddb4232ac8d973"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/4d1fc3c1bafbd5027f368278f16f5915c496ca6b","verification":{"payload":"tree 17491e1775d6c86ecb06f4bf14ddb4232ac8d973\nparent 1bd0b0c8bec2236fea3c0281761088ba452976d3\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1783335740 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783335740 +0300\n\nchore(build): switch dts generation to rolldown-plugin-dts (#58)\n\n* chore(build): switch dts generation to rolldown-plugin-dts\n\nReplace vite-plugin-dts with rolldown-plugin-dts across all 15 library\npackages. rolldown-plugin-dts is the rolldown-native declaration bundler\n(used by tsdown) and drops the @microsoft/api-extractor dependency chain.\nIt bundles types with the project''s own TypeScript 6.0.3 instead of\napi-extractor''s bundled 5.9.3, so the version-mismatch warning is gone.\n\nConfig changes per package:\n- import { dts } from \"rolldown-plugin-dts\" (default export -> named)\n- gate the plugin to the build command so it does not run under vitest\n  (vite-plugin-dts guarded this internally; this plugin does not, and its\n  buildStart hook throws in serve/test mode)\n- use object-form lib.entry so the emitted chunk keeps its .d.ts extension\n  (a string entry + fileName clobbers it to .ts)\n- add the oxc.exclude guard recommended for Vite so generated declaration\n  files are not re-transformed\n\nThe published type surface is unchanged. The only diff versus the previous\noutput is that api-extractor''s collision rename TransitionEvent_2 is gone;\nthe author''s intended export name TransitionEvent is kept. Declaration\noutput now code-splits shared types into a chunk, mirroring the existing\nJS code-splitting.\n\nAlso bump vite to ^8.1.3 and vitest to ^4.1.10 workspace-wide. pnpm added\na minimumReleaseAgeExclude entry for vitest@4.1.10 since it is newer than\nthe workspace release-age gate.\n\n* chore(build): pin rolldown-plugin-dts backend to a single rolldown\n\npnpm peer resolution was resolving rolldown-plugin-dts against two\ndifferent rolldown backends: most packages got rolldown@1.1.4 (from\nvite 8.1.x), but frontend-core and journeys-engine got the pre-release\nrolldown@1.0.0-rc.18 that is still in the tree via the examples'' vite\n8.0.x. That meant dts for those two packages was generated through a\ndifferent, pre-release backend than the rest of the workspace.\n\nAdd a scoped `rolldown-plugin-dts>rolldown: 1.1.4` override so every\npackage generates declarations through the same rolldown, without\ntouching the examples'' own vite. Full build (34/34) and typecheck\n(113/113) pass.\n\n* chore(examples): bump example shells to vite 8.1.3\n\nMove all 13 example shells to vite ^8.1.3 (nine were on ^8.0.3, four on\n^6.0.0), and bump the four vite-6 shells'' @vitejs/plugin-react to ^6.0.1\nto match the rest. This removes vite 8.0.11 and vite 6 from the tree,\nwhich also removes the pre-release rolldown@1.0.0-rc.18 that the earlier\ndts-backend split resolved through.\n\nThe rolldown-plugin-dts>rolldown override now has nothing older to\nresolve against, so it stays purely as a guard against a future example\nreintroducing an older vite. Comment reworded to reflect that.\n\nAll four vite 6->8 shells build under vite 8.1.3. Full build (34/34) and\ntypecheck (113/113) pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS4s8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjlQQACcSe7/LuO8IDNtaunwblNPd\ncP8nKnNVMjQ5zeji31dwQw1eX7zhwXfMT1uS3zUyTYSrsYbukxTppPZ9E3/HeUAP\n3i8VrJ94/oZqi3rcTBuZzsqjBn0LxPjo0A8pEMh/YjOguHxxuv61/6YspLlICz0q\nEMisFGp1nOT3xGbVGa91gWz2LKrbQAi9buWGwv+uGt+iuBYKKe/IuozKRchYiIg7\naXO+ETAA0qcICCP0HnKgF9xQLPGRC0PmrhSCLFuVemyMtA92tyj/erY91ZY5O0or\nQJRDIp+qMmTaILRlULAdXwbJty1+Udory1aSgjFQKRrig2w1aME5XW3Nc54dm8zF\npTLYQ6fb+eG9YkrYcrkL0HDt9QpuFP60e47gdV3X6JhCVw6zpSeqMdBIdhjYbjGk\nHiA2Czg5IBh6SxpvQzA+lFvkGaPST+B4RTpL7oDv9uT29MladCuCwmj1OngmFq0M\n9uWGCCC5fszSSnLuoI6s7bV72YvEIQECyW99qZcjs9HJVuqKazI8MxGbbNiB4JtP\nFeG98p/MBql0lUdTgEz7E60RqZSbmwUrukCF/YanVllChWNHY9MyqxUGOIbxFaCH\npptPekX8ckQHLXtDdYSD+zW2wBrC5PhUgCv19c49qD5vTbWfyD1UVnAI8e5XNxxj\nP/KX85sn/qqOjBbcXKss\n=TdSX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T11:02:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/4d1fc3c1bafbd5027f368278f16f5915c496ca6b","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKDRkMWZjM2MxYmFmYmQ1MDI3ZjM2ODI3OGYxNmY1OTE1YzQ5NmNhNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/1bd0b0c8bec2236fea3c0281761088ba452976d3","sha":"1bd0b0c8bec2236fea3c0281761088ba452976d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/1bd0b0c8bec2236fea3c0281761088ba452976d3"}],"sha":"4d1fc3c1bafbd5027f368278f16f5915c496ca6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/4d1fc3c1bafbd5027f368278f16f5915c496ca6b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/1bd0b0c8bec2236fea3c0281761088ba452976d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T10:06:34Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T10:06:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(vue): add @modular-vue/vue stores and context (PR-10) (#57)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/vue stores and context (PR-10)\n\nFirst package of Phase 1 of the Vue support initiative: the Vue 3 binding\nlayer for stores and context, the analog of @modular-react/react part 1.\n\nNew packages/vue (@modular-vue/vue, 0.1.0) with the repo''s standard package\nskeleton (vite build + vite-plugin-dts, vitest + happy-dom + @vue/test-utils,\ntsc typecheck). It depends on the neutral engine @modular-frontend/core, not\nthe React facade, plus a vue ^3.5 peer.\n\n- store-ref.ts: storeRef / reactiveServiceRef bridge a framework-neutral\n  Store<T> / ReactiveService<T> into a shallowRef, pushing snapshots from the\n  source''s subscribe callback and unsubscribing on onScopeDispose. The Vue\n  analog of React''s useSyncExternalStore; shallowRef''s Object.is dedupe gives\n  selector equality for free.\n- createSharedComposables (analog of createSharedHooks): useStore, useService,\n  useReactiveService, useOptional. Reactive accessors return a Ref; plain\n  services return the value directly.\n- createScopedStore with a useScoped composable.\n- Typed InjectionKeys + provide*/use* for the modules, navigation, and slots\n  contexts (useModules, getModuleMeta, useNavigation, useSlots,\n  useRecalculateSlots, DynamicSlotsProvider, createSlotsSignal).\n\nDynamicSlotsProvider uses defineComponent + a render function per decision D4,\nso no @vitejs/plugin-vue is needed in the package build.\n\n33 tests across 6 files mirror the React suites case-for-case, plus a\n.test-d.ts porting the typed-label / typed-meta navigation assertions and\nreactivity tests for subscribe/unsubscribe-on-unmount and selector equality.\nFull workspace typecheck (113 tasks) and build pass.\n\nUpdates the Vue support tracker: PR-10 marked done, status board advanced to\nPhase 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NUBajywtUJZ4y3dVe57tSd\n\n* refactor(vue): address review findings for @modular-vue/vue\n\n- context: look up services with `key in` instead of a truthy check so a\n  legitimately falsy plain-service value (0, false, \"\") is returned rather\n  than misreported as unregistered; collapse the three duplicate\n  lookup/throw blocks in useStore/useService/useReactiveService into a\n  shared requireDep() helper (which also carries the fix)\n- store-ref: extract a shared subscribeRef() helper behind storeRef and\n  reactiveServiceRef, keeping the leak-sensitive subscribe/teardown in one\n  place\n- slots-context: reuse core''s buildDepsSnapshot() in DynamicSlotsProvider\n  instead of hand-rolling the deps record; document that useSlots collides\n  by name with Vue''s built-in useSlots\n- package.json: move @modular-frontend/core to peerDependencies (+ keep as\n  a devDependency), mirroring how @modular-react/react declares its core\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CaJhMvixUQWfc393Dy4dta\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c24bb226bd824bfa7fd9e007308153da332637a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/c24bb226bd824bfa7fd9e007308153da332637a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/1bd0b0c8bec2236fea3c0281761088ba452976d3","verification":{"payload":"tree c24bb226bd824bfa7fd9e007308153da332637a3\nparent c2ffd8de163fd39220b6cbcf70d4d9ad3c37a7a5\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1783332394 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783332394 +0300\n\nfeat(vue): add @modular-vue/vue stores and context (PR-10) (#57)\n\n* feat(vue): add @modular-vue/vue stores and context (PR-10)\n\nFirst package of Phase 1 of the Vue support initiative: the Vue 3 binding\nlayer for stores and context, the analog of @modular-react/react part 1.\n\nNew packages/vue (@modular-vue/vue, 0.1.0) with the repo''s standard package\nskeleton (vite build + vite-plugin-dts, vitest + happy-dom + @vue/test-utils,\ntsc typecheck). It depends on the neutral engine @modular-frontend/core, not\nthe React facade, plus a vue ^3.5 peer.\n\n- store-ref.ts: storeRef / reactiveServiceRef bridge a framework-neutral\n  Store<T> / ReactiveService<T> into a shallowRef, pushing snapshots from the\n  source''s subscribe callback and unsubscribing on onScopeDispose. The Vue\n  analog of React''s useSyncExternalStore; shallowRef''s Object.is dedupe gives\n  selector equality for free.\n- createSharedComposables (analog of createSharedHooks): useStore, useService,\n  useReactiveService, useOptional. Reactive accessors return a Ref; plain\n  services return the value directly.\n- createScopedStore with a useScoped composable.\n- Typed InjectionKeys + provide*/use* for the modules, navigation, and slots\n  contexts (useModules, getModuleMeta, useNavigation, useSlots,\n  useRecalculateSlots, DynamicSlotsProvider, createSlotsSignal).\n\nDynamicSlotsProvider uses defineComponent + a render function per decision D4,\nso no @vitejs/plugin-vue is needed in the package build.\n\n33 tests across 6 files mirror the React suites case-for-case, plus a\n.test-d.ts porting the typed-label / typed-meta navigation assertions and\nreactivity tests for subscribe/unsubscribe-on-unmount and selector equality.\nFull workspace typecheck (113 tasks) and build pass.\n\nUpdates the Vue support tracker: PR-10 marked done, status board advanced to\nPhase 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NUBajywtUJZ4y3dVe57tSd\n\n* refactor(vue): address review findings for @modular-vue/vue\n\n- context: look up services with `key in` instead of a truthy check so a\n  legitimately falsy plain-service value (0, false, \"\") is returned rather\n  than misreported as unregistered; collapse the three duplicate\n  lookup/throw blocks in useStore/useService/useReactiveService into a\n  shared requireDep() helper (which also carries the fix)\n- store-ref: extract a shared subscribeRef() helper behind storeRef and\n  reactiveServiceRef, keeping the leak-sensitive subscribe/teardown in one\n  place\n- slots-context: reuse core''s buildDepsSnapshot() in DynamicSlotsProvider\n  instead of hand-rolling the deps record; document that useSlots collides\n  by name with Vue''s built-in useSlots\n- package.json: move @modular-frontend/core to peerDependencies (+ keep as\n  a devDependency), mirroring how @modular-react/react declares its core\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CaJhMvixUQWfc393Dy4dta\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS34qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuPEQAAJQ7uDs+z7H6MiaUsnjY/hj\nj9Ixw09MggCU23szpFXNjZXIO2a0wZUB01EglQNzf4zepNvzfcZXJKgAGQviol4l\nOXrPWwNhSijli0HZK8Qys2FbcAC0DhaZPYRfLyq8LlwWnEQkjSmRw9mXpDWuK1Vm\nn0rJIgswImRA8NEnQZyDeZJOvWOK83r+zqaJGsa8ZM0wc67YwSamIPdecw1P5IHA\nLc4pxF2oBV5m0Lq/hNU6pR20q/hPL/UOhxTODr4w14S3o0EvQAsolXikszeLyYLw\ng4AcbZY63/KBXDy1HCaN5T9CVr+fql6iLPVqDcmLFCZVQmifC7jj0L7/5FOP+e0X\nnE3MlmT37GqboAqGOnUthdUcbdlrLW1iEiAlZeWO3wGCyDyHjPcPebH7VGXpwQU4\nz0wyDqvGHfy8GZfyXOWtVuKO9oL0pm+ojDf/qW8gI2wpsMNULLVYoJV8u9Vg9NuZ\nllnLGe31X8lVin/3FJDWDhiQ9MsyCRgSXIbFZsK9iG8/GXMYSKfgyksknO8K/BCn\n9E/dwOcEkW/Of60AXr2NrzzHn+yotsZ3WN1pvY2t9IKeQd7w9YcZX18AkXWWEbSj\nlcd9LztNdZ6PT5E/XgNsfBoMtqaNu8MOk4UxSA5BrMBDyB2ITt3cqSb2CYmGrcyy\nFN5+R+/BfzGfQTTU6iQq\n=4DYD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T10:06:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/1bd0b0c8bec2236fea3c0281761088ba452976d3","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKDFiZDBiMGM4YmVjMjIzNmZlYTNjMDI4MTc2MTA4OGJhNDUyOTc2ZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/c2ffd8de163fd39220b6cbcf70d4d9ad3c37a7a5","sha":"c2ffd8de163fd39220b6cbcf70d4d9ad3c37a7a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c2ffd8de163fd39220b6cbcf70d4d9ad3c37a7a5"}],"sha":"1bd0b0c8bec2236fea3c0281761088ba452976d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/1bd0b0c8bec2236fea3c0281761088ba452976d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c2ffd8de163fd39220b6cbcf70d4d9ad3c37a7a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T07:37:11Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T07:37:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(compositions): extract framework-neutral @modular-frontend/compositions-engine (#56)\n\nPR-03 of the Vue-support initiative. Splits the framework-neutral guts of\n@modular-react/compositions into a new @modular-frontend/compositions-engine\npackage so a future Vue binding can reuse them, mirroring the journeys-engine\nextraction (#55) and the frontend-core extraction (#54).\n\nWhat moves: the pure files (runtime.ts, stores.ts, validation.ts,\ndefine-composition.ts, types.ts) plus their non-.tsx tests. The engine depends\nonly on @modular-frontend/core; happy-dom is a dev dep for the test\nenvironment. @modular-react/compositions keeps its React files (outlet.tsx,\nprovider.tsx, plugin.tsx, hooks.ts) and all .tsx tests, and re-exports the\nengine so its public export surface is unchanged.\n\nOne React reference had to be neutralized, matching #54/PR-02:\nCompositionZoneDescriptor.fallback used React.ComponentType; it moves to the\nneutral UiComponent seam from @modular-frontend/core. Source-compatible for\nauthors (a React component still satisfies UiComponent). Error-message\nprefixes stay [@modular-react/compositions] on purpose — they name the package\nusers import.\n\nTest counts preserved: 52 in the engine + 63 in the binding = the pre-split\ntotal of 115. Full workspace typecheck and lint clean.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sf7deW3iRQaaSjZuj3akTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b454c45ec18592eb919e716b7bfc922947ddae38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/b454c45ec18592eb919e716b7bfc922947ddae38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/c2ffd8de163fd39220b6cbcf70d4d9ad3c37a7a5","verification":{"payload":"tree b454c45ec18592eb919e716b7bfc922947ddae38\nparent 952475f84baa90793505e98fec5f14290950ea07\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1783323431 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783323431 +0300\n\nrefactor(compositions): extract framework-neutral @modular-frontend/compositions-engine (#56)\n\nPR-03 of the Vue-support initiative. Splits the framework-neutral guts of\n@modular-react/compositions into a new @modular-frontend/compositions-engine\npackage so a future Vue binding can reuse them, mirroring the journeys-engine\nextraction (#55) and the frontend-core extraction (#54).\n\nWhat moves: the pure files (runtime.ts, stores.ts, validation.ts,\ndefine-composition.ts, types.ts) plus their non-.tsx tests. The engine depends\nonly on @modular-frontend/core; happy-dom is a dev dep for the test\nenvironment. @modular-react/compositions keeps its React files (outlet.tsx,\nprovider.tsx, plugin.tsx, hooks.ts) and all .tsx tests, and re-exports the\nengine so its public export surface is unchanged.\n\nOne React reference had to be neutralized, matching #54/PR-02:\nCompositionZoneDescriptor.fallback used React.ComponentType; it moves to the\nneutral UiComponent seam from @modular-frontend/core. Source-compatible for\nauthors (a React component still satisfies UiComponent). Error-message\nprefixes stay [@modular-react/compositions] on purpose — they name the package\nusers import.\n\nTest counts preserved: 52 in the engine + 63 in the binding = the pre-split\ntotal of 115. Full workspace typecheck and lint clean.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sf7deW3iRQaaSjZuj3akTA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS1snCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvrsQAEh/7x+/TjbA4KDOV9H9X4OW\ncwDKAmHRgNa1OGPcMmCwqJG8umgXbJTzplG7CRDRRuTk8Oyy6ICx8gzGQ7L8uVnl\nnlJAVYCUTMRI7MXK6qDWDgr2Xta3AwqOK08BH00gFjPiaZnBDKMIyMf4/mI43WxQ\nxEWUCiBIAbqU0v7v6lkLKrt3fNo84QQ7OrszbEBZoye7urxMh8Elzy9n/GsBzsyx\nQhcP9zl/rdw65hy0rLNxvlatHjc8MRTfxT1mm8OT7I9k+veyeXq4C9yKrVNr18IJ\nRJtIYX1BcK9+zwxnoTdhmh+qsANJhiuzM3q7XOd3KX+LLO3diF5dSZ9SFy3mUUSA\nEIZORC+htRRQJ2d7W+x6zxpO6PyinkjDEPZI9QT5TB+Pv0SmtYI5nYPvY7B7ZVYl\nD6VE4H19tDVSETbQvlDvBS/1BVqJa9VAhLG4S0ATnEVGwP36Zs0UfDSOWApeAaYU\nkXlWQLUoqNWVYBy9Qr46AFZijQESCySOEDqkzMJeRuEBWKyvNJZPJHBwJO/2pt4t\ngVJgEV0LvWxYa3NZwpNswhBY0eSvvCCBgc6O9XTSPjXoNc9hJiEugpFOwRlUrWpJ\nm/ratTLrrWB+4idhqi/DZDe5IxIo7FaRSF/CDy8XdMJC957ubPNeWiyk/gq+eS/s\nVtPhhod2mvQRAUAMZfkd\n=7Ihx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T07:37:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/c2ffd8de163fd39220b6cbcf70d4d9ad3c37a7a5","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGMyZmZkOGRlMTYzZmQzOTIyMGI2Y2JjZjcwZDRkOWFkM2MzN2E3YTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/952475f84baa90793505e98fec5f14290950ea07","sha":"952475f84baa90793505e98fec5f14290950ea07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/952475f84baa90793505e98fec5f14290950ea07"}],"sha":"c2ffd8de163fd39220b6cbcf70d4d9ad3c37a7a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/c2ffd8de163fd39220b6cbcf70d4d9ad3c37a7a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/952475f84baa90793505e98fec5f14290950ea07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-05T21:01:09Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-05T21:01:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(journeys): extract framework-neutral @modular-frontend/journeys-engine (#55)\n\n* refactor(journeys): extract framework-neutral @modular-frontend/journeys-engine\n\nPR-02 of the Vue-support initiative. Split the framework-neutral guts of\n@modular-react/journeys into a new @modular-frontend/journeys-engine package so\na future Vue binding can reuse them, mirroring the @modular-frontend/core\nextraction from #54.\n\n- New packages/journeys-engine (@modular-frontend/journeys-engine): the runtime,\n  validation, persistence, authoring helpers (defineJourney/defineTransition/\n  selectModule), handles, simulate-journey, the test harness, and the full type\n  surface, plus their non-React tests. Depends only on @modular-frontend/core\n  (happy-dom is a dev dep for the storage-backed persistence tests). Two entries:\n  index + /testing.\n- @modular-react/journeys keeps its React files (outlet, module-tab, provider,\n  plugin, instance-hooks, use-journey-state, use-wait-for-exit, mount-adapter)\n  and re-exports the engine, so its public export surface is unchanged. A thin\n  testing.ts re-exports the engine''s /testing entry, keeping the existing\n  @modular-react/journeys/testing import path working.\n\nTwo forced deviations from the tracker''s PR-02 plan:\n\n- mount-adapter.ts stays in the binding, not the engine: createJourneyMountAdapter\n  supplies Outlet: JourneyOutlet (a React component), so it is binding-specific\n  glue over the neutral RuntimeMountAdapter seam rather than engine logic.\n- JourneyNavContribution.icon used the React.ComponentType namespace; it moves to\n  the neutral UiComponent seam, matching how NavigationItem.icon was neutralized\n  in #54. Source-compatible for authors (a React component still satisfies\n  UiComponent).\n\nError-message prefixes stay [@modular-react/journeys] / [@modular-react/journeys/\ntesting] on purpose: they name the package users import and point at real import\npaths, so the moved tests pass unmodified.\n\nVerification: engine 346 tests (26 files) + journeys 72 tests (8 files) = the\npre-split total; @modular-react/compositions (the createJourneyMountAdapter\nconsumer) 115 tests pass; full workspace typecheck (110 tasks) and pnpm lint\nclean. The only failing tests are the pre-existing Windows EPERM .test-output\nflake in the two router CLIs, unrelated to this change.\n\n* docs(journeys-engine): drop mount-adapter from the engine README\n\ncreateJourneyMountAdapter stays in the @modular-react/journeys binding (it\nsupplies the React JourneyOutlet), so the engine does not ship it. Listing it\nunder \"What''s included\" advertised an export this package does not provide.\n\n* docs(journeys): address PR review comments on the engine extraction\n\n- vue-support-tracker: soften the shared-engines header so it no longer reads\n  as if compositions-engine is already extracted, and add the #55 reference to\n  the PR-02 status-board row.\n- journeys/index.ts: point the getInternals note at @modular-frontend/journeys-engine;\n  runtime.ts no longer lives in this package.\n- journeys-engine/testing.ts: extract the repeated record + registration +\n  loading guard shared by fireExit/goBack/goForward into one activeRecordAndReg\n  helper.","tree":{"sha":"7925dea108e8814616a69d8168999ed8ac7def20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/7925dea108e8814616a69d8168999ed8ac7def20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/952475f84baa90793505e98fec5f14290950ea07","verification":{"payload":"tree 7925dea108e8814616a69d8168999ed8ac7def20\nparent 7249c1ec907b54850a511fe773760fcf8be6f481\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1783285269 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783285269 +0300\n\nrefactor(journeys): extract framework-neutral @modular-frontend/journeys-engine (#55)\n\n* refactor(journeys): extract framework-neutral @modular-frontend/journeys-engine\n\nPR-02 of the Vue-support initiative. Split the framework-neutral guts of\n@modular-react/journeys into a new @modular-frontend/journeys-engine package so\na future Vue binding can reuse them, mirroring the @modular-frontend/core\nextraction from #54.\n\n- New packages/journeys-engine (@modular-frontend/journeys-engine): the runtime,\n  validation, persistence, authoring helpers (defineJourney/defineTransition/\n  selectModule), handles, simulate-journey, the test harness, and the full type\n  surface, plus their non-React tests. Depends only on @modular-frontend/core\n  (happy-dom is a dev dep for the storage-backed persistence tests). Two entries:\n  index + /testing.\n- @modular-react/journeys keeps its React files (outlet, module-tab, provider,\n  plugin, instance-hooks, use-journey-state, use-wait-for-exit, mount-adapter)\n  and re-exports the engine, so its public export surface is unchanged. A thin\n  testing.ts re-exports the engine''s /testing entry, keeping the existing\n  @modular-react/journeys/testing import path working.\n\nTwo forced deviations from the tracker''s PR-02 plan:\n\n- mount-adapter.ts stays in the binding, not the engine: createJourneyMountAdapter\n  supplies Outlet: JourneyOutlet (a React component), so it is binding-specific\n  glue over the neutral RuntimeMountAdapter seam rather than engine logic.\n- JourneyNavContribution.icon used the React.ComponentType namespace; it moves to\n  the neutral UiComponent seam, matching how NavigationItem.icon was neutralized\n  in #54. Source-compatible for authors (a React component still satisfies\n  UiComponent).\n\nError-message prefixes stay [@modular-react/journeys] / [@modular-react/journeys/\ntesting] on purpose: they name the package users import and point at real import\npaths, so the moved tests pass unmodified.\n\nVerification: engine 346 tests (26 files) + journeys 72 tests (8 files) = the\npre-split total; @modular-react/compositions (the createJourneyMountAdapter\nconsumer) 115 tests pass; full workspace typecheck (110 tasks) and pnpm lint\nclean. The only failing tests are the pre-existing Windows EPERM .test-output\nflake in the two router CLIs, unrelated to this change.\n\n* docs(journeys-engine): drop mount-adapter from the engine README\n\ncreateJourneyMountAdapter stays in the @modular-react/journeys binding (it\nsupplies the React JourneyOutlet), so the engine does not ship it. Listing it\nunder \"What''s included\" advertised an export this package does not provide.\n\n* docs(journeys): address PR review comments on the engine extraction\n\n- vue-support-tracker: soften the shared-engines header so it no longer reads\n  as if compositions-engine is already extracted, and add the #55 reference to\n  the PR-02 status-board row.\n- journeys/index.ts: point the getInternals note at @modular-frontend/journeys-engine;\n  runtime.ts no longer lives in this package.\n- journeys-engine/testing.ts: extract the repeated record + registration +\n  loading guard shared by fireExit/goBack/goForward into one activeRecordAndReg\n  helper.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSsYVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzA8QACh7b2D6I2FWxkZhSR+Ax7vo\nDQq55FCu0JgxfbVdZHh8HnRd+oVK64CUU9ZkUroHCT8N4k7jF6VLANZEsxapnEv9\n6ah8SNE7/69Lj9NNm3M+T37XljRlL+ZGJ9Eqj3Lok/JhBjlz/HUe5f6qUFQbPHZJ\nyw05OX6pUuRd+xhOOOZswrI1+m91jib14+68Hjuks0haalzaBorHYRr/4/18fAkc\nib7B+D62mbaldsze3c/nrlO/vk5BBIRy+3NhFdZ5e/d4J0dR6TP2qt9Rlp3lYw45\nsDjQi4L/gpt1fWsUcyJYFO6Hqa7Plkn813AfA38hNoHgRhOyu+v0RQbnK9pVOBnX\n+o/jLfmraqxgpER4YMyh1K0tdoCQ6y0mcXHRp06HGQncn6S3yd3tl2l9XHzlr4hP\nAP6dX3k+oTWZTZhAO/RSiceMVYUxXBOyGNDZj3dfqfiG2+7QWzUxBfzioYSvtCzn\n+XJkQgU/NtTabehcy9XbmlBIFNpmFSIK2/lQjSAmfxQl0+yYC5CSpaEyk0x3c2xD\ni0GftJ3RXdHtwORyvq4FQgIcYjtxT1a+B/nvw8QNscdfqyoT803Ll3Ch5FMHMjBx\n35zKnKqgdm/6fu8KLjPS12iZjt5TnTdoNtW8HJpnMjzw+RWLC11clUpxUEXMdR75\nKJHNVYf7hpY2FqVl1vuk\n=wDKN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-05T21:01:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/952475f84baa90793505e98fec5f14290950ea07","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKDk1MjQ3NWY4NGJhYTkwNzkzNTA1ZTk4ZmVjNWYxNDI5MDk1MGVhMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/7249c1ec907b54850a511fe773760fcf8be6f481","sha":"7249c1ec907b54850a511fe773760fcf8be6f481","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/7249c1ec907b54850a511fe773760fcf8be6f481"}],"sha":"952475f84baa90793505e98fec5f14290950ea07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/952475f84baa90793505e98fec5f14290950ea07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/7249c1ec907b54850a511fe773760fcf8be6f481/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-05T20:14:35Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-05T20:14:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(core): extract framework-neutral @modular-frontend/core (#54)\n\n* refactor(core): extract framework-neutral @modular-frontend/core\n\nFirst step of the Vue-support initiative: split the framework-neutral guts\nof @modular-react/core into a new @modular-frontend/core package so a future\nVue binding can reuse them.\n\n- New packages/frontend-core (@modular-frontend/core): all the current core\n  logic and types, with no UI-framework dependency. React''s ComponentType /\n  ReactNode references become a two-line neutral seam (UiComponent / UiNode)\n  in ui-types.ts. @types/react is dropped from the package.\n- @modular-react/core becomes a thin facade that re-exports the neutral\n  surface (export * from \"@modular-frontend/core\"), so all existing consumers\n  keep importing from @modular-react/core unchanged. Name and version are\n  unchanged.\n- UiComponent is \"callable or constructable with props P\", which admits\n  React''s full ComponentType (function and class) and stays usable as a JSX\n  element type; a Vue binding can narrow it. UiNode is loose (any) so bindings\n  can pass nodes straight into their framework''s render slots.\n- Runtime error prefixes and package-name doc comments in the moved files\n  updated to @modular-frontend/core.\n- Add project CLAUDE.md documenting the repo-wide oxfmt workflow.\n\nFull workspace typecheck (108 tasks) and build (31 tasks) pass; the neutral\npackage''s 270 tests pass. The only failing test is the pre-existing Windows\nEPERM flake in @tanstack-react-modules/cli, unrelated to this change.\n\n* docs(frontend-core): fix UiComponent/UiNode seam docs, drop unused @types/react\n\nThe frontend-core README documented an earlier single-arm draft of the seam:\n`UiComponent<P> = (props: P) => any` and `UiNode = unknown`. The actual\nui-types.ts is `((props: P) => any) | (new (props: P) => any)` and\n`UiNode = any`. Update the snippet and prose to match, including the construct\narm (class components) and the rationale for `any` over `unknown`.\n\nThe @modular-react/core facade is now only `export * from \"@modular-frontend/core\"`\nwith no React type usage, so its @types/react devDependency and optional peer\nwere dead weight. Remove both; they can layer back when a real React refinement\nof the UiComponent seam lands here.\n\n* docs: add bash language tag to oxfmt fence in CLAUDE.md\n\nmarkdownlint MD040 flags fenced blocks without a language. The oxfmt example\nblock is a shell command, so tag it `bash`.","tree":{"sha":"652bae16c2750b0e06a4794a73006dbb4e788940","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/652bae16c2750b0e06a4794a73006dbb4e788940"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/7249c1ec907b54850a511fe773760fcf8be6f481","verification":{"payload":"tree 652bae16c2750b0e06a4794a73006dbb4e788940\nparent c22050bac2412cc0eb6aedcf24f4eb85d1590264\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1783282475 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783282475 +0300\n\nrefactor(core): extract framework-neutral @modular-frontend/core (#54)\n\n* refactor(core): extract framework-neutral @modular-frontend/core\n\nFirst step of the Vue-support initiative: split the framework-neutral guts\nof @modular-react/core into a new @modular-frontend/core package so a future\nVue binding can reuse them.\n\n- New packages/frontend-core (@modular-frontend/core): all the current core\n  logic and types, with no UI-framework dependency. React''s ComponentType /\n  ReactNode references become a two-line neutral seam (UiComponent / UiNode)\n  in ui-types.ts. @types/react is dropped from the package.\n- @modular-react/core becomes a thin facade that re-exports the neutral\n  surface (export * from \"@modular-frontend/core\"), so all existing consumers\n  keep importing from @modular-react/core unchanged. Name and version are\n  unchanged.\n- UiComponent is \"callable or constructable with props P\", which admits\n  React''s full ComponentType (function and class) and stays usable as a JSX\n  element type; a Vue binding can narrow it. UiNode is loose (any) so bindings\n  can pass nodes straight into their framework''s render slots.\n- Runtime error prefixes and package-name doc comments in the moved files\n  updated to @modular-frontend/core.\n- Add project CLAUDE.md documenting the repo-wide oxfmt workflow.\n\nFull workspace typecheck (108 tasks) and build (31 tasks) pass; the neutral\npackage''s 270 tests pass. The only failing test is the pre-existing Windows\nEPERM flake in @tanstack-react-modules/cli, unrelated to this change.\n\n* docs(frontend-core): fix UiComponent/UiNode seam docs, drop unused @types/react\n\nThe frontend-core README documented an earlier single-arm draft of the seam:\n`UiComponent<P> = (props: P) => any` and `UiNode = unknown`. The actual\nui-types.ts is `((props: P) => any) | (new (props: P) => any)` and\n`UiNode = any`. Update the snippet and prose to match, including the construct\narm (class components) and the rationale for `any` over `unknown`.\n\nThe @modular-react/core facade is now only `export * from \"@modular-frontend/core\"`\nwith no React type usage, so its @types/react devDependency and optional peer\nwere dead weight. Remove both; they can layer back when a real React refinement\nof the UiComponent seam lands here.\n\n* docs: add bash language tag to oxfmt fence in CLAUDE.md\n\nmarkdownlint MD040 flags fenced blocks without a language. The oxfmt example\nblock is a shell command, so tag it `bash`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSrsrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAProQAJQ96j36UW/pn+TSBqBx9IO1\nLrM6gTdEoAtj5yIQiiNn9xka4Wf0xj5RKdEYB9vQkTb5Vpy1y/4maK1do/bl2EG6\nH7SFJN+CiTHkZnRYlJ3W67H1qTZkjhG