82,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/de89cda3100ce41ff29acea0d1b9262f8275e79d","node_id":"C_kwDOR46l09oAKGRlODljZGEzMTAwY2U0MWZmMjlhY2VhMGQxYjkyNjJmODI3NWU3OWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad/modular-react/commit/d81a461f1356f97e01ba47bc5121e6cd27ff53a1","sha":"d81a461f1356f97e01ba47bc5121e6cd27ff53a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/d81a461f1356f97e01ba47bc5121e6cd27ff53a1"}],"sha":"de89cda3100ce41ff29acea0d1b9262f8275e79d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/de89cda3100ce41ff29acea0d1b9262f8275e79d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847934?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kibertoad","id":1847934,"login":"kibertoad","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5MzQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kibertoad","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/commits/d81a461f1356f97e01ba47bc5121e6cd27ff53a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T12:32:12Z","email":"iselwin@gmail.com","name":"Igor Savin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T12:32:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Revise CLI packages: refresh deps, fix stale template pins, add catalog bootstrap (#53)\n\n* Revise CLI packages: refresh deps, fix stale template pins, add catalog bootstrap\n\nDependency revision (CLI packages aligned with the rest of the repo):\n- typescript ^6.0.2 -> ^6.0.3, vitest ^4.1.0 -> ^4.1.5 in the router CLIs\n- @clack/prompts ^1.2.0 -> ^1.3.0 in cli-core\n- declare rimraf ^6.0.1 in the router CLIs (used by `clean`, previously\n  relied on hoisting)\n- bump pinned pnpm to 11.8.0 (latest; 12.x is not released) and regenerate\n  the lockfile\n\nTemplate freshness (generated projects now pull current library majors):\n- RUNTIME_VERSIONS: core/react ^1.0.0 -> ^2.0.0, journeys ^0.1.0 -> ^1.0.0\n- wire RUNTIME_VERSIONS into app-shared/module/shell templates instead of\n  the dead hardcoded ^1.0.0 literals the centralization comment warned about\n- TanStack preset router pin ^1.120.0 -> ^1.168.0 (matches example apps)\n\nCatalog bootstrap (new):\n- `create catalog` subcommand and `init --with-catalog` flag generate a root\n  catalog.config.ts (scanning modules/* + journeys/*) and wire\n  @modular-react/catalog plus catalog:build / catalog:serve scripts into the\n  workspace root package.json; idempotent, with a guard against double-wiring\n- tests covering both paths in each router CLI; READMEs updated\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A8ek5nug7A8AZrHgDj1Yjy\n\n* Address PR review: catalog bootstrap resilience, CI-safe flag, name escaping\n\n- bootstrapCatalog now reconciles the root package.json wiring on every run\n  (idempotent), so a workspace whose catalog.config.ts survived a previous\n  partial failure can self-heal instead of being stuck \"already configured\"\n- init: include --with-catalog in the non-interactive flag detection so\n  passing it alone fails fast in CI rather than blocking on stdin prompts\n- catalog config template: escape single quotes in the project title so\n  names like O''Reilly can''t break the generated single-quoted literal\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A8ek5nug7A8AZrHgDj1Yjy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f7044b7bbe17a1d1a02e71a0d6998ad381072886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/trees/f7044b7bbe17a1d1a02e71a0d6998ad381072886"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kibertoad/modular-react/git/commits/d81a461f1356f97e01ba47bc5121e6cd27ff53a1","verification":{"payload":"tree f7044b7bbe17a1d1a02e71a0d6998ad381072886\nparent 6ff164864a1ddfd4b1955c3b2e90d29be7ae422f\nauthor Igor Savin <iselwin@gmail.com> 1782045132 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782045132 +0300\n\nRevise CLI packages: refresh deps, fix stale template pins, add catalog bootstrap (#53)\n\n* Revise CLI packages: refresh deps, fix stale template pins, add catalog bootstrap\n\nDependency revision (CLI packages aligned with the rest of the repo):\n- typescript ^6.0.2 -> ^6.0.3, vitest ^4.1.0 -> ^4.1.5 in the router CLIs\n- @clack/prompts ^1.2.0 -> ^1.3.0 in cli-core\n- declare rimraf ^6.0.1 in the router CLIs (used by `clean`, previously\n  relied on hoisting)\n- bump pinned pnpm to 11.8.0 (latest; 12.x is not released) and regenerate\n  the lockfile\n\nTemplate freshness (generated projects now pull current library majors):\n- RUNTIME_VERSIONS: core/react ^1.0.0 -> ^2.0.0, journeys ^0.1.0 -> ^1.0.0\n- wire RUNTIME_VERSIONS into app-shared/module/shell templates instead of\n  the dead hardcoded ^1.0.0 literals the centralization comment warned about\n- TanStack preset router pin ^1.120.0 -> ^1.168.0 (matches example apps)\n\nCatalog bootstrap (new):\n- `create catalog` subcommand and `init --with-catalog` flag generate a root\n  catalog.config.ts (scanning modules/* + journeys/*) and wire\n  @modular-react/catalog plus catalog:build / catalog:serve scripts into the\n  workspace root package.json; idempotent, with a guard against double-wiring\n- tests covering both paths in each router CLI; READMEs updated\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A8ek5nug7A8AZrHgDj1Yjy\n\n* Address PR review: catalog bootstrap resilience, CI-safe flag, name escaping\n\n- bootstrapCatalog now reconciles the root package.json wiring on every run\n  (idempotent), so a workspace whose catalog.config.ts survived a previous\n  partial failure can self-heal instead of being stuck \"already configured\"\n- init: include --with-catalog in the non-interactive flag detection so\n  passing it alone fails fast in CI rather than blocking on stdin prompts\n- catalog config template: escape single quotes in the project title so\n  names like O''Reilly can''t break the generated single-quoted literal\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A8ek5nug7A8AZrHgDj1Yjy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqN9nMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZtgQAIXvkDY+/hEQNPYLbh2G2Kpo\nB5PxyA/e4dgtmtMqWLv/vLBzERbSMNcK8sEKrJlC+FVSTmKabZosJSNBBDIULvGs\nTymAXyYwfqAE+1u11H2XOe6G0DltTtKxpGu6f5L7dQT7EgRzzCXTaRMmWRCwdF3j\nXG9H9cL023Ib6q2E/tdtQXNinzjlKHv27qTwiRDzsXfIqMowl2ECAP367fRhbB7s\nTQwTxcjRa+VFRhE1tE9IETpY4RG0mGX